msgstr "piso duro de papel"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hard paper floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"Hardened cardboard floor made of chewed up trees and resin mixed with wasp "
"saliva."
msgstr ""
"Un piso de cartón duro hecho con árboles y resina machacados y mezclados con"
" saliva de avispa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid "paper brood cap"
msgstr "cobertura de papel de crías"

#. ~ Description of terrain "paper brood cap"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
msgid ""
"A thin paper floor, protecting the pupating wasp larva until it's ready to "
"emerge."
msgstr ""
"Un piso de papel fino, que protege a la larva de avispa pupante hasta que "
"esta lista para emerger."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_commercial.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_evac_center.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_hardcoded.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_lab.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_mall.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_recreational.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_residential.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_retirement_community.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_robofachq.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain_waste_junk.json
#: data/mods/Graphical_Overmap/go_overmap_terrain_ranch_camp.json
#: data/mods/Graphical_Overmap/go_overmap_terrain_waste_junk.json
#: data/mods/alt_map_key/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "open air"
msgstr "aire libre"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open air"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-indoor.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "This is open air."
msgstr "Esto es el aire libre."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "mound of sand"
msgstr "montículo de arena"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "A mound of sand."
msgstr "Un montón de arena."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "glassed sand"
msgstr "arena vitrificada"

#. ~ Description of terrain "glassed sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A patch of sand that has a crust of natural glass atop it, after exposure to"
" intense heat."
msgstr ""
"Un poco de arena que tiene una corteza de vidrio natural encima, por haber "
"sido expuesta a un calor intenso."

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "glassed sand"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "crunch"
msgstr "crujido"

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
msgid "mound of dirt"
msgstr "montículo de tierra"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of heaped dirt, not easily traversable.  If examined more closely, "
"it's quite favorable for planting seeds and the like."
msgstr ""
"Un área de suciedad amontonada, no fácilmente transitable. Si se examina más"
" de cerca, es bastante propicia para plantar semillas y similares."

#. ~ Description of terrain "mound of dirt"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A giant hill of dirt that looks like you could crawl inside for shelter."
msgstr ""
"Es una pilla gigante de tierra en la que parece que podrías meterte para "
"usar de refugio."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "odd fault"
msgstr "desperfecto extraño"

#. ~ Description of terrain "odd fault"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An unnaturally humanoid-shaped hole, it seems oddly familiar.  There's a "
"strange sensation to examine it closer, as if it belongs to you somehow."
msgstr ""
"Es un agujero antinatural con forma humanoide, y te resulta extrañamente "
"familiar. Sientes una extraña sensación al examinarlo, como si te "
"perteneciera de alguna manera."

#. ~ Message about the player in an effect
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"This wall is perfectly vertical.  Odd, twisted holes are set in it, leading "
"as far back into the solid rock as you can see.  The holes are humanoid in "
"shape, but with long, twisted, distended limbs."
msgstr ""
"Esta pared es perfectamente vertical. En ella hay agujeros extraños y "
"retorcidos que se adentran en la roca sólida hasta donde se puede ver. Los "
"agujeros tienen forma humanoide, pero con miembros largos, retorcidos y "
"distendidos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "grave"
msgstr "tumba"

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A dirt grave, with some grass growing on it.  At least some of the dead do "
"actually rest in peace."
msgstr ""
"Una tumba de tierra, con algo de hierba creciendo en ella. Al menos algunos "
"de los muertos descansan en paz."

#. ~ Description of terrain "grave"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A fresh grave, covered with stones, either to keep something from digging it"
" out or to keep one inside from digging out of it.  Two planks mark this "
"place of someone's eternal rest."
msgstr ""
"Una tumba fresca, cubierta con piedras, ya sea para evitar que algo la saque"
" o para evitar que alguien de adentro la saque. Dos tablones marcan este "
"lugar de descanso eterno de alguien."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "rubber mulch"
msgstr "suelo de caucho"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rubber mulch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large area mulched with shredded rubber.  It's a softer place to land than"
" regular dirt."
msgstr ""
"Una gran superficie cubierta con caucho triturado. Es un lugar más suave "
"para aterrizar que la tierra normal."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pavement"
msgstr "pavimento"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A segment of asphalt, slowly degrading from cracks, frost heaves and lack of"
" maintenance."
msgstr ""
"Un segmento de asfalto, que se degrada lentamente por las grietas, las "
"heladas y la falta de mantenimiento."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow pavement"
msgstr "pavimento amarillo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow pavement"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Streaks of carefully aligned yellow paint mark the road to inform drivers "
"not to cross.  No one is enforcing these rules anymore."
msgstr ""
"Son rayas de pintura amarilla cuidadosamente alineadas en la ruta para "
"informar a los conductores que no deben cruzarlas. Aunque ya nadie cuida que"
" estas cosas se cumplan."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "pedestrian crossing"
msgstr "paso de peatones"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pedestrian crossing"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"White polymer lines painted on the pavement which indicate places where "
"pedestrians should cross the road."
msgstr ""
"Líneas blancas de polímero pintadas en el pavimento que indican los lugares "
"donde los peatones deben cruzar la carretera."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "sidewalk"
msgstr "acera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sidewalk"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An area of common poured concrete, damaged by frost heaves and large cracks "
"due to lack of maintenance."
msgstr ""
"Una zona de hormigón vertido común, dañada por los fuertes vientos de las "
"heladas y las grandes grietas debido a la falta de mantenimiento."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "concrete"
msgid_plural "concrete"
msgstr[0] "hormigón"
msgstr[1] "hormigón"
msgstr[2] "hormigón"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles."
msgstr ""
"Un nuevo segmento de hormigón vertido con acabados superficiales para la "
"estética y la resistencia a los ciclos de congelación-descongelación."

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A newer segment of poured concrete with surface finishes for aesthetics and "
"resistance to freeze-thaw cycles.  Covered with a streak of yellow paint."
msgstr ""
"Un nuevo segmento de hormigón vertido con acabados superficiales para la "
"estética y la resistencia a los ciclos de congelación-descongelación. "
"Cubierto con una raya de pintura amarilla."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor"
msgstr "Piso de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Wooden floor created from boards, packed tightly together and nailed down.  "
"Common in patios."
msgstr ""
"Piso de madera creado a partir de tablas, apretadas y clavadas. Es común en "
"los patios."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "wooden floor gangway"
msgstr "pasarela con suelo de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Wooden gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but "
"not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr ""
"Pasarela de madera que cubre un corto espacio. Lo suficientemente resistente"
" como para servir de suelo, pero no lo suficiente como para soportar un "
"suelo adicional."

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"High-quality and tough checkered flooring to reduce risk of slips and falls."
msgstr ""
"Un suelo a cuadros de alta calidad y resistente para reducir el riesgo de "
"resbalones y caídas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "metal floor gangway"
msgstr "pasarela con suelo metálico"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal floor gangway"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Metal gangway bridging a short gap.  Sturdy enough to act as a floor, but "
"not sufficient to support additional flooring."
msgstr ""
"Pasarela metálica que cubre un corto espacio. Suficientemente resistente "
"para actuar como suelo, pero no lo suficiente para soportar un suelo "
"adicional."

#. ~ Description of terrain "dirt floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "Floor consisting of finely mixed earth that has been tamped down."
msgstr "El suelo consiste en tierra finamente mezclada que ha sido apisonada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "gelatinous ground"
msgstr "suelo gelatinoso"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gelatinous ground"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"An incursion of a large area of otherworldly substrate, it feels like "
"walking on hardened gelatin."
msgstr ""
"Una incursión en una gran área de sustrato de otro mundo, se siente como "
"caminar sobre gelatina endurecida."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "orifice"
msgstr "orificio"

#. ~ Description of terrain "orifice"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"A large round orifice with trails of fresh and dried up strange green liquid"
" with a strong acid odor covering its inner sides."
msgstr ""
"Un gran orificio redondo con estelas de un extraño líquido verde fresco y "
"seco con un fuerte olor ácido que cubre sus lados interiores."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elevator"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "An elevator section of the flight deck."
msgstr "Una sección del ascensor de la cabina de vuelo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta"

#. ~ Description of terrain "deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal coating of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix.  "
"Used for runways, and can't be melted by jet engine nozzles."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar. Se utiliza para las pistas de aterrizaje, y no puede"
" ser fundido por las boquillas de los motores de los aviones."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "yellow deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta amarilla"

#. ~ Description of terrain "yellow deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal covering of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix, and"
" painted in yellow color."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar, y pintado en color amarillo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "red deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta roja"

#. ~ Description of terrain "red deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal covering of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix, and"
" painted in red color."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar, y pintado en color rojo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid "white deck coating"
msgstr "cubierta blanca"

#. ~ Description of terrain "white deck coating"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-floors-outdoors.json
msgid ""
"Thick metal covering of a hull, covered with a military grade epoxy mix, and"
" painted in white color."
msgstr ""
"Revestimiento metálico grueso de un armazón, cubierto con una mezcla de "
"epoxi de grado militar, y pintado en color blanco."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "walnut tree"
msgstr "nogal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested walnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Juglans'. Si te fijas bien, puedes "
"ver algunas nueces sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "walnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Juglans' genus."
msgstr "Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Juglans'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "blackjack oak"
msgstr "roble negro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  You could peel off the bark "
"sections if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol caducifolio del género 'Quercus', con la corteza agrietada formando"
" placas negras rectangulares, separadas por estrechas fisuras naranjas. "
"Podrías arrancar secciones de la corteza si examinas el árbol."

#. ~ Description of terrain "blackjack oak"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the genus 'Quercus', with bark cracked into rectangular "
"black plates split by narrow orange fissures.  All usable bark has been "
"stripped off."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol caducifolio del género 'Quercus', con la corteza agrietada formando"
" placas negras rectangulares, separadas por estrechas fisuras naranjas. Toda"
" la corteza utilizable ha sido retirada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "alder tree"
msgstr "aliso"

#. ~ Description of terrain "alder tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous flowering tree with serrate, scalloped, round-obovate leaves, "
"commonly forming dense groves alongside water."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de floración caducifolio con hojas serradas, festoneadas y "
"redondeadas-obovadas, que suele formar densas arboledas junto al agua."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "chestnut tree"
msgstr "castaño"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested chestnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Castanea'. Si te fijas bien, puedes"
" ver algunas castañas sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "chestnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Castanea' genus."
msgstr "Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Castanea'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "beech tree"
msgstr "haya"

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus.  If you look closely, you can"
" see some unharvested beech nuts."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Fagus'. Si te fijas bien, puedes "
"ver algunas nueces de haya sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "beech tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A massive tree belonging to the 'Fagus' genus."
msgstr "Un enorme árbol perteneciente al género 'Fagus'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hazelnut tree"
msgstr "avellano"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus.  If you look closely, you "
"can see some unharvested hazelnuts."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol rechoncho perteneciente al género 'Corylus'. Si te fijas bien, "
"puedes ver algunas avellanas sin cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hazelnut tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "A stubby tree belonging to the 'Corylus' genus."
msgstr "Un árbol rechoncho perteneciente al género 'Corylus'."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "oak tree"
msgstr "roble"

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region.  If you look closely, you can see some "
"acorns the squirrels haven't gotten yet."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol caducifolio perteneciente al género 'Quercus', que se "
"encuentra comúnmente en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Si te fijas "
"bien, puedes ver algunas bellotas que las ardillas aún no han conseguido."

#. ~ Description of terrain "oak tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme árbol caducifolio perteneciente al género 'Quercus', que se "
"encuentra comúnmente en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "basswood tree"
msgstr "tilo rojo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the Summer"
" and you might be able to eat its young leaves in Spring."
msgstr ""
"El tilo americano. Tiene unas bonitas y olorosas flores en verano y se "
"pueden comer sus hojas jóvenes en primavera."

#. ~ Description of terrain "basswood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The American linden.  It has pretty and sweet-smelling flowers in the Summer"
" and its young leaves have already been harvested."
msgstr ""
"El tilo americano. Tiene unas bonitas y olorosas flores en verano y sus "
"hojas jóvenes ya se han cosechado."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cottonwood tree"
msgstr "árbol del algodoncillo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  You see some cottonwood tree bolls that can be "
"harvested."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol perteneciente al género 'Populus', que se encuentra comúnmente"
" en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Se ven algunas cápsulas de "
"algodoncillo que se pueden cosechar."

#. ~ Description of terrain "cottonwood tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Populus' genus, commonly found throughout the"
" New England region.  All the cottonwood tree bolls have been harvested."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol perteneciente al género 'Populus', que se encuentra comúnmente"
" en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Se han recogido todo el algodoncillo"
" que se puede cosechar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elm tree"
msgstr "olmo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elm tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large tree belonging to the 'Ulmus' genus, commonly found throughout the "
"New England region."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de gran tamaño perteneciente al género 'Ulmus', que se encuentra "
"comúnmente en toda la región de Nueva Inglaterra."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead tree"
msgstr "árbol seco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"An indiscernible tree that has withered away, whether by weather, fire or "
"otherworldly."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol indiscernible que se ha marchitado, ya sea por el clima, por el "
"fuego o por otro mundo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead tree"
msgstr "árbol muerto retorcido"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This deciduous tree's branches are warped into a spiral.  This appears to "
"have killed it."
msgstr ""
"Las ramas de este árbol de hoja caduca están retorcidas formando una "
"espiral.  Eso parece haber matado al árbol."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "young tree"
msgstr "árbol joven"

#. ~ Description of terrain "young tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/mods/innawood/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A relatively young sapling of an indeterminate species.  It could take "
"decades before reaching maturity, so there's no use waiting around."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol joven de una especie indeterminada. Podría tardar décadas en "
"alcanzar la madurez, así que no sirve de nada esperar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mega fern"
msgstr "mega helecho"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mega fern"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A gigantic fern like nothing you've seen before.  The leaves are a bright "
"scarlet color with a net like structure of green veins.  The multipronged "
"trunks appear to have the consistency of balsa wood."
msgstr ""
"Un helecho gigantesco como nada que haya visto antes. Las hojas son de un "
"color escarlata brillante con una estructura similar a una red de venas "
"verdes. Los troncos con múltiples puntas parecen tener la consistencia de la"
" madera de balsa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apple tree"
msgstr "manzano"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could probably "
"find a few mature ones in autumn."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género 'Malus', que produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como manzanas. Este árbol pertenece al género 'Malus', que produce"
" los frutos comúnmente conocidos como manzanas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Malus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as apples.  There do not appear to be any ripe apples now."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género 'Malus', que produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como manzanas. Actualmente no parece haber manzanas maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pear tree"
msgstr "peral"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces viable "
"pears in the fall.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could "
"probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'Pyrus communis', o peral común, que produce peras viables en "
"otoño. Si examinaras las ramas más de cerca, probablemente podrías encontrar"
" algunas maduras."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pear tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'Pyrus communis', or the common pear tree, which produces viable "
"pears in the fall.  Looks like all the ripe pears have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'Pyrus communis', o peral común, que produce peras viables en "
"otoño. Parece que todas las peras maduras han sido recogidas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "coffee tree"
msgstr "árbol del café"

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  If you examined the "
"branches more closely, you could probably find a few mature ones."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'gymnocladus dioicus', o cafeto de Kentucky, que produce vainas "
"de café que se pueden tostar y hojas que se pueden preparar en otoño. Si "
"examinaras las ramas más de cerca, probablemente podrías encontrar algunas "
"maduras."

#. ~ Description of terrain "coffee tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This is 'gymnocladus dioicus', or the kentucky coffee tree, which produces "
"roastable coffee pods and brewable leaves in the fall.  Looks like all the "
"ripe pods have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Este es el 'gymnocladus dioicus', o cafeto de Kentucky, que produce vainas "
"de café que se pueden tostar y hojas que se pueden preparar en otoño. Parece"
" que todas las vainas maduras han sido recogidas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "cherry tree"
msgstr "cerezo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could"
" probably find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, da cerezas en verano. Si examinas el follaje más de cerca, "
"probablemente podrá encontrar algunos racimos viables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "cherry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"cherries in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of cherries have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, da cerezas en verano. Parece que se han recogido todos los "
"racimos de cerezas maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "juniper tree"
msgstr "Enebro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years, first flowering.  On the second year "
"producing a green berry, the last, they produce their more famed blue "
"varieties.  If you examined the foliage more closely, you could probably "
"find some viable clusters."
msgstr ""
"Una de las especies de 'Juniperus' que crece en Nueva Inglaterra, las bayas "
"de enebro crecen a lo largo de dos o tres años, primero floreciendo. Al "
"segundo año producen una baya verde, y al último, sus más afamadas "
"variedades azules. Si examinara el follaje más de cerca, probablemente "
"podría encontrar algunos racimos viables."

#. ~ Description of terrain "juniper tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the species of 'Juniperus' that grows in New England, juniper berries"
" grow over two to three years.  In the first year they flower, in the second"
" year they produce a green berry, the last, they produce their more famed "
"blue varieties.  Looks like all the ripe bunches of berries have been "
"picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las especies de 'Juniperus' que crece en Nueva Inglaterra, las bayas "
"de enebro crecen a lo largo de dos o tres años, primero floreciendo. Al "
"segundo año producen una baya verde, y al último, sus más afamadas "
"variedades azules. Parece que se han recogido todos los racimos maduros de "
"bayas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "peach tree"
msgstr "melocotonero"

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  If you examined the branches more closely, you could"
" probably find some mature peaches."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, y da melocotones en verano. Si examinaras las ramas más de "
"cerca, probablemente podrías encontrar algunos melocotones maduros."

#. ~ Description of terrain "peach tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it bears "
"peaches in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe peaches have been picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra, y da melocotones en verano. Parece que se han recogido todos los"
" melocotones maduros."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "apricot tree"
msgstr "albaricoquero"

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely,"
" you could probably find some mature apricots."
msgstr ""
"Especie trasplantada de 'Prunus armeniaca', que rara vez se encuentra en "
"Nueva Inglaterra. Produce albaricoques en verano. Si se examinan los brotes "
"más de cerca, probablemente se puedan encontrar algunos albaricoques "
"maduros."

#. ~ Description of terrain "apricot tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A transplanted species of 'Prunus armeniaca', rarely found in New England.  "
"It produces apricots in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe apricots have "
"been picked."
msgstr ""
"Especie trasplantada de 'Prunus armeniaca', que rara vez se encuentra en "
"Nueva Inglaterra. Produce albaricoques en verano. Parece que todos los "
"albaricoques maduros han sido recogidos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "plum tree"
msgstr "ciruelo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  If you examined the spurs more closely, you "
"could probably find some ripe plums."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra y produce ciruelas en verano. Si examinaras los brotes más de "
"cerca, probablemente podrías encontrar algunas ciruelas maduras."

#. ~ Description of terrain "plum tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"One of the several species of 'Prunus' trees found in New England, it "
"produces plums in the summer.  Looks like all the ripe plums have been "
"picked."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de árboles 'Prunus' que se encuentran en Nueva "
"Inglaterra y produce ciruelas en verano. Parece que se han recogido todas "
"las ciruelas maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "mulberry tree"
msgstr "Morera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género \"Morus\" y produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como moras. En verano, se pueden recoger muchas bayas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "mulberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Morus' genus, producing fruit commonly known "
"as mulberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe mulberries now."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género 'Morus', que produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como moras. En la actualidad no parece haber moras maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "elderberry tree"
msgstr "árbol de saúco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  In the summer, many berries can be picked."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género \"Sambucus\" y produce los frutos comúnmente "
"conocidos como bayas de saúco. En verano, se pueden recoger muchas bayas."

#. ~ Description of terrain "elderberry tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"This tree is a member of the 'Sambucus' genus, producing fruit commonly "
"known as elderberries.  There do not appear to be any ripe elderberries now."
msgstr ""
"Este árbol pertenece al género \"Sambucus\" y produce los frutos conocidos "
"comúnmente como bayas de saúco. En la actualidad no parece que haya bayas de"
" saúco maduras."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pine tree"
msgstr "pino"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"If you examined the tree more closely, you might find usable sticky whorls, "
"resin clumps and unharvested pinecones."
msgstr ""
"Una conífera imponente que pertenece al género 'Pinus', con las especies de "
"Nueva Inglaterra que varían entre 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' y 'P. rigida'."
" Si se examina el árbol con más detenimiento, se pueden encontrar verticilos"
" pegajosos utilizables, acumulaciones de resina y piñas sin recoger."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"Some of the branches and resin clumps have been stripped away and many of "
"the pinecones aren't developed fully yet, but given a season, it could be "
"harvestable again."
msgstr ""
"Una imponente conífera que pertenece al género 'Pinus', con las especies de "
"Nueva Inglaterra que varían entre 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' y 'P. rigida'."
" Algunas de las ramas y los grupos de resina han sido despojados y muchas de"
" las piñas aún no se han desarrollado completamente, pero si se le da una "
"temporada, podría volver a ser cosechable."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead pine tree"
msgstr "pino seco"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A towering coniferous tree that belongs to the 'Pinus' genus, with the New "
"England species varying from 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' and 'P. rigida'.  "
"This trees branches are bare, and it appears to be dead."
msgstr ""
"Una imponente conífera que pertenece al género 'Pinus', con las especies de "
"Nueva Inglaterra que varían entre 'P. strobus', 'P. resinosa' y 'P. rigida'."
" Las ramas de este árbol están peladas y parece estar muerto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "warped dead pine tree"
msgstr "pino muerto retorcido"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped dead pine tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The branches of this dead pine have been twisted into a shape that remind "
"you of Sierpinski triangles.  It did not survive getting warped like this."
msgstr ""
"Las ramas de este pino muerto han sido retorcidas en una forma que te hace "
"recordar los triángulos de Sierpinski.  No sobrevivió al ser retorcido de "
"esa manera."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "birch tree"
msgstr "abedul"

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  You could tear "
"off some strips of bark if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Árbol alto de hoja perenne del género 'Betula', con la característica "
"corteza desconchada. Especies como 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera' y "
"'B. populifolia' son las más comunes en la región de Nueva Inglaterra. Se "
"pueden arrancar algunas tiras de corteza si se examina el árbol más de "
"cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "birch tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Betula' genus, with the characteristic peeling"
" bark.  Species like 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera', and 'B. "
"populifolia' are the most common in the New England region.  Looks like "
"there isn't enough rhytidome to peel off yet."
msgstr ""
"Árbol alto de hoja perenne del género 'Betula', con la característica "
"corteza desconchada. Especies como 'B. alleghaniensis', 'B. papyrifera' y "
"'B. populifolia' son las más comunes en la región de Nueva Inglaterra. "
"Parece que aún no hay suficiente ritidoma para pelar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "willow tree"
msgstr "sauce"

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long thin leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  You could tear off some bark."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol caducifolio alto y ancho del género 'Salix', con largas y finas "
"ramas frondosas que cuelgan como cortinas. Se puede arrancar la corteza."

#. ~ Description of terrain "willow tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall, wide deciduous tree of the 'Salix' genus, with long thin leafy "
"branches that hang down like curtains.  Looks like all usable bark has been "
"torn off, and new rhytidomes have not formed yet."
msgstr ""
"Árbol caducifolio, alto y ancho, del género 'Salix', con largas ramas de "
"hojas finas que cuelgan como cortinas. Parece que toda la corteza utilizable"
" ha sido arrancada, y aún no se han formado nuevos ritidios."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "maple tree"
msgstr "arce"

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  It could be tapped in order to extract maple "
"syrup."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol caducifolio del género 'Acer'. Las hojas tienen una forma "
"distintiva con cinco puntas. Se puede aprovechar para extraer jarabe de "
"arce."

#. ~ Description of terrain "maple tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A large deciduous tree of the 'Acer' genus.  The leaves are distinctively "
"shaped with five prongs.  A spigot is wedged into the trunk, and sweet maple"
" syrup can be extracted."
msgstr ""
"Un gran árbol caducifolio del género 'Acer'. Las hojas tienen una forma "
"distintiva con cinco puntas. En el tronco hay una espiga de la que se puede "
"extraer el dulce jarabe de arce."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "hickory tree"
msgstr "árbol nueces pecanas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for hickory nuts"
" if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol alto de hoja perenne del género 'Carya'. Podrías buscar nueces de "
"nogal si examinaras el árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It looks like the tree has been"
" picked clean of hickory nuts."
msgstr ""
"Un alto árbol caducifolio del género 'Carya'. Parece que el árbol ha sido "
"limpiado de nueces de nogal."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pistachio tree"
msgstr "árbol de pistacho"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  You could look for pistachio nuts if you "
"examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Pistacia'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado,"
" y no es nativo de esta región. Podrías buscar pistachos si examinaras el "
"árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pistachio tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Pistacia' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is"
" not native to this region.  Unfortunately, it looks like it has been picked"
" clean of pistachio nuts."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Pistacia'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado "
"y no es nativo de esta región. Desgraciadamente, parece que le han quitado "
"los pistachos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "almond tree"
msgstr "nogal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  You could look for fresh almonds if you examined"
" the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Prunus'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado y "
"no es nativo de esta región. Se podrían buscar almendras frescas si se "
"examinara el árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "almond tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A deciduous tree of the 'Prunus' genus.  This is a cultivated tree, and is "
"not native to this region.  There are no almonds left to pick on the tree."
msgstr ""
"Árbol de hoja perenne del género 'Prunus'. Se trata de un árbol cultivado, y"
" no es nativo de esta región. No quedan almendras para recoger en el árbol."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "pecan tree"
msgstr "árbol de nuez"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  You could look for pecan nuts "
"if you examined the tree more closely."
msgstr ""
"Un árbol alto de hoja caduca del género 'Carya'. Podrías buscar nueces de "
"pecanero si examinaras el árbol más de cerca."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pecan tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"A tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  It doesn't look like there are "
"any pecan nuts left on the tree."
msgstr ""
"Un alto árbol caducifolio del género 'Carya'. No parece que queden nueces en"
" el árbol."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid "dead hickory tree"
msgstr "árbol nueces pecanas muerto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead hickory tree"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"The dead remnants of a tall deciduous tree of the 'Carya' genus.  Nothing "
"useful can be foraged from this poor, dead tree."
msgstr ""
"Los restos muertos de un alto árbol caducifolio del género 'Carya'. No se "
"puede extraer nada útil de este pobre árbol muerto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/other.json
msgid "underbrush"
msgid_plural "underbrushes"
msgstr[0] "maleza"
msgstr[1] "malezas"
msgstr[2] "malezas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "underbrush"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-flora.json
msgid ""
"Small plants and shrubs that decorate the forest.  An observant forager "
"could obtain edible plants, acorns, eggs, and mushrooms from it."
msgstr ""
"Son pequeñas plantas y arbustos que decoran el bosque. Un buscador de comida"
" avezado puede obtener plantas comestibles, bellotas, huevos y hongos ahí."

