msgstr "Un interruptor cian. ¿Debería activarlo?"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
msgid "purple switch"
msgstr "interruptor púrpura"

#. ~ Description of terrain "purple switch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
msgid "A purple switch.  Should you activate it?"
msgstr "Un interruptor púrpura. ¿Debería activarlo?"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
msgid "checkered switch"
msgstr "interruptor de cuadros"

#. ~ Description of terrain "checkered switch"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
msgid "A checkered switch.  Should you activate it?"
msgstr "Un interruptor cuadriculado. ¿Debería activarlo?"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain.json
msgid "nuclear reactor core"
msgstr "núcleo del reactor nuclear"

#. ~ Description of terrain "nuclear reactor core"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-mechanisms.json
msgid ""
"Naval A1B reactor, used in Gerald R. Ford-class aircraft carriers, and can "
"produce enough steam to generate 125 megawatts of energy."
msgstr ""
"Es un reactor naval A1B, utilizado en los portaviones de clase Gerald R. "
"Ford. Puede producir suficiente vapor para generar 125 megawatts de energía."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "resin wall"
msgstr "muro de resina"

#. ~ Description of terrain "resin wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid ""
"This wall is made of a glistening, nearly opaque, plastic-like substance.  "
"Deep within the material making it up, you can barely see a network of "
"pulsating green conduits, snaking like blood vessels through it.  The "
"material is hard, warm to the touch, and slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Este muro está hecho de una sustancia brillante, casi opaco, parecido al "
"plástico. En lo profundo del material que lo compone, apenas se puede ver "
"una red de conductos verdes pulsantes, serpenteando como vasos sanguíneos a "
"través de ella. El material es duro, cálido al tacto y ligeramente húmedo."

#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "resin wall"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "resin cage"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "resin floor"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "resin roof"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "closed resin portal"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "open resin portal"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "resin-lined hole"
#. ~ Bashing sound of terrain "coral floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/maps/furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alienciv.json
msgid "boom!"
msgstr "¡Boom!"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "resin cage"
msgstr "jaula de resina"

#. ~ Description of terrain "resin cage"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid ""
"This resin wall opens into a series of small honeycomb-like hexagons, "
"allowing the passage of air and light.  While still made of the same sturdy "
"material, it is thinner and more delicate in appearance."
msgstr ""
"Este muro de resina se abre en una serie de pequeños hexágonos en forma de "
"panal, permitiendo el paso del aire y la luz. Aunque sigue siendo del mismo "
"material resistente, es más delgado y más delicado en apariencia."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "resin floor"
msgstr "suelo de resina"

#. ~ Description of terrain "resin floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid ""
"This nearly opaque, plastic-like floor has a gentle curve from wall to wall,"
" but in the central areas is quite flat.  The material is hard, warm to the "
"touch, and slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Este suelo casi opaco, parecido al plástico, tiene una suave curva de muro a"
" muro, pero en las zonas centrales es bastante plano. El material es duro, "
"cálido al tacto y ligeramente húmedo."

#. ~ Description of terrain "resin floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid ""
"This nearly opaque, plastic-like floor is smooth and flat.  The material is "
"hard, warm to the touch, and slightly damp."
msgstr ""
"Este suelo casi opaco, parecido al plástico, es liso y plano. El material es"
" duro, cálido al tacto y ligeramente húmedo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "resin roof"
msgstr "techo de resina"

#. ~ Description of terrain "resin roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid ""
"A wide, domed section of nearly opaque, plastic-like material.  When the "
"light hits it, a network of multicolored conduits like blood vessels can be "
"seen snaking through its glistening interior."
msgstr ""
"Una amplia sección abovedada de material casi opaco, parecido al plástico. "
"Cuando la luz la golpea, se puede ver una red de conductos multicolores como"
" vasos sanguíneos serpenteando por su brillante interior."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "closed resin portal"
msgstr "portal de resina cerrado"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed resin portal"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid ""
"A tricuspid hatch of some sort of damp, flexible, resinous material.  This "
"one is closed tightly, but it looks like a firm push would cause it to snap "
"open."
msgstr ""
"Una escotilla tricúspide de algún tipo de material resinoso, flexible y "
"húmedo. Esta está cerrada herméticamente, pero parece que un empujón firme "
"haría que se abriera."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "open resin portal"
msgstr "portal abierto de resina"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open resin portal"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid ""
"A tricuspid hatch of some sort of damp, flexible, resinous material.  This "
"one is open, the flaps held out by some sort of stringy mucus-like "
"substance."
msgstr ""
"Una escotilla tricúspide de algún tipo de material resinoso, flexible y "
"húmedo. Esta está abierta, las aletas están sostenidas por una especie de "
"sustancia fibrosa parecida al moco."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "resin-lined hole"
msgstr "agujero forrado de resina"

#. ~ Description of terrain "resin-lined hole"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-migo.json
msgid "An open hole in the resin wall, large enough to pass through."
msgstr ""
"Un agujero abierto en el muro de resina, lo suficientemente grande como para"
" pasar a través de él."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
msgid "black glass"
msgstr "vidrio negro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "black glass"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-nether.json
msgid ""
"An endless expanse of black glass.  It perfectly reflects the darkness "
"around it."
msgstr ""
"Una extensión infinita de vidrio negro. Refleja perfectamente la oscuridad a"
" su alrededor"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid "gravel"
msgstr "gravilla"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gravel"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid ""
"Gravel is a collection of small stones often used for roads, as railroad "
"ballast, and in many other applications."
msgstr ""
"La grava es un conjunto de pequeñas piedras que se utilizan a menudo en las "
"carreteras, como balasto ferroviario y en muchas otras aplicaciones."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid "railroad track"
msgstr "vía de ferrocarril"

#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad track"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks stand unused in the "
"face of the Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"Los trenes solían avanzar con esto. Estas vías de tren están sin usar frente"
" al Cataclismo.Los trenes solían avanzar con esto. Estas vías de tren están "
"sin usar frente al Cataclismo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid "railroad tie"
msgstr "enlace ferroviario"

#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad tie"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid "This crosstie is used to support the rails."
msgstr "Esta bifurcación se utiliza para apoyar los rieles."

#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad track"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid ""
"Trains used to chug along on these.  These rail tracks stand unused in the "
"face of the Cataclysm.  A crosstie sits underneath, supporting the rails."
msgstr ""
"Los trenes solían avanzar con esto. Estas vías de tren están sin usar frente"
" al Cataclismo. Una bifurcación se encuentra debajo, apoyando los rieles."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid "buffer stop"
msgstr "parachoques"

#. ~ Description of terrain "buffer stop"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid ""
"A tiny blockade on the train tracks, meant to signify the end of a track, or"
" mark a 'no-go' zone for trains."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño bloqueo en las vías del tren, que significa el final de una vía, "
"o una marca de una zona \"prohibida\" para los trenes."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid "railroad crossing signal"
msgstr "señal del cruce de trenes"

#. ~ Description of terrain "railroad crossing signal"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid ""
"Traffic lights meant to light and make noise when a train approaches, to "
"prevent people from turning into meaty mush while they cross the tracks.  "
"Won't stop people from turning into meaty mush by other means, though."
msgstr ""
"Los semáforos están pensados para iluminar y hacer ruido cuando se aproxima "
"un tren, para evitar que la gente se convierta en papilla mientras cruza las"
" vías. Sin embargo, no impedirá que la gente se convierta en papilla por "
"otros medios."

#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "railroad crossing signal"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "crossbuck"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "rain gutter"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "gutter drop"
#. ~ Bashing failed sound of terrain "downspout"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "clang."
msgstr "clonc."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid "crossbuck"
msgstr "cruce de vias"

#. ~ Description of terrain "crossbuck"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid ""
"A traffic sign intended to indicate a level railway crossing.  If the trains"
" were still running."
msgstr ""
"Una señal de tráfico destinada a indicar un cruce de ferrocarril a nivel. Si"
" los trenes aún estuvieran en marcha."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "small railroad track"
msgid_plural "small railroad tracks"
msgstr[0] "pequeña vía de ferrocarril"
msgstr[1] "pequeñas vías de ferrocarril"
msgstr[2] "pequeñas vías de ferrocarril"

#. ~ Description of terrain "small railroad track"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-railroads.json
msgid ""
"Like a railroad track, only smaller.  You could probably run a small vehicle"
" on this."
msgstr ""
"Como una vía férrea, sólo que más pequeña. Probablemente podrías hacer "
"funcionar un pequeño vehículo en esto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid "sandbox"
msgstr "arenero"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sandbox"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid ""
"Children used to play in this sandbox.  The population of lice probably "
"diminished considerably now that they no longer do."
msgstr ""
"Los niños solían jugar en este arenero. La población de piojos probablemente"
" disminuyó considerablemente ahora que ya no lo hacen."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid "slide"
msgstr "tobogán"

#. ~ Description of terrain "slide"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid "A children's slide.  Too small to slide on comfortably anymore."
msgstr "Un tobogán para niños. Demasiado pequeño para deslizarse cómodamente."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid "monkey bars"
msgstr "pasamanos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "monkey bars"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid ""
"A set of monkey bars, to be used by children to train their arms by hanging "
"from the bars, and have fun."
msgstr ""
"Un juego de barras de mono, para que los niños entrenen sus brazos colgando "
"de las barras, y se diviertan."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid "backboard"
msgstr "tablero"

#. ~ Description of terrain "backboard"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid "A basketball backboard."
msgstr "Un tablero de baloncesto."

#. ~ Description of terrain "backboard"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-recreational.json
msgid "A metal backboard."
msgstr "Una tabla de metal."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Description of terrain "this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo
#. terrain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-regional-pseudo.json
msgid "this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo terrain"
msgstr "esto no debería aparecer nunca, es un pseudo terreno"

#. ~ Description of terrain "this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo
#. terrain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-regional-pseudo.json
msgid ""
"this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo terrain.  For use where "
"people have trampled away grass, or otherwise cleared plant life."
msgstr ""
"esto no debería aparecer nunca, es un pseudo terreno. Para ser usado donde "
"la gente ha pisoteado la hierba, o despejado la vida vegetal de otra manera."

#. ~ Description of terrain "this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo
#. terrain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-regional-pseudo.json
msgid ""
"this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo terrain.  For use where "
"clean, curated grass is the only expected terrain - modified by whatever the"
" biome equivalent is"
msgstr ""
"esto no debería aparecer nunca, es un pseudo terreno. Para el uso donde la "
"hierba limpia y curada es el único terreno esperado - modificado por lo que "
"sea el equivalente del bioma"

#. ~ Description of terrain "this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo
#. terrain"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-regional-pseudo.json
msgid ""
"this should never actually show up, it's a pseudo terrain.  For use where "
"plants have been planted and grass/groundcover kept clear"
msgstr ""
"esto no debería aparecer nunca, es un pseudo terreno. Para ser usado donde "
"se han plantado plantas y se ha mantenido el pasto y la cubierta vegetal "
"despejada..."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "rain gutter"
msgstr "canalón de lluvia"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rain gutter"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "Channels water from the roof towards the ground, it looks flimsy."
msgstr "Canaliza el agua desde el techo hacia el suelo, se ve endeble."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "gutter drop"
msgstr "caída de la canaleta"

#. ~ Description of terrain "gutter drop"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid ""
"Funnels water from gutter system towards the ground, it looks flimsy.  You "
"may be able to climb down here."
msgstr ""
"Canalizar el agua del sistema de canaletas hacia el suelo, parece endeble. "
"Puede ser capaz de bajar por aquí."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "downspout"
msgstr "bajante"

#. ~ Description of terrain "downspout"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid ""
"A length of gutter running from the roof to the ground, you could place a "
"container underneath it to collect rainwater.  It looks flimsy.  You may be "
"able to climb up here."
msgstr ""
"Un tramo de canalón que va desde el tejado hasta el suelo, se podría colocar"
" un recipiente debajo para recoger el agua de lluvia. Parece endeble. Es "
"posible que puedas trepar por aquí."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "flat roof"
msgstr "techo plano"

#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A flat, gray section of rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección plana y gris de la azotea."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "tar paper flat roof"
msgstr "papel de alquitrán tejado plano"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tar paper flat roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A flat, gray section of rooftop covered with tar paper."
msgstr ""
"Una sección plana y gris de la azotea cubierta con papel de alquitrán."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "shingle flat roof"
msgstr "tejas de tejado plano"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shingle flat roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A flat section of rooftop covered in shingles."
msgstr "Una sección plana de la azotea cubierta de tejas."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "thatched roof"
msgstr "techo de paja"

#. ~ Description of terrain "thatched roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A section of roof made out of straw."
msgstr "Una sección del techo hecha de paja."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "metal flat roof"
msgstr "techo plano de metal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal flat roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A section of flat, sheet metal rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección de la azotea plana, de chapa de metal."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "tile flat roof"
msgstr "techo plano de tejastecho plano de tejas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "tile flat roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A section of tiled, flat rooftop."
msgstr "Una sección de tejas, una azotea plana.$"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "skylight"
msgstr "Tragaluz"

#. ~ Description of terrain "skylight"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid ""
"A giant sheet of glass inserted into the roof, lets light pass through."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina gUna lámina gigante de vidrio insertada en el techo, deja pasar "
"la luz.igante de vidrio insertada en el techo, deja pasar la luz."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "rock roof"
msgstr "techo de roca"

#. ~ Description of terrain "rock roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A section of flat natural rock."
msgstr "Una sección de roca natural plana."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "warped roof"
msgstr "techo deformado"

#. ~ Description of terrain "warped roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid ""
"A section of flat stone like roof.  It's pattern of grooves and lines is "
"constantly shifting."
msgstr ""
"Una sección de piedra plana como techo. Su patrón de ranuras y líneas cambia"
" constantemente."

#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A flat surface made of pulpy mass, covered in sticky wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Una superficie plana hecha de masa pulposa, cubierta de saliva pegajosa de "
"avispa."

#. ~ Description of terrain "flat roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid ""
"A flat surface made of hardened pulpy mass, covered in sticky wasp saliva."
msgstr ""
"Una superficie plana de masa pulposa endurecida, cubierta de saliva de "
"avispa pegajosa."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "concrete roof"
msgstr "techo de concreto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "concrete roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A flat, concrete section of rooftop."
msgstr "Es una sección plana de techo de concreto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden roof"
msgstr "techo de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wooden roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A flat section of wooden rooftop."
msgstr "Es una sección plana de techo de madera."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "treated wooden roof"
msgstr "techo de madera tratada"

#. ~ Description of terrain "treated wooden roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A flat section of flame resistant wooden rooftop."
msgstr "Es una sección plana de techo de madera resistente al fuego."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "metal roof"
msgstr "techo de metal"

#. ~ Description of terrain "metal roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A high-quality and sturdy section of metallic rooftop."
msgstr "Es una sección de techo metálico resistente de alta calidad."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "sod roof"
msgstr "techo de césped"

#. ~ Description of terrain "sod roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A section of roof made out of sod."
msgstr "Es una sección de techo hecha de césped."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "brick roof"
msgstr "techo de ladrillos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "brick roof"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-roofs.json
msgid "A brick section of rooftop."
msgstr "Es una sección de techo hecha de ladrillos."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "empty space"
msgstr "espacio vacío"

#. ~ Description of terrain "empty space"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "This is empty space."
msgstr "Es un espacio vacío"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "shallow pit"
msgstr "pozo poco profundo"

#. ~ Description of terrain "shallow pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A pit that could be dug even deeper or filled up.  Also useful as a starting"
" foundation for some constructions."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo que podría ser cavado aún más profundo o llenado. También es útil "
"como base de partida para algunas construcciones."

#. ~ Description of terrain "pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A steep hole that could seriously injure something if it fell in, "
"potentially fatal if it was filled with sharp and dangerous things.  Deep "
"enough for more advanced construction projects, and possibly to reach "
"groundwater if constructed properly."
msgstr ""
"Un agujero empinado que podría herir seriamente algo si se cae, "
"potencialmente mortal si se llena con cosas afiladas y peligrosas. "
"Suficientemente profundo para proyectos de construcción más avanzados, y "
"posiblemente para llegar al agua subterránea si se construye adecuadamente."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "corpse filled pit"
msgstr "pozo lleno de cadáveres"

#. ~ Description of terrain "corpse filled pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A giant trench full of corpses, maybe even a mass graveyard.  The bodies "
"could be dug out but none of it looks remotely usable."
msgstr ""
"Una zanja gigante llena de cadáveres, tal vez alguna especie de cementerio. "
"Los cuerpos podrían ser sacados, pero ninguno parece ni remotamente útil "
"para algo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "covered pit"
msgstr "pozo cubierto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "covered pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A deep pit with a plank placed across it, looks sturdy enough to cross "
"safely or the plank could be removed to turn it back into trap fall."
msgstr ""
"Un pozo profundo con un tablón colocado a través de él, parece lo "
"suficientemente robusto como para cruzar con seguridad o el tablón podría "
"ser retirado para convertirlo de nuevo en una trampa de caída."

#. ~ Description of terrain "spiked pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A narrow trench full of very pointy things that would easily puncture a "
"body."
msgstr ""
"Es una zanja angosta llena de cosas muy puntiagudas que fácilmente podrían "
"herir el cuerpo."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "covered spiked pit"
msgstr "pozo con púas cubierto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "covered spiked pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"Menacing with sharp spears along the bottom, this pit has a plank across it "
"to allow someone or something to cross safely.  The plank could be removed "
"to revert it back into a trap."
msgstr ""
"Este pozo, amenazante y con lanzas afiladas en el fondo, tiene un tablón que"
" lo atraviesa para que alguien o algo pueda cruzar con seguridad. El tablón "
"podría ser retirado para convertirlo de nuevo en una trampa."

#. ~ Description of terrain "glass pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"Looks like a ton of broken glass was dumped into this pit, maybe not fatal "
"to fall in but wouldn't be pleasant to try to crawl out."
msgstr ""
"Parece que tiraron un montón de vidrio roto en este pozo, quizás no te mate "
"la caida, pero ser será agradable intentar salir de el."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "covered glass pit"
msgstr "pozo con cristales cubierto"

#. ~ Description of terrain "covered glass pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A plank has been placed carefully to allow traversal over this ditch full of"
" large glass shards.  The wooden board could be removed so it couldn't be "
"safely crossed."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera se puso cuidadosamente sobre este pozo lleno de grandes "
"fragmentos de vidrio. La tabla puede ser sacada para que no pueda ser "
"cruzado con seguridad."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "dead drop pit"
msgstr "foso con caída "

#. ~ Description of terrain "dead drop pit"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A seemingly innocuous shallow pit.  Careful inspection reveals a black "
"canister half buried in the exposed soil."
msgstr ""
"Una fosa aparentemente inocua y poco profunda. Una inspección cuidadosa "
"revela un recipiente negro semienterrado en la tierra expuesta."

#. ~ Message about the player in an effect
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "You prepare the drop as instructed"
msgstr "Preparas el gotero según las instrucciones"

#. ~ Message about the player in an effect
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid "You dont have anything to deliver."
msgstr "No tienes nada que entregar."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
#: data/json/monsters/slimes.json
msgid "slime"
msgid_plural "slimes"
msgstr[0] "légamo"
msgstr[1] "légamos"
msgstr[2] "légamos"

#. ~ Description of terrain "slime"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-traps.json
msgid ""
"A disgusting and slippery mess that could be used to stash things because "
"who'd want to touch it?"
msgstr ""
"Un lío asqueroso y resbaladizo que podría usarse para esconder cosas porque "
"¿quién querría tocarlo?"

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "solid bark wall"
msgstr "muro sólido de corteza"

#. ~ Description of terrain "solid bark wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A solid wall of bark, enclosing the trunk of a massive tree.  It will "
"probably burn quite well."
msgstr ""
"Un sólido muro de corteza, que encierra el tronco de un enorme árbol. "
"Probablemente arderá bastante bien."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "chipped bark wall"
msgstr "muro astillado de corteza"

#. ~ Description of terrain "chipped bark wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A solid wall of bark enclosing the trunk of a massive tree.  Some of it has "
"been broken away."
msgstr ""
"Un sólid muro de corteza que encierra el tronco de un enorme árbol. Parte de"
" ella se ha roto."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "broken bark wall"
msgstr "muro roto de corteza"

#. ~ Description of terrain "broken bark wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A formerly solid wall of bark, now almost completely destroyed and waiting "
"to collapse."
msgstr ""
"Un muro de corteza antes sólido, ahora casi completamente destruido y a "
"punto de derrumbarse."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "solid wood wall"
msgstr "muro sólido de madera"

#. ~ Description of terrain "solid wood wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "A solid wall of naturally grown wood.  Likely very flammable."
msgstr ""
"Un muro sólido de madera cultivada naturalmente. Probablemente muy "
"inflamable."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "bark"
msgstr "corteza"

#. ~ Description of terrain "bark"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "A solid piece of bark covers the floor here."
msgstr "Una pieza sólida de corteza cubre el suelo aquí."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "branches with leaves"
msgstr "ramas con hojas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "branches with leaves"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "Thin branches emerge here, covered with thick, large leaves."
msgstr "De aquí surgen ramas finas, cubiertas de hojas gruesas y grandes."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "root floor"
msgstr "suelo de raíces"

#. ~ Description of terrain "root floor"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "A dirt floor covered with roots."
msgstr "Un suelo de tierra cubierto de raíces."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "downward root slope"
msgstr "pendiente de raíces descendente"

#. ~ Description of terrain "downward root slope"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "A downward-facing slope of root-covered dirt."
msgstr "Una pendiente descendente de tierra cubierta de raíces."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "upward root slope"
msgstr "pendiente de raíces ascendente"

#. ~ Description of terrain "upward root slope"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "An upward-facing slope of root-covered dirt."
msgstr "Una pendiente ascendente de tierra cubierta de raíces."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "closed bramble roots"
msgstr "raíces espinosas cerradas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "closed bramble roots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid ""
"A bramble of roots are here, covering a hole.  They could easily be pulled "
"apart."
msgstr ""
"Una maraña de raíces está aquí, cubriendo un agujero. Podrían separarse "
"fácilmente."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "open bramble roots"
msgstr "raíces espinosas abiertas"

#. ~ Description of terrain "open bramble roots"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-triffid.json
msgid "A bramble of roots are here, they are pulled apart revealing a hole."
msgstr "Una maraña de raíces están aquí, se separan revelando un agujero."

#. ~ Terrain name
#. ~ Overmap terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
#: data/json/overmap/overmap_terrain/overmap_terrain.json
#: data/mods/No_Hope/terrain.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-doors.json
msgid "wall"
msgstr "muro"

#. ~ Description of terrain "wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"The stereotypical wall with wooden support structure filled with insulation "
"and drywalled.  Paint job is the all too common and neutral off-white or "
"cream color, it could use more vibrant paint.  Appears as though the "
"material is still flammable."
msgstr ""
"El muro típico con estructura de soporte de madera rellena de aislamiento y "
"muros de yeso. El trabajo de pintura es bastante común con el color neutral "
"color blanco o crema, podría utilizar una pintura más vibrante. Parece como "
"si el material fuera todavía inflamable."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "half-built wall"
msgstr "muro a medio construir"

#. ~ Description of terrain "half-built wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"An incomplete wall of refined wood, dotted with carefully placed nails to "
"provide proper support.  It requires some more planks and nails before it'd "
"be considered a suitable wall."
msgstr ""
"Un muro incompleto de madera refinada, salpicado de clavos cuidadosamente "
"colocados para proporcionar un soporte adecuado. Requiere algunos tablones y"
" clavos más antes de que se considere unmuro adecuada."

#. ~ Terrain name
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid "pony wall"
msgstr "muro de poni"

#. ~ Description of terrain "pony wall"
#: data/json/furniture_and_terrain/terrain-walls.json
msgid ""
"A short divider wall with wooden support structure with drywall.  Paint job "
"is the all too common and neutral off-white or cream color.  Appears as "
"though the material is flammable."
msgstr ""
"Un corto muro divisorio con una estructura de soporte de madera con paneles "
"de yeso. El trabajo de pintura es demasiado común y de color blanco neutro o"
" crema. Parece como si el material fuera inflamable."

