"corporativo 1999\"."

#. ~ Snippet of item "bottle opener"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "This bottle opener reads 'I'd rather be drinking whiskey'."
msgstr "Este abridor de botellas dice: \"Preferiría estar bebiendo whisky\"."

#. ~ Snippet of item "bottle opener"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "This bottle opener is shaped like a phaser."
msgstr "Este abridor de botellas tiene la forma de un fáser."

#. ~ Snippet of item "bottle opener"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "This novelty bottle opener is designed to look like a hobo clown."
msgstr ""
"Este novedoso abridor de botellas está diseñado para parecerse a un payaso "
"vagabundo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "spork"
msgid_plural "sporks"
msgstr[0] "cuchador"
msgstr[1] "cuchadores"
msgstr[2] "cuchadores"

#. ~ Description of "spork"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"The bastardized hybrid of a spoon and fork, with all the power and "
"capabilities of both in a more annoying to use package."
msgstr ""
"El híbrido bastardo de una cuchara y un tenedor, con todo el poder y las "
"capacidades de ambos en un paquete más molesto de usar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "foon"
msgid_plural "foons"
msgstr[0] "tenuchara"
msgstr[1] "tenucharas"
msgstr[2] "tenucharas"

#. ~ Description of "foon"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "Clearly the superior instrument.  Sporks are just imitators."
msgstr ""
"Obviamente, el mejor instrumento. Los cuchadores son tristes imitaciones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "chopsticks"
msgid_plural "pairs of chopsticks"
msgstr[0] "par de palitos chinos"
msgstr[1] "pares de palitos chinos"
msgstr[2] "pares de palitos chinos"

#. ~ Description of "chopsticks"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"One of the most popular eating utensils in the world.  Does double duty as a"
" way of dealing with especially fragile vampires."
msgstr ""
"Uno de los utensilios para comer más populares del mundo. Hace doble turno "
"como una forma de tratar con vampiros especialmente frágiles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json data/mods/MMA/bludgeons.json
msgid "ladle"
msgid_plural "ladles"
msgstr[0] "cucharón"
msgstr[1] "cucharones"
msgstr[2] "cucharones"

#. ~ Description of "ladle"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "When you need to scoop some soup, this is the utensil for you."
msgstr "Cuando necesites servir sopa, este es el utensilio para ti."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "whisk"
msgid_plural "whisks"
msgstr[0] "batidora"
msgstr[1] "batidoras"
msgstr[2] "batidoras"

#. ~ Description of "whisk"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A tool designed for finely mixing ingredients or introducing air into the "
"blend.  Also known as a 'wire whip', but it's a less effective weapon than "
"that name makes it sound."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta diseñada para mezclar ingredientes o introducir aire en una "
"mezcla. También se la conoce como 'látigo de alambre' pero a pesar de ese "
"nombre, no funciona tan efectivamente como arma."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "potato masher"
msgid_plural "potato mashers"
msgstr[0] "machacador de patatas"
msgstr[1] "machacadores de patatas"
msgstr[2] "machacadores de patatas"

#. ~ Description of "potato masher"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A tool for mashing potatoes and soft root vegetables; it cannot do the "
"twist."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta que puede aplastar patatas y otros tubérculos suaves. No "
"puede hacer el giro."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "garlic press"
msgid_plural "garlic presses"
msgstr[0] "prensa de ajo"
msgstr[1] "prensas de ajo"
msgstr[2] "prensas de ajo"

#. ~ Description of "garlic press"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "A tool for squashing a clove or two of garlic into a fine paste."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta para aplastar uno o dos dientes de ajo y hacer un pasta "
"fina."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "can opener"
msgid_plural "can openers"
msgstr[0] "abridor de latas"
msgstr[1] "abridores de latas"
msgstr[2] "abridores de latas"

#. ~ Description of "can opener"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A tool for opening cans that lack pull-tabs.  Now that you think about it, "
"you haven't seen any of those around lately."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta para abrir latas que no tienen abre fácil.  Ahora que lo "
"piensas, no has visto una de esas por estos lares últimamente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "carving fork"
msgid_plural "carving forks"
msgstr[0] "tenedor de trinchar"
msgstr[1] "tenedores de trinchar"
msgstr[2] "tenedores de trinchar"

#. ~ Description of "carving fork"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A utensil used to hold meat still while you slice it.  It's like a tiny "
"pitchfork, or a very large dinner fork."
msgstr ""
"Un utensilio para sostener la carne mientras la cortas. Es como un tridente "
"pequeño o un tenedor muy grande."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "spatula"
msgid_plural "spatulas"
msgstr[0] "espátula"
msgstr[1] "espátulas"
msgstr[2] "espátulas"

#. ~ Description of "spatula"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A rubber scraper for making sure you get every last scrap of cookie dough."
msgstr ""
"Un raspador de goma para asegurarte de que recibes hasta el último resto de "
"masa de galletas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "rolling pin"
msgid_plural "rolling pins"
msgstr[0] "rodillo de cocina"
msgstr[1] "rodillos de cocina"
msgstr[2] "rodillos de cocina"

#. ~ Description of "rolling pin"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A stout piece of hardwood, turned and sanded smooth, with rounded handles at"
" the ends.  This timeless kitchen tool also doubles as a very effective "
"club."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza robusta de madera dura, torneada y lijada suavemente, con mangos "
"redondeados en los extremos. Este intemporal utensilio de cocina también es "
"un garrote muy efectivo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "pot"
msgid_plural "pots"
msgstr[0] "olla"
msgstr[1] "ollas"
msgstr[2] "ollas"

#. ~ Description of "pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "A cooking pot, useful for boiling water and making all kinds of food."
msgstr ""
"Una olla para cocinar, útil para hervir agua y hacer toda clase de comidas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "cast-iron pot"
msgid_plural "cast-iron pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de hierro fundido"
msgstr[1] "ollas de hierro fundido"
msgstr[2] "ollas de hierro fundido"

#. ~ Description of "cast-iron pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"This hefty black pot is made from cast iron and coated in a sturdy enamel."
msgstr ""
"Esta pesada olla negra está hecha de hierro fundido y recubierta de un "
"robusto esmalte."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "copper pot"
msgid_plural "copper pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de cobre"
msgstr[1] "ollas de cobre"
msgstr[2] "ollas de cobre"

#. ~ Description of "copper pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A cooking pot, useful for boiling water and making all kinds of food.  Made "
"from copper, with a lining of tin to prevent metal from leaching into acidic"
" foods."
msgstr ""
"Una olla para cocinar, útil para hervir agua y hacer toda clase de comidas. "
"Está hecha de cobre con un revestimiento de estaño para prevenir que el "
"metal se filtre en las comidas ácidas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "casserole pot"
msgid_plural "casserole pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de cacerola"
msgstr[1] "ollas de cacerola"
msgstr[2] "ollas de cacerola"

#. ~ Description of "casserole pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A ceramic pot made for both cooking and serving, particularly one-pot "
"dinners."
msgstr ""
"Una olla de cerámica hecha tanto para cocinar como para servir, "
"especialmente para cenas de una sola olla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "stock pot"
msgid_plural "stock pots"
msgstr[0] "marmita"
msgstr[1] "marmitas"
msgstr[2] "marmitas"

#. ~ Description of "stock pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A large pot with 20 gauge walls and a thick aluminum bottom, used for making"
" soup stocks.  You could fit a whole turkey in there, with a bit of shoving."
msgstr ""
"Una gran olla con grandes muros de acero inoxidable y un grueso fondo de "
"aluminio, usada para hacer grandes caldos. Podrías meter un pavo entero "
"apretando un poco."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "canning pot"
msgid_plural "canning pots"
msgstr[0] "bote de conserva"
msgstr[1] "botes de conserva"
msgstr[2] "botes de conserva"

#. ~ Description of "canning pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A very large 25 liter pot, primarily meant for canning food in glass jars "
"via the water bath method, though it can cook normal foods just as well.  "
"Canning foods with it will require a lot of water.  If you're only canning a"
" couple of jars at a time, you'd fill it up with rocks or something to "
"displace the water above the lids."
msgstr ""
"Una olla muy grande de 25 litros, destinada principalmente a enlatar "
"alimentos en tarros de cristal mediante el método de baño de agua, aunque "
"también puede cocinar alimentos normales. El enlatado de alimentos con ella "
"requerirá mucha agua. Si sólo se enlatan un par de frascos a la vez, se "
"llenaría con piedras o algo para desplazar el agua por encima de las tapas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "clay canning pot"
msgid_plural "clay canning pots"
msgstr[0] "bote de conserva de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "botes de conserva de arcilla"
msgstr[2] "botes de conserva de arcilla"

#. ~ Description of "clay canning pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A very large 25 liter earthenware pot, primarily meant for canning food via "
"the water bath method, though it can cook normal foods just as well.  "
"Canning foods with it will require a lot of water.  If you're only canning a"
" couple of jars at a time, you'd fill it up with rocks or something to "
"displace the water above the lids."
msgstr ""
"Una olla cerámica muy grande de 25 litros, pensada para hacer conservas con "
"el método del baño de agua, aunque puede usarse para cocinar normalmente. El"
" proceso de conservación de alimentos necesita mucha agua. Si solamente "
"estas haciendo conserva con un par de frascos a la vez, tendrías que "
"llenarla con piedras o algo para que el agua sobrepase los frascos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "cast-iron frying pan"
msgid_plural "cast-iron frying pans"
msgstr[0] "sartén de hierro fundido"
msgstr[1] "sartenes de hierro fundido"
msgstr[2] "sartenes de hierro fundido"

#. ~ Description of "cast-iron frying pan"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A cast-iron pan.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and is used for cooking."
msgstr ""
"Una olla de hierro fundido. Sirve como arma de c. a c., y es útil para "
"cocinar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "steel frying pan"
msgid_plural "steel frying pans"
msgstr[0] "sartén de acero"
msgstr[1] "sartenes de acero"
msgstr[2] "sartenes de acero"

#. ~ Description of "steel frying pan"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A steel frying pan.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and is used for cooking."
msgstr "Una sartén de acero. Un arma c. a c. decente y se usa para cocinar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "copper frying pan"
msgid_plural "copper frying pans"
msgstr[0] "sartén de cobre"
msgstr[1] "sartenes de cobre"
msgstr[2] "sartenes de cobre"

#. ~ Description of "copper frying pan"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A copper frying pan, coated in a thin layer of tin.  Makes a decent melee "
"weapon, and is used for cooking."
msgstr ""
"Una sartén de cobre, recubierta con una fina capa de estaño. Un arma c. a c."
" decente y se usa para cocinar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "makeshift pot"
msgid_plural "makeshift pots"
msgstr[0] "olla improvisada"
msgstr[1] "ollas improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "ollas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A sheet of metal crudely hammered into a cooking pot.  Good enough to cook "
"food and boil water, but not as useful as proper cookware."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de metal burdamente martillada para darle forma de olla. Es "
"suficiente para cocinar comida y hervir agua, pero no tan útil como un "
"utensilio adecuado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "makeshift copper pot"
msgid_plural "makeshift copper pots"
msgstr[0] "olla improvisada de cobre"
msgstr[1] "ollas improvisadas de cobre"
msgstr[2] "ollas improvisadas de cobre"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift copper pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A cooking pot crudely hammered out of copper.  Good enough to cook food and "
"boil water, but not as useful as proper cookware."
msgstr ""
"Una olla de cocina burdamente martillada a partir de cobre. Suficiente para "
"cocinar comida y hervir agua, pero no tan útil como un utensilio de cocina "
"adecuado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "kettle"
msgid_plural "kettles"
msgstr[0] "tetera"
msgstr[1] "teteras"
msgstr[2] "teteras"

#. ~ Description of "kettle"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "A stovetop kettle for boiling water."
msgstr "Una tetera para hervir agua."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "mesh colander"
msgid_plural "mesh colanders"
msgstr[0] "colador de malla"
msgstr[1] "coladores de malla"
msgstr[2] "coladores de malla"

#. ~ Description of "mesh colander"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A stainless steel mesh colander, for washing rice and vegetables, or "
"straining liquid off from noodles or other foods."
msgstr ""
"Un colador de acero inoxidable, se usa para lavar arroz, verduras o sacar el"
" líquido de los fideos u otras comidas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "splatter guard"
msgid_plural "splatter guards"
msgstr[0] "protector contra salpicaduras"
msgstr[1] "protectores contra salpicaduras"
msgstr[2] "protectores contra salpicaduras"

#. ~ Description of "splatter guard"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A stainless steel mesh screen for preventing flying oil from getting all "
"over your nice counters (or you) when frying."
msgstr ""
"Una pantalla de malla de acero inoxidable para evitar que el aceite volador "
"se desparrame sobre sus bonitos mostradores (o sobre usted) cuando se fríe."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "cutting board"
msgid_plural "cutting boards"
msgstr[0] "tabla para cortar"
msgstr[1] "tablas para cortar"
msgstr[2] "tablas para cortar"

#. ~ Description of "cutting board"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A large, flat piece of wood for chopping vegetables on without ruining your "
"knife or your countertop."
msgstr ""
"Un gran trozo plano de madera para cortar verduras sin arruinar el cuchillo "
"o la encimera."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "meal tray"
msgid_plural "meal trays"
msgstr[0] "bandeja de comida"
msgstr[1] "bandejas de comida"
msgstr[2] "bandejas de comida"

#. ~ Description of "meal tray"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A stainless steel tray used for serving food in cafeterias, mess halls, or "
"similar places."
msgstr ""
"Una bandeja de acero inoxidable usada para servir comida en cafeterías, "
"comedores o lugares similares."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "pizza cutter"
msgid_plural "pizza cutters"
msgstr[0] "cortador de pizza"
msgstr[1] "cortadores de pizza"
msgstr[2] "cortadores de pizza"

#. ~ Description of "pizza cutter"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "A utensil used for cutting pizza.  Practically useless in combat."
msgstr ""
"Un utensilio usado para cortar la pizza. Prácticamente inútil en combate."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "icecream scoop"
msgid_plural "icecream scoops"
msgstr[0] "cuchara de helado"
msgstr[1] "cucharas de helado"
msgstr[2] "cucharas de helado"

#. ~ Description of "icecream scoop"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A utensil used for scooping icecream into bowls.  It has a spring powered "
"lever to assist."
msgstr ""
"Un utensilio usado para servir helado en tazones. Tiene una palanca "
"accionada por resorte para ayudar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "cheese grater"
msgid_plural "cheese graters"
msgstr[0] "rayador de queso"
msgstr[1] "rayadores de queso"
msgstr[2] "rayadores de queso"

#. ~ Description of "cheese grater"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A stainless steel cheese grater with a plastic grip.  It is used to shred "
"cheese."
msgstr ""
"Un rallador de queso de acero inoxidable con mango de plástico. Se utiliza "
"para rallar queso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "cast-iron dutch oven"
msgid_plural "cast-iron dutch ovens"
msgstr[0] "horno holandés de hierro fundido"
msgstr[1] "hornos holandeses de hierro fundido"
msgstr[2] "hornos holandeses de hierro fundido"

#. ~ Description of "cast-iron dutch oven"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A cast-iron dutch oven, suitable for boiling, broiling, roasting, baking, "
"stewing, frying and any other method of cooking."
msgstr ""
"Un horno holandés de hierro fundido adecuado para hervir, asar, tostar, "
"cocinar, estofar, freír o cualquier otro método de cocción."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "improvised oven"
msgid_plural "improvised ovens"
msgstr[0] "horno improvisado"
msgstr[1] "hornos improvisados"
msgstr[2] "hornos improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "improvised oven"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A large pot converted into an improvised oven, suitable for basic baking on "
"a hot surface."
msgstr ""
"Una olla grande improvisada como horno, adecuada para métodos básicos de "
"cocina sobre una superficie caliente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "clay pot oven"
msgid_plural "clay pot ovens"
msgstr[0] "olla de horno de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "ollas de horno de arcilla"
msgstr[2] "ollas de horno de arcilla"

#. ~ Description of "clay pot oven"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A makeshift oven made of a big clay pot with a lid, containing firebricks to"
" hold heat and a smaller pot to bake in."
msgstr ""
"Un horno improvisado hecho con una olla grande de arcilla con tapa, "
"ladrillos refractantes para contener el calor y una olla más pequeña para "
"cocinar dentro."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "aluminum frying pan"
msgid_plural "aluminum frying pans"
msgstr[0] "sartén de aluminio"
msgstr[1] "sartenes de aluminio"
msgstr[2] "sartenes de aluminio"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum frying pan"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"An aluminum frying pan.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and is used for "
"cooking."
msgstr ""
"Una sartén de aluminio. Es una decente arma de c. a c. y también se usa para"
" cocinar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid "aluminum pot"
msgid_plural "aluminum pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de aluminio"
msgstr[1] "ollas de aluminio"
msgstr[2] "ollas de aluminio"

#. ~ Description of "aluminum pot"
#: data/json/items/generic/dining_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A cooking pot, useful for boiling water and making all kinds of food.  Made "
"from aluminum."
msgstr ""
"Una olla para cocinar, útil para hervir agua y hacer toda clase de comidas. "
"Está hecha de aluminio."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid "envelope"
msgid_plural "envelopes"
msgstr[0] "sobre"
msgstr[1] "sobres"
msgstr[2] "sobres"

#. ~ Description of "envelope"
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid ""
"A flat paper container with a sealable flap, used to enclose a letter or "
"other paper goods."
msgstr ""
"Un recipiente fino hecho de papel con una solapa, utilizado para contener "
"una carta u otros papeles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid "letter"
msgid_plural "letters"
msgstr[0] "carta"
msgstr[1] "cartas"
msgstr[2] "cartas"

#. ~ Description of "letter"
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid ""
"A written message from one person to another, usually put in an envelope.  "
"Reading it would be rude."
msgstr ""
"Un mensaje escrito por una persona, dentro de un sobre normalmente.\n"
"Leerlo sería de mala educación."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid "postcard"
msgid_plural "postcards"
msgstr[0] "postal"
msgstr[1] "postales"
msgstr[2] "postales"

#. ~ Description of "postcard"
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid ""
"A piece of thick, rectangular paper intended for writing and mailing without"
" an envelope."
msgstr ""
"Un pedazo de papel grueso, rectangular, con la intención de escribir en el  "
"y enviarlo por correos sin sobre."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid "gift card"
msgid_plural "gift cards"
msgstr[0] "tarjeta de regalo"
msgstr[1] "tarjetas de regalo"
msgstr[2] "tarjetas de regalo"

#. ~ Description of "gift card"
#: data/json/items/generic/mail.json
msgid ""
"A small card that can be exchanged for goods or services from a particular "
"business, usually given as a gift."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña tarjeta que se puede canjear por objetos o servicios de un "
"negocio específico, generalmente se dan como regalo."

