msgstr "3 rd."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "M16 auto rifle"
msgid_plural "M16 auto rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle automático M16"
msgstr[1] "rifles automáticos M16"
msgstr[2] "rifles automáticos M16"

#. ~ Description of gun "M16 auto rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"The M16 is a very common assault rifle descended from the AR-15, used by "
"militaries across the world for over 50 years.  Unlike its more common "
"brother, the M16 burst rifle, this one has full-auto capabilities.  It is "
"chambered in 5.56x45mm and accepts STANAG magazines."
msgstr ""
"El M16 es un rifle de asalto muy común que desciende del AR-15, utilizado "
"por militares de todo el mundo durante más de 50 años. A diferencia de su "
"hermano más común, el rifle de ráfaga M16, éste tiene capacidades "
"automáticas. Tiene cámara de 5.56x45mm y acepta cargadores STANAG."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "M16 auto rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "M16A3"
msgid_plural "M16A3s"
msgstr[0] "M16A3"
msgstr[1] "M16A3s"
msgstr[2] "M16A3s"

#. ~ Description of variant "M16 auto rifle" of gun "M16A3"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"The M16 is a very common assault rifle descended from the AR-15, used by "
"militaries across the world for over 50 years.  It is a gas-operated, "
"rotating bolt rifle known for its accuracy and controllable recoil.  This "
"one is a relatively rare M16A3, with full auto capability."
msgstr ""
"El M16 es un rifle de asalto muy común que desciende del AR-15, utilizado "
"por los militares de todo el mundo durante más de 50 años. Es un rifle de "
"cerrojo giratorio accionado por gas, conocido por su precisión y su "
"retroceso controlable. Este es un M16A3 relativamente raro, con capacidad de"
" funcionamiento totalmente automático."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "M16 auto rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "Remington ACR"
msgid_plural "Remington ACRs"
msgstr[0] "Remington ACR"
msgstr[1] "Remington ACRs"
msgstr[2] "Remington ACRs"

#. ~ Description of variant "M16 auto rifle" of gun "Remington ACR"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"This carbine was developed for military use in the early 21st century.  It "
"is damaging and accurate, though its rate of fire is a bit slower than "
"competing carbines."
msgstr ""
"Esta carabina fue desarrollada para el uso militar a principios del siglo "
"XXI. Es precisa y causa mucho daño, aunque su velocidad de disparo es un "
"poco lenta comparándola con otras carabinas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "M16 firing port gun"
msgid_plural "M16 firing port guns"
msgstr[0] "M16 de tronera"
msgstr[1] "M16 de tronera"
msgstr[2] "M16 de tronera"

#. ~ Description of gun "M16 firing port gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"The M16 firing port gun is an M16 rifle modified to fire with an open-bolt "
"design at ludicrous speeds, without sights.  It has a threaded handguard to "
"screw into an armored vehicle's firing ports.  It is chambered in 5.56x45mm "
"and accepts STANAG magazines."
msgstr ""
"La M16 de tronera es un rifle M16 modificado para disparar con un diseño de "
"cerrojo abierto a velocidades absurdas, sin miras. Tiene un guardamano con "
"rosca para ajustarse en las troneras de un vehículo. Tiene calibre 5.56x45mm"
" y puede utilizar cargadores STANAG."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "M16 firing port gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "M231 port firing weapon"
msgid_plural "M231 port firing weapons"
msgstr[0] "armasde tronera M231"
msgstr[1] "armas de tronera M231"
msgstr[2] "armas de tronera M231"

#. ~ Description of variant "M16 firing port gun" of gun "M231 port firing
#. weapon"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"The M231 PFW is an adaptation of the M16 assault rifle, designed to be used "
"in the firing ports of the M2 Bradley Infantry Fighting Vehicle.  It does "
"not have a buttstock or front sight post, and the smooth front hand guard "
"does nothing to protect you from the potentially scorching hot barrel "
"collar, making it slightly less than ergonomic.  You could screw it into a "
"firing port if you were so inclined.  The fire selector says only 'SAFE' and"
" 'AUTO'.  You can't help but wonder which one is preferable."
msgstr ""
"El M231 PFW es una adaptación del rifle de asalto M16, diseñado para ser "
"utilizado en la tronera del vehículo de infantería M2 Bradley. No tiene "
"culata ni mira frontal con poste y el guardamanos liso delantero no hace "
"nada para protegerte del cañón incandescente, haciéndola un poco menos "
"ergonómica. Podrías ajustarla en una tronera si quieres. El selector de "
"disparo dice solamente 'SEGURO' y 'AUTO'. No puedes evitar preguntarte cuál "
"será preferible."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "OA-93"
msgid_plural "OA-93s"
msgstr[0] "OA-93"
msgstr[1] "OA-93s"
msgstr[2] "OA-93s"

#. ~ Description of gun "OA-93"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"An AR-15 derivative pistol manufactured by Olympic Arms in the nineties.  "
"The main difference compared to the AR-15 is that the recoil spring has been"
" moved to the top of the gun, circumventing the necessity for a solid "
"buttstock."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola derivada del AR-15 fabricada por Olympic Arms en los años "
"noventa. La principal diferencia con el AR-15 es que el muelle recuperador "
"se ha trasladado a la parte superior del arma, evitando la necesidad de una "
"culata sólida."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "Ruger Mini-14"
msgid_plural "Ruger Mini-14s"
msgstr[0] "Ruger Mini-14"
msgstr[1] "Ruger Mini-14"
msgstr[2] "Ruger Mini-14"

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Mini-14"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A small, lightweight semi-auto carbine designed for civilian and police use."
"  Its superb accuracy and low recoil makes it more suitable than full-auto "
"rifles for some situations."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeña y ligera carabina semiautomática diseñada para uso civil y "
"policial. Su excelente precisión y bajo retroceso hace que sea más adecuada "
"que los rifles completamente automáticos para algunas situaciones."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "SIG assault rifle"
msgid_plural "SIG assault rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de asalto SIG"
msgstr[1] "rifles de asalto SIG"
msgstr[2] "rifles de asalto SIG"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG assault rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A compact selective fire automatic rifle designed for the Swiss military.  "
"It features a three-round burst mode and an integrated folding stock.  It is"
" chambered in 5.56x45mm and accepts STANAG magazines."
msgstr ""
"Rifle automático compacto de tiro selectivo diseñado para el ejército suizo."
" Cuenta con un modo de ráfaga de tres balas y una culata plegable integrada."
" Tiene cámara de 5.56x45 mm y acepta cargadores STANAG."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "SIG assault rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "SIG 553"
msgid_plural "SIG 553s"
msgstr[0] "SIG 553"
msgstr[1] "SIG 553s"
msgstr[2] "SIG 553s"

#. ~ Description of variant "SIG assault rifle" of gun "SIG 553"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A compact selective fire automatic rifle designed for the Swiss military.  "
"It features a three-round burst mode and an integrated folding stock."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle automático de fuego selectivo compacto diseñado para el ejército "
"suizo. Cuenta con un modo de ráfaga de tres balas y una culata plegable "
"integrada."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "AUG assault rifle"
msgid_plural "AUG assault rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de asalto AUG"
msgstr[1] "rifles de asalto AUG"
msgstr[2] "rifles de asalto AUG"

#. ~ Description of gun "AUG assault rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "An assault rifle chambered in 5.56x45mm and accepting AUG magazines"
msgstr ""
"Una rifle de asalto con camara de 5.56x45mm y que acepta cargadores AUG."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "AUG assault rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "Steyr AUG"
msgid_plural "Steyr AUGs"
msgstr[0] "Steyr AUG"
msgstr[1] "Steyr AUG"
msgstr[2] "Steyr AUG"

#. ~ Description of variant "AUG assault rifle" of gun "Steyr AUG"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"The Steyr AUG is an Austrian assault rifle that uses a bullpup design.  It "
"is used in the armed forces and police forces of many nations, and enjoys "
"low recoil and high accuracy."
msgstr ""
"El Steyr AUG es un rifle de asalto austríaco que utiliza el diseño bullpup. "
"Es usado por las fuerzas armadas y policiales de muchos países, y tiene poco"
" retroceso y mucha precisión."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "5.56x45mm AK"
msgid_plural "5.56x45mm AKs"
msgstr[0] "5.56x45mm AK"
msgstr[1] "5.56x45mm AK"
msgstr[2] "5.56x45mm AK"

#. ~ Description of gun "5.56x45mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "A civilian AK pattern rifle, chambered in 5.56x45 NATO."
msgstr "Un rifle tipo AK civil con calibre 5.56x45 NATO."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "5.56x45mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "ZPAP M90"
msgid_plural "ZPAP M90s"
msgstr[0] "ZPAP M90"
msgstr[1] "ZPAP M90"
msgstr[2] "ZPAP M90"

#. ~ Description of variant "5.56x45mm AK" of gun "ZPAP M90"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A Serbian-made AK pattern rifle made by Zastava in 5.56x45mm NATO.  To avoid"
" import restrictions, Zastava USA has added a number of American-made parts."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de tipo AK serbio fabricado por Zastava con calibre 5.56x45mm NATO."
" Para evitar las restricciones de importación, Zastava USA le agregó algunas"
" partes fabricadas en Estados Unidos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "5.56x45mm Mini Draco"
msgid_plural "5.56x45mm Mini Dracos"
msgstr[0] "5.56x45mm Mini Draco"
msgstr[1] "5.56x45mm Mini Draco"
msgstr[2] "5.56x45mm Mini Draco"

#. ~ Description of gun "5.56x45mm Mini Draco"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A civilian AK pattern rifle, chambered in 5.56x45 NATO.  This one is shorter"
" and without a stock"
msgstr ""
"Un rifle tipo AK civil con calibre 5.56x45 NATO. Este es más corto y no "
"tiene culata."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "5.56x45mm Mini Draco"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid "ZPAP 85"
msgid_plural "ZPAP 85s"
msgstr[0] "ZPAP 85"
msgstr[1] "ZPAP 85"
msgstr[2] "ZPAP 85"

#. ~ Description of variant "5.56x45mm Mini Draco" of gun "ZPAP 85"
#: data/json/items/gun/223.json
msgid ""
"A Serbian-made AK pattern rifle made by Zastava in 5.56x45mm NATO.  To avoid"
" import restrictions, Zastava USA has added a number of American-made parts."
"  This one is shorter and without a stock"
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de tipo AK serbio fabricado por Zastava con calibre 5.56x45mm NATO."
" Para evitar las restricciones de importación, Zastava USA le agregó algunas"
" partes fabricadas en Estados Unidos. Este es más corto y no tiene culata."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid "bolt-action hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "bolt-action hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de caza de cerrojo"
msgstr[1] "rifles de caza de cerrojo"
msgstr[2] "rifles de caza de cerrojo"

#. ~ Description of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid ""
"Featuring a handsome set of wooden furnishings, a classic design, and a no "
"nonsense .270 caliber chambering, this is a powerful hunting rifle.  With a "
"tried and proven pedigree dating back over 60 years, millions of such rugged"
" arms have been made, exported, and used throughout the United States and "
"the world at large.  Where hunting is concerned, this is a highly capable "
"and well proven weapon in all respects.  Fortunate, given that your prey in "
"these dark days may turn out to be a little bit more feisty than typical "
"White-Tailed deer, moose, and black bears."
msgstr ""
"Este poderoso rifle de caza posee un elegante conjunto de accesorios de "
"madera, un diseño clásico y un entendible calibre .270. Con un linaje "
"probado de más de 60 años, millones de estas robustas armas han sido "
"fabricadas, exportadas y utilizadas a lo largo de Estados Unidos y el mundo "
"entero. En cuanto a la caza se refiere, este es un rifle muy capaz y bien "
"probado en todos sus aspectos. Y eso es una suerte, ya que en estos días "
"oscuros tu presa puede resultar un poco más peleadora que los típicos "
"ciervos de cola blanca, alces y osos negros."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "bolt-action hunting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[0] "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[1] "Remington 700 .270 Win"
msgstr[2] "Remington 700 .270 Win"

#. ~ Description of variant "bolt-action hunting rifle" of gun "Remington 700
#. .270 Win"
#: data/json/items/gun/270win.json
msgid ""
"A classic bolt-action rifle chambered for .270 Winchester, very popular "
"among hunters.  This is a CDL SF model with a forged, fluted, 416 stainless "
"steel barrel threaded into the receiver and a recessed bolt face.  It has "
"checkered walnut furniture and a recoil pad to reduce perceived recoil."
msgstr ""
"Un clásico rifle de cerrojo con recámara para Winchester .270, muy popular "
"entre los cazadores. Este es un modelo CDL SF con un cañón de acero "
"inoxidable 416 forjado y estriado, roscado en el cañón y con una cara del "
"cerrojo empotrada. Tiene armazones de nogal a cuadros y una almohadilla de "
"retroceso para reducir el retroceso percibido."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "M2010 ESR"
msgid_plural "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[0] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[1] "M2010 ESR"
msgstr[2] "M2010 ESR"

#. ~ Description of gun "M2010 ESR"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"A bolt-action, box-magazine-fed sniper rifle chambered in the powerful .300 "
"Winchester Magnum round.  The M2010 had completely replaced the M24 rifle "
"series by 2017."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de francotirador de acción de bombeo y alimentado con cargador de "
"caja con la poderosa munición Winchester Magnum .300. El M2010 fue "
"reemplazado por la serie M24 en 2017."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "Weatherby Mark V"
msgid_plural "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[0] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[1] "Weatherby Mark V"
msgstr[2] "Weatherby Mark V"

#. ~ Description of gun "Weatherby Mark V"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"The Weatherby Mark V is one of the world's finest bolt-action rifles.  "
"Designed in 1955 by Roy Weatherby and Fred Jennie, it has a strong action "
"designed to safely fire high-pressure cartridges.  These rifles were "
"presented to celebrities as part of a marketing campaign."
msgstr ""
"El Weatherby Mark V es uno de los mejores rifles de cerrojo del mundo. "
"Diseñado en 1955 por Roy Weatherby y Fred Jennie, posee un diseño fuerte "
"para poder disparar de manera segura cartuchos de alta presión. Estos rifles"
" fueron regalados a celebridades como parte de una campaña publicitaria."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid "Winchester Model 70"
msgid_plural "Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[0] "Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[1] "Winchester Model 70"
msgstr[2] "Winchester Model 70"

#. ~ Description of gun "Winchester Model 70"
#: data/json/items/gun/300.json
msgid ""
"The Winchester Model 70 is a bolt-action sporting rifle.  It has an iconic "
"place in American sporting culture and has been held in high regard by "
"shooters since it was introduced in 1936."
msgstr ""
"El Winchester Model 70 es un rifle de cerrojo para tiro deportivo. Ocupa un "
"lugar icónico en la cultura deportiva estadounidense, y ha sido tenido en "
"gran consideración por los tiradores desde que fue presentada en 1936."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Browning BLR"
msgid_plural "Browning BLR"
msgstr[0] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[1] "Browning BLR"
msgstr[2] "Browning BLR"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning BLR"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A highly accurate lever-action hunting rifle chambered for the powerful "
".30-06 round.  Notable for using a detachable magazine instead of a "
"traditional tube."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de caza de acción de palanca, con muy buena precisión y calibre "
"para la poderosa .30-06. Conocido por utilizar un cargador extraíble en "
"lugar de la tradicional cámara."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "M1 Garand"
msgid_plural "M1 Garands"
msgstr[0] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[1] "M1 Garand"
msgstr[2] "M1 Garand"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1 Garand"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic .30-06 battle rifle, developed to replace the M1903 "
"Springfield.  It didn't completely supplant the older bolt-action until "
"after World War II."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de combate semiautomático de calibre .30-06, desarrollado para "
"reemplazar el M1903 Springfield. No llegó a reemplazarlo completamente hasta"
" después de la Segunda Guerra Mundial."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "M1903 Springfield"
msgid_plural "M1903 Springfields"
msgstr[0] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[1] "M1903 Springfield"
msgstr[2] "M1903 Springfield"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1903 Springfield"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A powerful military rifle chambered in .30-06, developed to replace the US "
"Army's older Krag rifle.  It served as the main American rifle in World War "
"I, was used alongside the M1 Garand in World War II, and was used as a "
"sniper rifle as late as the Vietnam War."
msgstr ""
"Un poderoso rifle militar calibre .30-06, desarrollado para reemplazar el "
"viejo rifle Krag del ejército de Estados Unidos. Fue el arma principal de "
"los estadounidenses durante la Primera Guerra Mundial, usado junto al M1 "
"Garand durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial, y llegó a ser usado como rifle de "
"francotirador incluso en la guerra de Vietnam."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Browning Automatic Rifle"
msgid_plural "Browning Automatic Rifles"
msgstr[0] "Rifle Automático Browning"
msgstr[1] "Rifles Automáticos Browning"
msgstr[2] "Rifles Automáticos Browning"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning Automatic Rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"Designed near the end of World War I, the BAR provided fire support for the "
"US Army from World War II all the way to the Vietnam War.  Too much "
"firepower to serve as a battle rifle, but not enough to be an ideal light "
"machine gun, it still found a niche on the battlefield."
msgstr ""
"Diseñado a fines de la Primera Guerra Mundial, el BAR (por sus siglas en "
"inglés) brindó apoyo al ejército de Estados Unidos desde la Segunda Guerra "
"Mundial hasta la guerra de Vietnam. Posee demasiada potencia como para ser "
"un rifle de combate, pero no la suficiente para ser una ametralladora "
"liviana ideal. De todas maneras, tiene su funcionalidad en el campo de "
"batalla."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgid_plural "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[0] "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[1] "Remington 700 .30-06"
msgstr[2] "Remington 700 .30-06"

#. ~ Description of gun "Remington 700 .30-06"
#: data/json/items/gun/3006.json
msgid ""
"A very popular and durable hunting or sniping rifle.  Popular among SWAT and"
" US Marine snipers.  Highly damaging, but perhaps not as accurate as the "
"competing Browning BLR."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de caza o francotirador muy popular y duradero. Popular entre los "
"francotiradores de SWAT y de la Marina de Estados Unidos. Causa mucho daño, "
"pero tal vez no sea tan preciso como su competidor, el Browning BLR."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgid_plural "Remington ACR .300BLKs"
msgstr[0] "Remington ACR .300BLK"
msgstr[1] "Remington ACR .300BLKs"
msgstr[2] "Remington ACR .300BLKs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Remington ACR .300BLK"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"This carbine was developed for military use in the early 21st century.  It "
"is damaging and accurate, though its rate of fire is a bit slower than "
"competing carbines.  This version is chambered for the .300 AAC Blackout "
"round."
msgstr ""
"Esta carabina fue desarrollada para uso militar a principios del siglo XXI. "
"Es dañina y precisa, aunque su velocidad de disparo es un poco más lenta que"
" la de las carabinas de la competencia. Esta versión está preparada para "
"balas de .300 AAC Blackout round."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgid_plural "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLKs"
msgstr[0] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
msgstr[1] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLKs"
msgstr[2] "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLKs"

#. ~ Description of gun "IWI Tavor X95 .300BLK"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"The IWI Tavor X95 (also called Micro-Tavor or MTAR) is an Israeli bullpup "
"assault rifle designed and produced by Israel Weapon Industries.  This is "
"the civilian version chambered for .300 AAC Blackout."
msgstr ""
"El IWI Tavor X95 (también llamado Micro-Tavor o MTAR) es un rifle de asalto "
"israelí diseñado y producido por Israel Weapon Industries. Esta es la "
"versión civil con cámara para un .300 AAC Blackout."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgid_plural "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[0] "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
msgstr[1] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"
msgstr[2] "SIG MCX Rattler SBRs"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG MCX Rattler SBR"
#: data/json/items/gun/300BLK.json
msgid ""
"This is a short-barreled, gas-operated rifle, with a 5.5 inch barrel, built-"
"in thin folding stock, and full rail mount on the upper receiver.  This "
"particular one is a select-fire military version."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de cañón corto operado por gas, con un cañón de 5.5 pulgadas, "
"culata plegable fina incorporada y montura de riel completa en el receptor "
"superior. Esta en particular es una versión militar con disparo selectivo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "FN FAL"
msgid_plural "FN FAL"
msgstr[0] "FN FAL"
msgstr[1] "FN FAL"
msgstr[2] "FN FAL"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN FAL"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"Originally designed during the Cold War, the FN FAL is probably the most "
"successful battle rifle ever designed.  Even though often labeled as "
"obsolete, its high rate of fire and powerful ammunition make it perfectly "
"capable of holding its ground against modern competitors."
msgstr ""
"Originalmente diseñado durante la Guerra Fría, el FN FAL probablemente sea "
"el rifle de combate más exitoso que se haya diseñado. Incluso aunque a veces"
" se lo tilda de obsoleto, su alta velocidad de disparo y munición poderosa "
"lo hacen perfectamente capaz de mantenerse entre los competidores modernos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "H&K G3"
msgid_plural "H&K G3"
msgstr[0] "H&K G3"
msgstr[1] "H&K G3"
msgstr[2] "H&K G3"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K G3"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"An early battle rifle developed after the end of WWII.  The G3 is designed "
"to unload large amounts of deadly ammunition, but it is less suitable over "
"long ranges."
msgstr ""
"Es un viejo rifle que fue desarrollado a fines de la Segunda Guerra Mundial."
" El G3 está diseñado para descargar cantidades de munición mortal, pero es "
"poco fiable a grandes distancias."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M134D-H Minigun"
msgid_plural "M134D-H Miniguns"
msgstr[0] "Minigun M134D-H"
msgstr[1] "Minigun M134D-H"
msgstr[2] "Minigun M134D-H"

#. ~ Description of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M134D-H Minigun is a (relatively) lightweight heavy rotary machine gun."
"  Its six barrels are rotated by an electric motor, powered by UPS or "
"vehicle.  If you could find enough ammo for it, it would become a "
"devastating weapon.  It must be mounted on a vehicle before use."
msgstr ""
"El Minigun M134D-H es una ametralladora rotativa (relativamente) ligera y "
"pesada. Sus seis cañones giran con un motor eléctrico, impulsado por un UPS "
"o un vehículo. Si pudieras encontrar suficiente munición para ella, se "
"convertiría en un arma devastadora. Debe ser montada en un vehículo antes de"
" su uso."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "low auto"
msgstr "bajo auto"

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M134D-H Minigun"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "CMES laser cannon"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json data/json/items/gun/ups.json
msgid "high auto"
msgstr "alto auto"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M14 EBR-RI"
msgid_plural "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[0] "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[1] "M14 EBR-RI"
msgstr[2] "M14 EBR-RI"

#. ~ Description of gun "M14 EBR-RI"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A highly modified version of the M14 rifle designed to cover both CQB and "
"designated marksman roles.  A very powerful and versatile rifle, if somewhat"
" heavy."
msgstr ""
"Una versión modificada del rifle M14, diseñado para cubrir tanto el combate "
"cercano como lejano. Un rifle muy poderoso y versátil, aunque un poco "
"pesado."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M1A"
msgid_plural "M1A"
msgstr[0] "M1A"
msgstr[1] "M1As"
msgstr[2] "M1As"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1A"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The child of the M1 Garand World War II rifle, the M1A is a semi-automatic "
"variant of the M14, favored for its accuracy and modular use."
msgstr ""
"El descendiente del rifle M1 Garand de la Segunda Guerra Mundial. El M1A es "
"una variante semi-automática del M14, preferido por su precisión y uso "
"modular."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M240"
msgid_plural "M240s"
msgstr[0] "M240"
msgstr[1] "M240"
msgstr[2] "M240"

#. ~ Description of gun "M240"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M240 is a medium machine gun used by the US military, replacing the "
"older M60.  Quite inaccurate and difficult to control, the M240 is designed "
"to fire many rounds very quickly."
msgstr ""
"La M240 es una ametralladora mediana utilizada por el Ejército de Estados "
"Unidos, y reemplaza la vieja M60. Bastante poco precisa y difícil de "
"controlar, la M240 está diseñada para disparar rápidamente muchas balas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M60"
msgid_plural "M60s"
msgstr[0] "M60"
msgstr[1] "M60s"
msgstr[2] "M60s"

#. ~ Description of gun "M60"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M60 is a general-purpose machine gun developed to replace the "
".30-caliber M1918 and M1919.  Heavy and difficult to handle fired from the "
"shoulder, as most people aren't action-movie heroes."
msgstr ""
"La M60 es una ametralladora de varios usos, desarrollada para reemplazar la "
"M1918 y M1919 de calibre .30. Pesada y difícil de controlar aguantándola con"
" el hombro, ya que casi nadie es un héroe de película de acción."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M60 Semi Auto"
msgid_plural "M60 Semi Autos"
msgstr[0] "M60 Semi Auto"
msgstr[1] "M60 Semi Autos"
msgstr[2] "M60 Semi Autos"

#. ~ Description of gun "M60 Semi Auto"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic civilian variant of the M60 machine gun, retaining the "
"ability to be belt fed, an uncommon feature in civilian firearms."
msgstr ""
"Una variante civil semiautomática de la ametralladora M60, retiene la "
"habilidad de usar alimentación por cinta, una característica inusual en las "
"armas civiles."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "Savage 111F"
msgid_plural "Savage 111F"
msgstr[0] "Savage 111F"
msgstr[1] "Savage 111F"
msgstr[2] "Savage 111F"

#. ~ Description of gun "Savage 111F"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A very accurate rifle chambered for the powerful .308 round.  Its very low "
"ammo capacity is offset by its accuracy and near-complete lack of recoil."
msgstr ""
"Es un rifle muy preciso con el poderoso calibre .308. El precio que hay que "
"pagar por su precisión y casi ausencia de retroceso es su capacidad muy "
"limitada para la munición."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "FN SCAR-H"
msgid_plural "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[0] "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[1] "FN SCAR-H"
msgstr[2] "FN SCAR-H"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN SCAR-H"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A highly accurate and modular battle rifle specially designed for the United"
" States Special Operations Command.  The 'H' in its name stands for heavy, "
"as it uses the powerful .308 round."
msgstr ""
"Es un rifle de combate modular y muy preciso, especialmente diseñado para el"
" Comando de Operaciones Especiales de Estados Unidos. La 'H' en el nombre "
"significa pesado (heavy), porque utiliza la poderosa bala .308."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M24"
msgid_plural "M24"
msgstr[0] "M24"
msgstr[1] "M24"
msgstr[2] "M24"

#. ~ Description of gun "M24"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"The M24 Sniper is the military and police version of the Remington Model 700"
" rifle, M24 being the model name assigned by the United States Army after "
"adoption as their standard sniper rifle in 1988.  The M24 is referred to as "
"a 'weapon system' because it consists of not only a rifle, but also a "
"detachable telescopic sight and other accessories."
msgstr ""
"El francotirador M24 es la versión militar y policial del rifle Remington "
"Modelo 700, siendo M24 el nombre del modelo asignado por el Ejército de los "
"Estados Unidos tras su adopción como su rifle de francotirador estándar en "
"1988. El M24 se denomina \"sistema de armas\" porque no sólo consiste en un "
"rifle, sino también en una mira telescópica desmontable y otros accesorios."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "HK417 A2"
msgid_plural "HK417 A2s"
msgstr[0] "HK417 A2"
msgstr[1] "HK417 A2s"
msgstr[2] "HK417 A2s"

#. ~ Description of gun "HK417 A2"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A German battle rifle with a 13\" barrel and telescopic stock.  It is a gas-"
"operated, rotating bolt rifle with a short-stroke piston design similar to "
"that of the G36."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de batalla alemán con un cañón de 13\" y un telescopio. Es un rifle"
" de cerrojo giratorio operado por gas con un diseño de pistón de carrera "
"corta similar al del G36."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "M110A1"
msgid_plural "M110A1s"
msgstr[0] "M110A1"
msgstr[1] "M110A1s"
msgstr[2] "M110A1s"

#. ~ Description of gun "M110A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A derivative of H&K's G28 with an aluminum upper receiver to meet US Army "
"weight requirements.  It is a gas-operated, rotating bolt rifle accurate to "
"1.5 MOA with standard ammunition."
msgstr ""
"Un derivado del G28 de H&K con un receptor superior de aluminio para cumplir"
" con los requisitos de peso del ejército de EE.UU. Es un rifle de cerrojo "
"giratorio operado por gas con una precisión de 1,5 MOA con munición "
"estándar."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "7.62x51mm AK"
msgid_plural "7.62x51mm AKs"
msgstr[0] "7.62x51mm AK"
msgstr[1] "7.62x51mm AK"
msgstr[2] "7.62x51mm AK"

#. ~ Description of gun "7.62x51mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "A civilian AK pattern rifle, chambered in 7.62x51mm NATO."
msgstr "Un rifle tipo AK civil con calibre 7.62x51mm NATO."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "7.62x51mm AK"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "PAP M77"
msgid_plural "PAP M77s"
msgstr[0] "PAP M77"
msgstr[1] "PAP M77"
msgstr[2] "PAP M77"

#. ~ Description of variant "7.62x51mm AK" of gun "PAP M77"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"A Serbian-made AK pattern rifle made by Zastava in 7.62x51mm NATO.  To avoid"
" import restrictions, Zastava USA has added a number of American-made parts."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de tipo AK serbio fabricado por Zastava con calibre 7.62x51mm NATO."
" Para evitar las restricciones de importación, Zastava USA le agregó algunas"
" partes fabricadas en Estados Unidos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid "AR-10"
msgid_plural "AR-10s"
msgstr[0] "AR-10"
msgstr[1] "AR-10s"
msgstr[2] "AR-10s"

#. ~ Description of gun "AR-10"
#: data/json/items/gun/308.json
msgid ""
"Somewhat similar to the later AR-15, the AR-10 is a gas-operated, rotating "
"bolt rifle chambered for 7.62x51mm rounds."
msgstr ""
"Similar al posterior AR-15, el AR-10 es un rifle rotativo de cerrojo "
"accionado por gas con calibre para balas 7.62x51mm."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid "M1 carbine"
msgid_plural "M1 carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina M1"
msgstr[1] "carabinas M1"
msgstr[2] "carabinas M1"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1 carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid ""
"A light rifle developed during the Second World War to provide a less "
"cumbersome weapon for soldiers that didn't need the firepower of the M1 "
"Garand.  Firing the .30 Carbine cartridge, it provides more firepower than a"
" pistol and is easier to carry than most other rifles."
msgstr ""
"Es un rifle ligero desarrollado durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial para que "
"los soldados tuvieran un arma menos incómoda cuando no necesitaban el poder "
"de fuego del M1 Garand. El cartucho Carabina .30 brinda más potencia que una"
" pistola y es más fácil de llevar que la mayoría de los demás rifles."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid "M2 carbine"
msgid_plural "M2 carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina M2"
msgstr[1] "carabinas M2"
msgstr[2] "carabinas M2"

#. ~ Description of gun "M2 carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/30carbine.json
msgid ""
"An improved version of the M1 carbine offering full-auto capability, the M2 "
"carbine was rare and coveted among collectors even before the world ended.  "
"Takes M1 carbine magazines."
msgstr ""
"Una versión mejorada de la carabina M1 que ofrece capacidad automática. La "
"carabina M2 fue rara y codiciada por los coleccionistas incluso antes de que"
" el mundo llegara a su fin. Utiliza los cartuchos de la carabina M1."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid "SIG Sauer P230"
msgid_plural "SIG Sauer P230"
msgstr[0] "SIG Sauer P230"
msgstr[1] "SIG Sauer P230"
msgstr[2] "SIG Sauer P230"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG Sauer P230"
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid ""
"The SIG Sauer P230 is a small, semi-automatic handgun chambered in .32 ACP."
"  Due to its small dimensions, it was often carried as a backup weapon."
msgstr ""
"La SIG Sauer P320 es una pistola pequeña semi-automática con calibre .32 "
"ACP. Debido a su pequeño tamaño, a menudo se la lleva como arma de apoyo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid "Škorpion vz. 61"
msgid_plural "Škorpion vz. 61s"
msgstr[0] "Škorpion vz. 61"
msgstr[1] "Škorpion vz. 61"
msgstr[2] "Škorpion vz. 61"

#. ~ Description of gun "Škorpion vz. 61"
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid ""
"The Škorpion vz. 61 is a Czechoslovak submachine gun from the 1950s, "
"chambered in .32 ACP."
msgstr ""
"La Skorpion Vz. 61 es un subfusil checoslovaco de los años 50, de calibre "
".32 ACP."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid "Walther PPK"
msgid_plural "Walther PPK"
msgstr[0] "Walther PPK"
msgstr[1] "Walther PPK"
msgstr[2] "Walther PPK"

#. ~ Description of gun "Walther PPK"
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid ""
"One of the most famous handguns of the 20th century.  Your name is not Bond,"
" but you might find this little gun still useful."
msgstr ""
"Es una de las pistolas más famosas del siglo XX. Tu nombre no es Bond, pero "
"igual vas a encontrarle utilidad a esta pequeña pistola."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid "Kel-Tec P-32"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec P-32s"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec P-32"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tecs P-32"
msgstr[2] "Kel-Tecs P-32"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kel-Tec P-32"
#: data/json/items/gun/32.json
msgid ""
"One of Kel-Tec's oldest designs, the P-32 is a popular option for deep "
"concealment and backup usage.  Despite its extreme light weight and small "
"size, its .32 ACP chambering makes for good handling and recoil control."
msgstr ""
"Uno de los diseños más antiguos de Kel-Tec, el P-32 es una opción popular "
"como arma oculta y uso de apoyo. A pesar de ser extremadamente ligera y "
"pequeña, tiene un calibre .32 ACP que hace fácil de manejar y controlar su "
"retroceso."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid "SIG P226"
msgid_plural "SIG P226s"
msgstr[0] "SIG P226"
msgstr[1] "SIG P226s"
msgstr[2] "SIG P226s"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG P226"
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid ""
"A SIG Sauer P226 chambered for .357 SIG.  The P226 is a DA/SA, short-recoil "
"operated semi-automatic pistol."
msgstr ""
"Es una SIG Sauer P226 calibre .357 SIG. La P226 es una DA/SA, una pistola "
"semiautomática con poco retroceso."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid "Glock 31"
msgid_plural "Glock 31s"
msgstr[0] "Glock 31"
msgstr[1] "Glock 31s"
msgstr[2] "Glock 31s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock 31"
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid ""
"A full size .357 SIG Glock pistol.  It is extremely similar to the Glock 22,"
" and could be converted to fire .40 S&W by switching the barrel."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola Glock .357 SIG de tamaño completo. Es extremadamente similar a "
"la Glock 22, y podría ser convertida en una pistola de .40 S&W cambiando el "
"cañón."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid "SIG P320 Compact"
msgid_plural "SIG P320 Compacts"
msgstr[0] "SIG P320 Compact"
msgstr[1] "SIG P320 Compacts"
msgstr[2] "SIG P320 Compacts"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG P320 Compact"
#: data/json/items/gun/357sig.json
msgid ""
"The P320 Compact is a semi-automatic, short recoil operated pistol.  This "
"one is chambered for .357 SIG."
msgstr ""
"La P320 Compact es una pistola semiautomática de retroceso corto. Esta tiene"
" recámara para .357 SIG."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/36paper.json
msgid "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgid_plural "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgstr[0] "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgstr[1] "Colt M1861 Navy"
msgstr[2] "Colt M1861 Navy"

#. ~ Description of gun "Colt M1861 Navy"
#: data/json/items/gun/36paper.json
msgid ""
"The Colt Model 1861 Navy cap & ball .36-caliber revolver was a six-shot, "
"single-action percussion weapon produced by Colt's Manufacturing Company "
"from 1861 until 1873."
msgstr ""
"El Colt Model 1861 Navy, revólver de llave de percusión, calibre .36, era un"
" arma de percusión de una sola acción, con seis disparos, producida por "
"Colt's Manufacturing Company desde 1861 hasta 1873."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "2 Shot Special"
msgid_plural "2 Shot Specials"
msgstr[0] "2 Tiros Especial"
msgstr[1] "2 Tiros Especial"
msgstr[2] "2 Tiros Especial"

#. ~ Description of gun "2 Shot Special"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A crudely made double barrel pistol firing .38 Special ammo.  Unfortunately,"
" the name is less about the double barrels and more about the number of "
"shots you'll get before it breaks down on you."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola de doble cañón hecha toscamente, que dispara munición .38 "
"Especial.  Lamentablemente, el nombre tiene poco que ver con el doble cañon,"
" pero más con el número de disparos que podrás hacer antes de que se rompa."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "COP .357 Derringer"
msgid_plural "COP .357 Derringers"
msgstr[0] "COP .357 Derringer"
msgstr[1] "COP .357 Derringers"
msgstr[2] "COP .357 Derringers"

#. ~ Description of gun "COP .357 Derringer"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A small, chubby derringer pistol bearing a slight resemblance to the "
"Mossberg Brownie.  It uses a rotating firing pin to fire the individual "
"hammers of the four barrels arranged in a square formation."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña y regordeta pistola Derringer con un ligero parecido a la "
"Brownie de Mossberg. Utiliza un percutor giratorio para disparar los "
"martillos individuales de los cuatro barriles dispuestos en una formación "
"cuadrada."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "S&W Model 10"
msgid_plural "S&W Model 10"
msgstr[0] "S&W Model 10"
msgstr[1] "S&W Model 10"
msgstr[2] "S&W Model 10"

#. ~ Description of gun "S&W Model 10"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A six-shot revolver, produced since 1899 and known as the most popular "
"handgun of the 20th century.  It has a swing-out cylinder for ease of "
"reloading."
msgstr ""
"Un revólver de seis disparos, producido desde 1899 y conocido como el arma "
"de mano más popular del siglo XX. Tiene un cilindro giratorio para facilitar"
" su recarga."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "Manurhin MR 73"
msgid_plural "Manurhin MR 73"
msgstr[0] "Manurhin MR 73"
msgstr[1] "Manurhin MR 73"
msgstr[2] "Manurhin MR 73"

#. ~ Description of gun "Manurhin MR 73"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A finely made .357 Magnum revolver with a 4 inch barrel.  It has adjustable "
"sights, big plastic grips and a very smooth trigger."
msgstr ""
"Un revolver .357 Magnum con un cañon de 10 centimetros de largo (4 pulgadas)"
" finamente hecho. Sus miras son ajustables, con empuñadura de plástico "
"grande y un gatillo muy suave."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "pipe rifle: .38 Special"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: .38 Special"
msgstr[0] "rifle de tubo: .38 Especial"
msgstr[1] "rifles de tubo: .38 Especial"
msgstr[2] "rifles de tubo: .38 Especial"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "Ruger LCR .38"
msgid_plural "Ruger LCR .38"
msgstr[0] "Ruger LCR .38"
msgstr[1] "Ruger LCR .38"
msgstr[2] "Ruger LCR .38"

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger LCR .38"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A compact, double-action-only revolver designed for easy concealment, with a"
" stainless steel cylinder and aluminum frame."
msgstr ""
"Un revólver compacto de doble acción, diseñado para ser fácil de ocultar, "
"con cilindro de acero inoxidable y estructura de aluminio."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid "S&W 619"
msgid_plural "S&W 619"
msgstr[0] "S&W 619"
msgstr[1] "S&W 619"
msgstr[2] "S&W 619"

#. ~ Description of gun "S&W 619"
#: data/json/items/gun/38.json
msgid ""
"A seven-round .38 revolver sold by Smith & Wesson.  It features a fixed rear"
" sight and a reinforced frame."
msgstr ""
"Un revólver de siete disparos calibre .38, vendida por Smith & Wesson. Posee"
" una mira trasera fija y una estructura reforzada."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "MAC-11"
msgid_plural "MAC-11s"
msgstr[0] "MAC-11"
msgstr[1] "MAC-11s"
msgstr[2] "MAC-11s"

#. ~ Description of gun "MAC-11"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"A lesser known variant of the MAC-10, this machine pistol is chambered in "
".380 ACP for a smaller overall size while remaining inherently subsonic.  "
"Smaller in almost every dimension, this inexpensive automatic weapon was "
"declared 'fit only for combat in a phone booth' due to its low weight and "
"absurd fire rate ranging from 1200 to 1400 rounds per minute."
msgstr ""
"Una variante menos conocida de la MAC-10, esta pistola de máquina está "
"alojada en una cámara de .380 ACP para un tamaño general más pequeño, "
"mientras que sigue siendo inherentemente subsónica. Más pequeña en casi "
"todas las dimensiones, esta arma automática barata fue declarada \"apta sólo"
" para el combate en una cabina telefónica\" debido a su bajo peso y a su "
"absurda velocidad de disparo que va de 1200 a 1400 disparos por minuto."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Kel-Tec P-3AT"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec P-3ATs"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec P-3AT"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tecs P-3AT"
msgstr[2] "Kel-Tecs P-3AT"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kel-Tec P-3AT"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"Essentially a slightly scaled up Kel-Tec P-32 in .380 ACP, the ever popular "
"P-3AT offers better ballistics in a small, concealable lightweight package."
"  Handling leaves something to be desired due to snappier recoil and "
"diminutive controls."
msgstr ""
"Esencialmente una Kel-tec P-32 ligeramente escalada en .380 ACP, la popular "
"P3AT ofrece una mejor balística en un paquete pequeño, ligero y ocultable. "
"El manejo deja algo que desear debido a un retroceso más rápido y a unos "
"controles más reducidos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "FN 1910 .380"
msgid_plural "FN 1910 .380s"
msgstr[0] "FN 1910 .380"
msgstr[1] "FN 1910 .380s"
msgstr[2] "FN 1910 .380s"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN 1910 .380"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"Made infamous in Sarajevo in 1914, the FN1910 was a popular pocket pistol, "
"albeit in .32 ACP.  Collectors value the .380 model for its notoriety and "
"more modern terminal performance.  If such a humble firearm could start a "
"world war, could it perhaps protect you from the undead?"
msgstr ""
"Hecha infame en Sarajevo en 1914, la FN1910 era una popular pistola de "
"bolsillo, aunque en .32 ACP. Los coleccionistas valoran el modelo .380 por "
"su notoriedad y su rendimiento terminal más moderno. Si un arma de fuego tan"
" humilde pudiera iniciar una guerra mundial, ¿podría quizás protegerte de "
"los no-muertos?"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Ruger LCP"
msgid_plural "Ruger LCPs"
msgstr[0] "Ruger LCP"
msgstr[1] "Ruger LCPs"
msgstr[2] "Ruger LCPs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger LCP"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"One of the best-selling modern day 'pocket pistols', the LCP is an "
"affordable, polymer framed pistol chambered in .380 ACP.  Despite the "
"round's relatively low power, the pistol's low weight and short sight radius"
" make for moderately poor handling."
msgstr ""
"Una de las \"pistolas de bolsillo\" más vendidas en la actualidad, la LCP es"
" una pistola de marco polimérico asequible, con una cámara de .380 ACP.  A "
"pesar de la potencia relativamente baja del cartucho, el bajo peso de la "
"pistola y su corto radio de visión hacen que sea una pistola de manejo "
"moderadamente pobre."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Hi-Point CF-380"
msgid_plural "Hi-Point CF-380s"
msgstr[0] "Hi-Point CF-380"
msgstr[1] "Hi-Point CF-380s"
msgstr[2] "Hi-Point CF-380s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Hi-Point CF-380"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"The Hi-Point CF-380 is a blowback operated semi-automatic pistol designed by"
" Hi-Point Firearms, which is known for making inexpensive firearms, and for "
"making said firearms bulky and uncomfortable.  Hi-Points have slides made "
"with a zinc pot-metal which is relatively fragile compared to steel slides."
msgstr ""
"La Hi-Point CF-380 es una pistola semiautomática operada por retroceso "
"diseñada por Hi-Point Firearms, conocida por fabricar armas de fuego baratas"
" y por hacer dichas armas voluminosas e incómodas. Las Hi-Point tienen "
"correderas hechas con una aleación de zinc que es relativamente frágil "
"comparada con las correderas de acero."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid "Taurus Spectrum"
msgid_plural "Taurus Spectrum"
msgstr[0] "Taurus Spectrum"
msgstr[1] "Taurus Spectrum"
msgstr[2] "Taurus Spectrum"

#. ~ Description of gun "Taurus Spectrum"
#: data/json/items/gun/380.json
msgid ""
"A .380 subcompact pistol.  Designed for concealed carry and built from high-"
"quality, durable materials."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola subcompacta del calibre 380. Diseñada para llevarla oculta y "
"construida con materiales de alta calidad y durabilidad."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/38super.json
msgid "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgid_plural "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgstr[0] "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgstr[1] "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
msgstr[2] "AF2011A1 .38 Super"

#. ~ Description of gun "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
#: data/json/items/gun/38super.json
msgid ""
"A double-barrel semi-automatic pistol of Italian origin, firing two bullets "
"per shot, a derivative of the M1911 pistol."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática de doble cañón de origen italiano, que dispara "
"dos balas por disparo, un derivado de la pistola M1911."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "AF2011A1 .38 Super"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "double-barrel pipe shotgun"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "double barrel shotgun"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "double slam-fire pipe shotgun"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "C.R.I.T .5 LP"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "elephant rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/38super.json data/json/items/gun/shot.json
#: data/mods/CRT_EXPANSION/items/crt_gun.json
#: data/mods/Generic_Guns/firearms/rifle_huge.json
msgid "double"
msgstr "doble"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#. ~ Variant name of gun "M1911A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/38super.json data/mods/classic_zombies/items/guns.json
msgid "M1911A1"
msgid_plural "M1911A1s"
msgstr[0] "M1911A1"
msgstr[1] "M1911A1s"
msgstr[2] "M1911A1s"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1911A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/38super.json
msgid ""
"The M1911A1 is an extremely popular pistol known for its reliability.  This "
"one is chambered for .38 Super."
msgstr ""
"La M1911A1 es una pistola extremadamente popular conocida por su fiabilidad."
" Esta tiene una cámara para el .38 Super."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "Beretta 90-two .40 S&W"
msgid_plural "Beretta 90-two .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[0] "Beretta 90-two .40 S&W"
msgstr[1] "Beretta 90-two .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[2] "Beretta 90-two .40 S&Ws"

#. ~ Description of gun "Beretta 90-two .40 S&W"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"A more modern version of Beretta's popular 92 series of handguns, the 90-two"
" performs largely the same.  The main difference is a sleeker, almost "
"futuristic-looking design owed in large part to the polymer underbarrel rail"
" cover.  This one is chambered in .40 S&W."
msgstr ""
"Una versión más moderna de la popular serie de pistolas 92 de Beretta, la "
"90-two tiene prácticamente el mismo rendimiento. La principal diferencia es "
"un diseño más elegante, casi futurista, debido en gran parte a la cubierta "
"de polímero bajo el cañón. Este modelo tiene la recámara en .40 S&W."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "Glock 22"
msgid_plural "Glock 22"
msgstr[0] "Glock 22"
msgstr[1] "Glock 22"
msgstr[2] "Glock 22"

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock 22"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"A .40 S&W variant of the popular Glock 17 pistol.  The standard-issue "
"firearm of the FBI and of countless other law enforcement agencies "
"worldwide."
msgstr ""
"Una variante .40 S&W de la popular pistola Glock 17. Es el arma de mano "
"estándar del FBI y de otras innumerables agencias en todo el mundo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "Beretta Px4 Storm .40 S&W"
msgid_plural "Beretta Px4 Storm .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[0] "Beretta Px4 Storm .40 S&W"
msgstr[1] "Beretta Px4 Storm .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[2] "Beretta Px4 Storm .40 S&Ws"

#. ~ Description of gun "Beretta Px4 Storm .40 S&W"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"Lighter than Beretta's iconic 92 series of guns, the Px4 Storm was built by "
"utilizing light-weight polymer construction with steel inserts.  Its shape "
"was also optimized for concealed carry.  This one is chambered in .40 S&W."
msgstr ""
"Más ligera que la icónica serie de pistolas 92 de Beretta, la Px4 Storm se "
"construyó utilizando una estructura de polímero ligero con inserciones de "
"acero. Su forma también fue optimizada para el porte oculto. Esta pistola "
"tiene recámara en .40 S&W."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "pipe rifle: .40 S&W"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: .40 S&W"
msgstr[0] "rifle de tubo: .40 S&W"
msgstr[1] "rifles de tubo: .40 S&W"
msgstr[2] "rifles de tubo: .40 S&W"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "SIG Pro .40"
msgid_plural "SIG Pro .40"
msgstr[0] "SIG Pro .40"
msgstr[1] "SIG Pro .40"
msgstr[2] "SIG Pro .40"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG Pro .40"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"Originally marketed as a lightweight and compact alternative to older SIG "
"handguns, the Pro .40 is popular among European police forces."
msgstr ""
"Originalmente pensada para el mercado de las compactas ligeras como "
"alternativa a las viejas pistolas SIG, la Pro .40 es popular entre las "
"fuerzas policiales europeas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "Luty SMG: .40 S&W"
msgid_plural "Luty SMGs: .40 S&W"
msgstr[0] "Luty SMG: .40 S&W"
msgstr[1] "Luty SMGs: .40 S&W"
msgstr[2] "Luty SMGs: .40 S&W"

#. ~ Description of gun "Luty SMG: .40 S&W"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"A Luty pattern makeshift smoothbore SMG crudely constructed out of various "
"steel parts using advanced powered hand tools; likely one of the most "
"complex guns that is feasible to make outside of a machine shop, but still "
"very unreliable.  This one is chambered for .40 S&W cartridges and accepts "
"custom-made makeshift magazines."
msgstr ""
"Un patrón de Luty hace que el SMG de cañón liso sea construido crudamente "
"con varias piezas de acero usando algunas de las herramientas manuales más "
"avanzadas; probablemente una de las armas más complejas que son factibles de"
" hacer fuera de un taller de máquinas, pero aún así muy poco fiable. Esta "
"tiene una cámara para cartuchos de .40 S&W y acepta cargadores improvisados "
"hechos a medida."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "handmade six-shooter"
msgid_plural "handmade six-shooters"
msgstr[0] "seis disparos hecho a mano"
msgstr[1] "seis disparos hechos a mano"
msgstr[2] "seis disparos hechos a mano"

#. ~ Description of gun "handmade six-shooter"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"A homemade 6-shot revolver.  While it's not as good as the pre-Cataclysm "
"manufactured weapons, it's a decent piece of work, all things considered."
msgstr ""
"Un revólver de 6 disparos hecho en casa. Aunque no es tan buena como las "
"armas fabricadas antes del Cataclismo, es una pieza decente considerando la "
"situación."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "Browning Hi-Power .40 S&W"
msgid_plural "Browning Hi-Power .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[0] "Browning Hi-Power .40 S&W"
msgstr[1] "Browning Hi-Power .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[2] "Browning Hi-Power .40 S&Ws"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning Hi-Power .40 S&W"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"The Browning Hi-Power is a semi-automatic handgun developed shortly before "
"the Second World War.  Widely issued since then, it remains in use by India,"
" Canada, and Australia.  This is a commercial variant produced by Browning "
"Arms in .40 S&W."
msgstr ""
"La Browning Hi-Power es un arma de mano semiautomática desarrollada poco "
"antes de la Segunda Guerra Mundial. Muy usada desde entonces, sigue en uso "
"en India, Canadá y Australia. Esta es la versión comercial producida por "
"Browning Arms con calibre .40 S&W."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "Walther PPQ .40 S&W"
msgid_plural "Walther PPQ .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[0] "Walther PPQ .40 S&W"
msgstr[1] "Walther PPQ .40 S&Ws"
msgstr[2] "Walther PPQ .40 S&Ws"

#. ~ Description of gun "Walther PPQ .40 S&W"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"The Walther PPQ is a semi-automatic pistol originating from the Walther "
"P99QA, and maintains compatibility with some of its predecessor's "
"accessories.  This model is chambered in .40 S&W."
msgstr ""
"La Walther PPQ es una pistola semiautomática originada en la Walther P99QA, "
"y mantiene la compatibilidad con algunos de los accesorios de su "
"predecesora. Este modelo está alojado en una cámara de .40 S&W."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid "Hi-Point Model JCP"
msgid_plural "Hi-Point Model JCPs"
msgstr[0] "Hi-Point Model JCP"
msgstr[1] "Hi-Point Model JCPs"
msgstr[2] "Hi-Point Model JCPs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Hi-Point Model JCP"
#: data/json/items/gun/40.json
msgid ""
"The Hi-Point Model JCP is a blowback operated semi-automatic pistol designed"
" by Hi-Point Firearms, which is known for making inexpensive firearms, and "
"for making said firearms bulky and uncomfortable.  Hi-Points have slides "
"made with a zinc pot-metal which is relatively fragile compared to steel "
"slides."
msgstr ""
"El modelo Hi-Point JCP es una pistola semiautomática operada por retroceso "
"diseñada por Hi-Point Firearms, que es conocida por hacer armas de fuego "
"baratas, y por hacer dichas armas de fuego voluminosas e incómodas. Las Hi-"
"Point tienen correderas hechas con correderas de zinc que es relativamente "
"frágil en comparación con las correderas de acero."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "tube 40mm launcher"
msgid_plural "tube 40mm launchers"
msgstr[0] "lanzador de tubo de 40mm"
msgstr[1] "lanzadores de tubo de 40mm"
msgstr[2] "lanzadores de tubo de 40mm"

#. ~ Description of gun "tube 40mm launcher"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid ""
"A simple, home-made grenade launcher.  Basically a tube with a pin firing "
"mechanism to activate the grenade."
msgstr ""
"Un lanzagranadas simple, hecho en casa. Básicamente, es un tubo con un "
"mecanismo para activar las granadas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "M320 standalone launcher"
msgid_plural "M320 standalone launchers"
msgstr[0] "lanzador independiente M320"
msgstr[1] "lanzadores independientes M320"
msgstr[2] "lanzadores independientes M320"

#. ~ Description of gun "M320 standalone launcher"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid ""
"Heckler & Koch's M320 grenade launcher offers the functionality of larger "
"launchers in a very small package at the cost of decreased accuracy.  This "
"one is combined with a buttstock for standalone operation."
msgstr ""
"El lanzagranadas M320 de Heckler & Koch ofrece la funcionalidad de los "
"lanzadores más grandes en un paquete muy pequeño a costa de una menor "
"precisión. Este se combina con un culatazo para operar de forma "
"independiente."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "M79 launcher"
msgid_plural "M79 launchers"
msgstr[0] "lanzador M79"
msgstr[1] "lanzadores M79"
msgstr[2] "lanzadores M79"

#. ~ Description of gun "M79 launcher"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid ""
"A widely-used grenade launcher that first saw use by American forces in the "
"Vietnam War.  Though mostly replaced by more modern launchers, the M79 still"
" sees use with many units worldwide."
msgstr ""
"Un lanzagranadas muy usado que fue utilizado por primera vez por las fuerzas"
" americanas en la guerra de Vietnam. Aunque fue reemplazado en su mayoría "
"por lanzadores más modernos, el M79 todavía se usa con muchas unidades en "
"todo el mundo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "Milkor MGL"
msgid_plural "Milkor MGL"
msgstr[0] "Milkor MGL"
msgstr[1] "Milkor MGL"
msgstr[2] "Milkor MGL"

#. ~ Description of gun "Milkor MGL"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid ""
"The Milkor Multi-Grenade Launcher is designed to compensate for the drawback"
" of single-shot grenade launchers by allowing sustained heavy firepower.  "
"However, it is still slow to reload and must be used with careful planning."
msgstr ""
"El Multi-Lanzagranadas Milkor está diseñado para compensar la desventaja de "
"los lanzagranadas de un solo disparo, permitiendo poder de fuego sostenido. "
"Sin embargo, sigue siendo lento para recargar y debe ser usado con una buena"
" planificación previa."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "RM802 grenade launcher"
msgid_plural "RM802 grenade launchers"
msgstr[0] "lanzagranadas RM802"
msgstr[1] "lanzagranadas RM802"
msgstr[2] "lanzagranadas RM802"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM802 grenade launcher"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid ""
"The Rivtech RM802 pump-action 40mm grenade launcher was designed to be a "
"step ahead of single-shot grenade launchers by allowing sustained heavy "
"firepower.  However, its capacity is fairly limited so it must be used with "
"careful planning."
msgstr ""
"El lanzagranadas de 40mm de acción de bombeo Rivtech RM802, fue diseñado "
"para ser un avance en los lanzagranadas de un solo disparo, permitiendo "
"poder de fuego sostenido. Sin embargo, su capacidad es bastante limitada así"
" que debe ser usado con una buena planificación previa."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "triple-barrel 40mm launcher"
msgid_plural "triple-barrel 40mm launchers"
msgstr[0] "lanzador 40mm de triple cañón"
msgstr[1] "lanzadores 40mm de triple cañón"
msgstr[2] "lanzadores 40mm de triple cañón"

#. ~ Description of gun "triple-barrel 40mm launcher"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid ""
"A homemade triple-barrel 40mm grenade launcher.  Capable of launching all "
"three grenades at once, it is extremely powerful for a homemade weapon."
msgstr ""
"Es un lanzador de granadas de 40mm con triple tubo, hecho en casa. Es capaz "
"de lanzar tres granadas a la vez, y es extremadamente poderosa para ser un "
"arma casera."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "triple-barrel 40mm launcher"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "multi"
msgstr "multi"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid "M203 array"
msgid_plural "M203 arrays"
msgstr[0] "conjunto de M203"
msgstr[1] "conjuntos de M203"
msgstr[2] "conjuntos de M203"

#. ~ Description of gun "M203 array"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x46mm.json
msgid ""
"An array of six M203 grenade launchers for use on the TALON UGV platform."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de seis lanzagranadas M203 para su uso en la plataforma del "
"TALON UGV."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/40x53mm.json
msgid "Mark 19 grenade launcher"
msgid_plural "Mark 19 grenade launchers"
msgstr[0] "lanzagranadas Mark 19"
msgstr[1] "lanzagranadas Mark 19"
msgstr[2] "lanzagranadas Mark 19"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mark 19 grenade launcher"
#: data/json/items/gun/40x53mm.json
msgid ""
"A heavy, tripod-mounted belt-fed grenade launcher used by the US Military "
"since the start of the Cold War all the way to the Cataclysm, and if you can"
" find some 40mm grenades, maybe even beyond."
msgstr ""
"Un pesado lanzagranadas de cinturón montado en un trípode usado por el "
"ejército de EE.UU. desde el comienzo de la Guerra Fría hasta el Cataclismo, "
"y si puedes encontrar algunas granadas de 40 mm, tal vez incluso más allá."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/410shot.json
msgid "Saiga-410"
msgid_plural "Saiga-410s"
msgstr[0] "Saiga-410"
msgstr[1] "Saiga-410s"
msgstr[2] "Saiga-410s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Saiga-410"
#: data/json/items/gun/410shot.json
msgid ""
"The Saiga-410 is a semi-automatic shotgun designed on the same Kalashnikov "
"pattern as the AK-47 rifle.  It reloads with a magazine, rather than one "
"shell at a time like most shotguns."
msgstr ""
"La Saiga-410 es una escopeta semiautomática diseñada con el mismo patrón "
"Kalashnikov de los rifles AK-47. Utiliza un cargador en lugar de tener que "
"poner cada cartucho uno a uno como en la mayoría de las escopetas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/410shot.json
msgid "Winchester M37 .410"
msgid_plural "Winchester M37 .410s"
msgstr[0] "Winchester M37 .410"
msgstr[1] "Winchester M37 .410s"
msgstr[2] "Winchester M37 .410s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Winchester M37 .410"
#: data/json/items/gun/410shot.json
msgid ""
"A single-shot break-action shotgun, chambered in .410 bore.  Designed as a "
"lower-recoil alternative to 12 gauge shotguns, it is light and easy to "
"manufacture."
msgstr ""
"Una escopeta de un solo tiro, con un calibre de .410. Diseñada como una "
"alternativa de bajo retroceso a las escopetas de calibre 12, es ligera y "
"fácil de fabricar."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid "Desert Eagle .44"
msgid_plural "Desert Eagle .44"
msgstr[0] "Desert Eagle .44"
msgstr[1] "Desert Eagle .44"
msgstr[2] "Desert Eagle .44"

#. ~ Description of gun "Desert Eagle .44"
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid ""
"One of the most recognizable handguns due to its popularity in movies and "
"video games, the Desert Eagle is better known for its menacing appearance "
"than its performance.  It's a large pistol, but its heavy weight reduces "
"recoil."
msgstr ""
"Una de las pistolas más reconocibles debido a su popularidad en el cine y "
"los videojuegos, la Desert Eagle es más conocida por su aspecto amenazante "
"en su ejecución. Es una pistola grande, pero su elevado peso reduce el "
"retroceso."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid "Henry Big Boy .44"
msgid_plural "Henry Big Boy .44"
msgstr[0] "Henry Big Boy .44"
msgstr[1] "Henry Big Boy .44"
msgstr[2] "Henry Big Boy .44"

#. ~ Description of gun "Henry Big Boy .44"
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid ""
"This fine lever-action rifle is chambered in the powerful .44 Magnum "
"cartridge and features a sleek octagonal barrel with a tube fed magazine.  "
"Go get 'em cowboy!"
msgstr ""
"Este excelente rifle de acción de palanca utiliza el poderoso calibre .44 "
"Magnum, y posee un elegante cañón octogonal con cargador de tubo. ¡A por "
"ellos vaquero!"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid "pipe rifle: .44 Magnum"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: .44 Magnum"
msgstr[0] "rifle de caño: .44 Magnum"
msgstr[1] "rifles de caño: .44 Magnum"
msgstr[2] "rifles de caño: .44 Magnum"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid "Ruger Redhawk"
msgid_plural "Ruger Redhawk"
msgstr[0] "Ruger Redhawk"
msgstr[1] "Ruger Redhawk"
msgstr[2] "Ruger Redhawk"

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger Redhawk"
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid ""
"One of the most powerful handguns in the world when it was released in 1979,"
" the Redhawk offers very sturdy construction, with an appearance that is "
"reminiscent of \"Wild West\" revolvers."
msgstr ""
"Una de las pistolas más poderosas del mundo cuando fue presentada en 1979. "
"La Redhawk ofrece una estructura muy resistente, con la apariencia de los "
"revólveres del Lejano Oeste."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid "S&W 629"
msgid_plural "S&W 629"
msgstr[0] "S&W 629"
msgstr[1] "S&W 629"
msgstr[2] "S&W 629"

#. ~ Description of gun "S&W 629"
#: data/json/items/gun/44.json
msgid ""
"A stainless steel, six-shot, double-action revolver with a matte black "
"plastic handle manufactured by Smith & Wesson.  Though hardly the most "
"powerful handgun in the world any more, it could still blow a zombie's head "
"clean off."
msgstr ""
"Un revolver de doble acción, de seis disparos, de acero inoxidable con mango"
" de plástico negro mate fabricado por Smith & Wesson. Aunque ya no sea la "
"pistola más poderosa del mundo, todavía puede volarle la cabeza a un zombi."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/44paper.json
msgid "Colt M1860 Army"
msgid_plural "Colt M1860 Army"
msgstr[0] "Colt M1860 Army"
msgstr[1] "Colt M1860 Army"
msgstr[2] "Colt M1860 Army"

#. ~ Description of gun "Colt M1860 Army"
#: data/json/items/gun/44paper.json
msgid ""
"The Colt Army Model 1860 is a cap & ball .44-caliber revolver.  It was used "
"during the American Civil War, and made by Colt's Manufacturing Company."
msgstr ""
"El Colt Model 1860 Army, revólver de llave de percusión, calibre .44. Fue "
"usada durante la Guerra de Secesión, y fue producida por Colt's "
"Manufacturing Company."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/44paper.json
msgid "LeMat revolver"
msgid_plural "LeMat revolvers"
msgstr[0] "revólver LeMat"
msgstr[1] "revólveres LeMat"
msgstr[2] "revólveres LeMat"

#. ~ Description of gun "LeMat revolver"
#: data/json/items/gun/44paper.json
msgid ""
"A Pietta reproduction of the Civil War era LeMat revolver, a rare and "
"unusual cap & ball .44-caliber revolver.  While its original non-standard "
".42 or .35 caliber curbed its usefulness for the CSA army, this reproduction"
" is offered in more prevalent .44 caliber.  Despite modern quality "
"materials, the design is still rather delicate."
msgstr ""
"Una reproducción Pietta del revólver LeMat de la era de la guerra civil, un "
"raro e inusual revólver de calibre 44. Mientras que su calibre original no "
"estándar de .42 o .35 disminuyó su utilidad para el ejército CSA, esta "
"reproducción se ofrece en el calibre .44 más común. A pesar de la calidad de"
" los materiales modernos, el diseño sigue siendo bastante delicado."

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "A submachine gun chambered in .45 ACP, accepting Glock magazines."
msgstr "Un subfusil con calibre .45 ACP que utiliza cargadores Glock."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Glock SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Vector SMG .45"
msgid_plural "Vector SMG .45s"
msgstr[0] "Vector SMG .45"
msgstr[1] "Vector SMG .45s"
msgstr[2] "Vector SMG .45s"

#. ~ Description of variant "Glock SMG" of gun "Vector SMG .45"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"The Vector SMG is a delayed blowback submachine gun with a unique, in-line "
"design that places both the shooter's hand and shoulder in line with the "
"bore axis, reducing muzzle climb during bursts.  This one is chambered in "
".45 ACP."
msgstr ""
"El Vector SMG es un subfusil de retroceso lento con un diseño único, en "
"línea, que coloca la mano y el hombro del tirador en línea con el eje del "
"cañón, reduciendo la subida de la boca durante las ráfagas. Esta arma tiene "
"la recámara en .45 ACP."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "UMP45 SMG"
msgid_plural "UMP45 SMGs"
msgstr[0] "SMG UMP45"
msgstr[1] "SMGs UMP45"
msgstr[2] "SMGs UMP45"

#. ~ Description of gun "UMP45 SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "A submachine gun chambered in .45 ACP and accepting UMP45 magazines."
msgstr "Un subfusil con calibre .45 ACP y que utiliza cargadores UMP45."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "UMP45 SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "H&K UMP45"
msgid_plural "H&K UMP45s"
msgstr[0] "H&K UMP45"
msgstr[1] "H&K UMP45"
msgstr[2] "H&K UMP45"

#. ~ Description of variant "UMP45 SMG" of gun "H&K UMP45"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"Developed as a successor to the MP5 submachine gun, the UMP45 retains the "
"earlier model's supreme accuracy and low recoil, but in the higher .45 "
"caliber."
msgstr ""
"Desarrollado como sucesor del subfusil MP5, el UMP45 conserva la precisión "
"suprema del modelo anterior y su bajo retroceso, pero en calibre .45."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "M1911 pistol"
msgid_plural "M1911 pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola M1911"
msgstr[1] "pistolas M1911"
msgstr[2] "pistolas M1911"

#. ~ Description of gun "M1911 pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic pistol chambered in .45 ACP and accepting M1911 magazines."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática con recámara de .45 ACP que acepta cargadores "
"M1911."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "M1911 pistol"
#. ~ Variant name of gun "M1911A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json data/mods/classic_zombies/items/guns.json
msgid "M1911"
msgid_plural "M1911s"
msgstr[0] "M1911"
msgstr[1] "M1911s"
msgstr[2] "M1911s"

#. ~ Description of variant "M1911 pistol" of gun "M1911"
#. ~ Description of variant "M1911A1" of gun "M1911"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json data/mods/classic_zombies/items/guns.json
msgid ""
"The M1911 was the US Military standard-issue sidearm for most of the 20th "
"Century.  It remains one of the most popular .45 pistols today."
msgstr ""
"La M1911 fue el arma de apoyo del Ejército de los Estados Unidos por la "
"mayor parte del siglo XX. Aún hoy, sigue siendo una de las más populares "
"pistolas calibre .45."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "M1911 pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "M45A1"
msgid_plural "M45A1s"
msgstr[0] "M45A1"
msgstr[1] "M45A1s"
msgstr[2] "M45A1s"

#. ~ Description of variant "M1911 pistol" of gun "M45A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"The M45A1 supplanted earlier M45 MEUSOC pistols in use by Force Recon "
"elements of Marine Expeditionary Units.  Where the original M45 pistols were"
" gutted M1911A1s hand-fitted by USMC armorers, the updated M45A1s are hardly"
" different from any other commercial 1911 design, save for their dual recoil"
" springs.  Most were replaced in 2016 with Glock 19s due to logistics "
"issues."
msgstr ""
"El M45A1 sustituyó a las anteriores pistolas M45 MEUSOC que usaban los "
"elementos de reconocimiento de la fuerza de las unidades expedicionarias de "
"los marines.  Mientras que las pistolas M45 originales fueron destripadas "
"por los blindados del USMC, las M45A1 actualizadas apenas difieren de "
"cualquier otro diseño comercial de 1911, excepto por sus muelles de doble "
"retroceso. La mayoría fueron reemplazadas en 2016 por Glock 19 debido a "
"problemas de logística."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "MAC-10 SMG"
msgid_plural "MAC-10 SMGs"
msgstr[0] "SMG MAC-10"
msgstr[1] "SMGs MAC-10"
msgstr[2] "SMGs MAC-10"

#. ~ Description of gun "MAC-10 SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "A submachine gun chambered in .45 ACP and accepting MAC-10 magazines."
msgstr "Un subfusil con calibre .45 ACP y que utiliza cargadores MAC-10."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "MAC-10 SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "MAC-10"
msgid_plural "MAC-10s"
msgstr[0] "MAC-10"
msgstr[1] "MAC-10"
msgstr[2] "MAC-10"

#. ~ Description of variant "MAC-10 SMG" of gun "MAC-10"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"The MAC-10 is a popular machine pistol originally designed for military use."
"  For many years it was the most inexpensive automatic weapon in the US, and"
" enjoyed great popularity among criminals less concerned with quality "
"firearms."
msgstr ""
"La MAC-10 es una pistola ametralladora popular, diseñada originalmente para "
"uso militar.  Por muchos años, fue el arma automática más barata de Estados "
"Unidos y disfrutó de gran popularidad entre los criminales que no les "
"importaba la calidad del arma."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "pipe rifle: .45"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: .45"
msgstr[0] "rifle de tubo: .45"
msgstr[1] "rifles de tubo: .45"
msgstr[2] "rifles de tubo: .45"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "H&K USC 45 Carbine"
msgid_plural "H&K USC 45 Carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina H&K USC 45"
msgstr[1] "carabinas H&K USC 45"
msgstr[2] "carabinas H&K USC 45"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K USC 45 Carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A compact, lightweight carbine chambering the popular .45 ACP pistol round."
"  Resembling the popular UMP submachine gun in both its blowback operating "
"system and lightweight polymer frame construction.  This civilian variant is"
" distinguished by its skeletonized stock and 16 inch barrel."
msgstr ""
"Una carabina compacta y liviana con la popular munición de pistola .45 ACP."
"  Similar al subfusil UMP tanto en su sistema de operación de retroceso "
"diferido y su construcción en polímero liviano.  La variante civil se "
"distingue por su culata esquelética y su cañón de 16 pulgadas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Luty SMG: .45"
msgid_plural "Luty SMGs: .45"
msgstr[0] "Luty SMG: .45"
msgstr[1] "Luty SMGs: .45"
msgstr[2] "Luty SMGs: .45"

#. ~ Description of gun "Luty SMG: .45"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A Luty pattern makeshift smoothbore SMG crudely constructed out of various "
"steel parts using advanced powered hand tools; likely one of the most "
"complex guns that is feasible to make outside of a machine shop, but still "
"very unreliable.  This one is chambered for .45 ACP cartridges and accepts "
"MAC-10 compatible magazines."
msgstr ""
"Un patrón de Luty hace que el subfusil de cañón liso sea construido "
"toscamente con varias piezas de acero usando algunas de las herramientas "
"manuales más avanzadas; probablemente una de las armas más complejas que son"
" factibles de hacer fuera de un taller de máquinas, pero aún así muy poco "
"fiable. Esta tiene una cámara para cartuchos de .45 ACP y acepta cargadores "
"compatibles con MAC-10."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "homemade hand cannon"
msgid_plural "homemade hand cannons"
msgstr[0] "cañón de mano casero"
msgstr[1] "cañones de mano caseros"
msgstr[2] "cañones de mano caseros"

#. ~ Description of gun "homemade hand cannon"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A large and heavy pistol evidently welded from scrap.  It's not pretty, but "
"the .45 it's chambered with packs a serious punch.  Just watch out for the "
"kick."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola grande y pesada, evidentemente fabricada con chatarra. No es "
"linda, pero el calibre .45 la hace ser muy potente. Pero ten cuidado con el "
"culatazo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Thompson SMG"
msgid_plural "Thompson SMGs"
msgstr[0] "SMG Thompson"
msgstr[1] "SMGs Thompson"
msgstr[2] "SMGs Thompson"

#. ~ Description of gun "Thompson SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A submachine gun chambered in .45 ACP and accepting Thompson magazines."
msgstr "Un subfusil con calibre .45 ACP y que utiliza cargadores Thompson."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Thompson SMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Thompson M1928A1"
msgid_plural "Thompson M1928A1s"
msgstr[0] "Thompson M1928A1"
msgstr[1] "Thompson M1928A1s"
msgstr[2] "Thompson M1928A1s"

#. ~ Description of variant "Thompson SMG" of gun "Thompson M1928A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"An American-made submachine gun developed during the very end of World War "
"I, too late to see action.  Infamous during the 1920s for its use by "
"gangsters, and used during World War II before being mostly replaced with "
"less-expensive alternatives."
msgstr ""
"Un subfusil de fabricación estadounidense desarrollado durante el final de "
"la Primera Guerra Mundial, un poco tarde para ver acción. Famoso durante la "
"década de 1920 como arma de los mafiosos, también fue utilizado en la "
"Segunda Guerra Mundial antes de ser reemplazado por alternativas más "
"económicas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "USP pistol"
msgid_plural "USP pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola USP"
msgstr[1] "pistolas USP"
msgstr[2] "pistolas USP"

#. ~ Description of gun "USP pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic pistol chambered in .45 ACP and accepting USP magazines."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática con recámara de .45 ACP que acepta cargadores "
"USP."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "USP pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "USP .45"
msgid_plural "USP .45s"
msgstr[0] "USP .45"
msgstr[1] "USP .45s"
msgstr[2] "USP .45s"

#. ~ Description of variant "USP pistol" of gun "USP .45"
#. ~ Description of gun "USP 9x19mm"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A popular pistol, widely used among law enforcement.  Extensively tested for"
" durability, it has been found to stay accurate even after being subjected "
"to extreme abuse."
msgstr ""
"Es una pistola popular, muy utilizada por las fuerzas de la ley. Su "
"durabilidad ha sido extensivamente probada, se sabe que puede mantener su "
"precisión incluso luego de sufir maltrato extremo."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "USP pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "MK 23 MOD 0"
msgid_plural "MK 23 MOD 0s"
msgstr[0] "MK 23 MOD 0"
msgstr[1] "MK 23 MOD 0s"
msgstr[2] "MK 23 MOD 0s"

#. ~ Description of variant "USP pistol" of gun "MK 23 MOD 0"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"Jokingly referred to as \"The World's Only Crew-Served Pistol\", this "
"massive pistol was designed as a primary weapon for select \"special "
"operators\".  Its cumbersome nature, the introduction of the derivative HK "
"USP series, and the logistics of getting .45 ACP ammunition in theater "
"doomed this behemoth to US SOCOM armories.  Like the USP, the MK 23 is a "
"remarkably reliable gun; someone could probably take out a nuclear-equipped "
"walking tank with this in their holster."
msgstr ""
"Conocida en broma como \"La única pistola para tripulantes del mundo\", esta"
" enorme pistola fue diseñada como arma principal para selectos \"operadores "
"especiales\".  Su naturaleza engorrosa, la introducción de la serie derivada"
" HK USP y la logística de conseguir munición de .45 ACP en el teatro de "
"operaciones condenó a este gigante a las armerías del US SOCOM.  Al igual "
"que la USP, el MK 23 es un arma notablemente fiable; alguien podría "
"probablemente sacar un tanque de paseo equipado con armas nucleares con esto"
" en su funda."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "PPQ pistol"
msgid_plural "PPQ pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola PPQ"
msgstr[1] "pistolas PPQ"
msgstr[2] "pistolas PPQ"

#. ~ Description of gun "PPQ pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic pistol chambered in .45 ACP and accepting PPQ magazines"
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática con recámara de .45 ACP que acepta cargadores "
"PPQ."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "PPQ pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Walther PPQ 45"
msgid_plural "Walther PPQ 45s"
msgstr[0] "Walther PPQ 45"
msgstr[1] "Walther PPQ 45s"
msgstr[2] "Walther PPQ 45s"

#. ~ Description of variant "PPQ pistol" of gun "Walther PPQ 45"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"The Walther PPQ is a semi-automatic pistol originating from the Walther "
"P99QA, and maintains compatibility with some of its predecessor's "
"accessories.  This model is chambered in .45 ACP."
msgstr ""
"The Walther PPQ is a semi-automatic pistol originating from the Walther "
"P99QA, and maintains compatibility with some of its predecessor's "
"accessories. This model is chambered in .45 ACP."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Hi-Point pistol"
msgid_plural "Hi-Point pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola Hi-Point"
msgstr[1] "pistolas Hi-Point"
msgstr[2] "pistolas Hi-Point"

#. ~ Description of gun "Hi-Point pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic pistol chambered in .45 ACP and accepting Hi-Point "
"magazines."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática con recámara de .45 ACP que acepta cargadores Hi-"
"Point."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Hi-Point pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Hi-Point Model JHP"
msgid_plural "Hi-Point Model JHPs"
msgstr[0] "Hi-Point Model JHP"
msgstr[1] "Hi-Point Model JHPs"
msgstr[2] "Hi-Point Model JHPs"

#. ~ Description of variant "Hi-Point pistol" of gun "Hi-Point Model JHP"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"The Hi-Point Model JHP is a blowback operated semi-automatic pistol designed"
" by Hi-Point Firearms, which is known for making inexpensive firearms, and "
"for making said firearms bulky and uncomfortable.  Hi-Points have slides "
"made with a zinc pot-metal which is relatively fragile compared to steel "
"slides."
msgstr ""
"El modelo Hi-Point JHP es una pistola semiautomática operada por retroceso "
"diseñada por Hi-Point Firearms, conocida por fabricar armas de fuego "
"baratas, y por hacer dichas armas de fuego voluminosas e incómodas. Hi-Point"
" tiene correderas hechas con una aleación de zinc que es relativamente "
"frágil en comparación con las correderas de acero."

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic pistol chambered in .45 ACP and accepting Glock magazines."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática con recámara de .45 ACP que acepta cargadores "
"Glock."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Glock pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid "Glock 21"
msgid_plural "Glock 21s"
msgstr[0] "Glock 21"
msgstr[1] "Glock 21s"
msgstr[2] "Glock 21s"

#. ~ Description of variant "Glock pistol" of gun "Glock 21"
#: data/json/items/gun/45.json
msgid ""
"A full-sized version of the highly successful Glock.  This model is "
"chambered in .45 ACP."
msgstr ""
"Una versión de tamaño completo de la exitosa Glock. Este modelo tiene la "
"recámara en .45 ACP."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/454.json
msgid "Taurus Raging Bull"
msgid_plural "Taurus Raging Bull"
msgstr[0] "Taurus Raging Bull"
msgstr[1] "Taurus Raging Bull"
msgstr[2] "Taurus Raging Bull"

#. ~ Description of gun "Taurus Raging Bull"
#: data/json/items/gun/454.json
msgid ""
"The Taurus Raging Bull is a 5-shot revolver chambered in .454 Casull.  It "
"has impressive stopping power."
msgstr ""
"El Taurus Raging Bull es un revólver de 5 disparos con calibre .454 Casull."
"  Tiene una potencia de parada impresionante."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/454.json
msgid "Taurus Raging Judge Magnum"
msgid_plural "Taurus Raging Judge Magnum"
msgstr[0] "Taurus Raging Judge Magnum"
msgstr[1] "Taurus Raging Judge Magnum"
msgstr[2] "Taurus Raging Judge Magnum"

#. ~ Description of gun "Taurus Raging Judge Magnum"
#: data/json/items/gun/454.json
msgid ""
"The Taurus Raging Judge Magnum is a 6-shot revolver chambered in .454 "
"Casull.  It can fire .410 shotshells and .45 Colt cartridges as well."
msgstr ""
"El Taurus Raging Judge Magnum es un revólver de 6 disparos con cámara en el "
".454 Casull. Puede disparar cartuchos de .410 y .45 Colt también."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/4570.json
msgid "Marlin 1895 SBL"
msgid_plural "Marlin 1895 SBLs"
msgstr[0] "Marlin 1895 SBL"
msgstr[1] "Marlin 1895 SBLs"
msgstr[2] "Marlin 1895 SBLs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Marlin 1895 SBL"
#: data/json/items/gun/4570.json
msgid ""
"A handy but powerful lever-action rifle chambered for .45-70 Government.  "
"Designed for wilderness guides for defense against large predators such as "
"grizzly bears, moose, and dinosaurs."
msgstr ""
"Un práctico pero poderoso rifle de acción de palanca con cámara para .45-70 "
"Government. Diseñado para los guías de la naturaleza para la defensa contra "
"grandes depredadores como osos pardos, alces y dinosaurios."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/4570.json
msgid "Magnum Research BFR"
msgid_plural "Magnum Research BFRs"
msgstr[0] "Magnum Research BFR"
msgstr[1] "Magnum Research BFRs"
msgstr[2] "Magnum Research BFRs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Magnum Research BFR"
#: data/json/items/gun/4570.json
msgid ""
"A massive single-action revolver.  While the .45-70 rifle round loses "
"significant velocity in its short pistol barrel, it still competes with "
"other large magnum handguns in terms of power."
msgstr ""
"Un revólver grande de una sola acción. Mientras que la bala de un rifle "
"45-70 pierde una velocidad significativa en su corto cañón de pistola, "
"todavía compite con otras grandes armas de mano magnum en términos de "
"potencia."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/4570.json
msgid "1874 Sharps"
msgid_plural "1874 Sharps"
msgstr[0] "1874 Sharp"
msgstr[1] "1874 Sharps"
msgstr[2] "1874 Sharps"

#. ~ Description of gun "1874 Sharps"
#: data/json/items/gun/4570.json
msgid ""
"A reproduction of an antique single-shot .45-70 rifle once used to hunt "
"buffalo and other large game in the late 19th Century.  Highly accurate and "
"powerful for the time, this one is made to handle modern smokeless "
"ammunition."
msgstr ""
"Una reproducción de un antiguo rifle de un solo tiro .45-70 usado una vez "
"para cazar búfalos y otros animales de caza mayor a finales del siglo XIX. "
"Altamente preciso y poderoso para la época, este está hecho para manejar "
"munición moderna sin humo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "Bond Arms Derringer"
msgid_plural "Bond Arms Derringers"
msgstr[0] "Bond Arms Derringers"
msgstr[1] "Bond Arms Derringers"
msgstr[2] "Bond Arms Derringers"

#. ~ Description of gun "Bond Arms Derringer"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid ""
"The Bond Arms Derringer is a series of multi-barrel compact pistols.  Most "
"commonly chambered for .45 Colt, with chambers long enough to accept .410 "
"shotgun shells."
msgstr ""
"El Bond Arms Derringer es una serie de pistolas compactas de varios cañones."
" Comúnmente con cámara para un Colt .45, con cámaras lo suficientemente "
"largas para aceptar cartuchos de escopeta .410."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "Colt Lightning .45 Carbine"
msgid_plural "Colt Lightning .45 Carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina Colt Lightning .45"
msgstr[1] "carabinas Colt Lightning .45"
msgstr[2] "carabinas Colt Lightning .45"

#. ~ Description of gun "Colt Lightning .45 Carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid ""
"A modern reproduction of a Colt pump-action rifle.  Originally chambered in "
".44-40, modern versions most commonly use .45 Colt, complementing the Single"
" Action Army as a Cowboy Action Shooting firearm."
msgstr ""
"Una reproducción moderna de un rifle de acción de bombeo Colt. Originalmente"
" con cámara en .44-40, las versiones modernas usan más comúnmente un Colt "
".45, complementando al Colt Single Action Army como un arma de fuego de "
"competición vaquera."

#. ~ Reload noise of gun "Colt Lightning .45 Carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "chik chik."
msgstr "pollito pollito."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid "Uberti Cattleman"
msgid_plural "Uberti Cattlemans"
msgstr[0] "Uberti Cattleman"
msgstr[1] "Uberti Cattleman"
msgstr[2] "Uberti Cattleman"

#. ~ Description of gun "Uberti Cattleman"
#: data/json/items/gun/45colt.json
msgid ""
"This 7.5\" barreled Uberti Cattleman is a modern reproduction of the "
"legendary Colt Single Action Army, or Colt Peacemaker, one of the first "
"revolvers to use a modern self-contained cartridge.  Made famous by "
"Westerns, it is still in demand for Cowboy Action Shooting, reenactors, and "
"collectors.  Unlike modern revolvers, the cylinder cannot swing out for "
"loading, and spent brass must be ejected one at a time."
msgstr ""
"Este Uberti Cattleman con cañón de 7.5\" es una reproducción moderna del "
"legendario Colt Single Action Army o Colt Peacemaker, uno de los primeros "
"revólveres en usar un cartucho moderno incorporado. Hecho famoso por los "
"westerns, todavía hoy es demandado en la disciplina Cowboy Action Shooting, "
"las representaciones y los coleccionistas. A diferencia de los revólveres "
"modernos, el cilindro no sale para cargarlo y los casquillos deben ser "
"extraídos uno a uno."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/46.json
msgid "H&K MP7A2"
msgid_plural "H&K MP7A2s"
msgstr[0] "H&K MP7A2"
msgstr[1] "H&K MP7A2s"
msgstr[2] "H&K MP7A2s"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K MP7A2"
#: data/json/items/gun/46.json
msgid ""
"Designed as a personal defense weapon, the MP7 fires the high-powered "
"4.6x30mm round while being lightweight, compact in size, and practically "
"recoil-free."
msgstr ""
"Diseñada como un arma de defensa personal, el MP7 dispara la poderosa "
"munición calibre 4.6x30mm, es liviano, pequeño y prácticamente no posee "
"retroceso."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/460.json
msgid "1911-460"
msgid_plural "1911-460s"
msgstr[0] "1911-460"
msgstr[1] "1911-460s"
msgstr[2] "1911-460s"

#. ~ Description of gun "1911-460"
#: data/json/items/gun/460.json
msgid ""
"This 1911 has been customized to chamber powerful .460 Rowland ammunition.  "
"It now sports a large, integral compensator to aid in taming recoil and "
"reducing slide velocity.  Notably, normal .45 ACP can also be fired through "
"the weapon."
msgstr ""
"Esta 1911 ha sido modificada a medida para usar el potente calibre .460 "
"Rowland. Ahora tiene un gran compensador integrado para ayudar a controlar "
"el retroceso y reducir la velocidad de la corredera. Notablemente, con este "
"arma también se puede disparar munición .45 ACP."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid "Barrett M107A1"
msgid_plural "Barrett M107A1"
msgstr[0] "Barrett M107A1"
msgstr[1] "Barrett M107A1"
msgstr[2] "Barrett M107A1"

#. ~ Description of gun "Barrett M107A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid ""
"A large, shoulder-fired, .50 caliber anti-materiel rifle.  Its large size, "
"recoil, and noise is offset by its damage and range."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle antimaterial grande y portátil, con calibre .50. Su gran tamaño, "
"retroceso y ruido son las desventajas de su gran daño y alcance."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid "M2HB Browning HMG"
msgid_plural "M2HB Browning HMG"
msgstr[0] "M2HB Browning HMG"
msgstr[1] "M2HB Browning HMG"
msgstr[2] "M2HB Browning HMG"

#. ~ Description of gun "M2HB Browning HMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid ""
"A heavy machine gun used by the US Military from its inception to the "
"Cataclysm, and even rarely by Cataclysm survivors.  Its massive size and "
"design make it impossible to use unless deployed or mounted to a vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Una ametralladora pesada usada por el ejército de los EE.UU. desde su inicio"
" hasta el cataclismo, e incluso raramente por los supervivientes del "
"cataclismo. Su enorme tamaño y diseño la hacen imposible de usar a menos que"
" sea desplegada o montada en un vehículo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid ".50 caliber rifle"
msgid_plural ".50 caliber rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle calibre .50"
msgstr[1] "rifles calibre .50"
msgstr[2] "rifles calibre .50"

#. ~ Description of gun ".50 caliber rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid ""
"Modified from the massive M2 Browning, this pared-down rifle has been "
"altered to be fired unmounted.  The burst fire has been disabled, and its "
"belt-fed mechanism has been modified into a much smaller single round "
"chamber."
msgstr ""
"Modificación del enorme M2 Browning, un rifle reducido al mínimo y alterado "
"para ser disparado sin montar. El disparo en ráfaga ha sido desactivado, y "
"el mecanismo de alimentación con cinta fue modificado para tener una cámara"
"  mucho mas pequeña de una sola munición."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun ".50 caliber rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid "manual"
msgstr "manual"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid "AI AS50"
msgid_plural "AI AS50s"
msgstr[0] "AI AS50"
msgstr[1] "AI AS50"
msgstr[2] "AI AS50"

#. ~ Description of gun "AI AS50"
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid ""
"Developed by the British firearms producer Accuracy International, the AI "
"AS50 is a semi-automatic .50 caliber anti-materiel rifle produced for the "
"British armed forces and the United States Navy SEALs.  With a free-floated "
"barrel, titanium frame, and an accessory rail integrated into the weapon’s "
"machined-steel receiver with two others mounted on each side of the barrel "
"shroud, the rifle features commendable ergonomics and a notable level of "
"modularity.  Providing operators with the capability to engage targets at a "
"maximum estimated range of around 1500 meters, the firearm feeds from "
"detachable 10-round box magazines."
msgstr ""
"Desarrollado por el fabricante de armas británicas Accuracy International, "
"el AI AS50 es un rifle semiautomático calibre .50 antitanque producido para "
"las fuerzas armadas británicas y para los SEAL de la Armada de Estados "
"Unidos. El rifle tiene una ergonomía admirable y un nivel notable de "
"modularidad, con un cañón flotante, armazón de titanio, una ranura para "
"accesorios integrada en el receptor de acero mecanizado y dos más montadas a"
" los costados del cañón. Le brinda al usuario la capacidad de atacar "
"objetivos a una distancia máxima estimada de 1500 metros. Se alimenta con "
"cargadores de caja extraíbles de 10 balas."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid "McMillan TAC-50"
msgid_plural "McMillan TAC-50s"
msgstr[0] "McMillan TAC-50"
msgstr[1] "McMillan TAC-50s"
msgstr[2] "McMillan TAC-50s"

#. ~ Description of gun "McMillan TAC-50"
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid ""
"A long-range anti-materiel and anti-personnel sniper rifle made by McMillan "
"Firearms, serving the Canadian Army since 2000 as the C15, and the Navy "
"Seals as the Mk 15 Mod 0.  This .50 caliber bolt-action rifle is capable of "
"defeating light vehicles, radar installations and crew-served weapons at "
"extreme distances.  It notably holds the longest-range confirmed sniper "
"kill, as well as the 4th and 5th longest."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de francotirador de largo alcance anti-material y anti-personal "
"fabricado por McMillan Firearms, que sirve al ejército canadiense desde 2000"
" como el C15, y a los Navy Seals como el Mk 15 Mod 0. Este rifle de cerrojo "
"de calibre .50 es capaz de derrotar a vehículos ligeros, instalaciones de "
"radar y armas de servicio de la tripulación a distancias extremas. Es "
"notablemente el francotirador de mayor alcance confirmado, así como el 4º y "
"5º más largo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid "Serbu BFG-50"
msgid_plural "Serbu BFG-50s"
msgstr[0] "Serbu BFG-50"
msgstr[1] "Serbu BFG-50s"
msgstr[2] "Serbu BFG-50s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Serbu BFG-50"
#: data/json/items/gun/50.json
msgid ""
"A single-shot, bolt-action rifle made by Serbu Firearms, the BFG-50 is a "
"very affordable firearm for those wishing to shoot .50 BMG."
msgstr ""
"El BFG-50 es un rifle de un solo tiro y acción de perno hecho por Serbu "
"Firearms, es un arma de fuego muy asequible para aquellos que desean "
"disparar .50 BMG."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid ".500 Magnum lever gun"
msgid_plural ".500 Magnum lever guns"
msgstr[0] "arma de palanca .500 Magnum"
msgstr[1] "armas de palanca .500 Magnum"
msgstr[2] "armas de palanca .500 Magnum"

#. ~ Description of gun ".500 Magnum lever gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid ""
"A finely put together rifle, constructed in the image of old west lever-"
"guns, this weapon features an impressive chambering of .500 Magnum.  Less "
"unmanageable and impractical than within a handgun platform, the power "
"potential of the huge round is nevertheless preserved within this rifle "
"sized package.  Capable of taking down most forms of game, including deer, "
"boars, and small dinosaurs, this is a respectable weapon for only the most "
"enthusiastic of large-calibre shooters."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle muy bien construido, a la imagen y semejanza de los rifles de "
"palanca del viejo oeste, con una impresionante recamara con calibre .500 "
"Magnum. Aunque menos manejable e impráctico que en una torreta, el potencial"
" de esta enorme munición esta preservado en este conjunto de tamaño rifle. "
"Capaz de tumbar todo tipo de piezas, incluyendo ciervos, jabalís y pequeños "
"dinosaurios, esta es una respetable arma solo para los mas entusiastas de "
"los grandes calibres."

#. ~ Variant name of gun ".500 Magnum lever gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid "Big Horn Model 89"
msgid_plural "Big Horn Model 89"
msgstr[0] "Big Horn Model 89"
msgstr[1] "Big Horn Model 89"
msgstr[2] "Big Horn Model 89"

#. ~ Description of variant ".500 Magnum lever gun" of gun "Big Horn Model 89"
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid ""
"Built in the image of the venerable Winchester Model 1886, Big Horn Armory's"
" Model 89 rifle packs all the power of the .500 S&W Magnum cartridge into a "
"package less likely to break one's wrist."
msgstr ""
"Construido a imagen del venerable Winchester Modelo 1886, el rifle Big Horn "
"Modelo 89 de Armory tiene toda la potencia del cartucho .500 S&W Magnum en "
"un arma que es menos propensa a romperte la muñeca."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid ".500 Magnum revolver"
msgid_plural ".500 Magnum revolvers"
msgstr[0] "revolver .500 Magnum"
msgstr[1] "revolveres .500 Magnum"
msgstr[2] "revolveres .500 Magnum"

#. ~ Description of gun ".500 Magnum revolver"
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid ""
"The definition of ‘overkill,’ this behemoth handgun puts large .44 calibre "
"revolvers to shame with its sheer size, power, and immense chambering.  "
"Firing the appropriately named .500 Magnum cartridge, the most powerful "
"handgun round in the world, the weapon has seen work in both sport shooting "
"and hunting roles.  A pistol for those of the ‘bigger is better’ mentality, "
"a high recoil junky’s personal dream, and an all-around useless military "
"sidearm, should the urge to assault the Cataclysm in fine style grip you, "
"this giant provides you with 5 rounds with which to reduce a zombie into an "
"afterthought."
msgstr ""
"La definición de 'abrumador', este engendro de arma deja en ridículo a los "
"revólveres de calibre .44 con su inmensa potencia y recámara. Haciendo uso "
"cartuchos del calibre .500 Magnum, el mas poderoso del mundo, este arma ha "
"sido usada tanto en deportes de tiro como en roles de caza. Una pistola para"
" aquellos que piensan que 'mas grande es mejor', para los adictos a enormes "
"retrocesos, e inútil como arma militar secundaria, si sientes la urgencia de"
" asaltar el Cataclismo con elegancia, este gigante te proporcionara 5 "
"cartuchos de munición con los que convertir a un zombi en un pensamiento."

#. ~ Variant name of gun ".500 Magnum revolver"
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid "S&W 500"
msgid_plural "S&W 500"
msgstr[0] "S&W 500"
msgstr[1] "S&W 500"
msgstr[2] "S&W 500"

#. ~ Description of variant ".500 Magnum revolver" of gun "S&W 500"
#: data/json/items/gun/500.json
msgid ""
"The 5-shot Smith and Wesson 500 revolver fires the comparably-named .500 S&W"
" Magnum.  It's an impressive weapon."
msgstr ""
"El revólver de cinco disparos Smith & Wesson 500 usa la bala .500 S&W "
"Magnum. Es un arma impresionante."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
msgid "AK-74M"
msgid_plural "AK-74Ms"
msgstr[0] "AK-74M"
msgstr[1] "AK-74M"
msgstr[2] "AK-74M"

#. ~ Description of gun "AK-74M"
#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
msgid ""
"The successor to the well-known AK-47 rifle.  It combines the reliability of"
" the AK series with the high-velocity, lightweight 5.45x39mm cartridge."
msgstr ""
"El sucesor del conocido rifle AK-47.  Combina la fiabilidad de la serie de "
"AK con el cartucho de alta velocidad ligero de 5.45x39mm."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
msgid "Kord 6P67"
msgid_plural "Kord 6P67s"
msgstr[0] "Kord 6P67"
msgstr[1] "Kord 6P67s"
msgstr[2] "Kord 6P67s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kord 6P67"
#: data/json/items/gun/545x39.json
msgid ""
"A special forces Russian rifle chambered in 5.45.  This version uses "
"standard Picatinny rails, has modern lightweight furniture and a unique "
"complex recoil balance system for high fire rate with minimal recoil.  It "
"combines the reliability of the AK series with the high-velocity, "
"lightweight 5.45x39mm cartridge and accepts standard AK-74M magazines."
msgstr ""
"Rifle ruso de las fuerzas especiales con recámara 5.45. Esta versión utiliza"
" raíles Picatinny estándar, cuenta con un moderno y ligero diseño así como "
"un exclusivo y complejo sistema de balance de retroceso para conseguir una "
"alta cadencia de fuego con un retroceso mínimo. Combina la fiabilidad de la "
"serie AK con el cartucho 5.45x39mm de alta velocidad y peso ligero y acepta "
"cargadores estándar AK-74M."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "FN Five-seveN"
msgid_plural "FN Five-seveNs"
msgstr[0] "FN Five-seveN"
msgstr[1] "FN Five-seveNs"
msgstr[2] "FN Five-seveNs"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN Five-seveN"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"Designed to work with FN's proprietary 5.7x28mm round, the Five-seveN is a "
"lightweight pistol with a very high capacity, best used against armored "
"opponents."
msgstr ""
"Diseñada para trabajar con la bala 5.7x28mm de FN, la Five-seveN es una "
"pistola ligera con muy buena capacidad, y buen desempeño contra oponentes "
"con armadura."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "FN 5.7x28mm PDW"
msgid_plural "FN 5.7x28mm PDWs"
msgstr[0] "FN 5.7x28mm PDW"
msgstr[1] "FN 5.7x28mm PDW"
msgstr[2] "FN 5.7x28mm PDW"

#. ~ Description of gun "FN 5.7x28mm PDW"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"An FN manufactured personal defence weapon, this automatic firearm is "
"chambered for the high-velocity proprietary 5.7x28mm cartridge.  Accepting "
"top-mounted 50-round custom magazines which are fitted to the receiver of "
"the weapon behind the grip, thus making it a bullpup design, this little "
"submachine gun packs quite the nasty payload.  Its comparatively small, "
"high-speed caliber makes it excellent at both defeating armoured opponents "
"and firing short bursts manageably."
msgstr ""
"Esta arma de defensa personal, fabricada por FN, está preparada para "
"munición de alta velocidad de 5,7x28 mm. Este pequeño subfusil, acepta "
"cargadores personalizados de 50 balas montados en la parte superior de la "
"carcasa del arma, detrás de la empuñadura, lo que lo convierte en un diseño "
"bullpup. Su calibre relativamente pequeño y de alta velocidad hace que sea "
"excelente tanto para derrotar a oponentes blindados como para disparar "
"ráfagas cortas de forma manejable."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "FN 5.7x28mm PDW"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "FN P90"
msgid_plural "FN P90s"
msgstr[0] "FN P90"
msgstr[1] "FN P90"
msgstr[2] "FN P90"

#. ~ Description of variant "FN 5.7x28mm PDW" of gun "FN P90"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"The first in a new genre of guns, termed \"personal defence weapons.\"  FN "
"designed the P90 to use their proprietary high-velocity 5.7x28mm ammunition."
"  Made to fulfill NATO requests for a weapon chambered in a more suitable "
"cartridge for potentially defeating body armour than their standard 9mm "
"submachine guns, the FN P90 is excellent at firing short and controllable "
"bursts manageably.  The PDW’s comparatively small-diameter, high-speed 5.7mm"
" ammunition, of which 50 rounds comfortably fit in the P90’s top mounted "
"magazine, packs quite the lethal payload for any armoured opponent, whilst "
"the firearm’s bullpup design makes it commendably compact to boot."
msgstr ""
"La primera de un nuevo género de armas, denominadas \"armas de defensa "
"personal\". FN diseñó la P90 para utilizar su propia munición de alta "
"velocidad de 5,7x28 mm. Fabricada para satisfacer las peticiones de la OTAN "
"de un arma con un cartucho más adecuado para destruir el blindaje corporal "
"en lugar de sus subfusiles estándar de 9 mm, la FN P90 es excelente para "
"disparar ráfagas cortas y controlables de forma manejable. La munición de "
"alta velocidad de 5,7 mm de diámetro comparativamente pequeño del PDW, "
"cabiendo cómodamente 50 cartuchos en el cargador superior del P90, supone "
"una carga letal para cualquier adversario blindado, mientras que el diseño "
"del arma en forma de bullpup le confiere un tamaño compacto encomiable."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm pistol"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm"
msgstr[1] "pistolas Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm"
msgstr[2] "pistolas Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"A large retro-looking semi-automatic pistol chambered for the high-velocity "
"5.7x28mm cartridge, mainly constructed out of polymer-based materials.  "
"Making use of standard 5.7x28mm 50-round box magazines which are inserted "
"horizontally over the grip, the top of the gun swings forwards and away from"
" the frame to facilitate reloading.  If you were looking to add a touch of "
"retro-futuristic spice to your new life in the ruins of New England, this "
"firearm just might become your best friend."
msgstr ""
"Una voluminosa pistola semiautomática de aspecto retro con recámara para el "
"cartucho de alta velocidad de 5,7x28 mm, construida principalmente con "
"materiales de polímero. Utiliza cargadores estándar de 5,7x28 mm de 50 "
"rondas que se insertan horizontalmente sobre la empuñadura, y la parte "
"superior del arma se inclina hacia delante y se separa del armazón para "
"facilitar la recarga. Si busca añadir un toque de sabor retrofuturista a su "
"nueva vida en las ruinas de Nueva Inglaterra, esta arma de fuego podría "
"convertirse en su mejor amiga."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "Kel-Tec P50"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec P50s"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec P50"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tec P50s"
msgstr[2] "Kel-Tec P50s"

#. ~ Description of variant "Kel-Tec 5.7x28mm pistol" of gun "Kel-Tec P50"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"Unique, adaptable, and extremely retro, the Kel-Tec P50 is a truly bizarre "
"semi-automatic pistol.  Having been regarded as possibly one of the most "
"innovative firearms from Kel-Tec’s entire line-up of guns, the P50 makes use"
" of the high velocity 5.7x28mm cartridge, and feeds from standard FN P90 "
"magazines.  Boasting ambidextrous controls, an AR-15-like T-shaped charging "
"handle, and a reload which involves swinging the receiver and barrel "
"assemblies up and away from the frame to insert the magazine horizontally "
"over the grip, this weapon lends a decidedly retro-futuristic touch to "
"almost any situation."
msgstr ""
"Única, adaptable y extremadamente retro, la Kel-Tec P50 es una pistola "
"semiautomática realmente extraña. Considerada posiblemente una de las armas "
"más innovadoras de toda la gama de Kel-Tec, la P50 utiliza el cartucho de "
"alta velocidad 5,7x28 mm y se alimenta de cargadores FN P90 estándar. Con "
"controles ambidiestros, una empuñadura de carga en forma de T similar a la "
"de un AR-15, y una recarga que consiste en girar los conjuntos de carcasa y "
"cañón hacia arriba y fuera del armazón para insertar el cargador "
"horizontalmente sobre la empuñadura, esta arma aporta un toque decididamente"
" retrofuturista a casi cualquier situación."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "Ruger-57"
msgid_plural "Ruger-57s"
msgstr[0] "Ruger-57"
msgstr[1] "Ruger-57s"
msgstr[2] "Ruger-57s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Ruger-57"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"A full-sized polymer framed handgun chambered in the unusual 5.7x28mm "
"cartridge, the Ruger-57 was one of the first commercially available 5.7mm "
"pistols on the market, with its main competitor being FN’s decades-old, and "
"far pricier, Five-seveN pistol.  Featuring a lightweight ergonomic design, "
"1911-style thumb-safety, a high visibility green front-sight with adjustable"
" black rear iron-sights, and a price point which hovered a good 500 dollars "
"below its competition, the Ruger-57 made the comparatively niche 5.7x28mm "
"round far more accessible to a wider margin of potential shooters."
msgstr ""
"La Ruger-57, una pistola de polímero de tamaño completo con recámara para el"
" inusual cartucho de 5,7x28 mm, fue una de las primeras pistolas de 5,7 mm "
"disponibles en el mercado, siendo su principal competidora la pistola Five-"
"seveN de FN, que tenía décadas de antigüedad y era mucho más cara.  Con un "
"diseño ergonómico y ligero, un seguro para el pulgar tipo 1911, una mira "
"delantera verde de alta visibilidad con miras de hierro negras ajustables y "
"un precio que se situaba  en unos 500 dólares por debajo de su competencia, "
"la Ruger-57 hizo que la munición de 5,7x28 mm, comparativamente muy "
"especializada, fuera mucho más accesible para un mayor número de tiradores "
"potenciales."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "civilian FN 5.7x28mm carbine"
msgid_plural "civilian FN 5.7x28mm carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina civil FN 5.7x28mm"
msgstr[1] "carabinas civiles FN 5.7x28mm"
msgstr[2] "carabinas civiles FN 5.7x28mm"

#. ~ Description of gun "civilian FN 5.7x28mm carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"The civilian version of FN’s older 5.7x28mm PDW, this carbine features a 16 "
"inch long barrel, feeds from the same 50-round magazines as its predecessor,"
" and is only capable of semi-automatic fire in order to keep it in line with"
" American firearm restrictions."
msgstr ""
"La versión civil de la antigua PDW de 5,7x28 mm de FN, esta carabina cuenta "
"con un cañón de 16 pulgadas de largo, se alimenta de los mismos cargadores "
"de 50 balas que su predecesora, y sólo es capaz de disparar de forma "
"semiautomática con el fin de mantenerla en línea con las restricciones de "
"armas de fuego estadounidenses."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "civilian FN 5.7x28mm carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid "FN PS90"
msgid_plural "FN PS90s"
msgstr[0] "FN PS90"
msgstr[1] "FN PS90s"
msgstr[2] "FN PS90s"

#. ~ Description of variant "civilian FN 5.7x28mm carbine" of gun "FN PS90"
#: data/json/items/gun/57.json
msgid ""
"Originally introduced in 2005, the PS90 is the civilian clone of the "
"venerable FN P90, sharing much of the same characteristics and features as "
"its fully-automatic older brother.  Chambering the same 5.7x28mm cartridge "
"as its predecessor, in order to make it a legally distributable carbine in "
"the eyes of the law the PS90 was manufactured to only be capable of semi-"
"automatic fire, with a fitted-on 16-inch long barrel to sidestep NFA "
"regulations on short-barreled rifles."
msgstr ""
"Presentada originalmente en 2005, la PS90 es el copia civil de la venerable "
"FN P90, y comparte muchas de las características y prestaciones de su "
"hermano mayor totalmente automático. Con el mismo cartucho de 5,7x28mm que "
"su predecesora, para que fuera una carabina legalmente distribuible a los "
"ojos de la ley, la PS90 se fabricó para que sólo fuera capaz de disparar en "
"modo semiautomático, con un cañón de 16 pulgadas de largo para eludir las "
"regulaciones de la NFA sobre rifles de cañón corto."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/5x50.json
msgid "RM216 SPIW"
msgid_plural "RM216 SPIWs"
msgstr[0] "RM216 SPIW"
msgstr[1] "RM216 SPIW"
msgstr[2] "RM216 SPIW"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM216 SPIW"
#: data/json/items/gun/5x50.json
msgid ""
"This light carbine fires 5x50mm armor-piercing flechette cartridges.  "
"Classified as a special purpose individual weapon, this advanced firearm was"
" developed by Rivtech for the US military shortly before the end of the "
"world.  Designed to be fired in bursts, it excels in close combat."
msgstr ""
"Esta carabina ligera dispara cartuchos 5x50mm de dardos perforantes de "
"blindaje. Clasificada como arma individual de propósito especial, esta arma "
"de fuego avanzada fue desarrollada por Rivtech para el Ejército de Estados "
"Unidos poco antes de que el mundo se terminara. Diseñada para disparar en "
"ráfaga, es excelente en el combate cercano."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "RM216 SPIW"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "CMES laser cannon"
#: data/json/items/gun/5x50.json data/json/items/gun/ups.json
msgid "5 rd."
msgstr "5 rd."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/5x50.json
msgid "RM232 IDW"
msgid_plural "RM232 IDWs"
msgstr[0] "RM232 IDW"
msgstr[1] "RM232 IDW"
msgstr[2] "RM232 IDW"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM232 IDW"
#: data/json/items/gun/5x50.json
msgid ""
"This lightweight machine pistol fires 5x50mm armor-piercing flechette "
"cartridges.  Classified as an individual defense weapon, this advanced "
"firearm was developed by Rivtech for the US military shortly before the end "
"of the world.  Designed to be fired in bursts, it excels in close combat."
msgstr ""
"Esta pistola ametralladora liviana dispara cartuchos 5x50mm de dardos "
"perforantes de blindaje. Clasificada como arma de defensa personal, esta "
"arma de fuego avanzada fue desarrollada por Rivtech para el Ejército de "
"Estados Unidos poco antes de que el mundo se terminara. Diseñada para "
"disparar en ráfaga, es excelente en el combate cercano."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "RM232 IDW"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "integral railgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/5x50.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/advanced.json
msgid "2 rd."
msgstr "2 rd."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/66mm.json
msgid "M202A1 FLASH"
msgid_plural "M202A1 FLASH"
msgstr[0] "M202A1 FLASH"
msgstr[1] "M202A1 FLASH"
msgstr[2] "M202A1 FLASH"

#. ~ Description of gun "M202A1 FLASH"
#: data/json/items/gun/66mm.json
msgid ""
"An American rocket launcher designed in the 1970s to replace WWII-era "
"flamethrowers still in use in Vietnam.  It has four barrels sharing the 66mm"
" caliber of the M72 LAW."
msgstr ""
"Un lanzacohetes estadounidense diseñado en la década de los 70 para "
"reemplazar los lanzallamas de la Segunda Guerra Mundial que se usaron hasta "
"la guerra de Vietnam. Tiene cuatro cañones que comparten el calibre 66mm del"
" M72 LAW."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M202A1 FLASH"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "1025 Goa"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "Wraitheon Armory 2519"
#: data/json/items/gun/66mm.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/25mm.json
msgid "single shot"
msgstr "un solo disparo"

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "M202A1 FLASH"
#: data/json/items/gun/66mm.json
msgid "all barrels"
msgstr "todos los cañones"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/700nx.json
msgid "Elephant gun"
msgid_plural "Elephant guns"
msgstr[0] "Rifle para Elefantes"
msgstr[1] "Rifles para Elefantes"
msgstr[2] "Rifles para Elefantes"

#. ~ Description of gun "Elephant gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/700nx.json
msgid ""
"A custom-made single shot rifle specially designed for the hunting of huge "
"game.  You could obviously kill everything with this, EVERYTHING.  If you "
"ever find enough ammo of course."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de disparo único hecho a medida diseñado especialmente para la caza"
" del gran juego. Se podría, obviamente, matar todo con esto, TODO. Si alguna"
" vez encuentra munición suficiente, por supuesto."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "AKM"
msgid_plural "AKMs"
msgstr[0] "AKM"
msgstr[1] "AKM"
msgstr[2] "AKM"

#. ~ Description of gun "AKM"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"One of the most recognizable assault rifles ever made, the AKM is renowned "
"for its durability even under the worst conditions."
msgstr ""
"Uno de los rifles de asalto más reconocibles que se haya fabricado. El AKM "
"es reconocido por su durabilidad incluso bajo las peores condiciones."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Beretta ARX-160"
msgid_plural "Beretta ARX-160"
msgstr[0] "Beretta ARX-160"
msgstr[1] "Beretta ARX-160"
msgstr[2] "Beretta ARX-160"

#. ~ Description of gun "Beretta ARX-160"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"The Beretta ARX-160 was a Phase II contender in the United States Army "
"Individual Carbine competition to replace the M4 carbine.  It failed to "
"replace it, but it is widely used by military all around the world.  This "
"version is chambered for 7.62x39mm."
msgstr ""
"La Beretta ARX-160 era una competidora de la Phase II en la competición de "
"Carabina Individual del Ejército de Estados Unidos, para reemplazar la "
"carabina M4. No logró reemplazarla, pero es usada por ejércitos de todo el "
"mundo. Esta versión utiliza balas 7.62x39mm."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "SKS"
msgid_plural "SKSs"
msgstr[0] "SKS"
msgstr[1] "SKS"
msgstr[2] "SKS"

#. ~ Description of gun "SKS"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Developed by the Soviets in 1945, this rifle was quickly replaced by the "
"full-auto AK-47.  However, due to its superb accuracy, low recoil, and "
"deployable integrated bayonet, this gun maintains immense popularity."
msgstr ""
"Desarrollado por los soviéticos en 1945, este rifle fue rápidamente "
"reemplazado por el AK-47 automático. Sin embargo, debido a su magnífica "
"precisión, poco retroceso y bayoneta integrada retráctil, este arma todavía "
"tiene una inmensa popularidad."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "AK-47"
msgid_plural "AK-47s"
msgstr[0] "AK-47"
msgstr[1] "AK-47s"
msgstr[2] "AK-47s"

#. ~ Description of gun "AK-47"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Civilian-legal clones of the iconic Kalashnikov, like this one, were "
"manufactured and imported by many different firms.  Even without full-auto "
"function, their solid firepower and reliability in harsh conditions make "
"them valuable weapons in this new world."
msgstr ""
"Los clones civiles del emblemático Kalashnikov, como éste, fueron fabricados"
" e importados por muchas empresas diferentes. Incluso sin la función full-"
"auto, su sólida potencia de fuego y su fiabilidad en condiciones adversas "
"las convierten en armas valiosas en este nuevo mundo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Mini Draco"
msgid_plural "Mini Dracos"
msgstr[0] "Mini Draco"
msgstr[1] "Mini Dracos"
msgstr[2] "Mini Dracos"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mini Draco"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Essentially a semi-auto AK with a short barrel and no stock, this unwieldy "
"\"pistol\" has seen some popularity with civilian shooters and gangbangers "
"alike."
msgstr ""
"Esencialmente un AK semiautomático con un cañón corto y sin culata, esta "
"\"pistola\" poco manejable ha visto cierta popularidad entre los tiradores "
"civiles y los pandilleros por igual."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Mk47 Mutant"
msgid_plural "Mk47 Mutants"
msgstr[0] "Mk47 Mutant"
msgstr[1] "Mk47 Mutants"
msgstr[2] "Mk47 Mutants"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mk47 Mutant"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"The CMMG Mk47 Mutant is an American rifle, natively chambered for 7.62x39mm "
"ammo.  Features a characteristic free-floating handguard, with a similar "
"action mechanism to the AR-15, repurposed for the bigger, more potent ammo."
msgstr ""
"El CMMG Mk47 Mutant es un rifle americano, con recámara nativa para munición"
" de 7,62x39mm. Cuenta con un característico guardamanos de flotación libre, "
"con un mecanismo de acción similar al del AR-15, reutilizado para la "
"munición más grande y potente."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "vz. 58 combat rifle"
msgid_plural "vz. 58 combat rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de combate vz. 58"
msgstr[1] "rifles de combate vz. 58"
msgstr[2] "rifles de combate vz. 58"

#. ~ Description of gun "vz. 58 combat rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"A Cold War-era Czechoslovak assault rifle, likely constructed stateside from"
" a pre-1986 imported parts kit or brought back from a third world war zone."
"  Externally similar to the AK family of rifles, this weapon nevertheless "
"only shares the former’s 7.62x39mm chambering.  Featuring no interchangeable"
" parts with its Russian doppelganger, this firearm makes use of a completely"
" different internal operating system, is far more svelte than its other "
"Warsaw Pact counterparts, and feeds from proprietary box magazines."
msgstr ""
"Un rifle de asalto checoslovaco de la época de la Guerra Fría, probablemente"
" construido en los Estados Unidos con partes importadas antes de 1986 o "
"traídas de una zona de guerra del tercer mundo. Similar en su exterior a la "
"familia de rifles AK, sin embargo solo comparte el calibre 7.62x39mm de "
"aquellos rifles. No tiene partes intercambiables con su gemelo ruso, este "
"rifle utiliza un sistema de operación interno completamente diferente. Es "
"más esbelto que otros similares del Pacto de Varsovia y se alimenta con "
"cargadores de caja exclusivos."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "vz. 58 combat rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Samopal vz. 58 P"
msgid_plural "Samopal vz. 58 Ps"
msgstr[0] "Samopal vz. 58 P"
msgstr[1] "Samopal vz. 58 P"
msgstr[2] "Samopal vz. 58 P"

#. ~ Description of variant "vz. 58 combat rifle" of gun "Samopal vz. 58 P"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"This lightweight and relatively svelte Cold War assault rifle was originally"
" developed for use by the Czechoslovak army, in place of the various "
"licensed Kalashnikov rifles which were then prevalent around eastern Europe."
"  Bearing more than a passing resemblance to the AK-47, this weapon "
"nevertheless features a completely different array of internals and "
"possesses no interchangeable parts with its Russian counterpart.  Making use"
" of proprietary magazines and a 15.4 inch barrel, the vz. 58 was regarded by"
" some to be the Kalashnikov’s lesser-known superior.  Likely reconstructed "
"from a pre-1986 imported parts kit, or brought back from a third world war "
"zone, this particular weapon features a removable wood impregnated plastic "
"buttstock and a 'P' suffixed designation, which both mark it as an original "
"infantry model."
msgstr ""
"Este ligero y relativamente esbelto fusil de asalto de la Guerra Fría fue "
"desarrollado originalmente para ser utilizado por el ejército checoslovaco, "
"en lugar de los diversos fusiles Kalashnikov con licencia que entonces "
"predominaban en Europa del Este. Aunque tiene un gran parecido con el AK-47,"
" esta arma cuenta con una serie de componentes completamente diferentes y no"
" posee piezas intercambiables con su homólogo ruso. Haciendo uso de "
"cargadores propietarios y un cañón de 15,4 pulgadas, el vz. 58 fue "
"considerado por algunos como el mejorado y menos conocido del Kalashnikov. "
"Probablemente reconstruido a partir de un equipo de piezas importado antes "
"de 1986, o traído de una zona de guerra tercermundista, este arma en "
"particular cuenta con una culata extraíble de plástico impregnado de madera "
"y una designación con el sufijo \"P\", que lo identifica como un modelo "
"original de infantería."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "vz. 58 combat rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "Samopal VZ 58 V"
msgid_plural "Samopal VZ 58 Vs"
msgstr[0] "Samopal VZ 58 V"
msgstr[1] "Samopal VZ 58 Vs"
msgstr[2] "Samopal VZ 58 Vs"

#. ~ Description of variant "vz. 58 combat rifle" of gun "Samopal VZ 58 V"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"This lightweight and relatively svelte Cold War assault rifle was originally"
" developed for use by the Czechoslovak army, in place of the various "
"licensed Kalashnikov rifles which were then prevalent around eastern Europe."
"  Bearing more than a passing resemblance to the AK-47, this weapon "
"nevertheless features a completely different array of internals and "
"possesses no interchangeable parts with its Russian counterpart.  Making use"
" of proprietary magazines and a 15.4 inch barrel, the vz. 58 was regarded by"
" some to be the Kalashnikov’s lesser-known superior.  Likely reconstructed "
"from a pre-1986 imported parts kit, or brought back from a third world war "
"zone, this particular weapon features a removable side-folding buttstock and"
" a 'V' suffixed designation, which both mark it as an original airborne or "
"crew issued model."
msgstr ""
"Este ligero y relativamente esbelto fusil de asalto de la Guerra Fría fue "
"desarrollado originalmente para ser utilizado por el ejército checoslovaco, "
"en lugar de los diversos fusiles Kalashnikov con licencia que entonces "
"predominaban en Europa del Este. Aunque tiene un gran parecido con el AK-47,"
" esta arma cuenta con una serie de componentes completamente diferentes y no"
" posee piezas intercambiables con su homólogo ruso. Haciendo uso de "
"cargadores propietarios y un cañón de 15,4 pulgadas, el VZ. 58 es "
"considerado por algunos como el mejorado y menos conocido del Kalashnikov. "
"Probablemente reconstruido a partir de un equipo de piezas importado antes "
"de 1986, o traído de una zona de guerra tercermundista, este arma en "
"particular cuenta con una culata plegable lateral desmontable y una "
"designación con el sufijo \"V\", que lo identifica como un modelo original "
"para la aviación o la tripulación."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "vz. 58 tactical rifle"
msgid_plural "vz. 58 tactical rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle táctico vz. 58"
msgstr[1] "rifles tácticos vz. 58"
msgstr[2] "rifles tácticos vz. 58"

#. ~ Description of gun "vz. 58 tactical rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"Inspired and built primarily from older Czechoslovak military combat rifles,"
" this weapon bears an uncanny resemblance to the Kalashnikov despite sharing"
" no components with it, including magazines.  Chambering the Soviet "
"7.62x39mm cartridge and featuring an American produced folding buttstock, "
"receiver, and barrel in order to comply with US importation laws, the weapon"
" is equipped with a side mounted rail assembly as well as a detachable "
"muzzle brake.  Despite the firearm’s Cold War design being nearly 80 years "
"old, this modern iteration makes for a relatively portable and serviceable "
"cataclysmic problem solver."
msgstr ""
"Inspirada y construida principalmente a partir de antiguos rifles de combate"
" militares checoslovacos, esta arma tiene un asombroso parecido con el "
"Kalashnikov a pesar de no compartir ningún componente con él, incluidos los "
"cargadores. Con el cartucho soviético 7,62x39mm y con una culata, carcasa y "
"cañón plegables fabricados en EE.UU. para cumplir con las leyes de "
"importación estadounidenses, el arma está equipada con un raíl lateral y un "
"freno de boca desmontable. A pesar de que el diseño del arma de la Guerra "
"Fría tiene casi 80 años de antigüedad, esta iteración moderna hace que sea "
"un solucionador de problemas cataclísmicos relativamente portátil y útil."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "vz. 58 tactical rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid "vz. 58 Tactical Sporter"
msgid_plural "vz. 58 Tactical Sporters"
msgstr[0] "Sporter Táctico vz. 58"
msgstr[1] "Sporters Tácticos vz. 58"
msgstr[2] "Sporters Tácticos vz. 58"

#. ~ Description of variant "vz. 58 tactical rifle" of gun "vz. 58 Tactical
#. Sporter"
#: data/json/items/gun/762.json
msgid ""
"A modern semi-automatic clone of the Czechoslovak-produced vz. 58 assault "
"rifle, chambered in the Soviet 7.62x39mm cartridge.  Built off of surplus "
"vz. 58 parts, the rifle makes use of additional American made components "
"such as the receiver, barrel, and buttstock to comply with US importation "
"laws.  Featuring an extended 16 inch barrel, an M4 style stock adapter and "
"tube, and an integrated side rail for optics mounting, this Cold War rifle "
"makes for a relatively handy post-apocalyptic companion."
msgstr ""
"Una moderna copia del fusil semiautomático de asalto vz. 58 de producción "
"checoslovaca, con recámara del cartucho soviético 7,62x39mm. Construido a "
"partir de piezas sobrantes del vz. 58, el rifle utiliza componentes "
"adicionales fabricados en EE.UU., como el receptor, el cañón y la culata, "
"para cumplir con las leyes de importación de EE.UU. Con un cañón extendido "
"de 16 pulgadas, un adaptador de culata y tubo estilo M4, y un raíl lateral "
"integrado para el montaje de la óptica, este rifle de la Guerra Fría es un "
"compañero post-apocalíptico relativamente práctico."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin carbine"
msgid_plural "Mosin carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina Mosin"
msgstr[1] "carabinas Mosin"
msgstr[2] "carabinas Mosin"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"A later produced and substantially shortened version of Imperial Russia’s "
"original service rifle, this variant of the Mosin features a notably more "
"compact barrel and an integral side-folding bayonet.  Produced during the "
"latter days of the Second World War for the Soviet Union, the weapon "
"exhibits less overall stopping power than its full-length older brother "
"thanks to the former’s stubbier barrel.  Despite the arm being somewhat "
"weaker than its forefather, the 7.62x54mm round that it chambers still packs"
" a hefty punch, whilst its smaller size helps to make the weapon wieldier."
msgstr ""
"Una versión tardía producida y substancialmente acortada del rifle de "
"servicio de la Rusia Imperial, esta variante del Mosin tiene un cañón "
"notablemente mas compacto y una bayoneta integral plegable. Producida "
"durante los últimos días de la Segunda Guerra Mundial para la Unión "
"Soviética, el arma exhibe menos poder de parada que su hermano mayor que "
"tenia un cañon mas fornido y largo. A pesar de ser mas débil que su "
"antecesora, la munición de 7.62x54mm que la recamara acepta todavía pega "
"fuerte, mientras que su menor tamaño hace que sea mas cómoda de portar."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin-Nagant M44"
msgid_plural "Mosin-Nagant M44"
msgstr[0] "Mosin-Nagant M44"
msgstr[1] "Mosin-Nagant M44"
msgstr[2] "Mosin-Nagant M44"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin carbine" of gun "Mosin-Nagant M44"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"The Model 44 is the carbine-sized variant of the standard 1891/30.  It has a"
" shorter barrel, making it weaker than the 1891/30, but easier to carry.  "
"This weapon also comes with an integrated side-folding bayonet."
msgstr ""
"El Modelo 44 es la variante tamaño carabina del estándar 1891/30. Tiene un "
"cañón más corto y por lo tanto más débil que el 1891/30 pero más fácil de "
"llevar. Esta arma también viene con una bayoneta integrada plegable."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Mosin carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR"
msgid_plural "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR"
msgstr[0] "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR"
msgstr[1] "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR"
msgstr[2] "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin carbine" of gun "Mosin-Nagant M44-EBR"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"This carbine packs the classic Mosin-Nagant Model 44 action in a modern-day "
"stock capable of accepting modifications."
msgstr ""
"Esta carabina provee el clásico Mosin-Nagant Modelo 44 con una culata "
"moderna que acepta modificaciones."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Mosin battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de combate Mosin"
msgstr[1] "rifles de combate Mosin"
msgstr[2] "rifles de combate Mosin"

#. ~ Description of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"Developed by the Russian Empire prior to the onset of the First World War, "
"the Mosin is a bolt-action military battle rifle chambered for 7.62x54mm "
"rounds.  Powerful, unwieldy, and prolific across the world as military "
"surplus, this sizable rifle is a Soviet updated version of the venerable "
"Mosin."
msgstr ""
"Desarrollado por el Imperio Ruso antes de la Primera Guerra Mundial, el "
"Mosin es un rifle de cerrojo de batalla con la recámara para cartuchos de "
"munición 7.62x54mm. Poderoso, difícil de manejar y muy usado mundialmente "
"como arma adicional. Esta es una versión actualizada del venerable Mosin."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgid_plural "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgstr[0] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgstr[1] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
msgstr[2] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin battle rifle" of gun "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"The Mosin-Nagant 1891/30 is a bolt-action, internal magazine-fed military "
"rifle, developed by the Russian Empire and later used and perfected by the "
"Soviet Union."
msgstr ""
"El Mosin-Nagant 1891/30 es un rifle militar de cerrojo, con cargador "
"interno, desarrollado por el Imperio Ruso, y luego utilizado y perfeccionado"
" por la Unión Soviética."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Mosin battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgid_plural "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgstr[0] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgstr[1] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"
msgstr[2] "Mosin-Nagant 1891/30-EBR"

#. ~ Description of variant "Mosin battle rifle" of gun "Mosin-Nagant
#. 1891/30-EBR"
#: data/json/items/gun/762R.json
msgid ""
"This Mosin-Nagant has exchanged the classic wooden stock for a modern "
"synthetic model, carefully balanced to the same weight and handling, to "
"allow support for modern accessories."
msgstr ""
"El Mosin-Nagant cambió su clásica culata de madera por un modelo sintético "
"moderno, cuidadosamente balanceado y con capacidad para añadirle accesorios "
"modernos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid "PPSh-41"
msgid_plural "PPSh-41s"
msgstr[0] "PPSh-41"
msgstr[1] "PPSh-41"
msgstr[2] "PPSh-41"

#. ~ Description of gun "PPSh-41"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid ""
"The Soviet-made PPSh-41 is a mass-produced selective-fire submachine gun.  "
"It has a relatively high rate of fire."
msgstr ""
"La fabricación soviética PPSh-41 es una ametralladora de fuego selectiva "
"producida en masa. Tiene una relativamente alta tasa de fuego."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid "Tokarev TT-33"
msgid_plural "Tokarev TT-33"
msgstr[0] "Tokarev TT-33"
msgstr[1] "Tokarev TT-33"
msgstr[2] "Tokarev TT-33"

#. ~ Description of gun "Tokarev TT-33"
#: data/json/items/gun/762x25.json
msgid ""
"The Tokarev TT-33 is an antique Russian semiautomatic pistol, famous for its"
" durability, accuracy, and uncomfortable grip angle.  It was chambered for "
"the 7.62x25mm due to the popularity of the C96 pistol among Russian "
"revolutionaries."
msgstr ""
"La Tokarev TT-33 es una pistola antigua semiautomática rusa, famosa por su "
"durabilidad, precisión y agarre del ángulo incómodo. Usa el calibre "
"7.62x25mm debido a la popularidad de la pistola C96 entre los "
"revolucionarios rusos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/84x246mm.json
msgid "M3 recoilless rifle"
msgid_plural "M3 recoilless rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle sin retroceso M3"
msgstr[1] "rifles sin retroceso M3"
msgstr[2] "rifles sin retroceso M3"

#. ~ Description of gun "M3 recoilless rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/84x246mm.json
msgid ""
"Manufactured in Sweden, the Carl Gustaf M3 is a breech-loading 84 millimeter"
" man-portable, reusable, multi-role recoilless rifle commonly used by the US"
" military."
msgstr ""
"Fabricado en Suecia, el Carl Gustaf M3 es un fusil sin retroceso de 84 "
"milímetros, reutilizable y de múltiples funciones, utilizado habitualmente "
"por el ejército estadounidense."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/84x246mm.json
msgid "M3E1 recoilless rifle"
msgid_plural "M3E1 recoilless rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle sin retroceso M3E1"
msgstr[1] "rifles sin retroceso M3E1"
msgstr[2] "rifles sin retroceso M3E1"

#. ~ Description of gun "M3E1 recoilless rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/84x246mm.json
msgid ""
"The Carl Gustaf M3E1 is a breech-loading 84 millimeter man-portable, "
"reusable, multi-role recoilless rifle.  This is a lighter, shorter, and more"
" advanced development of the M3."
msgstr ""
"El Carl Gustaf M3E1 es un fusil sin retroceso de 84 milímetros, reutilizable"
" y de uso múltiple. Es un desarrollo más ligero, más corto y más avanzado "
"del M3."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/84x246mm.json
msgid "AT4"
msgid_plural "AT4s"
msgstr[0] "AT4"
msgstr[1] "AT4s"
msgstr[2] "AT4s"

#. ~ Description of gun "AT4"
#: data/json/items/gun/84x246mm.json
msgid ""
"A milspec rocket launcher - an 84mm unguided, portable, single-shot "
"recoilless smoothbore weapon used primarily by the US military."
msgstr ""
"Un lanzacohetes milspec, un arma de 84mm sin guía, portátil, de un solo "
"disparo, sin retroceso y de cañón liso usada principalmente por el ejército "
"de los Estados Unidos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid "RM103A automagnum"
msgid_plural "RM103A automagnums"
msgstr[0] "RM103A automagnum"
msgstr[1] "RM103A automagnums"
msgstr[2] "RM103A automagnums"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM103A automagnum"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid ""
"Considered overkill by many, the Rivtech RM103A remains one of the most "
"powerful sidearms ever developed.  Accepts stick magazines."
msgstr ""
"Aunque algunos la consideran una exageración, la Rivtech RM103A sigue siendo"
" una de las armas de apoyo más poderosas que se hayan desarrollado. Acepta "
"cargadores rectos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid "RM11B scout rifle"
msgid_plural "RM11B scout rifles"
msgstr[0] "Rifle de reconocimiento RM11B"
msgstr[1] "Rifles de reconocimiento RM11B"
msgstr[2] "Rifles de reconocimiento RM11B"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM11B scout rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid ""
"Intended to function as a long-range sharpshooter support weapon for the "
"military, the Rivtech RM11B scout rifle was designed for durability and "
"accuracy under less than ideal circumstances.  Its bullpup layout, "
"integrated suppressor and digital scope, and two round burst mode allow it "
"to deliver precise long-range takedowns, utilizing the proprietary Rivtech "
"8mm caseless round.  Accepts stick magazines."
msgstr ""
"Pensado para funcionar como arma de apoyo para los francotiradores "
"militares, el rifle de explorador Rivtech RM11B fue diseñado para ser "
"duradero y preciso bajo circunstancias poco ideales. Su diseño bullpup, "
"silenciador integrado, mira digital y modo de disparo en ráfaga de dos "
"balas, le permite derribar objetivos a larga distancia, utilizando la bala "
"sin casquillo de Rivtech 8mm. Puede usar cargadores rectos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid "RM2000 submachine gun"
msgid_plural "RM2000 submachine guns"
msgstr[0] "subfusil RM2000"
msgstr[1] "subfusiles RM2000"
msgstr[2] "subfusiles RM2000"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM2000 submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid ""
"Utilizing a powerful and unusual caliber, the Rivtech RM2000 submachine gun "
"was designed for durability and ease of carrying under less than ideal "
"circumstances.  Accepts stick magazines."
msgstr ""
"Utilizando un poderoso e inusual calibre, el subfusil Rivtech RM2000 fue "
"diseñado para ser duradero y fácil de llevar bajo condiciones poco ideales. "
"Acepta cargadores rectos."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid "RM298 HMG"
msgid_plural "RM298 HMGs"
msgstr[0] "RM298 HMG"
msgstr[1] "RM298 HMGs"
msgstr[2] "RM298 HMGs"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM298 HMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid ""
"Utilizing a powerful and unusual caliber, the Rivtech RM298 heavy machine "
"gun was designed for durability and extreme volume of sustained fire under "
"the worst possible circumstances.  Accepts RMXB500 box and RMGD250 drum "
"magazines."
msgstr ""
"Utilizando un poderoso e inusual calibre, la ametralladora pesada Rivtech "
"RM298 fue diseñada para ser duradera y poseer un volumen extremo de disparo "
"sostenido, incluso bajo las peores condiciones posibles. Acepta cargadores "
"de caja RMXB500 y cargadores de tambor RMGD250."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid "RM51 assault rifle"
msgid_plural "RM51 assault rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de asalto RM51"
msgstr[1] "rifles de asalto RM51"
msgstr[2] "rifles de asalto RM51"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM51 assault rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid ""
"Originally produced for military use, the Rivtech RM51 assault rifle was "
"designed for durability and ease of use under less than ideal circumstances,"
" with its considerable bulk minimized by a compact and ergonomic layout.  "
"Accepts box magazines."
msgstr ""
"Originalmente producido para uso militar, el rifle de asalto Rivtech RM51 "
"fue diseñado para ser duradero y fácil de usar bajo condiciones poco "
"ideales, ya que su incomodidad ha sido minimizada por su diseño compacto y "
"ergonómico. Acepta cargadores de caja."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid "RM614 LMG"
msgid_plural "RM614 LMGs"
msgstr[0] "RM614 LMG"
msgstr[1] "RM614 LMGs"
msgstr[2] "RM614 LMGs"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM614 LMG"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid ""
"Utilizing a powerful and unusual caliber, the Rivtech RM614 light machine "
"gun was designed for durability and extreme volume of sustained fire under "
"the worst possible circumstances.  Accepts RMXB500 box and RMGD250 drum "
"magazines."
msgstr ""
"Utilizando un poderoso e inusual calibre, la ametralladora ligera Rivtech "
"RM614 fue diseñada para ser duradera y poseer un volumen extremo de disparo "
"sostenido, incluso bajo las peores condiciones posibles. Acepta cargadores "
"de caja RMXB500 y cargadores de tambor RMGD250."

#. ~ Firing mode of gun "RM614 LMG"
#. ~ Firing mode of gun "eidolon derringer"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/gun/5x50.json
msgid "4 rd."
msgstr "4 rd."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid "RM88 battle rifle"
msgid_plural "RM88 battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de combate RM88"
msgstr[1] "rifles de combate RM88"
msgstr[2] "rifles de combate RM88"

#. ~ Description of gun "RM88 battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/8x40mm.json
msgid ""
"Originally produced for military use, the Rivtech RM88 battle rifle was "
"designed for durability and extreme firepower under less than ideal "
"circumstances, with a heavy ported barrel for maximum controllability.  "
"Accepts box and RMGD250 drum magazines."
msgstr ""
"Originalmente producido para uso militar, el rifle de combate Rivtech RM88 "
"fue diseñado para ser duradero y tener mucho poder de fuego bajo condiciones"
" poco ideales, con un caño pesada para tener máxima controlabilidad. Acepta "
"cargadores de caja y cargadores de tambor RMGD250."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Calico automatic carbine"
msgid_plural "Calico automatic carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabinas automáticas Calico"
msgstr[1] "carabinas automáticas Calico"
msgstr[2] "carabinas automáticas Calico"

#. ~ Description of gun "Calico automatic carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Calico automatic carbine is a submachine gun with a unique circular "
"magazine that allows for high capacities and reduced recoil."
msgstr ""
"La carabina automática Calico es un subfusil con un cargador circular único "
"que permite una gran capacidad y un retroceso reducido."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Calico automatic carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Calico M960"
msgid_plural "Calico M960"
msgstr[0] "Calico M960"
msgstr[1] "Calico M960"
msgstr[2] "Calico M960"

#. ~ Description of variant "Calico automatic carbine" of gun "Calico M960"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A compact submachine gun designed evidently under the 'spray and pray' "
"mentality, this Calico M960 automatic carbine is not notably powerful, or "
"dependable, or even particularly accurate to shoot.  Intended for military "
"and law enforcement use, it never saw any noteworthy service due to its poor"
" reliability and overall performance, and would be an unremarkable weapon in"
" all respects, save for its enormous magazine capacity.  Making use of "
"uniquely designed 50 or 100 round circular magazines, the Calico might not "
"be a particularly good gun, but will throw an overwhelming amount of led "
"down range for a long time providing that it doesn’t choke, jam, and die."
msgstr ""
"Un subfusil compacto diseñado con la evidente mentalidad del 'dispara y "
"olvídate', la carabina automática Calico M960 no es muy potente, dependiente"
" o incluso particularmente precisa al disparar. Pensada para uso militar y "
"de las fuerzas de la ley, nunca tuvo un papel destacado debido a su pobre "
"eficiencia y poco desempeño, y seria un arma poco remarcable, excepto por su"
" cargador de enorme capacidad. Haciendo uso de cargadores circulares de "
"munición diseñados exclusivamente de 50 o 100 balas, y aunque el Calico "
"puede que no sea muy buena como arma, pero soltara una increíble cantidad de"
" plomo por un largo periodo de tiempo, siempre que no se obture, encasquille"
" o muera."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "9x19mm pistol-caliber carbine"
msgid_plural "9x19mm pistol-caliber carbines"
msgstr[0] "carabina de calibre pistola 9x19mm"
msgstr[1] "carabinas de calibre pistola 9x19mm"
msgstr[2] "carabinas de calibre pistola 9x19mm"

#. ~ Description of gun "9x19mm pistol-caliber carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"Designed to be a companion rifle with provided M9 handguns, this compact and"
" light weight pistol-caliber carbine makes use of the same 9x19mm magazines."
"  Originally intended for use by law enforcement units, this style of small "
"caliber, semi-automatic carbine failed to achieve the same level of "
"popularity as regular and more potent rifles.  However, despite being "
"inadequate for their original purpose, before the Cataclysm these modestly "
"sized weapons still found a home in sport shooting and self-defense civilian"
" roles."
msgstr ""
"Diseñado para ser un rifle secundario de las pistolas M9, esta carabina "
"compacta y ligera de calibre pistola hace uso de los cargadores 9x19mm. "
"Originalmente diseñado para ser usado por las fuerzas policiales, este "
"estilo de calibre pequeño y carabina semiautomática fallo en alcanzar el "
"mismo nivel de popularidad que otros rifles mas regulares y potentes. Aun "
"así, a pesar de no ser adecuado para su propósito original, antes del "
"Cataclismo estas modestamente pequeñas armas encontraron su rol en los "
"deportes de tiro y la auto defensa civil."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "9x19mm pistol-caliber carbine"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Cx4 Storm"
msgid_plural "Cx4 Storms"
msgstr[0] "Cx4 Storm"
msgstr[1] "Cx4 Storms"
msgstr[2] "Cx4 Storms"

#. ~ Description of variant "9x19mm pistol-caliber carbine" of gun "Cx4 Storm"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A small pistol caliber carbine designed for police use and civilian self-"
"defense, the Cx4 Storm uses magazines that are interchangeable with other "
"Beretta 9x19mm handguns."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña carabina con calibre de pistola, diseñada para uso policial y la"
" defensa personal de los civiles. El Cx4 Storm usa cargadores que son "
"intercambiables con las pistolas Beretta 9x19mm."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Glock carry pistol"
msgid_plural "Glock carry pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola Glock de transporte"
msgstr[1] "pistolas Glock de transporte"
msgstr[2] "pistolas Glock de transporte"

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock carry pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A common 9x19mm pistol of modest proportions, produced by the popular Glock "
"gun company and mainly built from plastic polymers.  Making use of aptly-"
"named Glock magazines and being a decades-long popular concealed carry "
"option for civilians due to its small size, it is a tried, tested, and "
"reliable design."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola calibre 9x19mm de modestas proporciones, producida por la "
"popular empresa de armas Glock y principalmente fabricada con plástico de "
"polímeros. Haciendo uso de cargadores Glock y siendo una de las opciones mas"
" populares de armas ocultas para uso civil debido a su pequeño tamaño. Mas "
"que probada y con un diseño fiable."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Glock carry pistol"
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#: data/mods/Xedra_Evolved/monsters/monsterattacks.json
msgid "Glock 19"
msgid_plural "Glock 19"
msgstr[0] "Glock 19"
msgstr[1] "Glock 19"
msgstr[2] "Glock 19"

#. ~ Description of variant "Glock carry pistol" of gun "Glock 19"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"Possibly the most popular pistol in existence, the Glock 19 can be summed up"
" as being fundamentally a more compact brother to the full-sized Glock 17 "
"pistol.  Sporting a mainly polymer-based design, the Glock 19 is often "
"derided for its plastic construction which lends the handgun a deceptively "
"flimsy feel.  Even so, the Glock 19 remains both a remarkably reliable "
"firearm and a quite shootable gun in its own right."
msgstr ""
"Posiblemente la pistola más popular que existe, la Glock 19 puede resumirse "
"como un hermano más compacto de la pistola Glock 17 de tamaño normal.  Con "
"un diseño basado principalmente en el polímero, la Glock 19 es a menudo "
"ridiculizada por su construcción de plástico, que da a la pistola una "
"sensación engañosa de debilidad.  Aun así, la Glock 19 sigue siendo un arma "
"de fuego notablemente fiable y un arma bastante fácil de disparar por "
"derecho propio."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "H&K MP5A2"
msgid_plural "H&K MP5A2s"
msgstr[0] "H&K MP5A2"
msgstr[1] "H&K MP5A2s"
msgstr[2] "H&K MP5A2s"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K MP5A2"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Heckler & Koch MP5 is one of the most widely-used submachine guns in the"
" world, and has been adopted by special police forces and militaries alike."
"  Its high degree of accuracy and low recoil are universally praised."
msgstr ""
"El Heckler & Koch MP5 es uno de los subfusiles más utilizados en el mundo, y"
" ha sido adoptado por las fuerzas policiales y militares especiales. Su alto"
" grado de precisión y su poco retroceso son elogiados universalmente."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "H&K MP5SD"
msgid_plural "H&K MP5SDs"
msgstr[0] "H&K MP5SD"
msgstr[1] "H&K MP5SD"
msgstr[2] "H&K MP5SD"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K MP5SD"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The H&K MP5SD offers subsonic performance in almost the same footprint as "
"the H&K MP5, retaining its handiness.  The large suppressor cuts down on "
"muzzle flash greatly, aiding in night operations.  It has also seen some "
"popularity with SWAT teams, as it lowers the risk of fire and explosions in "
"illegal laboratories.  With body armor in more common use, the MP5SD has "
"waned in popularity among special forces due to its decreased terminal "
"performance."
msgstr ""
"El H&K MP5SD ofrece un rendimiento subsónico en casi la misma huella que el "
"H&K MP5, manteniendo su manejabilidad. El gran supresor reduce en gran "
"medida el flash de la boca, ayudando en las operaciones nocturnas. También "
"ha tenido cierta popularidad entre los equipos SWAT, ya que reduce el riesgo"
" de incendios y explosiones en laboratorios ilegales. Con los chalecos "
"antibalas de uso más común, el MP5SD ha disminuido su popularidad entre las "
"fuerzas especiales debido a su menor rendimiento terminal."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "H&K MP5K-PDW"
msgid_plural "H&K MP5K-PDWs"
msgstr[0] "H&K MP5K-PDW"
msgstr[1] "H&K MP5K-PDWs"
msgstr[2] "H&K MP5K-PDWs"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K MP5K-PDW"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Heckler & Koch MP5 is one of the most widely-used submachine guns in the"
" world, and has been adopted by special police forces and militaries alike."
"  Its high degree of accuracy and low recoil are universally praised.  The "
"MP5K-PDW model features a shorter barrel, a built-in foregrip, and a side "
"folding stock for vehicle or aircraft crew use."
msgstr ""
"La Heckler & Koch MP5 es una de las metralletas más utilizadas en el mundo, "
"y ha sido adoptada tanto por las fuerzas especiales de la policía como por "
"los militares. Su alto grado de precisión y bajo retroceso son "
"universalmente elogiados. El modelo MP5K-PDW tiene un cañón más corto, una "
"pinza integrada y una culata lateral plegable para uso de la tripulación de "
"vehículos o aeronaves."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "PTR 603"
msgid_plural "PTR 603s"
msgstr[0] "PTR 603"
msgstr[1] "PTR 603s"
msgstr[2] "PTR 603s"

#. ~ Description of gun "PTR 603"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The PTR 603 is a semi-automatic copy of the famous MP5 series, domestically "
"produced for the US market on original Heckler & Koch tooling by PTR "
"Industries.  Like the MP5, its roller delayed blowback action offers smooth "
"shooting and precision, setting it apart from other submachine guns and "
"pistol caliber carbines.  This model is configured as a pistol to avoid "
"inconvenient and costly NFA regulations.  A welded-on section of M1913 rail "
"offers convenient mounting for aftermarket optics, but precludes the use of "
"claw mounts."
msgstr ""
"El PTR 603 es una copia semiautomática de la famosa serie MP5, producida "
"nacionalmente para el mercado estadounidense en herramientas originales "
"Heckler y Koch de PTR Industries.  Al igual que el MP5, su acción de "
"retroceso con rodillo retardado ofrece un disparo suave y preciso, lo que lo"
" diferencia de otras subfusiles y carabinas de calibre pistola.  Este modelo"
" está configurado como una pistola para evitar las incómodas y costosas "
"regulaciones de la NFA.  Una sección soldada del carril M1913 ofrece un "
"montaje conveniente para la óptica del mercado de accesorios, pero excluye "
"el uso de montajes de garras."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "H&K operational briefcase"
msgid_plural "H&K operational briefcases"
msgstr[0] "maletín de operaciones de H&K"
msgstr[1] "maletines de operaciones de H&K"
msgstr[2] "maletines de operaciones de H&K"

#. ~ Description of gun "H&K operational briefcase"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A hard-sided briefcase with a trigger in the handle and a concealed hole in "
"the side.  To fire the internally mounted MP5K-PDW, one braces the briefcase"
" at the waist, ensures the hole is pointed at the enemy, and squeezes the "
"trigger.  Precision and handling are severely hampered by the shape of the "
"briefcase, but if you need to 'hand over the goods' or look low profile "
"while bodyguarding, this is your gun.  When the briefcase is open, the MP5 "
"may be reloaded or dismounted."
msgstr ""
"Un maletín de tapa dura con un gatillo en el mango y un agujero oculto en el"
" lateral. Para disparar el MP5K-PDW montado internamente, se sujeta el "
"maletín en la cintura, se asegura de que el maletín apunte al enemigo y se "
"aprieta el gatillo. La precisión y el manejo se ven severamente "
"obstaculizados por la forma del maletín, sin embargo si necesitas \"entregar"
" la mercancía\" o pasar desapercibido mientras estás de guardaespaldas, esta"
" es tu arma. Cuando el maletín está abierto, el MP5 puede ser recargado o "
"desmontado."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Luger P08"
msgid_plural "Luger P08s"
msgstr[0] "Luger P08"
msgstr[1] "Luger P08s"
msgstr[2] "Luger P08s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Luger P08"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic 9x19mm military issued pistol with an unusual toggle-lock "
"action.  Well-known for its use by the Germans during both World Wars, it's "
"a notably accurate handgun even by modern standards, and this example of a "
"P08 was more than likely either brought back state-side as a war trophy by a"
" veteran, or imported."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática de 9x19mm de uso militar con una inusual acción "
"de cierre de palanca. Conocida por su uso por parte de los alemanes durante "
"las dos guerras mundiales, es una pistola notablemente precisa incluso para "
"los estándares modernos, y es más que probable que este ejemplo de una P08 "
"fuera traído de vuelta al estado como trofeo de guerra por un veterano, o "
"importado."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "MP 18 submachine gun"
msgid_plural "MP 18 submachine guns"
msgstr[0] "subfusil MP 18"
msgstr[1] "subfusiles MP 18"
msgstr[2] "subfusiles MP 18"

#. ~ Description of gun "MP 18 submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"An early German submachine gun introduced near the end of the First World "
"War, the MP 18 chambers 9x19mm cartridges and makes use of Luger magazines."
"  Sporting a fixed wooden stock, the weapon more than likely entered the US "
"as a personal holdover from the Great War."
msgstr ""
"La MP 18, una de las primeras subametralladoras alemanas introducidas a "
"finales de la Primera Guerra Mundial, utiliza cartuchos de 9x19 mm y "
"cargadores Luger. Con una culata de madera fija, es más que probable que el "
"arma entrara en los Estados Unidos como un remanente personal de la Gran "
"Guerra."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "MP 18 submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Bergmann MP 18"
msgid_plural "Bergmann MP 18s"
msgstr[0] "Bergmann MP 18"
msgstr[1] "Bergmann MP 18s"
msgstr[2] "Bergmann MP 18s"

#. ~ Description of variant "MP 18 submachine gun" of gun "Bergmann MP 18"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"An incredibly rare German automatic firearm developed by Hugo Schmeisser "
"whilst working under Bergmann Waffenfabrik during 1918; the MP 18 holds the "
"reputation of being the world’s first proper and practical submachine gun.  "
"Chambered for 9x19mm and designed for use in close quarters trench-based "
"combat by assault troops, a role in which it excelled, the weapon was "
"outlawed from military use by the Versailles treaty and was relegated to "
"police and counterinsurgency use in the interwar period.  More than likely "
"entering the US as a personal holdover from the Great War, this century-old "
"grandfather to most classic SMGs just might be better off coming out of "
"retirement now that the world’s entered the true greatest war."
msgstr ""
"Una increíblemente rara arma automática alemana, desarrollada por Hugo "
"Schmeisser mientras trabajaba bajo Bergmann Waffenfabrik durante 1918. El MP"
" 18 tiene la reputación de ser el primer subfusil apropiado y práctico del "
"mundo. Con calibre 9x19mm y siendo capaz de ser usada en combate en espacios"
" cerrados por tropas de asalto, un rol en el cual se distinguió, fue "
"prohibida para uso militar en el Tratado de Versalles y fue relegada a uso "
"policial y contra insurgencia en el período entre guerras. Es probable que "
"haya ingresado a EEUU como reliquia personal de la Gran Guerra, este abuelo "
"de cien años de casi todos los subfusiles clásicos podría salir del retiro "
"ahora que el mundo entró en la verdadera Guerra Mayor."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Broomhandle pistol"
msgid_plural "Broomhandle pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola Broomhandle"
msgstr[1] "pistolas Broomhandle"
msgstr[2] "pistolas Broomhandle"

#. ~ Description of gun "Broomhandle pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A semi-automatic German pistol developed prior to 1900, the firearm features"
" a burned and painted number ‘9’ on its broom handle-shaped grip to signify "
"its chambering, 9x19mm parabellum, and makes use of appropriate stripper "
"clips or single round loading.  Quite possibly the most aesthetically "
"steampunk weapon that one could ever possibly get their hands on, this "
"example likely found its way into the US via early import or as a holdover "
"from the Great War."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de una pistola semiautomática alemana desarrollada antes de 1900, "
"que presenta un número \"9\" quemado y pintado en su empuñadura en forma de "
"palo de escoba para indicar su recámara, 9x19mm parabellum, y que hace uso "
"de los cargadores apropiados o de un solo cartucho. Posiblemente sea el arma"
" más estéticamente steampunk que uno pueda tener en sus manos, este ejemplo "
"probablemente llegó a los Estados Unidos a través de una importación "
"temprana o como un remanente de la Gran Guerra."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Broomhandle pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Mauser C96 Broomhandle"
msgid_plural "Mauser C96 Broomhandles"
msgstr[0] "Mauser C96 Broomhandle"
msgstr[1] "Mauser C96 Broomhandles"
msgstr[2] "Mauser C96 Broomhandles"

#. ~ Description of variant "Broomhandle pistol" of gun "Mauser C96
#. Broomhandle"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A late 19th century semi-automatic German pistol with an integral magazine "
"loaded from the top via stripper clips, and quite possibly the most "
"steampunk gun one could ever possibly lay their hands on.  A red number '9' "
"burned and painted into the weapon's broom handle-shaped grip marks it as a "
"variant chambered for 9x19mm rounds.  Both exported for commercial use and "
"produced for the German military during the First World War to make up for "
"production shortages of the standard Luger, this example likely entered the "
"US as a holdover from the Great War.  You suppose that it’s only fitting "
"that one of the globe’s first produced and oldest semi-automatic handguns "
"gets reinstated into service now that the planet’s facing its end."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola alemana semiautomática de finales del siglo XIX con un cargador "
"integrado que se carga desde la parte superior mediante clips de extracción,"
" y posiblemente el arma más steampunk que uno pueda tener en sus manos.  Un "
"número \"9\" rojo quemado y pintado en la empuñadura en forma de palo de "
"escoba del arma marca que se trata de una variante con recámara para balas "
"de 9x19 mm.  Tanto exportada para uso comercial como producida para el "
"ejército alemán durante la Primera Guerra Mundial, para compensar la escasez"
" de producción de la Luger estándar, este ejemplar probablemente entró en "
"los EE.UU. como un remanente de la Gran Guerra.  Supongo que es lógico que "
"una de las primeras y más antiguas pistolas semiautomáticas del mundo vuelva"
" a entrar en servicio ahora que el planeta se enfrenta a su fin."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "reproduction Broomhandle pistol"
msgid_plural "reproduction Broomhandle pistols"
msgstr[0] "réplica de pistola Broomhandle"
msgstr[1] "réplicas de pistola Broomhandle"
msgstr[2] "réplicas de pistola Broomhandle"

#. ~ Description of gun "reproduction Broomhandle pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A modern take on the original Mauser design, this variant is chambered for "
"9x19mm cartridges and, unlike its elder brother, the pre-1900 Mauser "
"Broomhandle, this firearm feeds from detachable box magazines.  Whilst it "
"features surplus Mauser parts in its construction, the frame of the pistol "
"is of relatively modern manufacture."
msgstr ""
"Una versión moderna del diseño original de Mauser.  Esta variante tiene "
"calibre 9x19mm y, a diferencia de su hermana mayor, la Mauser Broomhandle "
"anterior a 1900, se alimenta con cargadores de caja desechables.  Aunque "
"tiene partes de la Mauser en su construcción, el armazón de la pistola es de"
" producción relativamente moderna."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "reproduction Broomhandle pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "M714 Broomhandle"
msgid_plural "M714 Broomhandles"
msgstr[0] "M714 Broomhandle"
msgstr[1] "M714 Broomhandle"
msgstr[2] "M714 Broomhandle"

#. ~ Description of variant "reproduction Broomhandle pistol" of gun "M714
#. Broomhandle"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"Recognized the world over as one of the first practical self-loading "
"pistols, the Mauser C96 and its derivatives are nearly universally regarded "
"as some of the most classic and rugged guns in history, with the model being"
" praised as a true marvel of industrial craftsmanship.  However, what rests "
"before you is not an original production C96, but rather a modern American "
"spin on the original Mauser recipe.  Feeding from detachable box magazines "
"rather than an internal clip, the M714 is crafted out of a mix of modern and"
" surplus parts, being chambered for 9x19mm rounds, with some other models "
"being offered in the Mauser’s own 7.63x25mm cartridge."
msgstr ""
"Reconocida en el mundo entero como una de las primeras pistolas de auto "
"recarga, la Mauser C96 y sus derivadas son casi universalmente consideradas "
"como una de las armas más clásicas y resistentes de la historia, y su modelo"
" es elogiado como una verdadera maravilla de la fabricación industrial y la "
"mayoría de los coleccionistas desean tener una en su poder. Sin embargo, lo "
"que está frente a usted no es una producción C96 original sino una versión "
"moderna estadounidense de la receta original de Mauser. Se alimenta con "
"cargadores de caja desechables en lugar del peine interno. La M714 está "
"fabricada con una mezcla de partes modernas y sobrantes con calibre 9x19mm, "
"aunque hay algunos otros modelos que utilizan el cargador 7.63x25mm de "
"Mauser."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "MP 40 submachine gun"
msgid_plural "MP 40 submachine guns"
msgstr[0] "subfusil MP 40"
msgstr[1] "subfusiles MP 40"
msgstr[2] "subfusiles MP 40"

#. ~ Description of gun "MP 40 submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"An antique German-issued submachine gun from the Second World War, likely "
"having entered the United States as a personal holdover by a veteran.  "
"Chambered in 9x19mm and utilising proprietary box magazines, the firearm has"
" an integrated under folding wire stock."
msgstr ""
"Un subfusil antiguo alemán de la Segunda Guerra Mundial que probablemente "
"haya ingresado a Estados Unidos como una reliquia personal de algún "
"veterano. Con calibre 9x19mm, utiliza cargadores de caja propiertarios. Esta"
" arma tiene integrada una culata inferior plegable."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "MP 40 submachine gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Schmeisser MP 40"
msgid_plural "Schmeisser MP 40s"
msgstr[0] "Schmeisser MP 40"
msgstr[1] "Schmeisser MP 40"
msgstr[2] "Schmeisser MP 40"

#. ~ Description of variant "MP 40 submachine gun" of gun "Schmeisser MP 40"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A simple and renowned 9x19mm submachine gun developed by Hugo Schmeisser for"
" the German army.  Adopted  in 1940, it saw extensive service on both fronts"
" of the Second World War and was much regarded by soldiers who fielded the "
"weapon in combat, being praised for its reliability and relatively modern "
"design.  Featuring an integral folding wire butt stock, this weapon more "
"than likely entered the United States as a war trophy by a returning "
"veteran."
msgstr ""
"Un simple y reconocido subfusil 9x19mm desarrollado por Hugo Schmeisser para"
" el ejército alemán. Adoptado en 1940, cumplió un servicio extensivo en "
"ambos frentes durante la Segunda Guerra Mundial y fue apreciado por los "
"soldados que usaron esta arma en combate, siendo elogiado por su fiabilidad "
"y diseño relativamente moderno. Tiene una culata plegable integrada y es "
"probable que haya ingresado a Estados Unidos como trofeo de guerra de algún "
"veterano."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Semi Automatic MP 40"
msgid_plural "Semi Automatic MP 40s"
msgstr[0] "MP 40 semiautomática"
msgstr[1] "MP 40 semiautomáticas"
msgstr[2] "MP 40 semiautomáticas"

#. ~ Description of gun "Semi Automatic MP 40"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A modern semi-automatic replica of the MP 40 submachine gun, which lacks a "
"butt stock to make it legally be considered a pistol.  It actually bears "
"only a visual resemblance to the original, differing substantially from "
"originally manufactured MP 40 submachine guns in its internal operations."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica moderna semiautomática de la MP 40 SMG, sin culata, para que sea"
" considerada legalmente como una pistola.  En realidad sólo tiene un "
"parecido visual con la original, difiriendo sustancialmente de los MP 40 "
"fabricados originalmente en su funcionamiento interno."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Kel-Tec SUB-2000"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec SUB-2000"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec SUB-2000"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tec SUB-2000"
msgstr[2] "Kel-Tec SUB-2000"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kel-Tec SUB-2000"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"With its claim to fame being its ease of portability when compared to other "
"conventional rifles and carbines, the Kel-Tec SUB-2000 is a uniquely-"
"designed pistol caliber carbine sporting an integral folding mechanism and "
"chambered for 9x19mm cartridges, making use of regular Glock compatible "
"magazines.  With its mechanism engaged, the barrel assembly swings rearwards"
" and causes the firearm to fold to half its regular length, packing up into "
"a very compact package with ergonomics unfortunately having to take a "
"backseat to allow for the weapon’s extreme portability.  With a mainly "
"polymer constructed receiver, the carbine is relatively light and incredibly"
" transportable when fully folded."
msgstr ""
"Famosa por ser fácil de llevar cuando se la compara con otros rifles y "
"carabinas convencionales, la Kel-Tec SUB-2000 tiene diseño único con calibre"
" de pistola, mecanismo de plegado integrado y calibre 9x19mm, usando los "
"cargadores compatibles con Glock.  Cuando se activa el mecanismo plegado, el"
" cañón va hacia atrás y hace que el arma se doble a la mitad de su tamaño, "
"formando un paquete compacto perdiendo ergonomía para permitir mejorar la "
"portabilidad. Con un receptor mayormente de polímero, la carabina es "
"relativamente liviana e increíblemente transportable cuando está plegada, un"
" arma ingeniosa."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "M9 combat pistol"
msgid_plural "M9 combat pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola de combate M9"
msgstr[1] "pistolas de combate M9"
msgstr[2] "pistolas de combate M9"

#. ~ Description of gun "M9 combat pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A rugged, iconic, and long-serving 9mm handgun, the M9 is a sleek pistol "
"that has enjoyed fame in military, law enforcement, and civilian circles "
"ever since its inception.  Adopted as the primary service sidearm across all"
" United States armed branches from the early eighties until the late two "
"thousand and tens, the weapon has seen a great deal of popular media "
"coverage in both videogames and television alike."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de 9mm robusta, icónica, y de largo servicio, la M9 es una pistola "
"elegante que ha disfrutado de la fama militar, fuerzas armadas y en círculos"
" civiles desde su creación. Adoptada como el arma de servicio principal "
"alrededor de los Estados Unidos por entidades anteriores a los ochenta hasta"
" finales de dos mil diez, este arma ha tenido una cobertura mediática tanto "
"en videojuegos como televisión."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "M9 combat pistol"
#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
#: data/json/monster_special_attacks/monster_gun.json
msgid "Beretta M9A1"
msgid_plural "Beretta M9A1"
msgstr[0] "Beretta M9A1"
msgstr[1] "Beretta M9A1"
msgstr[2] "Beretta M9A1"

#. ~ Description of variant "M9 combat pistol" of gun "Beretta M9A1"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"An iconic 9x19mm pistol, the M9 was the standard issue sidearm of the US "
"armed forces from 1985 until only recently.  It was formerly popular amongst"
" law enforcement before the advent of commercially available polymer-framed "
"handguns and the FBI's adoption of .40 S&W."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola icónica de 9x19mm, la M9 fue el arma lateral estándar de las "
"fuerzas armadas de EE.UU. desde 1985 hasta hace poco.  Fue muy popular entre"
" las fuerzas del orden antes de la llegada de las pistolas con armazón de "
"polímero disponibles en el mercado y la adopción por parte del FBI de la "
".40S&W."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "M9 combat pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Beretta 90-two"
msgid_plural "Beretta 90-twos"
msgstr[0] "Beretta 90-two"
msgstr[1] "Beretta 90-twos"
msgstr[2] "Beretta 90-twos"

#. ~ Description of variant "M9 combat pistol" of gun "Beretta 90-two"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A more modern version of Beretta's popular 92 series of handguns, the 90-two"
" performs largely the same.  The main difference is a sleeker, almost "
"futuristic-looking design owed in large part to the polymer underbarrel rail"
" cover."
msgstr ""
"Una versión más moderna de la popular serie de pistolas 92 de Beretta, la "
"90-two tiene prácticamente el mismo rendimiento. La principal diferencia es "
"un diseño más elegante, casi futurista, debido en gran parte a la cubierta "
"de polímero bajo el cañón."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Beretta Px4 Storm"
msgid_plural "Beretta Px4 Storms"
msgstr[0] "Beretta Px4 Storm"
msgstr[1] "Beretta Px4 Storms"
msgstr[2] "Beretta Px4 Storms"

#. ~ Description of gun "Beretta Px4 Storm"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"Lighter than Beretta's iconic 92 series of guns, the Px4 Storm was built by "
"utilizing light-weight polymer construction with steel inserts.  Its shape "
"was also optimized for concealed carry, while maintaining the reliability "
"that the 92 series is known for."
msgstr ""
"Más ligera que la emblemática serie de pistolas 92 de Beretta, la Px4 Storm "
"se ha construido utilizando un polímero ligero con inserciones de acero. Su "
"forma también fue optimizada para el transporte oculto, manteniendo la "
"fiabilidad por la que es conocida la serie 92."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "pipe rifle: 9x19mm"
msgid_plural "pipe rifles: 9x19mm"
msgstr[0] "rifle de tubo: 9x19mm"
msgstr[1] "rifles de tubo: 9x19mm"
msgstr[2] "rifles de tubo: 9x19mm"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Luty SMG: 9x19mm"
msgid_plural "Luty SMGs: 9x19mm"
msgstr[0] "Luty SMG: 9x19mm"
msgstr[1] "Luty SMG: 9x19mm"
msgstr[2] "Luty SMG: 9x19mm"

#. ~ Description of gun "Luty SMG: 9x19mm"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A Luty pattern makeshift smoothbore SMG crudely constructed out of various "
"steel parts using advanced powered hand tools; likely one of the most "
"complex guns that is feasible to make outside of a machine shop, but still "
"very unreliable.  This one is chambered for 9x19mm cartridges and accepts "
"STEN-compatible magazines."
msgstr ""
"Un patrón de Luty hace que el subfusil de cañón liso sea construido "
"toscamente con varias piezas de acero usando algunas de las herramientas "
"manuales más avanzadas; probablemente una de las armas más complejas que son"
" factibles de hacer fuera de un taller de máquinas, pero aún así muy poco "
"fiable. Esta tiene una cámara para cartuchos de .9x19mm y acepta cargadores "
"compatibles STEN."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "STEN Mk II"
msgid_plural "STENs Mk II"
msgstr[0] "STEN Mk II"
msgstr[1] "STEN Mk II"
msgstr[2] "STEN Mk II"

#. ~ Description of gun "STEN Mk II"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The standard issue 9mm submachine gun of the British military throughout "
"most of the Second World War.  The STEN is aesthetically far from pretty.  "
"Featuring an iconic side mounted magazine well and a design optimized for "
"mass production using unskilled labor, the STEN was developed to make up for"
" drastic supply shortages during the early days of the war.  Likely entering"
" the US prior to the 1960s, either as a war time holdover or a museum "
"purchase; you suppose that if you were to try and defend your nation, "
"whatever the cost may be, and fight the undead ‘on the beaches, fight on the"
" landing grounds, fight in the fields and in the streets, fight in the "
"hills; and never surrender’, than it might be the time for the STEN to come "
"back into frontline service."
msgstr ""
"El subfusil estándar de 9mm del ejército británico durante la mayor parte de"
" la Segunda Guerra Mundial. El STEN está lejos de ser estéticamente "
"agradable. Tiene un icónico cargador montado lateral y un diseño optimizado "
"para la producción en masa utilizando trabajo no especializado. El STEN fue "
"desarrollado para suplir la drástica escasez durante los primeros días de la"
" guerra. Probablemente, fue exportado a EEUU antes de la década de 1960, ya "
"sea como reliquia o como compra para museo. Si tuvieras que intentar "
"defender tu nación, al costo que fuera necesario y luchar contra los muertos"
" vivientes 'en las playas, en zonas de aterrizaje, en los campos y en las "
"calles, en las montañas y nunca rendirse', entonces puede que sea el momento"
" de que vuelva el STEN al servicio activo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "TEC-9"
msgid_plural "TEC-9"
msgstr[0] "TEC-9"
msgstr[1] "TEC-9"
msgstr[2] "TEC-9"

#. ~ Description of gun "TEC-9"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The TEC-9 is a semi-automatic 'pistol' made of cheap polymers and machine "
"stamped parts.  Its rise in popularity among criminals is largely due to its"
" intimidating looks, low cost and relative ease of converting to fully "
"automatic."
msgstr ""
"La TEC-9 es una \"pistola\" semiautomática hecha con polímeros baratos y con"
" partes troqueladas de metal.  El aumento de su popularidad entre los "
"criminales fue a causa de su apariencia intimidante, su bajo costo y "
"relativa facilidad en convertirse en automática."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "USP 9x19mm"
msgid_plural "USP 9x19mm"
msgstr[0] "USP 9x19mm"
msgstr[1] "USP 9x19mm"
msgstr[2] "USP 9x19mm"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Uzi 9x19mm"
msgid_plural "Uzi 9x19mm"
msgstr[0] "Uzi 9x19mm"
msgstr[1] "Uzi 9x19mm"
msgstr[2] "Uzi 9x19mm"

#. ~ Description of gun "Uzi 9x19mm"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Uzi 9x19mm has enjoyed immense popularity, selling more units than any "
"other submachine gun.  It is widely used as a personal defense weapon, or as"
" a primary weapon by elite frontline forces."
msgstr ""
"La Uzi 9x19mm ha disfrutado de una popularidad inmensa, vendiendo más "
"unidades que cualquier otro subfusil. Es muy usada como arma de defensa "
"personal, o como arma primaria en las fuerzas fronterizas de elite."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Glock duty pistol"
msgid_plural "Glock duty pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola Glock reglamentaria"
msgstr[1] "pistolas Glock reglamentarias"
msgstr[2] "pistolas Glock reglamentarias"

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock duty pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"Designed for all shooters, this offering from the Glock gun company is a "
"full-sized 9x19mm pistol marketed towards law-enforcement and military "
"users."
msgstr ""
"Diseñada para todos los tiradores, esta oferta de la empresa de armas Glock "
"es una pistola de tamaño completo 9x19mm orientada comercialmente para uso "
"de las fuerzas de la ley y militares."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Glock duty pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Glock 17"
msgid_plural "Glock 17s"
msgstr[0] "Glock 17"
msgstr[1] "Glock 17s"
msgstr[2] "Glock 17s"

#. ~ Description of variant "Glock duty pistol" of gun "Glock 17"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"Commonly seen tucked away in the holsters of police officers, certain "
"military professionals, and civilian shooters, this is a larger, older, "
"service-oriented version of the popular Glock 19.  Similarly firing the "
"9x19mm cartridge and using higher capacity magazines, it performs largely "
"the same."
msgstr ""
"Típica arma que se suele ver colgando de las fundas de oficiales de policía,"
" algunos profesionales militares y tiradores civiles, una versión mas larga "
"y vieja, orientada al servicio de la popular Glock 19. Usando el mismo "
"cartucho 9x19mm y usando los mismos cargadores de alta capacidad, se "
"comporta mas o menos igual."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Glock machine pistol"
msgid_plural "Glock machine pistols"
msgstr[0] "pistola ametralladora Glock"
msgstr[1] "pistolas ametralladoras Glock"
msgstr[2] "pistolas ametralladoras Glock"

#. ~ Description of gun "Glock machine pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A military, fully automatic capable version of the popular 9x19mm handguns "
"produced by the Glock arms company, this machine pistol makes use of Glock "
"magazines.  The weapon has had its barrel modified to lessen recoil, a "
"useful feature considering its high rate of fire and lack of a default "
"buttstock."
msgstr ""
"Un versión militar, totalmente automática de las populares pistolas 9x19mm "
"producidas por la empresa de armas Glock, esta pistola automática es "
"compatible con cargadores de pistola Glock. Esta arma tiene su cañón "
"modificado para tener un menor retroceso, una mejora agradable considerando "
"el alto ratio de disparos y la falta de una culata."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Glock machine pistol"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Glock 18C"
msgid_plural "Glock 18Cs"
msgstr[0] "Glock 18C"
msgstr[1] "Glock 18Cs"
msgstr[2] "Glock 18Cs"

#. ~ Description of variant "Glock machine pistol" of gun "Glock 18C"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A selective-fire variation on the Glock 17, originally designed for "
"Austria's EKO Cobra unit.  It has compensator cuts along its barrel to make "
"recoil more manageable."
msgstr ""
"Una variación de disparo selectivo de la Glock 17, originalmente diseñada "
"para la unidad Cobra EKO de Austria. Tiene cortes compensatorios a lo largo "
"de su cañón para hacer el retroceso más manejable."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Kel-Tec PF-9"
msgid_plural "Kel-Tec PF-9s"
msgstr[0] "Kel-Tec PF-9"
msgstr[1] "Kel-Tec PF-9s"
msgstr[2] "Kel-Tec PF-9s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Kel-Tec PF-9"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Kel-Tec PF-9 remains one of the most popular backup pistols due to its "
"history of reliability, affordability, and concealability.  Chambered in "
"9x19mm, recoil is best described as unpleasant, and follow-up shots are "
"difficult to place quickly."
msgstr ""
"La Kel-Tec PF-9 sigue siendo una de las pistolas de reserva más populares "
"debido a su historial de fiabilidad, asequibilidad y capacidad de "
"ocultamiento. Con una cámara de 9x19mm, el retroceso se describe mejor como "
"desagradable, y los disparos de seguimiento son difíciles de realizar "
"rápidamente."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "M11"
msgid_plural "M11s"
msgstr[0] "M11"
msgstr[1] "M11s"
msgstr[2] "M11s"

#. ~ Description of gun "M11"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"Made by SIG Sauer, the M11 is a compact semi-automatic, short recoil "
"operated pistol, also known as the P228."
msgstr ""
"Hecha por SIG Sauer, la M11 es una pistola compacta semiautomática de "
"retroceso corto, también conocida como P228."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "service handgun"
msgid_plural "service handguns"
msgstr[0] "arma de servicio"
msgstr[1] "armas de servicio"
msgstr[2] "armas de servicio"

#. ~ Description of gun "service handgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The general-issue military handgun of the United States army before the "
"Cataclysm, this is a sizable pistol that fires 9x19mm cartridges.  Based off"
" successful civilian designs and capable of taking magazines of various "
"round capacities, the gun features a plastic polymer frame which helps to "
"reduce overall weight."
msgstr ""
"El arma reglamentaria militar del ejercito de los Estados Unidos antes del "
"Cataclismo, una pistola de tamaño considerable que dispara munición 9x19mm. "
"Basado en exitosos diseños civiles y capaz de aceptar cargadores de varios "
"tipos de capacidades de munición, con un chasis de plástico de polímeros que"
" ayuda a reducir el peso total."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "service handgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "M17"
msgid_plural "M17s"
msgstr[0] "M17"
msgstr[1] "M17s"
msgstr[2] "M17s"

#. ~ Description of variant "service handgun" of gun "M17"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The M17 is an army issued semi-automatic, short recoil operated pistol "
"derived from the SIG Sauer P320."
msgstr ""
"La M17 es una pistola semiautomática, de retroceso corto, derivada de la SIG"
" Sauer P320."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "compact service handgun"
msgid_plural "compact service handguns"
msgstr[0] "arma de servicio compacta"
msgstr[1] "armas de servicio compactas"
msgstr[2] "armas de servicio compactas"

#. ~ Description of gun "compact service handgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A more petite version of the United States army’s general issue sidearm, "
"this is a modestly-sized pistol firing 9x19mm rounds.  Making use of the "
"same magazines as its larger brother, the weapon features a shorter barrel "
"and frame which helps to reduce its overall profile and make it more "
"concealable as a result."
msgstr ""
"Una versión mas pequeña del arma reglamentaria del ejercito de los Estados "
"Unidos, esta modestamente pequeña pistola dispara munición calibre 9x19mm. "
"Haciendo uso de los mismos cargadores que su hermano mayor, este arma tiene "
"un cañón y chasis mas corto que ayuda a reducir su perfil haciendo que sea "
"mas fácil ocultarlo."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "compact service handgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "M18"
msgid_plural "M18s"
msgstr[0] "M18"
msgstr[1] "M18s"
msgstr[2] "M18s"

#. ~ Description of variant "compact service handgun" of gun "M18"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The M18 is a compact, semi-automatic, short recoil operated pistol derived "
"from the SIG Sauer P320 Carry, used by US Armed Forces.  Practically the "
"same as its big brother, the M17, in every respect, the M18 features a "
"moderately shorter slide and barrel which terminates at the end of the frame"
" rather than extending partway beyond it like the M17."
msgstr ""
"La M18 es una pistola compacta, semiautomática de poco retroceso derivada de"
" la SIG Sauer P320 Carry, utilizada por las fuerzas armadas estadounidenses."
"  Prácticamente igual a su hermana mayor, la M17, en todo, la M18 tiene una "
"corredera y un cañón moderadamente más corto que termina en el armazón en "
"lugar de extenderse más allá como en la M17."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "SIG P226 MK25"
msgid_plural "SIG P226 MK25s"
msgstr[0] "SIG P226 MK25"
msgstr[1] "SIG P226 MK25s"
msgstr[2] "SIG P226 MK25s"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG P226 MK25"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The P226 MK25 is a full-size semi-automatic DA/SA, short-recoil operated "
"pistol with corrosion-resistant internal coating and an engraved anchor on "
"the side of the slide."
msgstr ""
"La P226 MK25 es una pistola semiautomática DA/SA de tamaño completo, con "
"retroceso corto, revestimiento interno resistente a la corrosión y un ancla "
"grabada en el lateral de la corredera."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "SIG Pro SP2022 9mm"
msgid_plural "SIG Pro SP2022 9mms"
msgstr[0] "SIG Pro SP2022 9mm"
msgstr[1] "SIG Pro SP2022 9mms"
msgstr[2] "SIG Pro SP2022 9mms"

#. ~ Description of gun "SIG Pro SP2022 9mm"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A polymer-frame, semi-automatic, DA/SA operated pistol, featuring a "
"Picatinny rail and a Nitron stainless steel slide."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola semiautomática con armazón de polímero, de funcionamiento DA/SA,"
" con carril Picatinny y corredera de acero inoxidable Nitron."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Browning Hi-Power 9x19mm"
msgid_plural "Browning Hi-Power 9x19mms"
msgstr[0] "Browning Hi-Power 9x19mm"
msgstr[1] "Browning Hi-Power 9x19mms"
msgstr[2] "Browning Hi-Power 9x19mms"

#. ~ Description of gun "Browning Hi-Power 9x19mm"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Browning Hi-Power is a semi-automatic handgun developed shortly before "
"the Second World War.  Widely issued since then, it remains in use by India,"
" Canada, and Australia.  This is a commercial variant produced by Browning "
"Arms in 9x19mm Parabellum."
msgstr ""
"La Browning Hi-Power es un arma de mano semiautomática desarrollada poco "
"antes de la Segunda Guerra Mundial. Muy usada desde entonces, sigue en uso "
"en India, Canadá y Australia. Esta es la versión comercial producida por "
"Browning Arms con calibre 9x19mm Parabellum."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Walther P38"
msgid_plural "Walther P38s"
msgstr[0] "Walther P38"
msgstr[1] "Walther P38s"
msgstr[2] "Walther P38s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Walther P38"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Walther P38 is a semi-automatic handgun adopted shortly before the "
"Second World War.  Developed due to the high production costs of its "
"predecessor, the Luger P08, the P38 is also chambered in 9mm Parabellum.  "
"This early DA/SA locked-breech design would introduce features later seen on"
" more modern firearms such as the Beretta 92 series, and served Germany "
"until 2004."
msgstr ""
"La Walther P38 es una pistola semiautomática adoptada poco antes de la "
"segunda guerra mundial. Desarrollada debido al alto coste de producción de "
"su predecesora, la Luger P08, la P38 también tiene la recamara Parabellum de"
" 9 mm. Este temprano diseño de cierre DA/SA introduciría características que"
" más tarde se verían en armas de fuego más modernas como la serie Beretta "
"92, y sirvió a Alemania hasta 2004."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Walther PPQ 9mm"
msgid_plural "Walther PPQ 9mms"
msgstr[0] "Walther PPQ 9mm"
msgstr[1] "Walther PPQ 9mms"
msgstr[2] "Walther PPQ 9mms"

#. ~ Description of gun "Walther PPQ 9mm"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Walther PPQ is a semi-automatic pistol originating from the Walther "
"P99QA, and maintains compatibility with some of its predecessor's "
"accessories.  This model is chambered in 9x19mm Parabellum."
msgstr ""
"La Walther PPQ es una pistola semiautomática originada en la Walther P99QA, "
"y mantiene la compatibilidad con algunos de los accesorios de su "
"predecesora. Este modelo tiene una cámara de 9x19mm Parabellum."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Hi-Point C-9"
msgid_plural "Hi-Point C-9s"
msgstr[0] "Hi-Point C-9"
msgstr[1] "Hi-Point C-9s"
msgstr[2] "Hi-Point C-9s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Hi-Point C-9"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Hi-Point C-9 is a blowback operated semi-automatic pistol designed by "
"Hi-Point Firearms, which is known for making inexpensive firearms, and for "
"making said firearms bulky and uncomfortable.  Hi-Points have slides made "
"with a zinc pot-metal which is relatively fragile compared to steel slides."
msgstr ""
"La Hi-Point C-9 es una pistola semiautomática operada por retroceso diseñada"
" por Hi-Point Firearms, conocida por fabricar armas de fuego baratas y por "
"hacer dichas armas voluminosas e incómodas. Hi-Point tiene correderas hechos"
" con una aleación de zinc que es relativamente frágil comparado con las "
"correderas de acero."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "CZ 75 B"
msgid_plural "CZ 75 Bs"
msgstr[0] "CZ 75 B"
msgstr[1] "CZ 75 Bs"
msgstr[2] "CZ 75 Bs"

#. ~ Description of gun "CZ 75 B"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The CZ 75 B is a semi-automatic pistol developed in Czechoslovakia, and is "
"one of the original wonder nines.  Though designed for export to western "
"countries, it was declared a state secret; lack of international patent "
"protection meant that many clones and variants were produced and distributed"
" around the world, with Česká zbrojovka only joining in the 90's.  This "
"pistol remains wildly popular among competition shooters."
msgstr ""
"La CZ 75 B es una pistola semiautomática desarrollada en Checoslovaquia, y "
"es una de las wonder nines originales. Aunque se diseñó para su exportación "
"a los países occidentales, fue declarada secreto de Estado; la falta de "
"protección internacional de patentes hizo que se produjeran y distribuyeran "
"muchos clones y variantes en todo el mundo, a los que sólo se sumó Česká "
"zbrojovka en los años 90. Esta pistola sigue siendo muy popular entre los "
"tiradores de competición."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Walther CCP"
msgid_plural "Walther CCPs"
msgstr[0] "Walther CCP"
msgstr[1] "Walther CCPs"
msgstr[2] "Walther CCPs"

#. ~ Description of gun "Walther CCP"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Walther CCP is a gas-delayed blowback semi-automatic pistol intended for"
" the concealed carry consumer market.  Internally, it is nearly identical to"
" the cult classic H&K P7.  Its fixed barrel design makes it potentially more"
" accurate than many other pistols, though this may be difficult to realize "
"with its average trigger and short sight radius."
msgstr ""
"La Walther CCP es una pistola semiautomática de retroceso retardado por gas "
"destinada al mercado de consumidores de transporte oculto.  Internamente, es"
" casi idéntica al clásico de culto H&K P7.  Su diseño de cañón fijo la hace "
"potencialmente más precisa que muchas otras pistolas, aunque esto puede ser "
"difícil de hacer con su gatillo medio y su radio de visión corto."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "Colt Model 635"
msgid_plural "Colt Model 635s"
msgstr[0] "Colt Model 635"
msgstr[1] "Colt Model 635s"
msgstr[2] "Colt Model 635s"

#. ~ Description of gun "Colt Model 635"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"A 9x19mm submachine gun based on the M16 rifle design, it is a closed bolt, "
"blowback operated firearm.  There is a large plastic brass deflector mounted"
" by the ejection port, and no forward assist.  It looks very similar to an "
"M4 carbine, except for the magazine well that accepts Uzi-style magazines."
msgstr ""
"Un subfusil de 9x19mm basado en el diseño del fusil M16. Es un arma de "
"cerrojo cerrado, operada por retroceso. Hay un gran deflector de latón "
"montado junto al puerto de eyección y no hay asistencia de avance. Su "
"aspecto es muy similar al de una carabina M4, excepto por el hueco del "
"cargador, que acepta cargadores de tipo Uzi."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid "B&T APC9 PRO K"
msgid_plural "B&T APC9 PRO Ks"
msgstr[0] "B&T APC9 PRO K"
msgstr[1] "B&T APC9 PRO Ks"
msgstr[2] "B&T APC9 PRO Ks"

#. ~ Description of gun "B&T APC9 PRO K"
#: data/json/items/gun/9mm.json
msgid ""
"The Brügger & Thomet APC9 PRO K is a closed bolt blowback submachine gun in "
"9x19mm Parabellum.  It has a collapsible shoulder stock and a red dot sight."
msgstr ""
"El Brügger & Thomet APC9 PRO K es un subfusil de recámara cerrada y "
"retroceso diferido, con calibre 9x19mm Parabellum. Tiene culata plegable "
"para hombro y mirilla de punto rojo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9x18.json
msgid "Makarov PM"
msgid_plural "Makarov PMs"
msgstr[0] "Makarov PM"
msgstr[1] "Makarov PM"
msgstr[2] "Makarov PM"

#. ~ Description of gun "Makarov PM"
#: data/json/items/gun/9x18.json
msgid ""
"The Pistolet Makarova was developed by the Soviet Union to replace the WWII-"
"era TT-33 pistol.  It uses the 9x18mm cartridge, which remains in use among "
"various former Soviet countries."
msgstr ""
"La Pistolet Makarova fue desarrollada por la Unión Soviética para reemplazar"
" la pistola TT-33 de la Segunda Guerra Mundial. Utiliza el cartucho de "
"9x18mm, que sigue siendo utilizado por varios países de la antigua Unión "
"Soviética."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/9x18.json
msgid "Škorpion vz. 82"
msgid_plural "Škorpion vz. 82s"
msgstr[0] "Škorpion vz. 82"
msgstr[1] "Škorpion vz. 82"
msgstr[2] "Škorpion vz. 82"

#. ~ Description of gun "Škorpion vz. 82"
#: data/json/items/gun/9x18.json
msgid ""
"A version of the Škorpion submachine gun chambered in 9x18mm Makarov, with a"
" slightly longer barrel than the original design."
msgstr ""
"Una versión del subfusil Škorpion con calibre 9x18mm Makarov, con el cañón "
"un poco más largo que el diseño original."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid "the Obrez"
msgid_plural "the Obrez"
msgstr[0] "el Obrez"
msgstr[1] "el Obrez"
msgstr[2] "el Obrez"

#. ~ Description of gun "the Obrez"
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid ""
"A cut-down, modified Mosin-Nagant.  It has a short barrel and the stock has "
"been cut down and fitted with a mace head, with new low profile front and "
"rear sights added.  The sides of the firearm have been reinforced with metal"
" to withstand a beating."
msgstr ""
"Un Mosin-Nagant cortado y modificado. Tiene el cañón corto y la culata ha "
"sido cortada y reemplazada con una especie de maza, con miras de perfil bajo"
" añadidas delante y detras. Los costados del arma han sido reforzados con "
"metal para soportar los golpes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid "the Disorder"
msgid_plural "the Disorders"
msgstr[0] "el Disorder"
msgstr[1] "el Disorder"
msgstr[2] "el Disorder"

#. ~ Description of "the Disorder"
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy sledge hammer converted for use as a weapon.  It features a "
"notable safety on the side, and the back of the head has a firing mechanism "
"that can be loaded with rifle blanks.  When the head impacts and the safety "
"is off, the blanks are engaged, sending the moving piston forward and "
"causing massive damage.  Etched into the head are the words 'she's lost "
"control'."
msgstr ""
"Una almádena grande y pesada convertida para ser usada como arma. Tiene un "
"seguro notable en el lateral y en la parte trasera la punta tiene un "
"mecanismo de disparo que puede ser cargado con balas de salva de rifle. "
"Cuando la cabeza impacta y el seguro no está puesto, las salvas se activan "
"enviando un pistón hacia adelante causando un daño enorme. En la cabeza, "
"tiene grabadas las palabras 'está fuera de control'."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid "the Louverture"
msgid_plural "the Louverture"
msgstr[0] "la Louverture"
msgstr[1] "la Louverture"
msgstr[2] "la Louverture"

#. ~ Description of "the Louverture"
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid ""
"An oddly-vented mace with an internal fuel reservoir built into the pommel."
"  Can be engaged to ignite large puffs of gasoline and start fires."
msgstr ""
"Una maza con unos tajos extraños y un tanque de combustible en el pomo. "
"Puede usarse para encender grandes nubes de gasolina y prender fuego."

#. ~ Spell name
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid "Ignite Gasoline"
msgstr "Encender Gasolina"

#. ~ Description of spell "Ignite Gasoline"
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid "Releases a blast of ignited gasoline directly in front of you."
msgstr "Larga una ráfaga de gasolina encendida directamente delante tuyo."

#. ~ Message of spell "Ignite Gasoline"
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid "with a crack a cloud of gasoline ignites!"
msgstr "con un chasquido se enciende una nube de gasolina!"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid "the Pressin"
msgid_plural "the Pressin"
msgstr[0] "la Pressin"
msgstr[1] "la Pressin"
msgstr[2] "la Pressin"

#. ~ Description of gun "the Pressin"
#: data/json/items/gun/artisan_guns.json
msgid ""
"A compact short-range pistol without a pistol grip.  When in use, the entire"
" gun body is pointed at targets and squeezed.  The body also conceals a "
"switchblade for close quarters use."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola compacta de corto alcance sin mango.  Cuando se usa, toda el "
"arma se apunta al objetivo y se aprieta el gatillo.  El armazón también "
"esconde una navaja para usar en combate cuerpo a cuerpo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/atgm.json
msgid "BGM-71F TOW"
msgid_plural "BGM-71F TOW"
msgstr[0] "BGM-71F TOW"
msgstr[1] "BGM-71F TOW"
msgstr[2] "BGM-71F TOW"

#. ~ Description of gun "BGM-71F TOW"
#: data/json/items/gun/atgm.json
msgid ""
"A launcher for anti-tank guided missiles, capable of being deployed as a "
"crew-served weapon or mounted on vehicles.  While fairly accurate, it isn't "
"fire-and-forget."
msgstr ""
"Es un lanzador de misiles anti-tanque guiados, capaz de ser desplegado como "
"arma de manejo en equipo, o montado en un vehículo. Aunque es bastante "
"preciso, no es cuestión de un disparo y listo."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/bio.json data/mods/Generic_Guns/firearms/shot.json
msgid "bionic shotgun"
msgid_plural "bionic shotguns"
msgstr[0] "escopeta biónica"
msgstr[1] "escopetas biónicas"
msgstr[2] "escopetas biónicas"

#. ~ Description of gun "bionic shotgun"
#: data/json/items/gun/bio.json
msgid "Bionic one-shot retracting shotgun integrated with your arm."
msgstr "Escopeta biónica de un solo disparo retráctil integrada en tu brazo."

#. ~ Description of gun "EMP Projector"
#. ~ Description of gun "laser finger"
#. ~ Description of gun "Chain Lightning"
#. ~ Description of gun "Assault barbs"
#. ~ Description of gun "Ranged pulling implement"
#. ~ Description of "bio lockpick"
#: data/json/items/gun/bio.json data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "this a pseudo item"
msgstr "esto es un pseudo objeto"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/bio.json
msgid "laser finger"
msgid_plural "laser fingers"
msgstr[0] "dedo láser"
msgstr[1] "dedos láser"
msgstr[2] "dedos láser"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/bio.json
msgid "Assault barbs"
msgid_plural "Assault barbs"
msgstr[0] "Púas de asalto"
msgstr[1] "Púas de asalto"
msgstr[2] "Púas de asalto"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/bio.json
msgid "Ranged pulling implement"
msgid_plural "Ranged pulling implements"
msgstr[0] "Herramienta de empuje de rango"
msgstr[1] "Herramientas de empuje de rango"
msgstr[2] "Herramientas de empuje de rango"

#. ~ Description of gun "blunderbuss"
#: data/json/items/gun/blunderbuss.json
msgid "A homemade version of a crude precursor to the shotgun."
msgstr "Una versión casera de un burdo precursor de la escopeta."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/cannon.json
msgid "3-inch ordnance rifle"
msgid_plural "3-inch ordnance rifles"
msgstr[0] "fusiles de artillería de 3 pulgadas"
msgstr[1] "fusiles de artillería de 3 pulgadas"
msgstr[2] "fusiles de artillería de 3 pulgadas"

#. ~ Description of gun "3-inch ordnance rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/cannon.json
msgid ""
"A light cannon widely used in the American Civil War, noted for its "
"reliability."
msgstr ""
"Un cañón ligero muy utilizado en la Guerra de Secesión Estadounidense, que "
"destacó por su fiabilidad."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/chemical_spray.json
msgid "makeshift chemical thrower"
msgid_plural "makeshift chemical throwers"
msgstr[0] "lanzador químico improvisado"
msgstr[1] "lanzadores químicos improvisados"
msgstr[2] "lanzadores químicos improvisados"

#. ~ Description of gun "makeshift chemical thrower"
#: data/json/items/gun/chemical_spray.json
msgid ""
"A bulky, self-made chemical sprayer with an internal conversion mechanism "
"that allows all sorts of chemicals to be dispersed to your surroundings."
msgstr ""
"Un voluminoso rociador químico, con un mecanismo de conversión interno que "
"permite rociar toda clase de químicos a tu alrededor."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/combination.json
msgid "combination gun"
msgid_plural "combination guns"
msgstr[0] "pistola combinada"
msgstr[1] "pistolas combinadas"
msgstr[2] "pistolas combinadas"

#. ~ Description of gun "combination gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/combination.json
msgid ""
"A break action firearm comprised of a .30-06 barrel over two 12 gauge smooth"
" bore barrels.  Historically used by egomaniac hunters in Africa, now used "
"by their egomaniac descendants in New England."
msgstr ""
"Arma de cañón rompedora compuesta por un cañón .30-06 sobre dos cañones "
"suaves de calibre 12 gauge. Históricamente usada por los cazadores "
"egocéntricos en África, ahora es usada por los descendientes egocéntricos en"
" Nueva Inglaterra."

#. ~ Valid mod location of gun "combination gun"
#: data/json/items/gun/combination.json
msgid "conversion"
msgstr "conversión"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid "Exodii battle rifle"
msgid_plural "Exodii battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de combate Exodii"
msgstr[1] "rifles de combate Exodii"
msgstr[2] "rifles de combate Exodii"

#. ~ Description of gun "Exodii battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Exodii battle rifle" of gun "PA md. 68"
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid ""
"The most popular gun to use the 12.3ln cartridge was, of course, the PA md. "
"71.  Its predecessor, the md. 68, was viewed by many as a sort of failure: "
"although it was reliable and powerful, it was too heavy to be used as a good"
" infantry weapon, and not really heavy enough to be a good support gun.  "
"Enough were made, though, that during the zombie apocalypse, it gained a "
"great deal of resurgent popularity as a light emplacement gun that used "
"readily available ammunition.  It perfectly served the purposes of the "
"Exodii, who had far less concern about its unwieldiness."
msgstr ""
"El arma más popular que utilizaba el cartucho de 12,3ln era, por supuesto, "
"la PA md. 71. Su predecesor, el md. 68, fue visto por muchos como una "
"especie de fracaso: aunque era fiable y potente, era demasiado pesado para "
"ser utilizado como un buen arma de infantería, y no lo suficientemente "
"pesado para ser un buen arma de apoyo. Sin embargo, se fabricó lo suficiente"
" como para que, durante el apocalipsis zombi, ganara una gran popularidad "
"como arma ligera de emplazamiento que utilizaba munición fácilmente "
"disponible. Servía perfectamente a los propósitos de los Exodii, a quienes "
"les preocupaba mucho menos su falta de manejo."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Exodii battle rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid "PA md. 68"
msgid_plural "PA md. 68s"
msgstr[0] "PA md. 68"
msgstr[1] "PA md. 68s"
msgstr[2] "PA md. 68s"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid "Exodii zombie hunting rifle"
msgid_plural "Exodii zombie hunting rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de caza zombie exodii"
msgstr[1] "rifles de caza zombi exodii"
msgstr[2] "rifles de caza zombi exodii"

#. ~ Description of gun "Exodii zombie hunting rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "Exodii zombie hunting rifle" of gun "PS md. 71z"
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid ""
"This extremely popular Romanian rifle, made famous in the third Carpathian "
"War, has been redesigned slightly by the Exodii for precision shots against "
"high-priority targets.  In a pinch this modified design can fire an "
"extremely rapid 2-shot burst, with the goal of shredding the target and "
"preventing revivification."
msgstr ""
"Este rifle rumano extremadamente popular, que llegó a la fama en la tercera "
"Guerra de los Cárpatos, fue rediseñada levemente por los Exodii para "
"realizar tiros precisos contra objetivos prioritarios. En caso de necesidad,"
" este diseño modificado puede disparar una ráfaga extremadamente rápida de 2"
" tiros, con la intención de destrozar el objetivo y evitar la "
"revitalización."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "Exodii zombie hunting rifle"
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid "PS md. 71z"
msgid_plural "PS md. 71zs"
msgstr[0] "PS md. 71z"
msgstr[1] "PS md. 71z"
msgstr[2] "PS md. 71z"

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid "mountable PA md. 68 battle rifle"
msgid_plural "mountable PA md. 68 battle rifles"
msgstr[0] "rifle de combate PA md. 68 montable"
msgstr[1] "rifles de combate PA md. 68 montables"
msgstr[2] "rifles de combate PA md. 68 montables"

#. ~ Description of gun "mountable PA md. 68 battle rifle"
#. ~ Description of variant "mountable PA md. 68 battle rifle" of gun
#. "Mountable PA md. 68"
#: data/json/items/gun/exodii.json
msgid ""
"The most popular gun to use the 12.3ln cartridge was, of course, the PA md. "
"71.  Its predecessor, the md. 68, was viewed by many as a sort of failure: "
"although it was reliable and powerful, it was too heavy to be used as a good"
" infantry weapon, and not really heavy enough to be a good support gun.  "
"Enough were made, though, that during the zombie apocalypse, it gained a "
"great deal of resurgent popularity as a light emplacement gun that used "
"readily available ammunition.  It perfectly served the purposes of the "
"Exodii, who had far less concern about its unwieldiness.  This one has been "
"modified for use in vehicle turrets on Earth."
msgstr ""
"El arma más popular que utilizaba el cartucho de 12,3ln era, por supuesto, "
"la PA md. 71. Su predecesor, el md. 68, fue visto por muchos como una "
"especie de fracaso: aunque era fiable y potente, era demasiado pesado para "
"ser utilizado como un buen arma de infantería, y no lo suficientemente "
"pesado para ser un buen arma de apoyo. Sin embargo, se fabricó lo suficiente"
" como para que, durante el apocalipsis zombi, ganara una gran popularidad "
"como arma ligera de emplazamiento que utilizaba munición fácilmente "
"disponible. Servía perfectamente a los propósitos de los Exodii, a quienes "
"les preocupaba mucho menos su falta de manejo. Este ha sido modificado para "
"su uso en torretas de vehículos en la Tierra."

#. ~ Variant name of gun "mountable PA md. 68 battle rifle"
