msgstr ""
"Una enorme hacha diseñada para la guerra. Aunque fue pensada para usar como "
"arma, también puede servir como una torpe herramienta para cortar madera."

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A dull, cheaply-made replica of a huge axe designed for warfare."
msgstr "Una réplica sosa sin filo de un hacha enorme diseñada para la guerra."

#. ~ Description of "battle axe"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A huge axe designed for warfare.  Or it would be, but the axe heads aren't "
"seated properly at all."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme hacha diseñada para la guerra. O podría serlo si no fuera porque "
"la cabeza del hacha no está bien asentada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "blackjack"
msgid_plural "blackjacks"
msgstr[0] "blackjack(arma)"
msgstr[1] "blackjacks(armas)"
msgstr[2] "blackjacks(armas)"

#. ~ Description of "blackjack"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A short, easily concealed bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight embedded"
" at the end of a short leather shaft.  Formerly used by law enforcement, "
"this weapon is meant to stun or knock out the subject, although head strikes"
" have a high risk of causing a permanent, disabling brain injury or being "
"fatal."
msgstr ""
"Un arma corta contundente fácil de esconder, que consiste en un peso metido "
"en la punta de un mango de cuero. Usada anteriormente por las fuerzas de la "
"ley, esta arma está pensada para aturdir o noquear al objetivo, aunque los "
"golpes en la cabeza tiene un alto riesgo de causar un daño cerebral "
"permanente o de ser fatales."

#. ~ Not actually as damaging as a steel katana, by any stretch.  It's a
#. fancy, very well-carved wooden training sword, not a weapon of war.  It's
#. also completely rounded, so any cutting damage wouldn't make sense.  Also,
#. the heaviest bokken I could find were 700g, none were nearly close to a
#. kilogram.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bokken"
msgid_plural "bokken"
msgstr[0] "bokken"
msgstr[1] "bokkens"
msgstr[2] "bokkens"

#. ~ Not actually as damaging as a steel katana, by any stretch.  It's a
#. fancy, very well-carved wooden training sword, not a weapon of war.  It's
#. also completely rounded, so any cutting damage wouldn't make sense.  Also,
#. the heaviest bokken I could find were 700g, none were nearly close to a
#. kilogram.
#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A solid wood 'training' katana, exactingly crafted to mimic the weight and "
"balance of the real thing.  Despite its lack of a sharp metal edge, it's "
"still quite capable of inflicting deadly wounds."
msgstr ""
"Una katana de madera de entrenamiento, estrictamente fabricada para ser "
"igual en peso y balance a la verdadera. Más allá de su falta de filo de "
"metal, es capaz de infligir heridas mortales."

#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A solid wood 'training' katana.  It feels far too light to make an effective"
" weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una buena katana de madera de entrenamiento. Se siente demasiado liviana "
"como para actuar efectivamente como arma."

#. ~ Description of "bokken"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A solid wood 'training' katana.  It looks to be mass-produced, and not quite"
" as effective as the real deal."
msgstr ""
"Una buena katana de madera de entrenamiento. Parece producida en masa y no "
"tan efectiva como una de en serio."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The 7-10 Split"
msgid_plural "7-10 Splits"
msgstr[0] "The 7-10 Split"
msgstr[1] "7-10 Splits"
msgstr[2] "7-10 Splits"

#. ~ Description of "The 7-10 Split"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An improvised weapon made from a bowling pin with two spikes attached in the"
" shape of a 'T'."
msgstr ""
"Un arma improvisada hecha con dos puntas adheridas a un bolo formando una "
"'T'."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bowling pin"
msgid_plural "bowling pins"
msgstr[0] "bolo"
msgstr[1] "bolos"
msgstr[2] "bolos"

#. ~ Description of "bowling pin"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A standard bowling pin.  Makes a decent melee weapon, if somewhat short."
msgstr ""
"Un bolo de bolera romo. Una arma decente para c. a c., aunque un poco corta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "barbed wire bat"
msgid_plural "barbed wire bats"
msgstr[0] "bate con alambre de púas"
msgstr[1] "bates con alambre de púas"
msgstr[2] "bates con alambre de púas"

#. ~ Description of "barbed wire bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A baseball bat wrapped with barbed wire.  A brutal melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un bate de béisbol envuelto con alambre de púas. Un arma brutal c. a c."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "walking cane"
msgid_plural "walking canes"
msgstr[0] "bastón"
msgstr[1] "bastones"
msgstr[2] "bastones"

#. ~ Description of "walking cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Handicapped or not, you always walk in style.  Consisting of a metal "
"headpiece and a wooden body, this makes a great bashing weapon in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Discapacitado o no, con esto siempre caminas con estilo. Consiste en un "
"cabezal de metal en un cuerpo de madera, una buena arma contundente en caso "
"de necesidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "sinister cane"
msgid_plural "sinister canes"
msgstr[0] "bastón siniestro"
msgstr[1] "bastones siniestros"
msgstr[2] "bastones siniestros"

#. ~ Description of "sinister cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sinister looking cane made of plastic.  It has a shiny red orb gripped by "
"claws at the handle."
msgstr ""
"Un bastón de plástico de aspecto siniestro. Tiene una esfera brillante roja "
"en las garras del mango."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "cheap wizard cane (off)"
msgid_plural "cheap wizard canes (off)"
msgstr[0] "bastón barato de mago (apag.)"
msgstr[1] "bastones baratos de mago (apag.)"
msgstr[2] "bastones baratos de mago (apag.)"

#. ~ Description of "cheap wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An arcane but cheap-looking cane made of plastic.  It has a white light-up "
"orb on the end.  Using it will turn it on and provide a weak light."
msgstr ""
"Un bastón de aspecto arcano que parece barato, está hecho de plástico. Tiene"
" una esfera blanca que se prende en la punta. La puedes encender para que "
"emita una luz débil con el comando Usar."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "cheap wizard cane (off)"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You turn the wizard cane on."
msgstr "Enciendes el bastón de mago."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "cheap wizard cane (off)"
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The wizard cane's batteries are dead."
msgstr "El bastón de mago se quedó sin pilas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "cheap wizard cane (on)"
msgid_plural "cheap wizard canes (on)"
msgstr[0] "bastón barato de mago (enc.)"
msgstr[1] "bastones baratos de mago (enc.)"
msgstr[2] "bastones baratos de mago (enc.)"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "cheap wizard cane (on)"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "wizard cane (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You turn the wizard cane off."
msgstr "Apagas el bastón de mago."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wizard cane (off)"
msgid_plural "wizard canes (off)"
msgstr[0] "bastón de mago (apag.)"
msgstr[1] "bastones de mago (apag.)"
msgstr[2] "bastones de mago (apag.)"

#. ~ Description of "wizard cane (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An arcane-looking cane made of wood and aluminum.  It has a white light-up "
"orb on the end.  Using it will turn it on and illuminate the area around "
"you."
msgstr ""
"Un bastón de aspecto arcano hecho de madera y aluminio. Tiene una esfera "
"blanca que se prende en la punta. La puedes encender para que ilumine los "
"alrededores con el comando Usar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wizard cane (on)"
msgid_plural "wizard canes (on)"
msgstr[0] "bastón de mago (enc.)"
msgstr[1] "bastones de mago (enc.)"
msgstr[2] "bastones de mago (enc.)"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift walking cane"
msgid_plural "makeshift walking canes"
msgstr[0] "bastón improvisado"
msgstr[1] "bastones improvisados"
msgstr[2] "bastones improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift walking cane"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An improvised cane.  It also works as a basic bashing weapon in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Un bastón improvisado. También funciona como arma básica para golpear en "
"caso de necesidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wooden club"
msgid_plural "wooden clubs"
msgstr[0] "garrote de madera"
msgstr[1] "garrotes de madera"
msgstr[2] "garrotes de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A plank of wood that's been snapped in half, with a crude handle whittled "
"into one end.  It looks like a poorly-made cricket bat."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera partido por la mitad, con un mango rudimentario tallado "
"en una punta. Parece un bate de cricket mal hecho."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "large wooden club"
msgid_plural "large wooden clubs"
msgstr[0] "garrote grande de madera"
msgstr[1] "garrotes grandes de madera"
msgstr[2] "garrotes grandes de madera"

#. ~ Description of "large wooden club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long plank of wood with a crude handle whittled into one end.  It's barely"
" an improvement, but at least it is slightly easier to wield than just the "
"plank on its own."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón largo de madera con un mango rudimentario tallado en una punta. "
"Apenas si es una mejora pero por lo menos es un poco más fácil de empuñar "
"que un tablón común."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "crutches"
msgid_plural "pairs of crutches"
msgstr[0] "par de muletas"
msgstr[1] "pares de muletas"
msgstr[2] "pares de muletas"

#. ~ Description of "crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A pair of crutches."
msgstr "Un par de muletas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift crutches"
msgid_plural "pairs of makeshift crutches"
msgstr[0] "muletas improvisadas"
msgstr[1] "pares de muletas improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "pares de muletas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift crutches"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A pair of wooden makeshift crutches."
msgstr "Un par de muletas de madera improvisadas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json data/mods/MMA/bludgeons.json
msgid "cudgel"
msgid_plural "cudgels"
msgstr[0] "porra"
msgstr[1] "porras"
msgstr[2] "porras"

#. ~ Description of "cudgel"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long, slender wooden rod.  While traditionally intended as a training "
"tool, it still makes a good melee weapon in a pinch."
msgstr ""
"Es un palo fino y largo de madera. Aunque tradicionalmente se usa para "
"entrenar, es también una buena arma de c. a c. en caso de necesidad."

#. ~ Id retained to avoid breaking anything, same reason as with the makeshift
#. glaive.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift macuahuitl"
msgid_plural "makeshift macuahuitls"
msgstr[0] "macuahuitl improvisado"
msgstr[1] "macuahuitl improvisados"
msgstr[2] "macuahuitl improvisados"

#. ~ Id retained to avoid breaking anything, same reason as with the makeshift
#. glaive.
#. ~ Description of "makeshift macuahuitl"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A flat wooden club with sharpened pieces of stone stuck to both sides."
msgstr ""
"Un garrote plano de madera con fragmentos afilados de piedra sobresaliendo "
"de los dos lados."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "glass shiv"
msgid_plural "glass shivs"
msgstr[0] "navaja carcelaria de cristal"
msgstr[1] "navajas carcelarias de cristal"
msgstr[2] "navajas carcelarias de cristal"

#. ~ Description of "glass shiv"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A glass shard with wrapping at one end so it can be safely wielded."
msgstr ""
"Un fragmento de cristal con una punta envuelta con un trapo para que pueda "
"ser empuñado fácilmente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/weapons.json
msgid "golf club"
msgid_plural "golf clubs"
msgstr[0] "palo de golf"
msgstr[1] "palos de golf"
msgstr[2] "palos de golf"

#. ~ Description of "golf club"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long handle with a big metal head, flat on one side, for driving golf "
"balls.  Fore!"
msgstr ""
"Un mango largo con un cabezal grande de metal, chato de un lado, hecho para "
"golpear pelotas de golf. ¡Fore!"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "almádena"
msgstr[1] "almádenas"
msgstr[2] "almádenas"

#. ~ Description of "sledge hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large, heavy hammer.  A very hard-hitting melee weapon, but it's slow to "
"swing and will probably exhaust you quickly."
msgstr ""
"Un martillo grande y pesado. Es un arma de c. a c. que pega muy duro pero es"
" lenta para blandir y es probable que te agotes muy rápido."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "short sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "short sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "almádena corta"
msgstr[1] "almádenas cortas"
msgstr[2] "almádenas cortas"

#. ~ Description of "short sledge hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sledge hammer with a notably shorter handle.  This makes it worse as a "
"melee weapon, but a more portable tool."
msgstr ""
"Un mazo con un mango notablemente corto. Lo hace peor para el c. a c. pero "
"mas portable como herramienta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "engineer's hammer"
msgid_plural "engineer's hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo de ingeniería"
msgstr[1] "martillos de ingeniería"
msgstr[2] "martillos de ingeniería"

#. ~ Description of "engineer's hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout and hefty hammer, more akin to a sledge than a typical ball-peen.  "
"Useful for portable demolition work, but very unwieldy as a weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un robusto y fuerte martillo, más parecido a un mazo que la típica punta "
"redonda. Útil para trabajos de demolición portátil, pero muy difícil de "
"manejar como arma."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "heavy sledge hammer"
msgid_plural "heavy sledge hammers"
msgstr[0] "almádena pesada"
msgstr[1] "almádenas pesadas"
msgstr[2] "almádenas pesadas"

#. ~ Description of "heavy sledge hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large sledge hammer with a massive, heavy head.  This unwieldy tool is "
"meant to break concrete, rock, brick, anything really."
msgstr ""
"Una gran almádena con una enorme y pesada cabeza. Esta herramienta poco "
"manejable está hecha para romper hormigón, roca, ladrillos, en realidad "
"cualquier cosa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "hockey stick"
msgid_plural "hockey sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo de hockey"
msgstr[1] "palos de hockey"
msgstr[2] "palos de hockey"

#. ~ Description of "hockey stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A curved wooden stick with a wide and flat end.  Commonly used by hockey "
"players."
msgstr ""
"Es un palo curvado de madera con una punta ancha y plana. Es comúnmente "
"utilizado por los jugadores de hockey."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "homewrecker"
msgid_plural "homewreckers"
msgstr[0] "rompehogar"
msgstr[1] "rompehogares"
msgstr[2] "rompehogares"

#. ~ Description of "homewrecker"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A long piece of wood with several chunks of steel firmly tied to it.  The "
"resulting weapon is unwieldy and slow but very heavy hitting."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza grande de madera con varios trozos de acero atados firmemente. El "
"arma resultante es difícil de manejar y lenta pero con un golpe muy pesado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "ironshod quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "ironshod quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "vara larga con calzas de hierro"
msgstr[1] "varas largas con calzas de hierro"
msgstr[2] "varas largas con calzas de hierro"

#. ~ Description of "ironshod quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "A long wooden staff reinforced with metal bands and caps."
msgstr "Una vara larga de madera reforzada con franjas y puntas de metal."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "L-stick (off)"
msgid_plural "L-sticks (off)"
msgstr[0] "palo-L (off)"
msgstr[1] "palos-L (off)"
msgstr[2] "palos-L (off)"

#. ~ Description of "L-stick (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff functions not just as "
"a light source, but also a lightweight weapon thanks to its superalloy "
"construction.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over standard "
"light sources, batteries last longer in the L-stick."
msgstr ""
"Producido por la empresa Light, esta elegante vara no solo funciona como "
"fuente de luz sino que también es un arma liviana debido a su construcción "
"en superaleación. Dado sus mejoras de eficiencia sobre las fuentes de luz "
"comunes, las baterías duran más."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "L-stick (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The L-stick™ lights up."
msgstr "El Palo-L™ se enciende."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "L-stick (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The L-stick's™ batteries are empty."
msgstr "El Palo-L™ se quedó sin pilas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "L-stick (on)"
msgid_plural "L-sticks (on)"
msgstr[0] "palo-L (on)"
msgstr[1] "palos-L (on)"
msgstr[2] "palos-L (on)"

#. ~ Description of "L-stick (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Produced by the Light corporation, this stylish staff functions not just as "
"a light source, but also a lightweight weapon thanks to its superalloy "
"construction.  Due to proprietary efficiency improvements over standard "
"light sources, batteries last longer in the L-stick.  The staff is glowing "
"brightly, which is slowly draining the batteries."
msgstr ""
"Producido por la empresa Light, esta elegante vara no solo funciona como "
"fuente de luz sino que también es un arma liviana debido a su construcción "
"en superaleación. Dado sus mejoras de eficiencia sobre las fuentes de luz "
"comunes, las baterías duran más. La vara está brillando fuertemente, lo que "
"hace que sus baterías se consuman."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "L-stick (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "The L-stick's™ light fades away."
msgstr "El Palo-L™ se apaga lentamente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "lucerne hammer"
msgid_plural "lucerne hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo de lucerne"
msgstr[1] "martillos de lucerne"
msgstr[2] "martillos de lucerne"

#. ~ Description of "lucerne hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A versatile polearm with a spiked hammer head, a spike, and a hook attached "
"to a beefy wooden pole."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de asta versátil con una cabeza de martillo con púas, una punta y un"
" gancho unidos a una robusta vara de madera."

#. ~ Description of "lucerne hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A cheap piece of crap imitation of a versatile polearm with a spiked hammer "
"head, probably meant to be used for LARPing."
msgstr ""
"Una barata imitación de un arma de asta versátil con una cabeza de martillo "
"con púas, probablemente diseñada para usarse en juegos de rol en vivo."

#. ~ Same total damage and slightly higher weight than a morningstar -
#. exchanged.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "mace"
msgid_plural "maces"
msgstr[0] "maza"
msgstr[1] "mazas"
msgstr[2] "mazas"

#. ~ Same total damage and slightly higher weight than a morningstar -
#. exchanged.
#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy metal head.  It "
"is heavy and slow to swing, but its crushing damage is devastating."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un palo de madera con una cabeza muy pesada"
" de metal. Es lenta y pesada para blandir pero su golpe es devastador."

#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A light, cheaply-made replica of a medieval weapon that would normally "
"consist of a wood handle with a heavy metal head."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica ligera y barata de un arma medieval que normalmente consistiría "
"en un mango de madera con un pesado extremo de hierro."

#. ~ Description of "mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy metal head.  The "
"head feels a bit loose."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un mango de madera con un pesado extremo de"
" hierro. La cabeza se siente un poco suelta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "simple mace"
msgid_plural "simple maces"
msgstr[0] "maza simple"
msgstr[1] "mazas simples"
msgstr[2] "mazas simples"

#. ~ Description of "simple mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stick with a circular lump of metal tied to it in a facsimile of a mace.  "
"You could probably improve it by finding a way to pin the head to the "
"handle."
msgstr ""
"Un palo con una masa circular de metal atado a él que se parece a una maza. "
"Probablemente se podría mejorar encontrando una forma de fijar la cabeza al "
"mango."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "trench mace"
msgid_plural "trench maces"
msgstr[0] "maza de trinchera"
msgstr[1] "mazas de trinchera"
msgstr[2] "mazas de trinchera"

#. ~ Description of "trench mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A mace made from a circular chunk of steel pinned to the end of a stick.  "
"You can feel your inner Trench Raider come alive when you wield it."
msgstr ""
"Una maza hecha con un trozo circular de acero fijado a la punta de un palo. "
"Puedes sentir tu Asaltante de Trincheras cobrar vida cuando lo empuñas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "pipe mace"
msgid_plural "pipe maces"
msgstr[0] "maza de tubo"
msgstr[1] "mazas de tubo"
msgstr[2] "mazas de tubo"

#. ~ Description of "pipe mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A pipe with a handful of pipe fittings screwed onto the end to give it a "
"weighty head for bashing."
msgstr ""
"Un tubo con un puñado de equipos de cañería atornillados en una punta para "
"que sea más pesada y tenga más potencia de golpe."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "great pipe mace"
msgid_plural "great pipe maces"
msgstr[0] "maza grande de tubo"
msgstr[1] "mazas grandes de tubo"
msgstr[2] "mazas grandes de tubo"

#. ~ Description of "great pipe mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Two pipes fitted end-to-end with more pipe fittings screwed onto the far "
"end.  The result is a large, but awkward bludgeon."
msgstr ""
"Dos tubos llenos de punta a punta con equipos de cañería atornillados. El "
"resultado es un arma contundente grande e incómoda."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "pipe staff"
msgid_plural "pipe staffs"
msgstr[0] "vara de tubo"
msgstr[1] "varas de tubo"
msgstr[2] "varas de tubo"

#. ~ Description of "pipe staff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"Three pipes fitted end-to-end in a monstrously heavy facsimile of a "
"quarterstaff."
msgstr "Tres tubos juntos que arman un facsímil monstruoso de una vara larga."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bronze mace"
msgid_plural "bronze maces"
msgstr[0] "maza de bronce"
msgstr[1] "mazas de bronce"
msgstr[2] "mazas de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze mace"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"While nothing more than a bronze sphere on a stick, it is still surprisingly"
" effective."
msgstr ""
"Aunque no es nada más que una esfera de bronce en un palo, es "
"sorprendentemente efectiva."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "makeshift sap"
msgid_plural "makeshift saps"
msgstr[0] "porra improvisada"
msgstr[1] "porras improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "porras improvisadas"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift sap"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An improvised sap, also known as a cosh, slapjack and slapper.  A short, "
"flat bludgeoning weapon consisting of a weight embedded between two patches "
"of leather."
msgstr ""
"Una porra improvisada, también conocida como cachiporra, slapjack y slapper."
" Un arma corta y plana que consiste en un peso incrustado entre dos parches "
"de cuero."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json data/mods/Magiclysm/items/melee.json
msgid "Mjölnir"
msgid_plural "Mjölnirs"
msgstr[0] "Mjölnir"
msgstr[1] "Mjölnirs"
msgstr[2] "Mjölnirs"

#. ~ Description of "Mjölnir"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A large hammer, forged from the heart of a dying star.  It bears the inscription:\n"
"\n"
"Whosoever holds this hammer,\n"
"If he be worthy,\n"
"Shall possess the power to…\n"
"CRUSH!'"
msgstr ""
"Un gran martillo, forjado en el corazón de una estrella moribunda. Lleva la inscripción:\n"
"\n"
"Quienquiera que sostenga este martillo,\n"
"Si es digno,\n"
"Tendrá el poder de...\n"
"¡APLASTAR!'."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "morningstar"
msgid_plural "morningstars"
msgstr[0] "maza de armas"
msgstr[1] "mazas de armas"
msgstr[2] "mazas de armas"

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked metal "
"ball on the end.  It deals devastating crushing damage, and the spikes "
"easily puncture soft targets."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un palo de madera con una bola pesada y con"
" púas de metal en la punta. Causa un daño devastador y las púas perforan "
"fácilmente los objetivos blandos."

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A light, cheaply-made replica of a medieval weapon that would normally "
"consist of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked metal ball on the end."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica ligera y barata de un arma medieval que normalmente consistiría "
"en un mango de madera con una pesada bola de hierro con púas en el extremo."

#. ~ Description of "morningstar"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a wood handle with a heavy, spiked metal "
"ball on the end.  The weight feels off on this one, and the spikes are "
"blunted."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un palo de madera con una bola pesada y con"
" púas de metal en la punta. El peso parece desequilibrado y las púas están "
"romas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "nail bat"
msgid_plural "nail bats"
msgstr[0] "bate con clavos"
msgstr[1] "bates con clavos"
msgstr[2] "bates con clavos"

#. ~ Description of "nail bat"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A baseball bat with several nails driven through it, an excellent melee "
"weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un bate de béisbol con varios clavos atravesándolo. Es una excelente arma de"
" c. a c."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "nailboard"
msgid_plural "nailboards"
msgstr[0] "tabla con clavos"
msgstr[1] "tablas con clavos"
msgstr[2] "tablas con clavos"

#. ~ Description of "nailboard"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A plank of wood with several nails through one end; essentially a simple "
"mace.  Makes an acceptable melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera con varios clavos en una punta. Esencialmente una maza "
"simple. Es un arma aceptable para el c. a c."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "pool cue"
msgid_plural "pool cues"
msgstr[0] "palo de billar"
msgstr[1] "palos de billar"
msgstr[2] "palos de billar"

#. ~ Description of "pool cue"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A hardwood stick designed for hitting colorful balls around a felt table.  "
"Truly, the coolest of sports."
msgstr ""
"Un palo de madera duro diseñado para golpear pelotas coloridas en una mesa "
"de fieltro. La verdad, el mejor de los deportes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "PR-24 baton (extended)"
msgid_plural "PR-24 batons (extended)"
msgstr[0] "garrote PR-24 (extendido)"
msgstr[1] "garrotes PR-24 (extendidos)"
msgstr[2] "garrotes PR-24 (extendidos)"

#. ~ Description of "PR-24 baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"The Monadnock PR-24 baton is a collapsible, lightweight, side-handle baton "
"used by law enforcement all over the world.  The PR designation is rumored "
"to mean Public Relations.  Activate to retract."
msgstr ""
"El bastón Monadnock PR-24 es un bastón plegable, ligero, con mango lateral, "
"utilizado por las fuerzas del orden de todo el mundo. Se rumorea que la "
"designación PR significa Relaciones Públicas. Activar para retraerse."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "PR-24 baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "Retract"
msgstr "Retraer"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "PR-24 baton (extended)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You collapse your PR-24 baton."
msgstr "Cierras tu garrote PR-24."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
msgid_plural "PR-24 batons (retracted)"
msgstr[0] "garrote PR-24 (retraído)"
msgstr[1] "garrotes PR-24 (retraídos)"
msgstr[2] "garrotes PR-24 (retraídos)"

#. ~ Description of "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"The Monadnock PR-24 baton is a collapsible, lightweight, side-handle baton "
"used by law enforcement all over the world.  The PR designation is rumored "
"to mean Public Relations.  Activate to extend."
msgstr ""
"El bastón Monadnock PR-24 es un bastón plegable, ligero, con mango lateral, "
"utilizado por las fuerzas del orden de todo el mundo. Se rumorea que la "
"designación PR significa Relaciones Públicas. Activar para extender."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "C.R.I.T hatchet"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "Belt of The Iron Whip"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "Biomancer shifting spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
#: data/mods/CRT_EXPANSION/items/crt_tools.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_belts.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_melee.json
msgid "Extend"
msgstr "Extender"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "PR-24 baton (retracted)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "You snap open your PR-24 baton."
msgstr "Abres bruscamente tu garrote PR-24."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "vara larga"
msgstr[1] "varas largas"
msgstr[2] "varas largas"

#. ~ Description of "quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy staff carved out of wood.  Lightweight and long, it is surprisingly"
" easy to handle."
msgstr ""
"Una vara resistente tallada en madera. Es liviana, larga y sorprendentemente"
" fácil de manejar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "bō"
msgid_plural "bō"
msgstr[0] "bastón bō"
msgstr[1] "bastones bō"
msgstr[2] "bastones bō"

#. ~ Description of "bō"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A wooden staff weapon used in Okinawan martial arts.  Finely sanded and "
"treated with oil for integrity."
msgstr ""
"Una vara de madera usada en las artes marciales de Okinawa. Pulida y tratada"
" con aceite para darle firmeza."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "rock in a sock"
msgid_plural "rocks in socks"
msgstr[0] "piedra en una calcetín"
msgstr[1] "piedras en calcetines"
msgstr[2] "piedras en calcetines"

#. ~ Description of "rock in a sock"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A pair of nested socks with a stone tied inside.  A true weapon of "
"desperation."
msgstr ""
"Un par de calcetines anidados llenos de una piedra. Una verdadera arma "
"salida de la desesperación."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "plastic shank"
msgid_plural "plastic shanks"
msgstr[0] "asta de plástico"
msgstr[1] "astas de plástico"
msgstr[2] "astas de plástico"

#. ~ Description of "plastic shank"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An oblong plastic object with the far end ground down into a stabbing point."
msgstr ""
"Un objeto ovalado de plástico con la punta afilada para terminar en una "
"punta punzante."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "shillelagh"
msgid_plural "shillelaghs"
msgstr[0] "shillelagh(bastón maza)"
msgstr[1] "shillelaghs(bastón maza)"
msgstr[2] "shillelaghs(bastón maza)"

#. ~ Description of "shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout, knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to "
"cure in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was "
"originally used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner."
msgstr ""
"Un palo robusto con nudos y un bulto grande en la punta que ha sido curado "
"en una chimenea. Un arma tradicional de Irlanda, el shillelagh era "
"originalmente usado para resolver diputas entre caballeros."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "loaded stick"
msgid_plural "loaded sticks"
msgstr[0] " palo cargado"
msgstr[1] " palos cargados"
msgstr[2] " palos cargados"

#. ~ Description of "loaded stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout knotty stick with a large knob at the top that has been left to cure"
" in a chimney.  A traditional Irish weapon, the shillelagh was originally "
"used for settling disputes in a gentlemanly manner.  The knob has been "
"hollowed and filled with molten heavy metal to pack more of a punch."
msgstr ""
"Un palo robusto y nudoso con un gran pomo en la parte superior que se ha "
"dejado curar en una chimenea. Un arma tradicional irlandesa, el shillelagh "
"se usaba originalmente para resolver disputas de manera caballerosa. El pomo"
" ha sido ahuecado y rellenado con metal pesado fundido para dar un mayor "
"golpe."

#. ~ Description of "shillelagh"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A fake shillelagh massproduced as a souvenir for tourists.  This knotty "
"stick has not been cured in a chimney like a traditional shillelagh, but "
"instead has had fake black soot painted on."
msgstr ""
"Un shillelagh falso producido industrialmente como recuerdo para los "
"turistas. Este palo con nudos no está curado en una chimenea como el "
"tradicional shillelagh pero tiene pintura negra para simular el hollín."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "powered quarterstaff"
msgid_plural "powered quarterstaves"
msgstr[0] "vara larga aturdidora"
msgstr[1] "varas largas aturdidoras"
msgstr[2] "varas largas aturdidoras"

#. ~ Description of "powered quarterstaff"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"An ironshod quarterstaff that has a high-voltage stun gun built into the "
"handle.  The stun gun is wired to the metal caps at either end of the staff,"
" allowing you to zap a dangerous opponent should beating them senseless with"
" it prove too hazardous."
msgstr ""
"Una vara larga con calces de hierro que tiene un arma aturdidora de alto "
"voltaje dentro del mango. El arma aturdidora está conectada a los calces de "
"metal en las dos puntas de la vara, lo que permite dar choques eléctricos al"
" enemigo por si golpearlo hasta dejarlo inconsciente es muy peligroso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "tactical tonfa (off)"
msgid_plural "tactical tonfas (off)"
msgstr[0] "tonfa táctico (off)"
msgstr[1] "tonfas tácticos (off)"
msgstr[2] "tonfas tácticos (off)"

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (off)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-"
"yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed,"
" a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the "
"end of the tonfa, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in "
"contact with them.  It also has a nifty flashlight, which is off at the "
"moment."
msgstr ""
"Un tonfa de plástico reforzado. El centro está relleno con condensadores y "
"una batería recargable de alto rendimiento. Cuando se aprieta el botón que "
"está en el mango, se transmite un corriente de alto voltaje a los dos "
"electrodos montados en la punta del tonfa, y también a cualquiera que esté "
"lamentablemente en contacto con ella. También tiene una ingeniosa linterna, "
"que ahora está apagada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "tactical tonfa (on)"
msgid_plural "tactical tonfas (on)"
msgstr[0] "tonfa táctica (on)"
msgstr[1] "tonfas tácticas (on)"
msgstr[2] "tonfas tácticas (on)"

#. ~ Description of "tactical tonfa (on)"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced plastic tonfa; the core is filled with capacitors and a high-"
"yield rechargeable storage battery.  When a switch on the handle is pressed,"
" a high-voltage current is transmitted to the two electrodes mounted in the "
"end of the weapon, and by extension to anyone unfortunate enough to be in "
"contact with them.  The integral flashlight is turned on, continually "
"draining power and lighting the surrounding area."
msgstr ""
"Un tonfa de plástico reforzado. El centro está relleno con condensadores y "
"una batería recargable de alto rendimiento. Cuando se aprieta el botón que "
"está en el mango, se transmite un corriente de alto voltaje a los dos "
"electrodos montados en la punta del tonfa, y también a cualquiera que esté "
"lamentablemente en contacto con ella. La linterna integrada está encendida, "
"consumiendo gradualmente la energía e iluminando los alrededores."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "tonfa"
msgid_plural "tonfas"
msgstr[0] "tonfa"
msgstr[1] "tonfas"
msgstr[2] "tonfas"

#. ~ Description of "tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A hard plastic truncheon commonly employed by police.  Originally an "
"Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular handle attached"
" a third of the way down its length."
msgstr ""
"Es una cachiporra de plástico duro comúnmente utilizada por la policía. "
"Originalmente, es un arma de Okinawa que consiste en un palo con un mango "
"perpendicular cerca de uno de sus extremos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "wooden tonfa"
msgid_plural "wooden tonfas"
msgstr[0] "tonfa de madera"
msgstr[1] "tonfas de madera"
msgstr[2] "tonfas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden tonfa"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A stout wooden truncheon of the sort commonly employed by police.  "
"Originally an Okinawan weapon, it consists of a stick with a perpendicular "
"handle attached a third of the way down its length."
msgstr ""
"Es una cachiporra de madera resistente parecida a la utilizada por la "
"policía. Originalmente, es un arma de Okinawa que consiste en un palo con un"
" mango perpendicular cerca de uno de sus extremos."

#. ~ Craftable from steel, shouldn't be silver.  A warhammer is essentially
#. one end of a pickaxe with balancing weight on the other and crushes/pierces
#. the armor.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid "war hammer"
msgid_plural "war hammers"
msgstr[0] "martillo de guerra"
msgstr[1] "martillos de guerra"
msgstr[2] "martillos de guerra"

#. ~ Craftable from steel, shouldn't be silver.  A warhammer is essentially
#. one end of a pickaxe with balancing weight on the other and crushes/pierces
#. the armor.
#. ~ Description of "war hammer"
#: data/json/items/melee/bludgeons.json
msgid ""
"A medieval hammer with a spike on one end, made for battle.  Its odd shape "
"and balance make it an excellent weapon, but an ineffective tool."
msgstr ""
"Un martillo medieval con una púa en la punta hecho para el combate. Su "
"extraña forma y balance lo hace una excelente arma pero una herramienta "
"ineficaz."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "bionic claws"
msgid_plural "bionic claws"
msgstr[0] "garras biónicas"
msgstr[1] "garras biónicas"
msgstr[2] "garras biónicas"

#. ~ Description of "bionic claws"
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "Short, sharp claws made from a high-tech metal."
msgstr "Unas garras cortas y afiladas hechas de un metal de alta tecnología."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid "monomolecular blade"
msgid_plural "monomolecular blades"
msgstr[0] "cuchilla monomolecular"
msgstr[1] "cuchillas monomoleculares"
msgstr[2] "cuchillas monomoleculares"

#. ~ Description of "monomolecular blade"
#: data/json/items/melee/fake.json
msgid ""
"A foot-long blade made from high-tech alloy and edged with bonded "
"nanocrystals."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla de 30 cm de aleación de alta tecnología, y el borde con "
"nanocristales unidos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "generic kitchen knife"
msgid_plural "generic kitchen knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de cocina genérico"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de cocina genéricos"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de cocina genéricos"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "butcher knife"
msgid_plural "butcher knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de carnicero"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de carnicero"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de carnicero"

#. ~ Description of "butcher knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A sharp, heavy knife.  It makes a good melee weapon, and is an ideal item "
"for butchering corpses."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo grande y afilado. Sirve bien como arma de c. a c. y es ideal "
"para descuartizar cadáveres."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "steak knife"
msgid_plural "steak knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo para carne"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos para carne"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos para carne"

#. ~ Description of "steak knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A sharp knife designed for cutting meat.  It makes a poor melee weapon, but "
"is decent at butchering corpses."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo afilado diseñado para cortar carne. No sirve mucho como arma de "
"cuerpo a cuerpo pero es decente para descuartizar cadáveres."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "paring knife"
msgid_plural "paring knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo para pelar"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos para pelar"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos para pelar"

#. ~ Description of "paring knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A short-bladed knife with a sharp blade, made for fine controlled cuts to "
"vegetables without using a cutting board."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de hoja corta con un filo afilado, hecho para cortes finos y "
"controlados de vegetales sin usar una tabla de cortar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "chef knife"
msgid_plural "chef knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de chef"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de chef"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de chef"

#. ~ Description of "chef knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife.  The blade is wider than the handle, giving "
"room for the wielder's knuckles, and it has a characteristic curve for a "
"fast rocking action for chopping vegetables.  It makes an acceptable melee "
"weapon, but the wide blade is unwieldy for butchering."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de cocina con una hoja larga. La hoja es más ancha que la "
"empuñadura, tiene espacio para los nudillos y una curva característica que "
"permite cortar verduras a gran velocidad. Como arma de c. a c. funciona "
"aceptablemente pero la cuchilla ancha es un poco incómoda para descuartizar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "carving knife"
msgid_plural "carving knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo para trinchar"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos para trinchar"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos para trinchar"

#. ~ Description of "carving knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A long-bladed kitchen knife with a thin, slightly curved blade for deftly "
"slicing meat either in flat sheets or around the bone.  It makes a decent "
"melee weapon, and is excellent for butchery."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de cocina de hoja larga, fina y curva para poder cortar carne en"
" filetes o para deshuesar. Es un arma decente para el c. a c. pero es "
"excelente para descuartizado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "bread knife"
msgid_plural "bread knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de pan"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de pan"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de pan"

#. ~ Description of "bread knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"This knife has quite a long blade with a scalloped edge for cutting bread.  "
"It's not that sharp, but its length and heft mean it could do a bit of "
"damage and cause some nasty tearing."
msgstr ""
"Este cuchillo tiene una hoja bastante larga con un borde festoneado para "
"cortar el pan. No es tan afilado, pero su longitud y peso significan que "
"podría hacer un poco de daño y causar algunos desgarros desagradables."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "vegetable cleaver"
msgid_plural "vegetable cleavers"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de verduras"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de verduras"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de verduras"

#. ~ Description of "vegetable cleaver"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square shaped blade, curved for fast "
"vegetable chopping.  Its heft and sharpness make it a decent weapon as well,"
" although not as good as a meat cleaver."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de aspecto amenazante con una hoja ancha, medio cuadrada y curva"
" para cortar verduras de manera rápida. Su peso y filo la convierten en una "
"decente arma de c. a c. aunque no tan buena como una cuchilla de carnicero."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid "meat cleaver"
msgid_plural "meat cleavers"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de carnicería"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de carnicería"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de carnicería"

#. ~ Description of "meat cleaver"
#: data/json/items/melee/knives_kitchen.json
msgid ""
"A menacing-looking knife with a broad, square-shaped blade.  Its heft and "
"sharpness would make it a very effective melee weapon and an excellent "
"butchering tool."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de aspecto amenazante con una hoja ancha, medio cuadrada y "
"curva. Su peso y filo la convierten en un arma de c. a c. muy efectiva, y "
"una excelente herramienta para descuartizar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid "bullwhip"
msgid_plural "bullwhips"
msgstr[0] "látigo"
msgstr[1] "látigos"
msgstr[2] "látigos"

#. ~ Description of "bullwhip"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"A long strip of braided leather with a handle on one end.  Originally "
"developed to settle disagreements with cattle, it's better used now for "
"flaying the rotten flesh off of walking corpses.  Great for when a problem "
"comes along."
msgstr ""
"Una larga correa de cuero trenzado con un mango en un extremo. Originalmente"
" diseñado para ordenar el ganado, ahora es mejor usada para despellejar la "
"carne podrida de los cadáveres ambulantes. Muy útil cuando se te vienen los "
"problemas."

#. ~ There's no way you can swing this thing without hitting SOMETHING.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid "scourge"
msgid_plural "scourges"
msgstr[0] "cilicio"
msgstr[1] "cilicios"
msgstr[2] "cilicios"

#. ~ There's no way you can swing this thing without hitting SOMETHING.
#. ~ Description of "scourge"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"The \"cat 'o nine tails\", a handle with nine short leather whips, each "
"sporting a razor-sharp metal tip.  This ancient instrument of torture causes"
" massive bleeding, but by design is inefficient as a weapon."
msgstr ""
"El \"gato de las nueve colas\", un mango con nueve látigos cortos de cuero, "
"cada uno con una punta de metal afilada. Este antiguo instrumento de tortura"
" provoca hemorragias masivas, pero por su diseño es ineficiente como arma."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/weapons.json
msgid "lobotomizer"
msgid_plural "lobotomizers"
msgstr[0] "lobotomizador"
msgstr[1] "lobotomizadores"
msgstr[2] "lobotomizadores"

#. ~ Description of "lobotomizer"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"A hand-forged collapsible tool with two axe heads and a sharp shovel-like "
"tip on one end.  It can be used as a shovel, or you could chop some zombies "
"with it instead."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta plegable hecha a mano con dos cabezas de hacha y una punta "
"afilada similar a una pala. Se puede usar como pala, o se pueden triturar "
"algunos zombis, también."

#. ~ Yes, this is smaller than its magazine well. Go with it.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid "stun gun"
msgid_plural "stun guns"
msgstr[0] "pistola paralizante"
msgstr[1] "pistolas paralizantes"
msgstr[2] "pistolas paralizantes"

#. ~ Yes, this is smaller than its magazine well. Go with it.
#. ~ Description of "stun gun"
#: data/json/items/melee/misc.json
msgid ""
"A high-powered stun gun.  Use this item to attempt to electrocute an "
"adjacent enemy, temporarily paralyzing them."
msgstr ""
"Una pistola para aturdir de gran potencia. Usa este objeto para intentar "
"electrocutar a un enemigo adyacente, paralizándolo temporalmente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pitchfork"
msgid_plural "pitchforks"
msgstr[0] "horca"
msgstr[1] "horcas"
msgstr[2] "horcas"

#. ~ Description of "pitchfork"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"An agricultural tool with a long wooden shaft and four spikes.  Normally "
"used to lift hay."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta para la agricultura hecha con un palo largo con cuatro "
"puntas, y usada para levantar heno."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pointy stick"
msgid_plural "pointy sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo con punta"
msgstr[1] "palos con punta"
msgstr[2] "palos con punta"

#. ~ Description of "pointy stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A simple wooden pole with one end sharpened to a point."
msgstr "Un palo simple con una punta afilada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "long pointy stick"
msgid_plural "long pointy sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo largo con punta"
msgstr[1] "palos largos con punta"
msgstr[2] "palos largos con punta"

#. ~ Description of "long pointy stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout pole with one end sharpened to a point."
msgstr "Un palo grueso con una punta afilada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "fire-hardened wooden spear"
msgid_plural "fire-hardened wooden spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de madera endurecida al fuego"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de madera endurecidas al fuego"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de madera endurecidas al fuego"

#. ~ Description of "fire-hardened wooden spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a fire-hardened point."
msgstr "Un palo resistente de madera con la punta endurecida al fuego."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "wooden spear"
msgid_plural "wooden spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de madera"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de madera"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a whittled point."
msgstr "Un palo resistente de madera con la punta tallada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "sharpened spear shaft"
msgid_plural "sharpened spear shafts"
msgstr[0] "lanza de palo afilada"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de palo afiladas"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de palo afiladas"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened spear shaft"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"You've gone through the effort of making a proper spear shaft, but instead "
"of attaching something sharp to the end you just whittled a point into the "
"wood.  The peak of pointy stick technology."
msgstr ""
"Hiciste el esfuerzo para crear una lanza de palo apropiada pero en lugar de "
"ponerle algo afilado en la punta, tallaste directamente la punta en la "
"madera. Lo mejor en tecnología de palos afilados."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "makeshift war scythe"
msgid_plural "makeshift war scythes"
msgstr[0] "guadaña de guerra improvisada"
msgstr[1] "guadañas de guerra improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "guadañas de guerra improvisadas"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift war scythe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"This farming tool has been modified into an improvised weapon by rotating "
"its blade 90 degrees, transforming it into a deadly giant blade on the end "
"of a stick.  It's quite fragile, however."
msgstr ""
"Esta herramienta de granja ha sido modificada para funcionar como arma, con "
"una cuchilla giratoria de 90 grados, transformándola en una gigante cuchilla"
" letal en la punta de un palo. Sin embargo, es bastante frágil."

#. ~ Name changed to simple makeshift glaive, but changing the id would break
#. e.g.  tilesets.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "simple makeshift glaive"
msgid_plural "simple makeshift glaives"
msgstr[0] "guja simple improvisada"
msgstr[1] "gujas simples improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "gujas simples improvisadas"

#. ~ Name changed to simple makeshift glaive, but changing the id would break
#. e.g.  tilesets.
#. ~ Description of "simple makeshift glaive"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A large blade attached to a stout section of tree branch.  It could do a "
"considerable amount of damage, but the blade isn't secured very well and "
"could easily break off."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla grande unida a un pedazo robusto de rama. Puede hacer una "
"cantidad considerable de daño pero la cuchilla no está bien asegurada por lo"
" que se rompe fácilmente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "makeshift glaive"
msgid_plural "makeshift glaives"
msgstr[0] "guja improvisada"
msgstr[1] "gujas improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "gujas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift glaive"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A stout tree branch that has been carefully split and reinforced.  At the "
"split point, a sharp blade has been bolted into place and reinforced with "
"layers of sturdy wrapped bindings."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta rama de árbol que ha sido cuidadosamente dividida y reforzada. "
"En el punto de división, se ha atornillado una hoja afilada en su lugar y se"
" ha reforzado con capas de resistentes ataduras envueltas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/weapons.json
msgid "spike on a stick"
msgid_plural "spikes on sticks"
msgstr[0] "palos con púas"
msgstr[1] "palos con púas"
msgstr[2] "palos con púas"

#. ~ Description of "spike on a stick"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A flimsy pole made of wood with a basic metal spike tied to it.  It's barely"
" sharp, and crudely constructed, but it will keep the zombies out of arm's "
"reach until you can find something better."
msgstr ""
"Un poste endeble hecho de madera con una pua de metal básica atada a él. "
"Apenas es afilado, y está construido toscamente, pero mantendrá a los zombis"
" fuera del alcance de sus brazos hasta que puedas encontrar algo mejor."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "simple knife spear"
msgid_plural "simple knife spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza simple con cuchillo"
msgstr[1] "lanzas simple con cuchillo"
msgstr[2] "lanzas simple con cuchillo"

#. ~ Description of "simple knife spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A flimsy pole made of wood with a knife bound to the end.  It's long enough "
"to slice from a distance, but the knife isn't that well attached.  You could"
" take a bit more time to carefully split the shaft and attach the knife "
"blade more permanently."
msgstr ""
"Un poste endeble de madera con un cuchillo atado al final. Es lo "
"suficientemente largo para cortar a distancia, pero el cuchillo no está tan "
"bien sujeto. Podrías tomarte un poco más de tiempo para dividir "
"cuidadosamente el palo y fijar la hoja del cuchillo de forma más permanente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "makeshift knife spear"
msgid_plural "makeshift knife spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza improvisada con cuchillo"
msgstr[1] "lanzas improvisadas con cuchillo"
msgstr[2] "lanzas improvisadas con cuchillo"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift knife spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A long stick that has been carefully split and reinforced.  At the split "
"point, a sharp blade has been bolted into place and reinforced with layers "
"of sturdy wrapped bindings."
msgstr ""
"Un palo largo que ha sido separado en la punta y reforzado. En esa "
"separación se ha atornillado una cuchilla afilada y ha sido reforzada con "
"varias nudos resistentes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "knife spear"
msgid_plural "knife spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza cuchillo"
msgstr[1] "lanzas cuchillo"
msgstr[2] "lanzas cuchillo"

#. ~ Description of "knife spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A stout wooden pole with the blade of a knife bolted into place at the end."
"  The shape of a knife blade isn't ideal for a spear, but it's still very "
"sharp and effective."
msgstr ""
"Una vara resistente de madera con la hoja de un cuchillo atornillada en la "
"punta. La forma de la cuchilla no es la ideal para una lanza pero está muy "
"afilada y es efectiva."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "homemade halfpike"
msgid_plural "homemade halfpikes"
msgstr[0] "media pica casera"
msgstr[1] "medias picas caseras"
msgstr[2] "medias picas caseras"

#. ~ Description of "homemade halfpike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A short do-it-yourself spear made out of a long stick with a metal spike "
"seated and bound into place at its tip."
msgstr ""
"Una lanza corta casera con un palo largo, y una púa metálica puesta y atada "
"en la punta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "crude steel spear"
msgid_plural "crude steel spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza rudimentaria de acero"
msgstr[1] "lanzas rudimentarias de acero"
msgstr[2] "lanzas rudimentarias de acero"

#. ~ Description of "crude steel spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A stout wooden pole with a misshapen metal spike seated into the end and "
"bolted into place."
msgstr ""
"Un palo resistente de madera con una púa medio deforme de metal puesta en la"
" punta y atornillada."

#. ~ Block 2 until we re-implement defensive-disarm, I'm afraid.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "forked spear"
msgid_plural "forked spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza tridente"
msgstr[1] "lanzas tridente"
msgstr[2] "lanzas tridente"

#. ~ Block 2 until we re-implement defensive-disarm, I'm afraid.
#. ~ Description of "forked spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A wooden pole with three spikes tied to it.  It's specialized for catching "
"weapons, and not intended for extended use in combat."
msgstr ""
"Un palo de madera con tres púas atadas a él. Está especializado en la "
"captura de armas, y no está destinado a un uso prolongado en el combate."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "copper spear"
msgid_plural "copper spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de cobre"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de cobre"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de cobre"

#. ~ Description of "copper spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a spearhead worked from copper."
msgstr "Es un palo grueso de madera con una punta afilada de cobre."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "steel spear"
msgid_plural "steel spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de acero"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de acero"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de acero"

#. ~ Description of "steel spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a hand-forged steel spearhead."
msgstr "Un palo de madera robusto con una punta de acero forjado a mano."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "sharpened pipe"
msgid_plural "sharpened pipes"
msgstr[0] "tubo afilado"
msgstr[1] "tubos afilados"
msgstr[2] "tubos afilados"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened pipe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A pipe with one end cut off at an angle."
msgstr "Un tubo con un extremo cortado en ángulo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "basic pipe spear"
msgid_plural "basic pipe spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de tubo básica"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de tubo básicas"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de tubo básicas"

#. ~ Description of "basic pipe spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "Three pipes tightly fit together with one end cut down to a point."
msgstr "Tres tubos ajustados entre sí con un extremo cortado en punta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pipe spear"
msgid_plural "pipe spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de tubo"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de tubo"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de tubo"

#. ~ Description of "pipe spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"Three pipes tightly fit together with some wrappings for a handle around one"
" end and a sharp tip on the other."
msgstr ""
"Tres tubos atados firmemente con envolturas que funcionan como un mango en "
"un lado, y del otro una punta afilada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "pointed rebar"
msgid_plural "pointed rebars"
msgstr[0] "barra corrugada puntiaguda"
msgstr[1] "barras corrugadas puntiagudas"
msgstr[2] "barras corrugadas puntiagudas"

#. ~ Description of "pointed rebar"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A rod of rebar that's been crudely hammered into a point."
msgstr "Una barra corrugada que ha sido burdamente martillada en una punta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "sharpened rebar"
msgid_plural "sharpened rebars"
msgstr[0] "barra corrugada afilada"
msgstr[1] "barras corrugadas afiladas"
msgstr[2] "barras corrugadas afiladas"

#. ~ Description of "sharpened rebar"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A rod of rebar that's been cut and sharpened to a point."
msgstr "Un pedazo de varilla corrugada que fue cortada y afilada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "rebar spear"
msgid_plural "rebar spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de barra corrugada"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de barras corrugadas"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de barras corrugadas"

#. ~ Description of "rebar spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "Two rods of rebar welded together with a pointed tip."
msgstr ""
"Dos pedazos de barras corrugadas soldadas junta con una punta afilada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "qiang"
msgid_plural "qiang"
msgstr[0] "qiang"
msgstr[1] "qiangs"
msgstr[2] "qiangs"

#. ~ Description of "qiang"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"An ancient Chinese spear, typically with a tassel just below the spearhead "
"and larger than most European spears.  One of the four major weapons in "
"folklore, alongside the dao sabre, jian sword, and gun staff."
msgstr ""
"Una antigua lanza china, con una típica borla justo debajo de la punta y más"
" larga que las lanzas europeas. Una de las cuatro armas principales de la "
"tradición china junto con el sable dao, la espada jian y el bastón gun."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "halberd"
msgid_plural "halberds"
msgstr[0] "alabarda"
msgstr[1] "alabardas"
msgstr[2] "alabardas"

#. ~ Description of "halberd"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A versatile polearm with an axe blade, a spike, and other fun things "
"attached to a long, sturdy stick."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de asta versátil con una hoja de hacha, una púa y otras cosas "
"divertidas agregadas a un palo robusto y largo."

#. ~ Description of "halberd"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A dull, cheaply made replica of a polearm with an axe blade, a spike, and "
"other fun things attached to a thick pole."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica sosa sin filo de un arma de asta con una hoja de hacha, una púa "
"y otras cosas divertidas agregadas a una vara gruesa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "glaive"
msgid_plural "glaives"
msgstr[0] "guja"
msgstr[1] "gujas"
msgstr[2] "gujas"

#. ~ Description of "glaive"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A sturdy polearm with a sizable single-edged blade on the end."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta arma de asta con una considerable cuchilla de un solo filo en la"
" punta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "naginata"
msgid_plural "naginata"
msgstr[0] "naginata"
msgstr[1] "naginata"
msgstr[2] "naginata"

#. ~ Description of "naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy polearm with a curved blade, made in the same manner as the katana "
"and other Japanese blades.  Occasionally used by samurai in early periods, "
"or by their wives in defense of the household."
msgstr ""
"Una robusta arma de asta con una cuchilla curva, hecha a la manera de la "
"katana y otras espadas japonesas. Ocasionalmente era utilizada por los "
"samurai en los primeros tiempos, o por sus esposas en defensa de su hogar."

#. ~ Description of "naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy polearm with a curved blade, made in the same manner as the katana "
"and other Japanese blades.  This one has a bit of wiggle to its blade and "
"feels a bit shoddily made."
msgstr ""
"Un robust arma de asta con una hoja curva, hecho de la misma manera que la "
"katana y otras hojas japonesas. Este tiene un poco de movimiento en su hoja "
"y se siente un poco mal hecho."

#. ~ Description of "naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A dull, slightly floppy replica of a Japanese polearm with a curved blade.  "
"With a little difficulty, you could use it administer a solid slap from a "
"distance."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica sin filo y medio floja de un arma de asta japonesa con una "
"cuchilla curva. Con un poco de dificultad, podrías usarla para administrar "
"una buena torta a distancia."

#. ~ Description says it can slash. STAB currently doesn't slash, but at least
#. it doesn't give the spear bonus
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "survivor naginata"
msgid_plural "survivor naginata"
msgstr[0] "naginata de superviviente"
msgstr[1] "naginatas de superviviente"
msgstr[2] "naginatas de superviviente"

#. ~ Description says it can slash. STAB currently doesn't slash, but at least
#. it doesn't give the spear bonus
#. ~ Description of "survivor naginata"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"This sturdy steel shaft with a sword blade at the end is good for both "
"slashing and stabbing."
msgstr ""
"Esta robusta vara de acero con una hoja de espada en la punta, es buena "
"tanto para cortar como para apuñalar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "wooden javelin"
msgid_plural "wooden javelins"
msgstr[0] "jabalina de madera"
msgstr[1] "jabalinas de madera"
msgstr[2] "jabalinas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden javelin"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A fire-hardened wooden spear honed to a sharper point."
msgstr ""
"Una lanza de madera endurecida por el fuego, afilada a una punta más "
"afilada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "iron javelin"
msgid_plural "iron javelins"
msgstr[0] "jabalina de hierro"
msgstr[1] "jabalinas de hierro"
msgstr[2] "jabalinas de hierro"

#. ~ Description of "iron javelin"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "An iron-tipped wooden throwing spear."
msgstr "Una lanza de madera con punta de hierro."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "wooden pike"
msgid_plural "wooden pikes"
msgstr[0] "pica de madera"
msgstr[1] "picas de madera"
msgstr[2] "picas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft with a fire-"
"hardened point."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un palo de madera muy largo con una punta "
"endurecida al fuego."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "copper pike"
msgid_plural "copper pikes"
msgstr[0] "pica de cobre"
msgstr[1] "picas de cobre"
msgstr[2] "picas de cobre"

#. ~ Description of "copper pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft tipped with a "
"copper spearhead."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un palo muy largo de madera con una punta "
"de cobre."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgctxt "weapon"
msgid "pike"
msgid_plural "pikes"
msgstr[0] "lucio"
msgstr[1] "lucios"
msgstr[2] "lucios"

#. ~ Description of "pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft tipped with a steel"
" spearhead."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un palo muy largo de madera con una punta "
"de metal."

#. ~ Description of "pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A dull, cheaply made replica of a medieval weapon consisting of a very long "
"wooden shaft tipped with an iron spearhead."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica sin filo y barata de un arma medieval que consiste en un palo "
"muy largo de madera con una punta de hierro."

#. ~ Description of "pike"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A medieval weapon consisting of a very long wooden shaft tipped with an iron"
" spearhead.  The head seems to be pretty dull, and the whole thing feels "
"poorly made."
msgstr ""
"Un arma medieval que consiste en un palo muy largo de madera con una punta "
"de hierro. La punta parece no tener filo y el arma en general parece estar "
"hecha pobremente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "war scythe"
msgid_plural "war scythes"
msgstr[0] "guadaña de guerra"
msgstr[1] "guadañas de guerra"
msgstr[2] "guadañas de guerra"

#. ~ Description of "war scythe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A pole weapon with a curving single-edged blade.  Its blade bears some "
"superficial resemblance to that of an agricultural scythe from which it "
"likely evolved."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de asta con una hoja curva de un solo filo. Su hoja tiene un cierto "
"parecido superficial con la de una guadaña agrícola de la que probablemente "
"evolucionó."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "dory"
msgid_plural "dories"
msgstr[0] "dory"
msgstr[1] "dorus"
msgstr[2] "dorus"

#. ~ Description of "dory"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A well-made spear with a bronze head, Greek in origin.  Despite its large "
"size, it was frequently used one-handed."
msgstr ""
"Una lanza bien hecha con la punta de bronce, de origen griego. A pesar de su"
" gran tamaño, era utilizada frecuentemente con una sola mano."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "bronze spear"
msgid_plural "bronze spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de bronce"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de bronce"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A forged spear with a bronze head."
msgstr "Una lanza forjada con la punta de bronce."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "poleaxe"
msgid_plural "poleaxes"
msgstr[0] "alabarda"
msgstr[1] "alabardas"
msgstr[2] "alabardas"

#. ~ Description of "poleaxe"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A polearm with an axe head, a small hammer on the back, and a short dagger-"
"like spike on top.  It's less heavy than most polearms and has a smaller "
"head, making it slightly quicker."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de asta con cabeza de hacha, un pequeño martillo en la parte de "
"atrás y una daga corta funcionando como punta en el extremo. Es menos pesada"
" que la mayoría de las armas de asta y tiene una cabeza más pequeña, "
"haciéndola un poco más rápida."

#. ~ Couldn't find a good way to pluralize the transliteration.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "ji"
msgid_plural "ji"
msgstr[0] "ji"
msgstr[1] "ji"
msgstr[2] "ji"

#. ~ Couldn't find a good way to pluralize the transliteration.
#. ~ Description of "ji"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid ""
"A bronze polearm that originated in the Shang dynasty of China, if not "
"earlier.  It combines a spear head with the perpendicular blade of the "
"earlier ge or dagger-axe."
msgstr ""
"Un arma de asta de bronce con origen en la dinastía Shang de China, aunque "
"tal vez antes. Combina una punta de lanza con la cuchilla perpendicular del "
"ge o una daga-hacha."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "stone spear"
msgid_plural "stone spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza de piedra"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de piedra"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A stout wooden pole with a sharp stone spearhead."
msgstr "Es un palo grueso de madera con una piedra afilada en la punta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "simple stone spear"
msgid_plural "simple stone spears"
msgstr[0] "lanza sencilla de piedra"
msgstr[1] "lanzas sencillas de piedra"
msgstr[2] "lanzas sencillas de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "simple stone spear"
#: data/json/items/melee/spears_and_polearms.json
msgid "A long stick with a sharp stone spearhead."
msgstr "Un palo largo de madera con una piedra afilada en la punta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "2-by-sword"
msgid_plural "2-by-swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de madera"
msgstr[1] "espadas de madera"
msgstr[2] "espadas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "2-by-sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point.  Not much good for "
"slashing, but much better than your bare hands."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera con empuñadura y la punta tallada. No sirve mucho para "
"cortar pero es mucho mejor que tus manos desnudas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "zweitimber"
msgid_plural "zweitimbers"
msgstr[0] "espadón de madera"
msgstr[1] "espadones de madera"
msgstr[2] "espadones de madera"

#. ~ Description of "zweitimber"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A plank with a handle and a whittled-down point, left large enough to "
"require two hands.  Still not much good for slashing, but far better than "
"the plank on its own."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera con empuñadura y la punta tallada, pero suficientemente "
"grande como para necesitar ser usada con las dos manos. No corta casi nada, "
"pero es mucho mejor que un tablón común."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "nord"
msgid_plural "nords"
msgstr[0] "clavespada"
msgstr[1] "clavespadas"
msgstr[2] "clavespadas"

#. ~ Description of "nord"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A nail sword, or nord for short.  This wooden sword has a dozen nails "
"sticking out at jagged angles from the edge of the blade, making it much "
"better at chopping than slashing."
msgstr ""
"Una espada de clavos, o clavespada para abreviar. Esta espada de madera "
"tiene una decena de clavos sobresaliendo como dientes del filo de la hoja, "
"lo que la hace mucho mejor para golpear que para cortar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "scrap sword"
msgid_plural "scrap swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de chatarra"
msgstr[1] "espadas de chatarra"
msgstr[2] "espadas de chatarra"

#. ~ Description of "scrap sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"Several bits of thin scrap metal crudely beat into the semblance of an edge "
"over a wooden sword.  The added weight is unbalanced, but the jagged edge "
"offers a good bit of slashing power."
msgstr ""
"Varios trocitos de chatarra fina golpeados para darle un parecido de filo a "
"una espada de madera. El peso agregado está desbalanceado, pero el filo "
"dentado brinda una buena cantidad daño cortante."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "scrap greatsword"
msgid_plural "scrap greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande de chatarra"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes de chatarra"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes de chatarra"

#. ~ Description of "scrap greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A large wooden sword with scrap metal hammered over it into something "
"pretending to be an edge.  The extra weight almost completely front-loads "
"the balance, and it hurts your wrists just to wield."
msgstr ""
"Una espada grande de madera con la cuchilla hecha con chatarra metálica "
"puesta encima, que casi parece tener filo. El peso extra hace que se incline"
" completamente hacia adelante y hace que te duelan las muñecas cuando la "
"usas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "welded sword"
msgid_plural "welded swords"
msgstr[0] "espada soldada"
msgstr[1] "espadas soldadas"
msgstr[2] "espadas soldadas"

#. ~ Description of "welded sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A vicious single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered twice over "
"itself then welded together.  It's not as robust as a proper forged sword, "
"but the edge is wickedly sharp."
msgstr ""
"Es una espada despiadada de filo simple hecha con dos láminas de metal "
"soldadas juntas. No es tan robusta como una espada forjada pero es "
"maliciosamente afilada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "bolted sword"
msgid_plural "bolted swords"
msgstr[0] "espada atornillada"
msgstr[1] "espadas atornilladas"
msgstr[2] "espadas atornilladas"

#. ~ Description of "bolted sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A vicious single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered twice over "
"itself then bolted together.  It's not quite a katana made from steel folded"
" a thousand times over, but it has a certain industrial charm to it."
msgstr ""
"Una espada despiadada de filo simple hecha con dos láminas de metal "
"atornilladas juntas. No es como una katana que está hecha de acero doblado "
"cientos de veces, pero tiene cierto encanto industrial."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "welded greatsword"
msgid_plural "welded greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande soldada"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes soldadas"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes soldadas"

#. ~ Description of "welded greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long-handled single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered thrice "
"over itself then welded together.  The extra length and weight makes it a "
"tad awkward, but gives it a lot of slashing power."
msgstr ""
"Una espada larga de simple filo hecha con tres láminas de metal soldadas "
"juntas. La mayor longitud y peso la hace un poco incómoda, pero le da mucha "
"potencia de corte."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "bolted greatsword"
msgid_plural "bolted greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande atornillada"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes atornilladas"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes atornilladas"

#. ~ Description of "bolted greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long-handled single-edged sword made out of sheet metal layered thrice "
"over itself then bolted together.  It vaguely resembles a Japanese nagamaki "
"if you squint."
msgstr ""
"Una espada larga de simple filo hecha con tres láminas de metal atornilladas"
" juntas. Apenas si se parece a una nagamaki japonesa si la miras con los "
"ojos medio cerrados."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "metal sword"
msgid_plural "metal swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de metal"
msgstr[1] "espadas de metal"
msgstr[2] "espadas de metal"

#. ~ Description of "metal sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"An imitation of a true sword forged by someone who knows what swords look "
"like, at least.  Made from whatever scrap metal was on hand, it has the "
"general shape of a sword, and it is sharp, but it is a bit heavier than it "
"should be and the balance isn't quite right."
msgstr ""
"La imitación de una espada real forjada por alguien que sabe cómo es la "
"apariencia de una espada, por lo menos. Está hecha con la chatarra metálica "
"que había disponible, tiene la forma general de una espada y está afilada "
"pero es un poco más pesada de lo que debería y su equilibrio no es el "
"adecuado."

#. ~ It's not razor-sharp and most of the damage is coming from the heavy
#. weight, hence the high bash-to-cut ratio.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "metal greatsword"
msgid_plural "metal greatswords"
msgstr[0] "espada grande de metal"
msgstr[1] "espadas grandes de metal"
msgstr[2] "espadas grandes de metal"

#. ~ It's not razor-sharp and most of the damage is coming from the heavy
#. weight, hence the high bash-to-cut ratio.
#. ~ Description of "metal greatsword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A large, crudely-forged blade.  It's too big to be called a sword.  Too "
"massive, too thick, too heavy, and far too rough."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla grande forjada y rudimentaria. Es demasiado grande como para "
"llamarla espada. Demasiado enorme, gruesa, pesada y muy irregular."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "metal fencing sword"
msgid_plural "metal fencing swords"
msgstr[0] "espada de metal para esgrima"
msgstr[1] "espadas de metal para esgrima"
msgstr[2] "espadas de metal para esgrima"

#. ~ Description of "metal fencing sword"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"Calling this a rapier is a stretch.  It's robust and very pointy, but more "
"akin to a long metal spike with a handguard than the elegant swords of the "
"Renaissance."
msgstr ""
"Decirle espada ropera a esto sería demasiado. Es robusta y muy puntiaguda "
"pero más parecida a una púa larga de metal con un guardamano que a una "
"elegante espada del Renacimiento."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Variant name of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "switchblade"
msgid_plural "switchblades"
msgstr[0] "navaja automática"
msgstr[1] "navajas automáticas"
msgstr[2] "navajas automáticas"

#. ~ Description of "switchblade"
#. ~ Description of variant "switchblade" of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A long, thin knife with a spring-loaded blade that rests inside the handle "
"while not in use."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo largo y fino con una hoja que se oculta dentro de la empuñadura "
"cuando no está en uso y sale por la acción de un resorte."

#. ~ Variant name of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "balisong"
msgid_plural "balisongs"
msgstr[0] "navaja mariposa"
msgstr[1] "navajas mariposa"
msgstr[2] "navajas mariposa"

#. ~ Description of variant "balisong" of item "switchblade"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A flashy knife with hinged handles that completely conceal the blade while "
"folded.  Popular among movie gangbangers and people who thought fidget "
"spinners were too safe."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo llamativo con empuñadura plegable que guarda completamente la "
"hoja cuando está doblada. Es popular entre los pandilleros de las películas "
"y las personas que piensan que los fidget spinner eran demasiado seguros."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "folding knife"
msgid_plural "folding knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo plegable"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos plegables"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos plegables"

#. ~ Description of "folding knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A small folding knife with a locking blade and a pocket clip.  Not as good a"
" weapon as a solid fixed-blade knife, but better than a penknife."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño cuchillo plegable, con traba para la hoja y gancho para colgarlo "
"del cinto. No es tan buen arma como los que tienen cuchilla fija pero es "
"mejor que una navaja."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "combat knife"
msgid_plural "combat knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de combate"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de combate"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de combate"

#. ~ Description of "combat knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A military combat knife.  It is light and extremely sharp, and could be "
"deadly in either the right hands or when attached as a bayonet."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de combate militar. Es liviano, extremadamente afilado y puede "
"ser letal en las manos adecuadas o cuando se pone como bayoneta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "modified combat knife"
msgid_plural "modified combat knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de combate modificado"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de combate modificados"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de combate modificados"

#. ~ Description of "modified combat knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"A military combat knife.  It is light and extremely sharp, and could be "
"deadly in either the right hands or when attached as a bayonet.  This one "
"was modified and customized to mount on pretty much any weapon other than "
"pistols, if you so want."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo de combate militar. Es liviano, extremadamente afilado y puede "
"ser letal en las manos adecuadas o cuando se pone como bayoneta. Este ha "
"sido modificado y hecho a medida para poder ponerse en casi cualquier arma "
"si quieres, excepto pistolas."

#. ~ Highest non-powertool butchering quality.  It's made for skinning and
#. butchering game, which is what you're generally doing.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "hunting knife"
msgid_plural "hunting knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de caza"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de caza"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de caza"

#. ~ Highest non-powertool butchering quality.  It's made for skinning and
#. butchering game, which is what you're generally doing.
#. ~ Description of "hunting knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"Commonly used by hunters, this single-edged sheath knife is designed for "
"cutting and skinning game rather than combat."
msgstr ""
"Comúnmente utilizado por cazadores, este cuchillo de un solo filo está "
"diseñado para cortar y despellejar a los animales, no para el combate."

#. ~ This isn't really supposed to be a very good knife, or a very good saw.
#. It's more for looking scary.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "survival knife"
msgid_plural "survival knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de supervivencia"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de supervivencia"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de supervivencia"

#. ~ This isn't really supposed to be a very good knife, or a very good saw.
#. It's more for looking scary.
#. ~ Description of "survival knife"
#: data/json/items/melee/swords_and_blades.json
msgid ""
"This massive knife features a hollow handle with a compass built into the "
"pommel and a row of fearsome-looking saw teeth along the back of its blade."
msgstr ""
"Este enorme cuchillo tiene una empuñadura hueca con una brújula incorporada "
"en el pomo y una hilera de dientes de sierra imponentes en la parte de atrás"
