msgstr[1] "hilos Nomex"
msgstr[2] "hilos Nomex"

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Description of "Nomex thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Some heat-resistant Nomex thread that would be particularly useful for "
"making heat protection gear, though it's fine to use in place of normal "
"thread too, in most cases."
msgstr ""
"Algún hilo de Nomex resistente al calor que sería particularmente útil para "
"hacer equipo de protección contra el calor, aunque también se puede usar en "
"lugar del hilo normal, en la mayoría de los casos."

#. ~ heavyweight cotton canvas with a GSM of 400-450
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "canvas sheet"
msgid_plural "canvas sheets"
msgstr[0] "tela de lona"
msgstr[1] "telas de lona"
msgstr[2] "telas de lona"

#. ~ heavyweight cotton canvas with a GSM of 400-450
#. ~ Description of "canvas sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A 12 inch by 24 inch sheet of durable and waterproof waxed canvas fabric, "
"suitable for making tough bags and clothing."
msgstr ""
"Una tela de lona de 30x60cm, fuerte e impermeable, ideal para hacer ropa y "
"bolsos resistentes."

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "heavy duty thread"
msgid_plural "heavy duty threads"
msgstr[0] "hilo reforzado"
msgstr[1] "hilos reforzados"
msgstr[2] "hilos reforzados"

#. ~ 30 meters of thread per 1g, roughly 6 inches of thread per unit.
#. ~ Description of "heavy duty thread"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Some tough canvas-weight thread, sturdier than ordinary thread.  You could "
"meticulously weave this into a sheet of canvas cloth.  It would also be "
"useful for stitching such sheets together, though it's fine to use for "
"normal tailoring projects too."
msgstr ""
"Un poco de hilo reforzado de lona, más fuerte que el hilo común. Podrías "
"tejerlo meticulosamente y hacer una tela de lona. También sería útil para "
"coser esas telas aunque se puede usar para los trabajos de sastrería "
"normales."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "canvas scraps"
msgid_plural "canvas scraps"
msgstr[0] "pedazo de lona"
msgstr[1] "pedazos de lona"
msgstr[2] "pedazos de lona"

#. ~ Description of "canvas scraps"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"Oddly-shaped smallish bits of canvas, waste material from tailoring "
"projects.  Not useful for much and usually disposed of, but can be recycled "
"into some tough thread."
msgstr ""
"Pequeños pedazos irregulares de lona, desperdicio de algún trabajo de "
"sastrería. No son muy útiles pero pueden ser reciclados para hacer hilo "
"resistente."

#. ~ Roughly 400-450 GSM cotton, with a size of 6 inches square
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "canvas patch"
msgid_plural "canvas patches"
msgstr[0] "parche de lona"
msgstr[1] "parches de lona"
msgstr[2] "parches de lona"

#. ~ Roughly 400-450 GSM cotton, with a size of 6 inches square
#. ~ Description of "canvas patch"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A small, 6 inch square patch of tough canvas.  It could be used to repair "
"items made of canvas or stitched into patchwork sheets for tailoring "
"projects."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño parche cuadrado de 15 centímetros de lona resistente. Se puede "
"usar para reparar objetos hechos de tela o coser con otros para armar una "
"lona de retales para algún trabajo de sastrería."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid "patchwork canvas sheet"
msgid_plural "patchwork canvas sheets"
msgstr[0] "tela de retales de lona"
msgstr[1] "telas de retales de lona"
msgstr[2] "telas de retales de lona"

#. ~ Description of "patchwork canvas sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/tailoring.json
msgid ""
"A selection of various sections of canvas, sewn together in a patchwork "
"fashion.  Suitable for tailoring, though it's much less time-efficient than "
"if using proper material sheets."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de diversos pedazos de lona, cosidos para formar una tela de "
"retales. Útil para trabajos de sastrería aunque es mucho menos eficiente que"
" utilizar telas apropiadas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "log"
msgid_plural "logs"
msgstr[0] "leño"
msgstr[1] "leños"
msgstr[2] "leños"

#. ~ Description of "log"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A large chunk of log, cut from a tree.  (a)ctivate a wood axe or wood saw to"
" cut it into planks."
msgstr ""
"Un gran trozo de leño, cortado de un árbol. (a)ctivar un hacha de madera o "
"una sierra de madera para cortarlo en tablones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "splintered wood"
msgid_plural "splintered wood"
msgstr[0] "astilla de madera"
msgstr[1] "astillas de madera"
msgstr[2] "astillas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "splintered wood"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "A splintered piece of wood, could be used as a skewer or for kindling."
msgstr ""
"Una trozo de astilla de madera que puede ser usada como un pincho o leña."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json data/mods/MMA/bludgeons.json
msgid "stick"
msgid_plural "sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo"
msgstr[1] "palos"
msgstr[2] "palos"

#. ~ Description of "stick"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A respectable length of wood, just big enough to wrap your hand around.  "
"Makes a decent melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una longitud respetable de madera, lo suficientemente grande como para "
"envolver tu mano. Un arma de combate c. a c. decente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long stick"
msgid_plural "long sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo largo"
msgstr[1] "palos largos"
msgstr[2] "palos largos"

#. ~ Description of "long stick"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A straight section of wood, about eight feet long and a couple of inches in "
"diameter.  Makes a decent melee weapon, and can be broken into shorter "
"pieces for crafting."
msgstr ""
"Una sección recta de madera, de unos dos metros de largo y un par de "
"centímetros de diámetro. Constituye un arma de c. a c. decente, y puede "
"romperse en trozos más cortos para la fabricación."

#. ~ a long pole is a single piece of wood, and the heavy stick just isn't
#. large enough.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long pole"
msgid_plural "long poles"
msgstr[0] "palo largo"
msgstr[1] "palos largos"
msgstr[2] "palos largos"

#. ~ a long pole is a single piece of wood, and the heavy stick just isn't
#. large enough.
#. ~ Description of "long pole"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A stout, ten-foot pole.  Could be used similarly to a spear.  The Cataclysm "
"gives fresh meaning to walking softly and carrying a big stick."
msgstr ""
"Un palo robusto de tres metros. Podría usarse de forma similar a una lanza. "
"El Cataclismo le da un nuevo significado a caminar suavemente y llevar un "
"gran palo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "spear shaft"
msgid_plural "spear shaft"
msgstr[0] "lanza de palo"
msgstr[1] "lanzas de palo"
msgstr[2] "lanzas de palo"

#. ~ Description of "spear shaft"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A long stick, sanded and treated with oil for integrity and carved into a "
"smooth staff with a slight taper, for use in making spears.  It can also be "
"used as a makeshift quarterstaff as-is, but is too thin to be very effective"
" for just hitting people."
msgstr ""
"Un palo largo lijado, tratado con aceite para mayor solidez y tallado para "
"hacerlo suave y estrecho, utilizado para hacer lanzas. También puede usarse "
"para hacer una vara larga improvisada pero es demasiado fina para ser "
"efectiva para golpear."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "plank"
msgid_plural "planks"
msgstr[0] "tablón"
msgstr[1] "tablones"
msgstr[2] "tablones"

#. ~ Description of "plank"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A narrow, thick plank of wood, like a 2 by 4 or similar piece of dimensional"
" lumber.  Makes a decent melee weapon if you're desperate, and can be used "
"for all kinds construction."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera resistente y fino, similar a una tabla u otro pedazo de "
"madera. Es bastante decente como arma de c. a c. si estás medio desesperado,"
" y se puede usar para construir muchas cosas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "short plank"
msgid_plural "short planks"
msgstr[0] "tablón corto"
msgstr[1] "tablones cortos"
msgstr[2] "tablones cortos"

#. ~ Description of "short plank"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A short 2 by 4 plank of wood.  While less common and smaller than its 4 foot"
" cousin it can still be very useful in carpentry."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón corto de madera de 60cm por 120cm. Es menos común y pequeño que su"
" primo de 120cm pero aun es útil en materia de carpintería."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long plank"
msgid_plural "long planks"
msgstr[0] "tablón largo"
msgstr[1] "tablones largos"
msgstr[2] "tablones largos"

#. ~ Description of "long plank"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A long 2 by 4 plank of wood.  While not as common as the 4 foot variant, "
"still makes a decent melee weapon, and can be used for all kinds "
"construction."
msgstr ""
"Un tablón de madera de 60cm por 120cm. Aunque no es tan común como su "
"variante de 120cm, todavía es un arma de c. a c. decente, y se puede "
"utilizar para todo tipo de construcciones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "heavy wooden beam"
msgid_plural "heavy wooden beams"
msgstr[0] "viga de madera pesada"
msgstr[1] "vigas de madera pesadas"
msgstr[2] "vigas de madera pesadas"

#. ~ Description of "heavy wooden beam"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"An enormous beam of solid wood, very heavy and hard to lug around, but also "
"very sturdy for construction.  You could saw or chop it into smaller pieces,"
" like planks or panels."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme viga de madera maciza, muy pesada y difícil de arrastrar, pero "
"también muy resistente para la construcción. Podrías serrarla o cortarla en "
"trozos más pequeños, como tablones o paneles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "wooden post"
msgid_plural "wooden posts"
msgstr[0] "poste de madera"
msgstr[1] "postes de madera"
msgstr[2] "postes de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden post"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to "
"this are commonly used in mailboxes or as table legs."
msgstr ""
"Un poste de madera de 4 por 4 con base cuadrada. Postes con una longitud "
"similar a este son usados comúnmente en buzones y patas de mesas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "short wooden post"
msgid_plural "short wooden posts"
msgstr[0] "poste de madera corto"
msgstr[1] "postes de madera cortos"
msgstr[2] "postes de madera cortos"

#. ~ Description of "short wooden post"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to "
"this are commonly used as chair legs."
msgstr ""
"Un poste de madera de 4 por 4 con base cuadrada. Postes con una longitud "
"similar a este son usados comúnmente en patas de sillas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "long wooden post"
msgid_plural "long wooden posts"
msgstr[0] "poste de madera largo"
msgstr[1] "postes de madera largos"
msgstr[2] "postes de madera largos"

#. ~ Description of "long wooden post"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wooden post with a 4 by 4 square base.  Posts with a length similar to "
"this are commonly used in the construction of walls and floors."
msgstr ""
"Un poste de madera de 4 por 4 con base cuadrada. Postes con una longitud "
"similar a este son usados comúnmente en la construcción de muros y suelos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "small wood block"
msgid_plural "small wood blocks"
msgstr[0] "pequeño bloque de madera"
msgstr[1] "pequeños bloques de madera"
msgstr[2] "pequeños bloques de madera"

#. ~ Description of "small wood block"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A small 2x2x5 inches block of wood, primarily used for carving out small "
"wooden objects."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño bloque de madera de 5x5x12 centímetros, principalmente usado para"
" tallar objetos pequeños."

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 16 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  The actual
#. size of the panel likely varies wildly and the item entry may represent
#. several smaller pieces.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "wooden panel"
msgid_plural "wooden panels"
msgstr[0] "panel de madera"
msgstr[1] "paneles de madera"
msgstr[2] "paneles de madera"

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 16 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  The actual
#. size of the panel likely varies wildly and the item entry may represent
#. several smaller pieces.
#. ~ Description of "wooden panel"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A wide, thin wooden board - plywood, OSB, MDF, tongue-in-groove boards, or "
"similar, already cut to shape.  These large flat boards are good for all "
"kinds of construction, but for really big projects you'd need a proper sheet"
" of uncut plywood or the like."
msgstr ""
"Un tablero de madera ancho y delgado - contrachapado, OSB, MDF, tablas de "
"lengüeta en ranura, o similar, ya cortado en forma. Estos grandes tableros "
"planos son buenos para todo tipo de construcción, pero para proyectos "
"realmente grandes se necesita una hoja adecuada de madera contrachapada sin "
"cortar o similar."

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 32 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  Due to its
#. enormously bulky shape, volume is higher than actual displacement volume
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "large wooden sheet"
msgid_plural "large wooden sheets"
msgstr[0] "lamina de madera grande"
msgstr[1] "laminas de madera grandes"
msgstr[2] "laminas de madera grandes"

#. ~ Weight and volume assumes 32 square feet of 1/2 inch plywood.  Due to its
#. enormously bulky shape, volume is higher than actual displacement volume
#. ~ Description of "large wooden sheet"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"A standard 4x8 sheet of flat wood - usually plywood, OSB, or MDF.  Heavy and"
" bulky, this is extremely useful for all manner of construction, but you "
"might have to cut it to size before doing smaller projects."
msgstr ""
"Una hoja estándar de 4x8 de madera plana, normalmente de contrachapado, OSB "
"o MDF. Pesada y voluminosa, es extremadamente útil para todo tipo de "
"construcción, pero puede que tengas que cortarla a medida antes de hacer "
"proyectos más pequeños."

#. ~ weight for a bit less than 3x3x4 wooden beam at 0.60 g/cm3 density,
#. substracted from wood beam stats above
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid "giant wooden screw"
msgid_plural "giant wooden screws"
msgstr[0] "tornillo gigante de madera"
msgstr[1] "tornillos gigantes de madera"
msgstr[2] "tornillos gigantes de madera"

#. ~ weight for a bit less than 3x3x4 wooden beam at 0.60 g/cm3 density,
#. substracted from wood beam stats above
#. ~ Description of "giant wooden screw"
#: data/json/items/resources/wood.json
msgid ""
"An giant screw carved out of solid wood, a simple component used to convert "
"rotational energy into a downward movement of greater force."
msgstr ""
"Un tornillo gigante tallado en madera sólida, un componente sencillo "
"utilizado para convertir energía rotativa en un movimiento descendente de "
"mayor fuerza."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/container.json
msgid "steel bottle"
msgid_plural "steel bottles"
msgstr[0] "botella de acero"
msgstr[1] "botellas de acero"
msgstr[2] "botellas de acero"

#. ~ Description of "steel bottle"
#: data/json/items/tool/container.json
msgid "A stainless steel water bottle, holds 750ml of liquid."
msgstr "Es una botella de acero inoxidable, que puede contener hasta 750 ml."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/container.json
msgid "foldable plastic bottle"
msgid_plural "foldable plastic bottles"
msgstr[0] "botella plegable de plástico"
msgstr[1] "botellas plegables de plástico"
msgstr[2] "botellas plegables de plástico"

#. ~ Description of "foldable plastic bottle"
#: data/json/items/tool/container.json
msgid "A non-rigid plastic bottle for easy storage, holds 500 ml of liquid."
msgstr ""
"Una botella flexible de plástico, fácil de transportar, que puede contener "
"hasta 500 ml."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "atomic coffee maker"
msgid_plural "atomic coffee makers"
msgstr[0] "cafetera atómica"
msgstr[1] "cafeteras atómicas"
msgstr[2] "cafeteras atómicas"

#. ~ Description of "atomic coffee maker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a Curie-G coffeemaker, by CuppaTech.  It famously uses a radioactive"
" generator to heat water for coffee.  Normally the water is heated using "
"energy stored in a capacitor, and makes ordinary coffee.  However, as a "
"special feature, water from the RTG containment area can be used, giving the"
" coffee a very special kick.  The Curie-G is illegal in most countries."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una cafetera Curie-G, de CuppaTech. Es famosa por usar un generador "
"radioactivo para calentar agua para el café. Normalmente el agua se calienta"
" usando la energía almacenada en un condensador, y hace café ordinario. Sin "
"embargo, como característica especial, se puede utilizar el agua del área de"
" contención de RTG, dándole al café un toque muy especial. El Curie-G es "
"ilegal en la mayoría de los países."

#. ~ butcher knives and carving knives are between 30-40cm.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "butchering kit"
msgid_plural "butchering kits"
msgstr[0] "kit de descuartizamiento"
msgstr[1] "kits de descuartizamiento"
msgstr[2] "kits de descuartizamiento"

#. ~ butcher knives and carving knives are between 30-40cm.
#. ~ Description of "butchering kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a kit containing all the specialized knives you need to debone, "
"skin, and prepare cuts of meat from an animal."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de un kit que contiene todos los cuchillos especializados que "
"necesita para deshuesar, pelar y preparar cortes de carne de un animal."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "pseudo butter churn"
msgid_plural "pseudo butter churns"
msgstr[0] "pseudo mantequera"
msgstr[1] "pseudo mantequeras"
msgstr[2] "pseudo mantequeras"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "can sealer"
msgid_plural "can sealers"
msgstr[0] "enlatadora"
msgstr[1] "enlatadoras"
msgstr[2] "enlatadoras"

#. ~ Description of "can sealer"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A hand crank powered cast steel machine designed to automatically seal tin "
"cans."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina de acero fundido accionada por manivela diseñada para sellar "
"automáticamente las latas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/tools.json
msgid "electric carver (off)"
msgid_plural "electric carvers (off)"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo eléctrico (off)"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos eléctricos (off)"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos eléctricos (off)"

#. ~ Description of "electric carver (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"An electric meat carver powered by batteries.  Two serrated blades that "
"vibrate together to slice just about anything from turkey to ham… even "
"zombies!"
msgstr ""
"Una máquina eléctrica para cortar carne que funciona con baterías. Dos "
"cuchillas dentadas que vibran juntas para cortar casi cualquier cosa, desde "
"pavo hasta jamón... ¡incluso zombis!"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "electric carver (on)"
msgid_plural "electric carvers (on)"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo eléctrico (on)"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos eléctricos (on)"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos eléctricos (on)"

#. ~ Description of "electric carver (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "This carver is on and the blades are buzzing.  Use it to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"Este cuchillo está encendido y las cuchillas están vibrando. Usar para "
"apagar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "charcoal water purifier"
msgid_plural "charcoal water purifiers"
msgstr[0] "purificador agua a carbón"
msgstr[1] "purificadores agua a carbón"
msgstr[2] "purificadores agua a carbón"

#. ~ Description of "charcoal water purifier"
#. ~ Description of "large charcoal water purifier"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"Using this item on a container full of water will purify the water using "
"layered charcoal.  Once the charcoal has purified enough water, it will "
"become unusable and can be disassembled and recycled.  Water taken from "
"uncertain sources like a river may be dirty."
msgstr ""
"Al usar este objeto en un recipiente lleno de agua, vas a potabilizar el "
"agua usando capas de carbón. Una vez que el carbón vegetal ha purificado "
"suficiente agua, empezará a volverse inutilizable y puede ser desmontado y "
"reciclado. El agua recogida de fuentes inseguras como los ríos, puede estar "
"sucia."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "large charcoal water purifier"
msgid_plural "large charcoal water purifiers"
msgstr[0] "purificador de agua grande de carbón vegetal"
msgstr[1] "purificadores de agua grandes de carbón vegetal"
msgstr[2] "purificadores de agua grandes de carbón vegetal"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "charcoal smoker"
msgid_plural "charcoal smokers"
msgstr[0] "ahumador de carbón"
msgstr[1] "ahumadores de carbón"
msgstr[2] "ahumadores de carbón"

#. ~ Description of "charcoal smoker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable charcoal smoker.  Good for weekend barbecuing and "
"preserving meat with smoke."
msgstr ""
"Este es ahumador portátil de carbón vegetal. Bueno para asaderos en fines de"
" semana y ahumar carne com humo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "charcoal cooker"
msgid_plural "charcoal cookers"
msgstr[0] "cocina de carbón vegetal"
msgstr[1] "cocinas de carbón vegetal"
msgstr[2] "cocinas de carbón vegetal"

#. ~ Description of "charcoal cooker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a little metal tank for holding charcoal with a pilot light "
"attached.  You could use it for cooking food."
msgstr ""
"Este es un pequeño depósito metálico para contener carbón vegetal con un "
"piloto incorporado. Se puede utilizar para cocinar alimentos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "clay pot"
msgid_plural "clay pots"
msgstr[0] "olla de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "ollas de arcilla"
msgstr[2] "ollas de arcilla"

#. ~ Description of "clay pot"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "A crude clay pot with lid used for cooking."
msgstr "Una olla de arcilla con tapa que se usa para cocinar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "clay quern"
msgid_plural "clay querns"
msgstr[0] "mortero de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "morteros de arcilla"
msgstr[2] "morteros de arcilla"

#. ~ Description of "clay quern"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "This is a simple hand-powered clay quern for grinding grain."
msgstr "Es un simple mortero de mano hecho de arcilla, para moler grano."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "clay teapot"
msgid_plural "clay teapots"
msgstr[0] "tetera de arcilla"
msgstr[1] "teteras de arcilla"
msgstr[2] "teteras de arcilla"

#. ~ Description of "clay teapot"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "A clay teapot.  Now all you need is tea and water."
msgstr "Una tetera de arcilla. Ahora lo único que necesitas es té y agua."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "coffeemaker"
msgid_plural "coffeemakers"
msgstr[0] "cafetera"
msgstr[1] "cafeteras"
msgstr[2] "cafeteras"

#. ~ Description of "coffeemaker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a heating element with pot and frame for holding coffee or other "
"powders.  It's got a battery compartment for use when the power goes out.  "
"You can use it to make coffee, or other drinks if you so choose."
msgstr ""
"Este es un calentador eléctrico con una jarra y soporte para poner el café u"
" otros polvos. Tiene un compartimiento para la batería que usa cuando no "
"tiene corriente eléctrica. Se puede usar para hacer café, o alguna otra "
"bebida de tu elección."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "food dehydrator"
msgid_plural "food dehydrators"
msgstr[0] "deshidratador de comida"
msgstr[1] "deshidratadores de comida"
msgstr[2] "deshidratadores de comida"

#. ~ Description of "food dehydrator"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable electric food dehydrator.  It's powered by batteries, and"
" could be invaluable in preserving food."
msgstr ""
"Es un deshidratador eléctrico y portátil de comida. Está alimentado con "
"baterías, y puede ser muy importante para conservar comida."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "fermenting eggs jar"
msgid_plural "fermenting eggs jars"
msgstr[0] "bote de huevos fermentados"
msgstr[1] "botes de huevos fermentados"
msgstr[2] "botes de huevos fermentados"

#. ~ Description of "fermenting eggs jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This jar contains a batch of eggs in a pickling solution.  You can seal up "
"the jar once the process is completed."
msgstr ""
"Este tarro contiene un lote de huevos en una solución de encurtido. Puedes "
"sellar el tarro una vez que el proceso se haya completado."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "fermenting eggs jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"You examine the batch and see that the pickling solution has done its job, "
"so you seal the jar up for storage."
msgstr ""
"Examinas el lote y ves que la solución de encurtido ha hecho su trabajo, así"
" que sellas el frasco para el almacenamiento."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "fermenting eggs jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "The eggs are not done yet."
msgstr "Los huevos no están listos todavía."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "hexamine stove"
msgid_plural "hexamine stoves"
msgstr[0] "cocina de hexamina"
msgstr[1] "cocinas de hexamina"
msgstr[2] "cocinas de hexamina"

#. ~ Description of "hexamine stove"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"Known as an Esbit stove, this is a lightweight, folding stove designed to "
"use small hexamine tablets for cooking."
msgstr ""
"Conocida como la cocina Esbit, esta es una cocina liviana, plegable, "
"diseñada para usar pequeñas pastillas de hexamina para cocinar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "sealed yeast culture"
msgid_plural "sealed yeast culture"
msgstr[0] "cultivo de levadura sellada"
msgstr[1] "cultivo de levadura sellada"
msgstr[2] "cultivo de levadura sellada"

#. ~ Description of "sealed yeast culture"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A sealed jar holding sanitized yeast wort.  You may harvest the yeast inside"
" when it's done culturing."
msgstr ""
"Un tarro sellado que contiene mosto de levadura saneada. Puedes cosechar la "
"levadura en su interior cuando haya terminado de cultivarse."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "sealed yeast culture"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "You open the jar and harvest the culture."
msgstr "Abres el tarro y cosechas el cultivo."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "sealed yeast culture"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "The yeast isn't done culturing yet."
msgstr "La levadura todavía no terminó su proceso de cultivo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "food processor"
msgid_plural "food processors"
msgstr[0] "procesador de comida"
msgstr[1] "procesadores de comida"
msgstr[2] "procesadores de comida"

#. ~ Description of "food processor"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a kitchen appliance capable of slicing, chopping, shredding, "
"grinding, pureeing and mixing."
msgstr ""
"Este es un aparato de cocina capaz de rebanar, cortar, triturar, moler, "
"hacer puré y mezclar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "gasoline cooker"
msgid_plural "gasoline cookers"
msgstr[0] "cocina de gasolina"
msgstr[1] "cocinas de gasolina"
msgstr[2] "cocinas de gasolina"

#. ~ Description of "gasoline cooker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple heater powered by gasoline.  It is designed for cooking "
"food."
msgstr ""
"Es un simple calentador alimentado con gasolina. Está diseñado para cocinar "
"comida."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "heat pack"
msgid_plural "heat packs"
msgstr[0] "almohadilla termoquímica"
msgstr[1] "almohadillas termoquímicas"
msgstr[2] "almohadillas termoquímicas"

#. ~ Description of "heat pack"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a chemical heat pack.  It's used to treat sports injuries and heat "
"food.  It is usable only once."
msgstr ""
"Es una almohadilla térmica que funciona químicamente. Es utilizada para "
"tratar lesiones corporales y para calentar comida también. Solo se puede "
"usar una vez."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "used heat pack"
msgid_plural "used heat packs"
msgstr[0] "almohadilla termoquímica usada"
msgstr[1] "almohadillas termoquímicas usadas"
msgstr[2] "almohadillas termoquímicas usadas"

#. ~ Description of "used heat pack"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a chemical heat pack.  It's used to treat sports injuries and heat "
"food.  This one has been used and is chemically inert, rendering it useless."
msgstr ""
"Es una almohadilla térmica que funciona químicamente. Es utilizada para "
"tratar lesiones corporales y para calentar comida también. Esta ya ha sido "
"usada y es químicamente inerte, lo que la hace inservible."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "hotplate"
msgid_plural "hotplates"
msgstr[0] "placa térmica eléctrica"
msgstr[1] "placa térmica eléctricas"
msgstr[2] "placa térmica eléctricas"

#. ~ Description of "hotplate"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a small heating element on a stand, powered by batteries.  It is "
"indispensable for cooking and chemistry.  Try not to burn yourself."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño calentador eléctrico puesto en un soporte, alimentado con "
"baterías. Es indispensable para cocinar y para química. Intenta no quemarte."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "makeshift vacuum sealer"
msgid_plural "makeshift vacuum sealers"
msgstr[0] "sellador improvisado al vacío"
msgstr[1] "selladores improvisados al vacío"
msgstr[2] "selladores improvisados al vacío"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift vacuum sealer"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a homemade heat sealer unit with an air pump.  It's used for vacuum "
"packing food to preserve it."
msgstr ""
"Es un sellador por calor hecho en casa con una bomba de aire. Se usa para "
"empaquetar comida al vacío y preservarla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "mess kit"
msgid_plural "mess kits"
msgstr[0] "kit de utensilios"
msgstr[1] "kits de utensilios"
msgstr[2] "kits de utensilios"

#. ~ Description of "mess kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A self-contained camping mess kit, containing everything you might need for "
"wilderness cooking.  This model relies on a battery-operated hotplate, "
"rather than the more commonplace chemical-fueled Esbit stove."
msgstr ""
"Un kit de utensilios con todo lo que puedes necesitar para cuando cocinas "
"estando en la naturaleza. Este modelo depende de una placa térmica eléctrica"
" que funciona con baterías, en lugar del \"horno Esbit\" más común "
"alimentado con químicos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "mess tin"
msgid_plural "mess tins"
msgstr[0] "lata de utensilios"
msgstr[1] "latas de utensilios"
msgstr[2] "latas de utensilios"

#. ~ Description of "mess tin"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A compact military-style pan and tray, designed for heating food over a fire"
" or portable stove.  It is shallower than a proper pot or pan, and lacks the"
" integrated heating elements modern mess kits have."
msgstr ""
"Una olla-bandeja compacta, de estilo militar, diseñada para calentar la "
"comida sobre un fuego o cocina portátil. No es tan honda como una olla "
"propiamente dicha, y le faltan las resistencias térmicas que poseen los "
"modernos kits de utensilios."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "milk cream jar"
msgid_plural "milk cream jars"
msgstr[0] "tarro de crema de leche"
msgstr[1] "tarros de crema de leche"
msgstr[2] "tarros de crema de leche"

#. ~ Description of "milk cream jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This jar contains raw milk separated into cream.  It is sealed until you are"
" ready to use it."
msgstr ""
"Este tarro contiene leche cruda separada en crema. Está sellado hasta que "
"estés listo para usarlo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "rising cream jar"
msgid_plural "rising cream jars"
msgstr[0] "tarro de crema ascendente"
msgstr[1] "tarros de crema ascendente"
msgstr[2] "tarros de crema ascendente"

#. ~ Description of "rising cream jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This jar contains raw milk separating into cream.  You can seal up the jar "
"once the process is completed."
msgstr ""
"Este tarro contiene leche cruda que se separa en crema. Puedes sellar el "
"tarro una vez que el proceso se haya completado."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "rising cream jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"You examine the batch and see that the cream has risen to the top, so you "
"seal the jar up for storage."
msgstr ""
"Examinas el lote y ves que la crema ha subido a la parte superior, así que "
"sellas el frasco para su almacenamiento."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "rising cream jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "The cream has not risen yet."
msgstr "La crema no ha subido todavía."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "military mess kit"
msgid_plural "military mess kits"
msgstr[0] "kit militar de utensilios"
msgstr[1] "kits militares de utensilios"
msgstr[2] "kits militares de utensilios"

#. ~ Description of "military mess kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"Military mess kit designed for long-range reconnaissance patrols deployed "
"behind enemy lines.  All parts are made from thin sheet of aluminum / "
"superalloy composite and are insulated with ceramic coating.  Relies on a "
"battery-operated hotplate, rather than the smoke-producing chemical-fueled "
"Esbit stove.  Compact, durable and lightweight."
msgstr ""
"Un kit militar de utensilios diseñado para patrullas de reconocimiento que "
"pasan mucho tiempo detrás de las líneas enemigas. Todos sus componentes "
"están hechos de una delgada capa compuesto de aluminio y superaleación, y "
"están aislados con una cobertura cerámica. Depende de una placa térmica "
"eléctrica que funciona con baterías, en lugar del horno Esbit más común "
"alimentado con químicos. Compacto, duradero y liviano."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "mortar and pestle"
msgid_plural "mortars and pestles"
msgstr[0] "mortero y mazo"
msgstr[1] "morteros y mazos"
msgstr[2] "morteros y mazos"

#. ~ Description of "mortar and pestle"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple combination of a small grindstone and a bowl-shaped stone."
"  Used for grinding grain, but time-consuming compared to more complex "
"methods."
msgstr ""
"Es una simple combinación de una pequeña piedra de amolar y una piedra con "
"forma de tazón. Se usa para moler granos, pero lleva mucho más tiempo que "
"otros métodos más complejos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "multi cooker"
msgid_plural "multi cookers"
msgstr[0] "multicocina"
msgstr[1] "multicocinas"
msgstr[2] "multicocinas"

#. ~ Description of "multi cooker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A professional-grade multi-cooker, with a battery slot for camping trips or "
"tailgating.  Its multitude of settings and features promise to handle any "
"sort of cooking, from parboiling potatoes to cooking curry to popping "
"popcorn.  There's no manual, but you're sure you can work it out."
msgstr ""
"Una multicocina profesional, con compartimiento para baterías para cuando te"
" vas de camping. Su multitud de funciones prometen poder resolver cualquier "
"preparación de comidas, desde patatas a medio cocer hasta hacer curry o "
"maíz. No tiene manual de instrucciones, pero seguro que vas a saber usarla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "multi cooker - cooking"
msgid_plural "multi cooker - cookings"
msgstr[0] "multicocina - cocinando"
msgstr[1] "multicocinas - cocinando"
msgstr[2] "multicocinas - cocinando"

#. ~ Description of "multi cooker - cooking"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A professional-grade multi-cooker, with a battery slot for camping trips or "
"tailgating.  There is a dish in it."
msgstr ""
"Un multicocina profesional, con una ranura para la batería para viajes de "
"camping o para el transporte trasero. Tiene un plato."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "kerosene cooker"
msgid_plural "kerosene cookers"
msgstr[0] "cocina a queroseno"
msgstr[1] "cocinas a queroseno"
msgstr[2] "cocinas a queroseno"

#. ~ Description of "kerosene cooker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple heater powered by kerosene.  It is designed for cooking "
"food."
msgstr ""
"Un simple calentador alimentado con queroseno. Está diseñado para cocinar "
"comida."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "manual oil press"
msgid_plural "manual oil presses"
msgstr[0] "prensador manual de aceite"
msgstr[1] "prensadores manuales de aceite"
msgstr[2] "prensadores manuales de aceite"

#. ~ Description of "manual oil press"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a hand cranked press for creating vegetable oil.  A hotplate heats "
"the raw material to increase extraction efficiency."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una prensa de manivela para crear aceite vegetal. Una placa caliente"
" calienta la materia prima para aumentar la eficacia de la extracción."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "oil powered manual oil press"
msgid_plural "oil powered manual oil presses"
msgstr[0] "prensa manual a aceite para extracción de aceite"
msgstr[1] "prensas manuales a aceite para extracción de aceite"
msgstr[2] "prensas manuales a aceite para extracción de aceite"

#. ~ Description of "oil powered manual oil press"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A barrel with a large screw press for creating vegetable oil.  A kerosene "
"cooker heats the raw material to increase extraction efficiency."
msgstr ""
"Un barril con una prensa de tornillo grande para fabricar aceite vegetal.  "
"Una cocina de queroseno calienta el material crudo para incrementar la "
"eficiencia de la extracción."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "pasta extruder"
msgid_plural "pasta extruders"
msgstr[0] "máquina de pasta"
msgstr[1] "máquinas de pasta"
msgstr[2] "máquinas de pasta"

#. ~ Description of "pasta extruder"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A pasta extruder run by a hand-crank.  Useful in making pasta.  It comes "
"with various heads to make various kinds of pasta."
msgstr ""
"Una máquina para hacer pastas con una manivela. Se usa para hacer pastas. "
"Tiene diferentes cabezales para hacer distintas variedades de pasta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "fermenting pickle jar"
msgid_plural "fermenting pickle jars"
msgstr[0] "tarro de pepinillos fermentados"
msgstr[1] "tarros de pepinillos fermentados"
msgstr[2] "tarros de pepinillos fermentados"

#. ~ Description of "fermenting pickle jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This jar contains a batch of pickles set to ferment.  You can seal up the "
"jar once the process is completed."
msgstr ""
"Este tarro contiene un lote de pepinillos puestos a fermentar. Puedes sellar"
" el tarro una vez que el proceso se haya completado."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "fermenting pickle jar"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "fermenting sauerkraut jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"You test the batch, and it tastes good, so you seal the jar up for storage."
msgstr ""
"Pruebas la fermentación, y tiene buen gusto así que sellas la bote para "
"almacenarla."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "fermenting pickle jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "The pickles are not done fermenting yet."
msgstr "Los encurtidos no han terminado de fermentar todavía."

#. ~ Should be 20 but currently recipes do not utilize this value
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "soda can stove kit"
msgid_plural "soda can stove kits"
msgstr[0] "kit de cocina de latas de refresco"
msgstr[1] "kits de cocina de latas de refresco"
msgstr[2] "kits de cocina de latas de refresco"

#. ~ Should be 20 but currently recipes do not utilize this value
#. ~ Description of "soda can stove kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is an ultra-light alcohol-burning stove with simmer ring, crafted by "
"hand from a couple of aluminum soda cans.  It comes with a 500 ml plastic "
"bottle to hold concentrated alcohol fuel."
msgstr ""
"Es una cocina de alcohol ultraligera con un anillo de cocción lenta, creado "
"a mano con un par de latas de aluminio de refresco. Viene con una botella "
"plástica de 500 ml para el alcohol concentrado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "pressure cooker"
msgid_plural "pressure cookers"
msgstr[0] "olla de presión"
msgstr[1] "ollas de presión"
msgstr[2] "ollas de presión"

#. ~ Description of "pressure cooker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"Useful for boiling water when cooking spaghetti and more.  This sealed pot "
"is designed to cook food at higher pressures and temperatures.  Can also be "
"used for pressure sensitive chemical reactions."
msgstr ""
"Es útil para hervir el agua cuando se cocinan espaguetis y más. Esta olla "
"sellada está diseñada para cocinar alimentos a mayores presiones y "
"temperaturas. También se puede usar para reacciones químicas sensibles a la "
"presión."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "stone quern"
msgid_plural "stone querns"
msgstr[0] "molino de mano de piedra"
msgstr[1] "molinos de mano de piedra"
msgstr[2] "molinos de mano de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone quern"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple hand-powered stone quern with wooden handle, for grinding "
"grain."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de un sencillo molino manual con mango de madera, para moler grano."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "fermenting sauerkraut jar"
msgid_plural "fermenting sauerkraut jars"
msgstr[0] "bote de chucrut fermentando"
msgstr[1] "botes de chucrut fermentando"
msgstr[2] "botes de chucrut fermentando"

#. ~ Description of "fermenting sauerkraut jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This jar contains a batch of sauerkraut set to ferment.  You can seal up the"
" jar once the process is completed."
msgstr ""
"Esta tarro contiene un lote de chucrut preparada para fermentar. Puedes "
"sellar la tarro una vez que el proceso termine."

#. ~ "not_ready_msg" action message of item "fermenting sauerkraut jar"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "The sauerkraut isn't done fermenting yet."
msgstr "El chucrut todavía no terminó de fermentar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "wicker sieve"
msgid_plural "wicker sieves"
msgstr[0] "tamiz de mimbre"
msgstr[1] "tamices de mimbre"
msgstr[2] "tamices de mimbre"

#. ~ Description of "wicker sieve"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a primitive sieve constructed from woven strips of plant material.  "
"Early sieves like this were used to sift grain, though the openings on this "
"one are too small for that."
msgstr ""
"Este es un tamiz primitivo construido con tiras tejidas de material vegetal."
" Los primeros tamices como este se usaban para cribar el grano, aunque las "
"aberturas de este son demasiado pequeñas para eso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "sieve"
msgid_plural "sieves"
msgstr[0] "tamiz"
msgstr[1] "tamices"
msgstr[2] "tamices"

#. ~ Description of "sieve"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is no mere strainer for noodles; it's a sieve used to separate "
"particles of certain sizes.  You could use this to do a really good job "
"sifting flour, remove dust and soil from grain, or perhaps conduct gradation"
" tests for any civil engineers you might know.  This one has been "
"constructed from steel mesh."
msgstr ""
"Este no es un simple colador de fideos; es un tamiz que sirve para separar "
"partículas de determinados tamaños. Podrias utilizar esto para tamizar la "
"harina, eliminar el polvo y la tierra del grano, o tal vez realizar pruebas "
"de gradación para cualquier ingeniero civil que conozca. Este se ha "
"construido con malla de acero."

#. ~ Description of "still"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a still.  It's useful for creating distillations of alcohol and "
"other, more curious substances.  Features a slot for a thermometer."
msgstr ""
"Esto es un alambique. Es útil para crear destilaciones de alcohol y otras "
"sustancias más curiosas. Cuenta con una ranura para un termómetro."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "survivor mess kit"
msgid_plural "survivor mess kits"
msgstr[0] "kit de limpieza de sup."
msgstr[1] "kits de limpieza de sup."
msgstr[2] "kits de limpieza de sup."

#. ~ Description of "survivor mess kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"A homemade mess kit, containing everything you might need for creating post-"
"apocalyptic cuisine.  Powered by a kerosene burner, it is composed of simple"
" yet durable tools and materials."
msgstr ""
"Un kit de cocina casero que contiene todo lo necesario para crear una cocina"
" postapocalíptica. Alimentado por un quemador de queroseno, está compuesto "
"por herramientas y materiales sencillos pero duraderos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "teapot"
msgid_plural "teapots"
msgstr[0] "tetera"
msgstr[1] "teteras"
msgstr[2] "teteras"

#. ~ Description of "teapot"
#. ~ Description of "endless teapot"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_misc.json
msgid "A small metal teapot.  Teatime wouldn't be complete without one."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña tetera de metal. Si quieres beber un té, la vas a necesitar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "vacuum sealer"
msgid_plural "vacuum sealers"
msgstr[0] "sellador al vacío"
msgstr[1] "selladores al vacío"
msgstr[2] "selladores al vacío"

#. ~ Description of "vacuum sealer"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable heat sealer unit with an air pump.  It's used for vacuum "
"packing food to preserve it."
msgstr ""
"Es una unidad portátil de sellado por calor con una bomba de aire. Se usa "
"para empaquetar comida al vacío y preservarla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "waffle iron"
msgid_plural "waffle irons"
msgstr[0] "Gofrera de acero"
msgstr[1] "Gofreras de acero"
msgstr[2] "Gofreras de acero"

#. ~ Description of "waffle iron"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "A waffle iron.  For making waffles."
msgstr "Una gofrera de acero. Sirve para hacer gofres."

#. ~ Description of "water purifier"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a battery-powered device designed to purify drinking water.  Using "
"this item on a container full of water will purify the contents.  It could "
"be useful for water taken from uncertain sources like a river, as it may be "
"non-potable."
msgstr ""
"Es un dispositivo alimentado a batería, diseñado para potabilizar el agua. "
"Usando este objeto en un recipiente lleno de agua, purificará el contenido. "
"Puede ser útil para el agua recogida de fuentes inseguras como ríos, por si "
"no es potable."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid "propane cooker"
msgid_plural "propane cookers"
msgstr[0] "cocina de propano"
msgstr[1] "cocinas de propano"
msgstr[2] "cocinas de propano"

#. ~ Description of "propane cooker"
#: data/json/items/tool/cooking.json
msgid ""
"This is a simple heater powered by propane.  It is designed for cooking "
"food."
msgstr ""
"Es un simple calentador alimentado con propano. Está diseñado para cocinar "
"comida."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/debug_tools.json
msgid "debug lux meter"
msgid_plural "debug lux meters"
msgstr[0] "depurar medidor de luz"
msgstr[1] "depurar medidores de luz"
msgstr[2] "depurar medidores de luz"

#. ~ Description of "debug lux meter"
#: data/json/items/tool/debug_tools.json
msgid "This debug tool will tell you about light"
msgstr "Esta herramienta depuradora te da información sobre la luz"

#. ~ Description of "brazier"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A large metal stand used to contain a fire.  Fires set in a brazier will not"
" spread to surrounding flammable objects."
msgstr ""
"Un gran soporte de metal usado para contener el fuego. Los incendios que se "
"producen en un brasero no se propagan a los objetos inflamables "
"circundantes."

#. ~ Description of "hobo stove"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"This is a small improvised wood stove, made from a metal can or similar "
"container of the right size.  It's too small to fit anything much larger "
"than splintered wood.  Activate it to Deploy."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una pequeña estufa de leña improvisada, hecha con una lata de metal "
"o un recipiente similar del tamaño adecuado. Es demasiado pequeña para que "
"quepa algo mucho más grande que astillas de madera. Actívar para Desplegar."

#. ~ values based on real world 55 gallon metal barrel
#. ~ Description of "fire barrel (200L)"
#. ~ values based on real world 30 gal metal barrel
#. ~ Description of "fire barrel (100L)"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A large metal barrel used to contain a fire.  It has multiple holes punched "
"in its walls for air supply.  Fires set in a fire barrel will not spread to "
"surrounding flammable objects."
msgstr ""
"Un gran barril de metal usado para contener el fuego. Tiene múltiples "
"agujeros perforados en sus muros para el suministro de aire. Los incendios "
"que se producen en un barril de fuego no se propagan a los objetos "
"inflamables circundantes."

#. ~ values based on basic real world folding camp chair
#. ~ Description of "camp chair"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "Folded camp chair, deploy to sit down."
msgstr "Silla de campamento plegada, desplegada para sentarse."

#. ~ Description of "deck chair"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "Folded deck chair, deploy to sit down."
msgstr "Silla de campamento plegada, desplegar para sentarte."

#. ~ Description of "folding chair"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "Folded plastic chair on a metal frame, deploy to sit down."
msgstr ""
"Silla de plástico plegada en un marco metálico, despliega para sentarte."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "deployable antenna"
msgid_plural "deployable antennas"
msgstr[0] "antena desplegable"
msgstr[1] "antenas desplegables"
msgstr[2] "antenas desplegables"

#. ~ Description of "deployable antenna"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A directional antenna and accompanying tripod, folded into a shape vaguely "
"resembling an umbrella."
msgstr ""
"Una antena direccional y el trípode que la acompaña, plegados en una forma "
"que se asemeja vagamente a un paraguas."

#. ~ Description of "cot"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"This is a military style fold up cot.  While it may not be quite as "
"comfortable as a bed, it's better than slumming it on the ground."
msgstr ""
"Es un catre plegable de estilo militar. Aunque no es tan cómodo como una "
"cama, es mejor que estar tirado en el suelo."

#. ~ "done_message" action message of item "cot"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "You unfold the cot and place it on the ground."
msgstr "Despliegas la cama plegable y la colocas en el suelo."

#. ~ Description of "metal butchering rack"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"Metal butchering rack designed to hang a carcass in the air.  It is folded "
"for easy transportation."
msgstr ""
"Una estantería de descuartizado de metal diseñada para colgar un cadáver en "
"el aire. Está plegada para facilitar el transporte."

#. ~ Description of "metal smoking rack"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A metal rack designed to smoke food for better preservation and taste.  It "
"is folded for easy transportation."
msgstr ""
"Un estante de metal diseñado para ahumar la comida para una mejor "
"conservación y sabor. Está plegada para facilitar el transporte."

#. ~ values based on real world collapsible camping table
#. ~ Description of "folding table"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"Metal folding table for off-road trips.  It is currently folded for easy "
"transportation."
msgstr ""
"Mesa metálica plegable para viajes por el campo. Actualmente está plegada "
"para facilitar su transporte."

#. ~ Description of "leather tarp"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A large sheet of sewn leather that can be deployed instead of a picnic "
"blanket, but it's more valuable as a butchery appliance as it does not soak "
"in blood.  It's rolled and ready for carrying."
msgstr ""
"Una gran hoja de cuero cosido que puede desplegarse en lugar de una manta de"
" picnic, pero es más valiosa como aparato de carnicería ya que no se empapa "
"de sangre. Está enrollada y lista para ser transportada."

#. ~ Description of "fiber mat"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A large mat woven from fibrous material that can be used instead of a picnic"
" blanket, but it's more valuable as a butchery appliance.  Too thin to be "
"used as a comfortable sleeping place.  It's rolled and ready for carrying."
msgstr ""
"Una gran alfombra tejida de material fibroso que puede ser utilizada en "
"lugar de una manta de picnic, pero es más valiosa como un aparato de "
"carnicería. Demasiado delgada para ser usada como un lugar cómodo para "
"dormir. Está enrollada y lista para ser transportada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid "folded butter churn"
msgid_plural "folded butter churns"
msgstr[0] "mantequera plegable"
msgstr[1] "mantequeras plegables"
msgstr[2] "mantequeras plegables"

#. ~ Description of "folded butter churn"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A large wooden container used to turn raw milk into butter and buttermilk.  "
"This model uses a foot crank and holds three gallons of raw milk."
msgstr ""
"Un gran recipiente de madera utilizado para convertir la leche cruda en "
"mantequilla y suero de leche. Este modelo utiliza una manivela de pie y "
"tiene capacidad para 11 litros de leche cruda."

#. ~ Description of "water mill"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A small water-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  "
"Can be placed via the construction menu."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño molino de agua que puede convertir productos con almidón en "
"harina. Puede ser colocado a través del menú de construcción."

#. ~ Description of "wind mill"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A small wind-powered mill that can convert starchy products into flour.  Can"
" be placed via the construction menu."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño molino de viento que puede convertir productos con almidón en "
"harina. Puede ser colocado a través del menú de construcción."

#. ~ Description of "screw press"
#: data/json/items/tool/deployable.json
msgid ""
"A large screw press for the purpose of manually pressing oil out of fruit or"
" seed paste.  Needs to be placed via the construction menu."
msgstr ""
"Una gran prensa con el propósito de extraer aceite manualmente de pasta de "
"fruta o semillas. Usa el menú de construcción para colocarla en su sitio."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Spell name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/monspell.json
msgid "camera"
msgid_plural "cameras"
msgstr[0] "cámara"
msgstr[1] "cámaras"
msgstr[2] "cámaras"

#. ~ Description of "camera"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A point-and-shoot digital camera, with digital viewfinder, a backup 'iron-"
"sight', and flash.  You can look at your photos on the digital screen, or "
"transfer them with a memory card.  Takes conventional batteries."
msgstr ""
"Es una cámara digital compacta, con visor digital, una mirilla secundaria de"
" acero, y flash. Puedes mirar las fotos en la pantalla digital, o "
"transferirlas a una tarjeta de memoria. Usa baterías normales."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "professional camera"
msgid_plural "professional cameras"
msgstr[0] "cámara profesional"
msgstr[1] "cámaras profesionales"
msgstr[2] "cámaras profesionales"

#. ~ Description of "professional camera"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A 35mm digital SLR (single-lens reflex) camera, with optical and digital "
"viewfinders, zoom lens with auto-focus and stabilizer, and flash.  You can "
"view your photos on it or transfer them with a memory card; it runs on "
"conventional batteries.  Before the Cataclysm, you could have taken "
"professional-grade photos using this."
msgstr ""
"Una cámara digital SLR (réflex de un solo objetivo) de 35 mm, con visores "
"ópticos y digitales, un objetivo de ampliación con auto enfoque, "
"estabilizador y un flash. Puedes ver tus fotos en ella o transferirlas a una"
" tarjeta de memoria; funciona con pilas convencionales. Antes del "
"Cataclismo, podrías haber tomado fotos de calidad profesional con esta "
"cámara."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "cellphone"
msgid_plural "cellphones"
msgstr[0] "teléfono móvil"
msgstr[1] "teléfonos moviles"
msgstr[2] "teléfonos moviles"

#. ~ Description of "cellphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a cellphone, an older cousin of a smartphone but still popular in "
"certain circles due to its reliability, sturdiness and the ability to run on"
" common batteries.  Using this cellphone will turn it on and provide light, "
"assuming it is sufficiently charged.  It also has a clock app that includes "
"an alarm."
msgstr ""
"Este es un teléfono móvil, un primo antiguo de un smartphone pero todavía "
"popular en ciertos círculos debido a su fiabilidad, robustez y la capacidad "
"de funcionar con baterías comunes. Usar este teléfono móvil lo encenderá y "
"proporcionará luz, suponiendo que esté suficientemente cargado. También "
"tiene una aplicación de reloj que incluye una alarma."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "cellphone"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "laptop computer"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "control laptop"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "You light up the screen."
msgstr "Enciendes la luz de la pantalla."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "cellphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The cellphone's batteries need more charge."
msgstr "Las baterías del móvil necesitan más carga."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "cellphone - Flashlight"
msgid_plural "cellphones - Flashlight"
msgstr[0] "teléfono móvil - Linterna"
msgstr[1] "teléfonos moviles - Linterna"
msgstr[2] "teléfonos moviles - Linterna"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "cellphone - Flashlight"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "laptop computer - lit screen"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "control laptop - lit screen"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "You stop lighting up the screen."
msgstr "Deja de iluminar la pantalla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "directional antenna"
msgid_plural "directional antennas"
msgstr[0] "antena direccional"
msgstr[1] "antenas direccionales"
msgstr[2] "antenas direccionales"

#. ~ Description of "directional antenna"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is an antenna designed to pick up signals better when pointed at the "
"source.  You could use this with a radio to receive faint signals."
msgstr ""
"Es una antena diseñada para captar mejor señales cuando se apunta a la "
"fuente. Puedes usarla en una radio para recibir señales débiles."

#. ~ Don't add ELECTRONIC flag here, since these handcuffs have their own
#. behavior when affected by EMP blast
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/tools.json
msgid "electronic handcuffs"
msgid_plural "electronic handcuffs"
msgstr[0] "par de esposas electrónicas"
msgstr[1] "pares de esposas electrónicas"
msgstr[2] "pares de esposas electrónicas"

#. ~ Don't add ELECTRONIC flag here, since these handcuffs have their own
#. behavior when affected by EMP blast
#. ~ Description of "electronic handcuffs"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A pair of electronic handcuffs, used by police and riot bots to detain captives.  Their continuous siren clearly identifies the wearer as an arrested criminal and alerts human police.  Wait for their arrival, don't try to escape or to remove the cuffs - they will administer an electric shock.\n"
"However, since the only police likely to respond are undead, you may have a long wait ahead, unless you get creative…"
msgstr ""
"Un par de esposas electrónicas, usadas por la policía y los antidisturbios para detener a los cautivos. Su sirena continua identifica claramente al portador como un criminal arrestado y alerta a la policía humana. Espere su llegada, no intente escapar o quitar las esposas - le administrarán una descarga eléctrica.\n"
"Sin embargo, como los únicos policías que pueden responder son los no-muertos..."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "e-ink tablet PC"
msgid_plural "e-ink tablet PCs"
msgstr[0] "tableta de tinta electrónica PC"
msgstr[1] "tabletas de tinta electrónica PCs"
msgstr[2] "tabletas de tinta electrónica PCs"

#. ~ Description of "e-ink tablet PC"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A tablet PC using an efficient color e-ink display.  Before the Cataclysm, "
"these were nifty gadgets; now, it's an almost priceless resource.  Runs on "
"conventional batteries."
msgstr ""
"Una tableta PC que usa una eficiente pantalla de tinta electrónica a color. "
"Antes del Cataclismo, estos eran ingeniosos aparatos; ahora, es un recurso "
"casi invaluable. Funciona con baterías convencionales."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Turn on the screen"
msgstr "Encender pantalla"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "You power up the screen."
msgstr "Enciendes la pantalla."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The tablet batteries are dead."
msgstr "Las baterías de la tableta están agotadas."

#. ~ LIGHT_10 is the bare minimum for reading without penalties
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "e-ink tablet PC (on)"
msgid_plural "e-ink tablet PCs (on)"
msgstr[0] "tableta de tinta electrónica (on)"
msgstr[1] "tabletas de tinta electrónica (on)"
msgstr[2] "tabletas de tinta electrónica (on)"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Turn off the screen"
msgstr "Apagar pantalla"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "e-ink tablet PC (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "You power down the screen."
msgstr "Apagas la pantalla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "electrohack"
msgid_plural "electrohacks"
msgstr[0] "electrohackeador"
msgstr[1] "electrohackeadores"
msgstr[2] "electrohackeadores"

#. ~ Description of "electrohack"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This device has many ports attached, allowing it to connect to almost any "
"control panel or other electronic machine (but not computers).  With a "
"little skill, it can be used to crack passwords and more.  It requires 25 "
"charges of battery power per use."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo tiene muchos puertos, lo que permite conectarlo a casi "
"cualquier panel de control y otras máquinas electrónicas (excepto "
"ordenadores). Con un poco de habilidad, puede usarse para crackear claves de"
" seguridad y otras cosas. Utiliza 25 cargas de batería por uso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "geiger counter (off)"
msgid_plural "geiger counters (off)"
msgstr[0] "contador geiger (off)"
msgstr[1] "contadores geiger (off)"
msgstr[2] "contadores geiger (off)"

#. ~ Description of "geiger counter (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a tool for measuring radiation.  Using it will prompt you to choose "
"whether to scan yourself or the terrain, or to turn it on, which will "
"provide continuous feedback on ambient radiation.  It is currently off."
msgstr ""
"Es una herramienta para medir la radiación. Al usarlo te dará las opciones "
"de elegir si te quieres escanear a ti o al terreno, o encenderlo, lo que te "
"brinda continuamente las mediciones de la radiación del ambiente. Ahora está"
" apagado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "geiger counter (on)"
msgid_plural "geiger counters (on)"
msgstr[0] "contador geiger (on)"
msgstr[1] "contadores geiger (on)"
msgstr[2] "contadores geiger (on)"

#. ~ Description of "geiger counter (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a tool for measuring radiation.  It is in continuous scan mode, and "
"will produce quiet clicking sounds in the presence of ambient radiation.  "
"Using it allows you to turn it off, or scan yourself or the ground.  It is "
"currently on."
msgstr ""
"Es una herramienta para medir la radiación. Está en escaneo continuo, y "
"produce pequeños sonidos en presencia de radiación en el ambiente. Al usarlo"
" te dará las opciones de elegir apagarlo, o escanearte a ti mismo o el "
"terreno. Ahora está encendido."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "NRE recorder"
msgid_plural "NRE recorders"
msgstr[0] "grabadora NRE"
msgstr[1] "grabadoras NRE"
msgstr[2] "grabadoras NRE"

#. ~ Description of "NRE recorder"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A strange apparatus, seemingly consisting of a glass encased microphone "
"linked to a small thermal printer and digital screen.  The screen remains "
"perpetually blank, save for a battery indicator on its upper right, and on "
"its left side lies a single red button: \"PRINT DATA\"."
msgstr ""
"Un aparato raro, que parece consistir en un micrófono cubierto de vidrio "
"conectado a una pequeña impresora térmica y una pantalla digital. La "
"pantalla está en blanco excepto por el indicador de batería en la esquina "
"derecha superior, y en la parte izquierda tiene un solo botón rojo: "
"\"IMPRIMIR INFORMACIÓN\"."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "hand-crank charger"
msgid_plural "hand-crank chargers"
msgstr[0] "cargador de manivela"
msgstr[1] "cargadores de manivela"
msgstr[2] "cargadores de manivela"

#. ~ Description of "hand-crank charger"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a hand-powered battery charger.  It has an adjustable receptacle "
"designed to accept a wide variety of rechargeable battery cells."
msgstr ""
"Este es un cargador de baterías de mano. Tiene un receptáculo ajustable "
"diseñado para aceptar una amplia variedad de celdas de baterías recargables."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "laptop computer"
msgid_plural "laptop computers"
msgstr[0] "ordenador portátil"
msgstr[1] "ordenadores portátiles"
msgstr[2] "ordenadores portátiles"

#. ~ Description of "laptop computer"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "A laptop computer with replaceable batteries."
msgstr "Un ordenador portátil con baterias reemplazables."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "laptop computer"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "control laptop"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "Light up the screen"
msgstr "Encender la pantalla."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "laptop computer"
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "control laptop"
#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "portable virtual reality rig"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "The laptop's batteries need more charge."
msgstr "Las baterías del portátil necesitan más carga."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "laptop computer - lit screen"
msgid_plural "laptop computers - lit screen"
msgstr[0] "ordenador portátil - pantalla encendida"
msgstr[1] "ordenadores portátiles - pantalla encendida"
msgstr[2] "ordenadores portátiles - pantalla encendida"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "mp3 player (off)"
msgid_plural "mp3 players (off)"
msgstr[0] "reproductor de mp3 (off)"
msgstr[1] "reproductores de mp3 (off)"
msgstr[2] "reproductores de mp3 (off)"

#. ~ Description of "mp3 player (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This battery-powered device is loaded up with someone's music collection.  "
"Fortunately, there's lots of songs you like, and listening to it will raise "
"your morale slightly.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo a pilas está cargado con la colección de música de alguien."
" Afortunadamente, hay muchas canciones que te gustan, y escucharlas te "
"levantará un poco la moral. Usar para encender."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "mp3 player (on)"
msgid_plural "mp3 players (on)"
msgstr[0] "reproductor de mp3 (on)"
msgstr[1] "reproductores de mp3 (on)"
msgstr[2] "reproductores de mp3 (on)"

#. ~ Description of "mp3 player (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This mp3 player is turned on and playing some great tunes, raising your "
"morale steadily while on your person.  It runs through batteries quickly; "
"you can turn it off by using it.  It also obscures your hearing."
msgstr ""
"Este reproductor de mp3 está encendido y reproduciendo unas canciones muy "
"buenas, lo que levanta tu moral constantemente. Consume las baterías "
"rápidamente. Usalo para apagarlo. También obstruye tu audición."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/tools.json
msgid "noise emitter (off)"
msgid_plural "noise emitters (off)"
msgstr[0] "emisor de ruido (off)"
msgstr[1] "emisores de ruido (off)"
msgstr[2] "emisores de ruido (off)"

#. ~ Description of "noise emitter (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This device was constructed by 'enhancing' a speaker ripped off from some "
"electronic device with some amplifier circuits.  It has now no other use "
"beside emitting loud crackling static noise, that could distract zombies."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo se construyó \"realzando\" un altavoz arrancado de algún "
"aparato electrónico con algunos circuitos de amplificación. Ahora no tiene "
"otro uso que emitir un fuerte ruido estático y crepitante, que podría "
"distraer a los zombis."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/tools.json
msgid "noise emitter (on)"
msgid_plural "noise emitters (on)"
msgstr[0] "emisor de ruido (on)"
msgstr[1] "emisores de ruido (on)"
msgstr[2] "emisores de ruido (on)"

#. ~ Description of "noise emitter (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This device has been turned on and is emitting horrible crackles, pops and "
"other static sounds.  Quick, get away from it before it draws zombies to "
"you!"
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo ha sido encendido y está emitiendo horribles crujidos, "
"chasquidos y otros sonidos estáticos. ¡Rápido, aléjate de él antes de que "
"atraiga a los zombis hacia ti!"

#. ~ Based off the TRIFIELD EMF Meter Model TF2
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "EMF detector (off)"
msgid_plural "EMF detectors (off)"
msgstr[0] "detector CEM (off)"
msgstr[1] "detectores CEM (off)"
msgstr[2] "detectores CEM (off)"

#. ~ Based off the TRIFIELD EMF Meter Model TF2
#. ~ Description of "EMF detector (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This device detects and reads out different electromagnetic wave lengths.  "
"It beeps with proximity and is sensitive enough you could use it to get a "
"sense of direction."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo detecta y lee diferentes longitudes de onda "
"electromagnética. Emite un pitido de proximidad y es lo suficientemente "
"sensible como para que puedas utilizarlo para orientarte."

#. ~ lasts 12 hours with backlight off
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "EMF detector (on)"
msgid_plural "EMF detectors (on)"
msgstr[0] "detector CEM (on)"
msgstr[1] "detectores CEM (on)"
msgstr[2] "detectores CEM (on)"

#. ~ lasts 12 hours with backlight off
#. ~ Description of "EMF detector (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This device detects and reads out different wave lengths.  It currently is "
"humming and beeps with proximity.  It is sensitive enough you could use it "
"to get a sense of direction."
msgstr ""
"Este dispositivo detecta y lee diferentes longitudes de onda. Actualmente "
"zumba y emite un pitido con la proximidad. Es lo suficientemente sensible "
"como para que puedas usarlo para obtener un sentido de la dirección."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "handheld game system"
msgid_plural "handheld game systems"
msgstr[0] "consola portátil de videojuegos"
msgstr[1] "consolas portátiles de videojuegos"
msgstr[2] "consolas portátiles de videojuegos"

#. ~ Description of "handheld game system"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a portable games console in working condition, with a backlit screen"
" allowing you to play in the dark.  You can use it to play it for a little "
"while, but this requires batteries.  Multiple game systems can be linked "
"together for multiplayer games."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una consola de juegos portátil en condiciones de funcionamiento, con"
" una pantalla retroiluminada que permite jugar en la oscuridad. Se puede "
"utilizar para jugar un rato, pero esto requiere pilas. Se pueden enlazar "
"varios sistemas de juego para realizar partidas multijugador."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/electronic.json
msgid "smartphone"
msgid_plural "smartphones"
msgstr[0] "smartphone"
msgstr[1] "smartphones"
msgstr[2] "smartphones"

#. ~ Description of "smartphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"A popular, fancy smartphone.  Capable of taking photos with its integrated "
"camera and illuminating an area with its flashlight app, assuming it has "
"enough charge.  The smartphone also has a clock app that includes an alarm "
"and an app for tracking consumed calories.  Runs on a small, rechargeable "
"power cell compatible with a Unified Power Supply."
msgstr ""
"Un popular y elegante smartphone. Capaz de hacer fotos gracias a la cámara "
"integrada e iluminar un área según la aplicación de la linterna, suponiendo "
"que tenga suficiente carga. El smartphone también tiene una aplicación de "
"reloj que incluye una alarma y una app para seguir las calorias consumidas. "
"Funciona con una pequeña célula de energía recargable compatible con el "
"Sistema de Energía Unificado."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "smartphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "Turn on flashlight"
msgstr "Encender linterna"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "smartphone"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic smartphone"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "Wraitheon executive's smartphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "You activate the flashlight app."
msgstr "Activas la aplicación de linterna."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "smartphone"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The smartphone's charge is too low."
msgstr "La batería del smartphone tiene muy poca carga."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/electronic.json
msgid "smartphone - music"
msgid_plural "smartphones - music"
msgstr[0] "smartphone - música"
msgstr[1] "smartphones - música"
msgstr[2] "smartphones - música"

#. ~ Description of "smartphone - music"
#. ~ Description of "atomic smartphone - music"
#. ~ Description of "Wraitheon executive's smartphone - music"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid ""
"This phone is playing music, steadily raising your morale.  You can't hear "
"anything else while you're listening."
msgstr ""
"Este teléfono está tocando música, elevando constantemente tu moral. No "
"puedes oír nada más mientras estás escuchando."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/electronic.json
msgid "smartphone - Flashlight"
msgid_plural "smartphones - Flashlight"
msgstr[0] "smartphone - Linterna"
msgstr[1] "smartphones - Linterna"
msgstr[2] "smartphones - Linterna"

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "smartphone - Flashlight"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "atomic smartphone - Flashlight"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "Executive's smartphone - Flashlight"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "Turn off flashlight"
msgstr "Apagar linterna"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "smartphone - Flashlight"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic smartphone - Flashlight"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "Executive's smartphone - Flashlight"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "You deactivate the flashlight app."
msgstr "Desactivaste la aplicación Linterna."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/tools.json
msgid "UPS"
msgid_plural "UPSes"
msgstr[0] "UPS"
msgstr[1] "UPS"
msgstr[2] "UPS"

#. ~ Description of "UPS"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a unified power supply, or UPS.  It is a device developed jointly by"
" military and scientific interests for use in combat and the field.  The UPS"
" is designed to power bionics, armor and some guns, but drains batteries "
"quickly."
msgstr ""
"Este es un sistema de energía unificado, o UPS. Es un dispositivo "
"desarrollado conjuntamente por intereses militares y científicos para su uso"
" en combate y en el campo. El UPSestá diseñado para alimentar la biónica, la"
" armadura y algunas armas, pero agota las baterías rápidamente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "methanol fuel cell UPS"
msgid_plural "methanol fuel cell UPSes"
msgstr[0] "celda de combustible de metanol UPS"
msgstr[1] "celdas de combustible de metanol UPS"
msgstr[2] "celdas de combustible de metanol UPS"

#. ~ Description of "methanol fuel cell UPS"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a direct methanol fuel cell which can provide power to UPS-"
"compatible electronic devices by oxidizing methanol supplied from a "
"specialized fuel tank to produce electricity."
msgstr ""
"Una celda combustible de metanol directa que puede brindar energía a "
"dispositivos electrónicos compatibles con UPS, oxidando metanol suministrado"
" por un tanque especializado para producir electricidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "vibrator"
msgid_plural "vibrators"
msgstr[0] "vibrador"
msgstr[1] "vibradores"
msgstr[2] "vibradores"

#. ~ Description of "vibrator"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This battery-devouring device is just the thing to knead the tension out and"
" help you relax.  Use it to take a break and unwind."
msgstr ""
"Es un dispositivo que devora baterías, y es útil para calmar la tensión y "
"ayudarte a relajarte. Úsalo para tomarte un descanso y relajarte."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "gas-powered UPS (off)"
msgid_plural "gas-powered UPSes (off)"
msgstr[0] "UPS alimentado por combustible (apag.)"
msgstr[1] "UPS alimentados por combustible (apag.)"
msgstr[2] "UPS alimentados por combustible (apag.)"

#. ~ Description of "gas-powered UPS (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a compact thermoelectric generator.  Burns gas to charge UPS "
"devices.  Use it to turn it on."
msgstr ""
"Un generador termoeléctrico compacto. Quema gas para cargar dispositivos "
"compatibles con UPS. Usar para encender."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "gas-powered UPS (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "You turn the charger on."
msgstr "Enciendes el cargador."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "gas-powered UPS (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The charger's tank is empty."
msgstr "El depósito del cargador está vacío."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "gas-powered UPS (on)"
msgid_plural "gas-powered UPSes (on)"
msgstr[0] "UPS alimentado por combustible (enc.)"
msgstr[1] "UPS alimentados por combustible (enc.)"
msgstr[2] "UPS alimentados por combustible (enc.)"

#. ~ Description of "gas-powered UPS (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid ""
"This is a compact thermoelectric generator.  When connected to a fuel tank, "
"it will slowly charge UPS-compatible devices."
msgstr ""
"Un generador termoeléctrico compacto. Cuando este conectado a un tanque de "
"combustible, cargará lentamente dispositivos compatibles con UPS."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "gas-powered UPS (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/electronics.json
msgid "The charger is extinguished."
msgstr "El cargador se apaga."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "crowbar"
msgid_plural "crowbars"
msgstr[0] "palanca"
msgstr[1] "palancas"
msgstr[2] "palancas"

#. ~ Description of "crowbar"
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is a hefty prying tool.  Use it to open locked doors without destroying"
" them, or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash some "
"heads in."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una herramienta pesada para hacer palanca. Úsala para abrir puertas "
"cerradas con llave sin destruirlas o para levantar tapas de las "
"alcantarillas. También la puedes empuñar para reventar algunas cabezas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "rudimentary lockpick"
msgid_plural "rudimentary lockpicks"
msgstr[0] "ganzua rudimentaria"
msgstr[1] "ganzuas rudimentarias"
msgstr[2] "ganzuas rudimentarias"

#. ~ Description of "rudimentary lockpick"
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is a pair of thin pieces of metal, one bent in an 'L' shape to push "
"tumblers and the other a stiff object acting as a torsion wrench.  The tools"
" are almost totally inadequate for the job, but when you've got nothing "
"else, it might work."
msgstr ""
"Esto son un par de finas piezas de metal, una doblada en forma de \"L\" para"
" empujar los bombines y la otra un objeto rígido que actúa como llave de "
"torsión. Las herramientas son casi totalmente inadecuadas para el trabajo, "
"pero cuando no tienes nada más, puede funcionar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "improvised lockpick"
msgid_plural "improvised lockpicks"
msgstr[0] "ganzúa improvisada"
msgstr[1] "ganzúas improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "ganzúas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description of "improvised lockpick"
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is an improvised set of picks and torsion wrenches made from scrap "
"metal.  You need MacGyver-like skills to open locks with these as they are "
"brittle, but they lower the chances of alarms being set off."
msgstr ""
"Es un equipo improvisado de ganzúas y llaves de torsión, hechas con "
"chatarra. Necesitas tener habilidades como MacGyver para abrir cerraduras "
"con esto ya que son bastante frágiles, pero usándolas no vas a hacer sonar "
"tantas alarmas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "ice axe"
msgid_plural "ice axes"
msgstr[0] "picahielo"
msgstr[1] "picahielos"
msgstr[2] "picahielos"

#. ~ Description of "ice axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is an ice axe with hammer on its head, a multi-purpose hiking and "
"climbing tool used by mountaineers.  It is sturdy enough to pry open closed "
"doors or lift manhole covers."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de un piolet con un martillo en la cabeza, una herramienta "
"multiusos de senderismo y escalada utilizada por los montañeros. Es lo "
"suficientemente robusto como para abrir puertas cerradas o levantar tapas de"
" alcantarilla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "makeshift crowbar"
msgid_plural "makeshift crowbars"
msgstr[0] "palanca improvisada"
msgstr[1] "palancas improvisadas"
msgstr[2] "palancas improvisadas"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift crowbar"
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is a pipe with ends that have been bent and hammered flat so it "
"resembles a crowbar.  Use it to open locked crates without destroying them, "
"or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to fight with, in a "
"pinch."
msgstr ""
"Esto es una tubería con los extremos doblados y aplanados a martillazos que "
"se asemeja a una palanca. Úsala para abrir cajas cerradas sin destruirlas, o"
" para levantar tapas de alcantarilla. También puedes usarla para luchar, en "
"caso de necesidad."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "locksmith kit"
msgid_plural "locksmith kits"
msgstr[0] "equipo de cerrajero"
msgstr[1] "equipos de cerrajero"
msgstr[2] "equipos de cerrajero"

#. ~ Description of "locksmith kit"
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid ""
"This is a locksmith's set of sturdy steel lock picks and torsion wrenches.  "
"It is essential for silently and quickly opening locks, provided you have "
"some lock picking and mechanical skills."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de un juego de cerraduras de acero resistente y llaves de torsión. "
"Es esencial para abrir cerraduras de forma silenciosa y rápida, siempre que "
"se tengan algunas habilidades de apertura de cerraduras y de mecánica."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "bio lockpick"
msgid_plural "bio lockpicks"
msgstr[0] "bioganzúa"
msgstr[1] "bioganzúas"
msgstr[2] "bioganzúas"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid "heavy crowbar"
msgid_plural "heavy crowbars"
msgstr[0] "palanca pesada"
msgstr[1] "palancas pesadas"
msgstr[2] "palancas pesadas"

#. ~ Description of "heavy crowbar"
#: data/json/items/tool/entry_tools.json
msgid ""
"A 5 foot long construction prybar.  Essentially a long solid steel rod with "
"a hardened chisel tip."
msgstr ""
"Una palanca de construcción de 1,5 metros de largo. Esencialmente una "
"varilla larga de acero sólido con una punta de cincel endurecida."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "acid bomb"
msgid_plural "acid bombs"
msgstr[0] "bomba de ácido"
msgstr[1] "bombas de ácido"
msgstr[2] "bombas de ácido"

#. ~ Description of "acid bomb"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"This is a fragile container filled with acid.  Throw it to spill out a pool "
"of potent acid, it could also be used in a staff sling with a modified "
"cradle."
msgstr ""
"Este es un frágil contenedor lleno de ácido. Lánzalo para derramar un charco"
" de ácido potente, también podría usarse en una eslinga de bastón con un "
"soporte modificado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "C-4 explosive"
msgid_plural "C-4 explosives"
msgstr[0] "explosivo C-4"
msgstr[1] "explosivos C-4"
msgstr[2] "explosivos C-4"

#. ~ Description of "C-4 explosive"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"This is military grade RDX composition explosive.  A label reads: \"Highly "
"explosive, use with extreme caution!\" It comes with a small timer."
msgstr ""
"Es un explosivo compuesto RDX de grado militar. Tiene una etiqueta que dice:"
" \"¡Muy explosivo, usar con precaución extrema!\" Viene con un pequeño "
"temporizador."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "C-4 explosive (armed)"
msgid_plural "C-4 explosives (armed)"
msgstr[0] "explosivo C-4 (activado)"
msgstr[1] "explosivos C-4 (activados)"
msgstr[2] "explosivos C-4 (activados)"

#. ~ Description of "C-4 explosive (armed)"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"This is military grade RDX composition explosive.  A label reads: \"Highly "
"explosive, use with extreme caution!\" It comes with a small timer, which is"
" currently ticking down."
msgstr ""
"Es un explosivo compuesto RDX de grado militar. Tiene una etiqueta que dice:"
" \"¡Muy explosivo, usar con precaución extrema!\" Viene con un pequeño "
"temporizador, que en este momento está contando."

#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "C-4 explosive (armed)"
#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "mininuke"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#, c-format
msgid "You've already set the %s's timer, you might want to get away from it."
msgstr ""
"Ya estableciste el temporizador del %s, tal vez te convenga estar lo más "
"lejos posible ahora."

#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "C-4 explosive (armed)"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active EMP bomb"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active flashbang"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active grenade"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active EMP grenade"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "mininuke"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active scrambler grenade"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active tear gas payload"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "armed Kabura-ya antipersonnel device"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active demolition charge"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active cryo grenade"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json data/json/items/tool/misc.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/grenades.json
msgid "Tick."
msgstr "Tick."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "dynamite"
msgid_plural "dynamites"
msgstr[0] "dinamita"
msgstr[1] "dinamitas"
msgstr[2] "dinamitas"

#. ~ Description of "dynamite"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"These are several sticks of explosives with a fuse attached.  Use this item "
"to light the fuse.  You will, of course, need a lighter or matches in your "
"inventory to do this.  Shortly after lighting the fuse, this item will "
"explode, so get away!"
msgstr ""
"Son varios palos de explosivos con una mecha cada uno. Usala para encender "
"la mecha. Vas a necesitar un encendedor o fósforos en tu inventario para "
"usarla. Poco después de encender la mecha, este objeto explotará, ¡así que "
"alejate!"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "dynamite"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "dynamite bomb"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "You light the dynamite."
msgstr "Enciendes la dinamita."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "dynamite (lit)"
msgid_plural "dynamites (lit)"
msgstr[0] "dinamita (encendida)"
msgstr[1] "dinamitas (encendidas)"
msgstr[2] "dinamitas (encendidas)"

#. ~ Description of "dynamite (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"The fuse on this dynamite is lit and hissing.  It'll explode any moment now."
msgstr ""
"La mecha de esta dinamita está encendida y siseando. Va a explotar en "
"cualquier momento."

#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "dynamite (lit)"
#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "dynamite bomb (lit)"
#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "active pipebomb"
#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "homemade demolition charge
#. (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#, c-format
msgid "You've already lit the %s, try throwing it instead."
msgstr "Ya encendiste la %s, ahora intenta tirarla."

#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "dynamite (lit)"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "dynamite bomb (lit)"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "active pipebomb"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "homemade demolition charge (lit)"
#. ~ "sound_msg" action message of item "mana bomb (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
msgid "ssss…"
msgstr "ssss..."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "dynamite bomb"
msgid_plural "dynamite bombs"
msgstr[0] "bombasde dinamita"
msgstr[1] "bombas de dinamita"
msgstr[2] "bombas de dinamita"

#. ~ Description of "dynamite bomb"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"These are several sticks of explosives surrounded by shrapnel stuffed inside"
" a metal container.  The fuse is sticking out through a small hole.  Use "
"this item to light the fuse.  You will, of course, need a lighter or matches"
" in your inventory to do this.  Shortly after lighting the fuse, this item "
"will explode, so get away!"
msgstr ""
"Son varias barras de explosivos rodeadas de metralla dentro de un contenedor"
" de metal. La mecha sobresale a través de un pequeño agujero. Use este "
"artículo para encender la mecha. Por supuesto, necesitarás un encendedor o "
"cerillas en tu inventario para hacerlo. Poco después de encender la mecha, "
"este objeto explotará, ¡así que aléjate!"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "dynamite bomb (lit)"
msgid_plural "dynamite bombs (lit)"
msgstr[0] "bomba de dinamita (encendida)"
msgstr[1] "bombas de dinamita (encendidas)"
msgstr[2] "bombas de dinamita (encendidas)"

#. ~ Description of "dynamite bomb (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"The fuse on this dynamite bomb is lit and hissing.  It'll explode any moment"
" now."
msgstr ""
"La mecha de esta bomba de dinamita está encendida y silbando. Explotará en "
"cualquier momento."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "EMP bomb"
msgid_plural "EMP bombs"
msgstr[0] "bomba EMP"
msgstr[1] "bombas EMP"
msgstr[2] "bombas EMP"

#. ~ Description of "EMP bomb"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"This substantial device is a bomb that generates an electromagnetic pulse.  "
"When activated, the plutonium fuel cell is drained into a flux compression "
"generator, the detonation of which creates a strong magnetic field.  When "
"this magnetic field is fed into the antenna, it creates a strong electro-"
"magnetic pulse."
msgstr ""
"Este sustancial dispositivo es una bomba que genera un pulso "
"electromagnético. Cuando se activa, la pila de combustible de plutonio se "
"drena en un generador de compresión de flujo, cuya detonación crea un fuerte"
" campo magnético. Cuando este campo magnético se introduce en la antena, "
"crea un fuerte pulso electromagnético."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "EMP bomb"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "Activate bomb"
msgstr "Activar bomba"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "EMP bomb"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "You activate the EMP bomb."
msgstr "Tu activas la bomba EMP"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "active EMP bomb"
msgid_plural "active EMP bombs"
msgstr[0] "bomba EMP activa"
msgstr[1] "bombas EMP activas"
msgstr[2] "bombas EMP activas"

#. ~ Description of "active EMP bomb"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"This EMP bomb is active, and will shortly detonate, creating a large EMP "
"field that damages robots and drains bionic energy, as well as a sizeable "
"explosion.  You may not want to be holding it much longer."
msgstr ""
"Esta bomba EMP está activa, y pronto detonará, creando un gran campo EMP que"
" daña a los robots y drena la energía biónica, así como una considerable "
"explosión. Es posible que no quieras aguantar mucho más tiempo."

#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "active EMP bomb"
#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "armed Kabura-ya antipersonnel
#. device"
#. ~ "no_deactivate_msg" action message of item "active demolition charge"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/grenades.json
#, c-format
msgid "You've already activated the %s, try throwing it instead."
msgstr "Ya has activado el %s, intenta lanzarlo en su lugar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "firecracker"
msgid_plural "firecrackers"
msgstr[0] "petardo"
msgstr[1] "petardos"
msgstr[2] "petardos"

#. ~ Description of "firecracker"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"A solitary firecracker with a short fuse.  Use this item to light the fuse."
"  Of course, you will need a lighter or some matches to do so.  Shortly "
"after you light the fuse it will explode, so throw it quickly!"
msgstr ""
"Un petardo solo con una mecha corta. Usalo para encender la mecha. Claro, "
"vas a necesitar un encendedor o algunos fósforos para usarlo. Poco después "
"de que enciendas la mecha va a explotar, ¡así que tiralo rápido!"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "firecracker (lit)"
msgid_plural "firecrackers (lit)"
msgstr[0] "petardo (encendido)"
msgstr[1] "petardos (encendidos)"
msgstr[2] "petardos (encendidos)"

#. ~ Description of "firecracker (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"A firecracker that has been lit; the fuse is hissing.  Throw it quickly "
"before it explodes."
msgstr ""
"Un petardo que ha sido encendido, la mecha está siseando. Tiralo rápido "
"antes de que explote."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "pack of firecrackers"
msgid_plural "packs of firecrackers"
msgstr[0] "paquete de petardos"
msgstr[1] "paquetes de petardos"
msgstr[2] "paquetes de petardos"

#. ~ Description of "pack of firecrackers"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"This is a pack of 25 firecrackers with a starter fuse.  Use this item to "
"light the fuse.  Of course, you will need a lighter or some matches to do "
"so.  Shortly after you light the fuse they will begin to explode, so throw "
"them quickly!"
msgstr ""
"Es un paquete con 25 petardos con una mecha cada uno. Usalos para encender "
"la mecha. Claro, vas a necesitar un encendedor o algunos fósforos para "
"usarlos. Poco después de que enciendas la mecha van a empezar a explotar, "
"¡así que tiralos rápido!"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "pack of firecrackers (lit)"
msgid_plural "packs of firecrackers (lit)"
msgstr[0] "paquete de petardos (encendido)"
msgstr[1] "paquetes de petardos (encendidos)"
msgstr[2] "paquetes de petardos (encendidos)"

#. ~ Description of "pack of firecrackers (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"A pack of 25 firecrackers that has been lit; the fuse is hissing.  Throw "
"them quickly before the start to explode."
msgstr ""
"Un paquete de 25 petardos que ha sido encendido, la mecha está siseando. "
"Tiralos rápido antes de que empiecen a explotar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid "flashbang"
msgid_plural "flashbangs"
msgstr[0] "granada de destello"
msgstr[1] "granadas de destello"
msgstr[2] "granadas de destello"

#. ~ Description of "flashbang"
#: data/json/items/tool/explosives.json
msgid ""
"This is a military police style flashbang.  Use this item to pull the pin "
"and light the fuse.  You will then have five seconds before it detonates "
"with intense light and sound, blinding, deafening and disorienting anyone "
"nearby."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de un granada cegadora de estilo policial militar. Utiliza este "
"objeto para tirar del pasador y encender la mecha. Tendrás cinco segundos "
"antes de que detone con una luz y un sonido intensos, cegando, ensordeciendo"
" y desorientando a cualquiera que esté cerca."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "flashbang"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "fungicidal gas grenade"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "makeshift fungicidal gas grenade"
#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "grenade"
