msgstr[2] "magiclicks"

#. ~ Description of "electric firestarter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a crudely made electric firestarter, which can function as an "
"inefficient lighter."
msgstr ""
"Es un simple encendedor eléctrico, que puede funcionar ineficazmente como un"
" encendedor normal."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "bow fire drill"
msgid_plural "bow fire drills"
msgstr[0] "arco de rodamiento"
msgstr[1] "arcos de rodamiento"
msgstr[2] "arcos de rodamiento"

#. ~ Description of "bow fire drill"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This fire drill is a simple item for starting fires by friction between a "
"notched plank and wooden shaft.  The shaft is spun rapidly with a sawing "
"motion by a bowstring wrapped around it.  Very slow to acquire a usable "
"ember."
msgstr ""
"El arco de rodamiento es un objeto rudimentario para encender fuego por la "
"fricción entre un tablón agujereado y un palo de madera.  El palo se hace "
"girar rápidamente con una cuerda alrededor y un movimiento de serruchado.  "
"Se tarda mucho en conseguir una brasa útil."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "pump fire drill"
msgid_plural "pump fire drills"
msgstr[0] "taladro de bombeo"
msgstr[1] "taladros de bombeo"
msgstr[2] "taladros de bombeo"

#. ~ Description of "pump fire drill"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This fire drill is a simple item for starting fires by friction between a "
"notched plank and wooden shaft with a flywheel attached.  The shaft is spun "
"rapidly with a pumping motion by a cord wrapped around it.  Slow to acquire "
"a usable ember."
msgstr ""
"Este arco de rodamiento es un objeto rudimentario para encender fuego con la"
" fricción entre una tablón agujereado y una palo de madera con un volante de"
" inercia. El palo se hace girar rápidamente con una cuerda alrededor y un "
"movimiento de bombeo. Se tarda bastante en conseguir una brasa útil."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "flint and steel"
msgid_plural "sets of flint and steel"
msgstr[0] "yesquero"
msgstr[1] "yesqueros"
msgstr[2] "yesqueros"

#. ~ Description of "flint and steel"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a flint and a hardened high carbon steel striker.  Use it to spark a"
" flame."
msgstr ""
"Un pedernal y un golpeador duro de acero alto en carbono. Se utiliza para "
"hacer chispas e iniciar una llama."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "lighter"
msgid_plural "lighters"
msgstr[0] "encendedor"
msgstr[1] "encendedores"
msgstr[2] "encendedores"

#. ~ Description of "lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a disposable plastic lighter.  A lighter may be carried to use "
"various drugs, like cigarettes, light explosives like Molotov cocktails, or "
"light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Es un encendedor desechable de plástico. Puede ser necesario para usar "
"varias drogas, como cigarrillos, para encender explosivos como los cócteles "
"molotov y también para prender fuego a objetos cercanos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "magnifying glass"
msgid_plural "magnifying glasses"
msgstr[0] "lupa"
msgstr[1] "lupas"
msgstr[2] "lupas"

#. ~ Description of "magnifying glass"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a magnifying glass.  May be useful for starting fires during sunny "
"skies."
msgstr ""
"Es una lupa. Puede ser útil para encender fuegos si el día está soleado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "crude glass lens"
msgid_plural "crude glass lenses"
msgstr[0] "lente de vidrio rústico"
msgstr[1] "lentes de vidrio rústico"
msgstr[2] "lentes de vidrio rústico"

#. ~ Description of "crude glass lens"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"A very low-quality focusing lens, made from non-optical-grade glass.  "
"Useless for building most optical devices, but you can start a fire with it "
"if sunlight is available."
msgstr ""
"Una lente de muy baja calidad fabricada con vidrio no óptico. No sirve para "
"construir dispositivos ópticos pero se puede usar para encender un fuego si "
"hay luz del sol disponible."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "fire piston"
msgid_plural "fire pistons"
msgstr[0] "pistón incendiario"
msgstr[1] "pistones incendiarios"
msgstr[2] "pistones incendiarios"

#. ~ Description of "fire piston"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a firestarting tool of Southeast Asian origin consisting of a thin "
"hollow wooden cylinder sealed at one end and open at the other, and a wooden"
" piston forming an airtight circular seal with it, making use of rapid and "
"adiabatic air compression to ignite a piece of tinder.  It also comes with a"
" tinder container to keep tinder dry.  Use it to start a fire."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta para encender fuego con origen en el sureste de Asia, que "
"consiste en un cilindro hueco de madera fina sellado en una punta, abierto "
"en la otra y un pistón de madera formando un sello circular hermético, "
"usando compresión de aire rápida y adiabática para encender un poco de "
"yesca.  También tiene un recipiente para mantener seca la yesca.  Úsalo para"
" prender un fuego."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "matchbook"
msgid_plural "matchbooks"
msgstr[0] "cajita de cerillas"
msgstr[1] "cajitas de cerillas"
msgstr[2] "cajitas de cerillas"

#. ~ Description of "matchbook"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a small book of matches with a coarse strike surface on the outside "
"flap.  Matches may be carried to use various drugs like cigarettes, light "
"explosives like Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire.  Due to "
"the matches being lightly glued on the matchbook, they can be removed, but "
"not replaced on the book."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño librito de cerillas con una zona áspera de raspado en un costado."
"  Los fósforos pueden usarse para consumir diversas drogas como los "
"cigarrillos, encender explosivos ligeros como los cócteles molotov, o "
"prender fuego a otras cosas cercanas. Debido a que las cerillas están "
"pegadas al librito, se pueden quitar pero no reemplazar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "survival match"
msgid_plural "survival matches"
msgstr[0] "cerilla de supervivencia"
msgstr[1] "cerillas de supervivencia"
msgstr[2] "cerillas de supervivencia"

#. ~ Description of "survival match"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "A solid strike anywhere match.  One and done."
msgstr ""
"Una cerilla que se enciende al rozar cualquier superficie. Una y listo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "matchbox"
msgid_plural "matchboxes"
msgstr[0] "caja de fósforos"
msgstr[1] "cajas de fósforos"
msgstr[2] "cajas de fósforos"

#. ~ Description of "matchbox"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a small box of matches with a coarse strike surface on the side.  "
"Matches may be carried to use various drugs like cigarettes, light "
"explosives like Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Una caja de fósforos con una zona áspera de raspado en un costado.  Los "
"fósforos pueden usarse para consumir diversas drogas como los cigarrillos, "
"encender explosivos ligeros como los cócteles molotov, o prender fuego a "
"otras cosas cercanas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "refillable lighter"
msgid_plural "refillable lighters"
msgstr[0] "encendedor recargable"
msgstr[1] "encendedores recargables"
msgstr[2] "encendedores recargables"

#. ~ Description of "refillable lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a lighter featuring a flip top cover and refuelable tank.  A lighter"
" may be carried to use various drugs, like cigarettes, light explosives like"
" Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Un encendedor con la tapa abatible y el tanque recargable.  Puede usarse "
"para consumir diversas drogas como los cigarrillos, encender explosivos "
"ligeros como los cócteles molotov, o para prender fuego a otras cosas "
"cercanas."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "refillable lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "You flick the lighter."
msgstr "Enciendes el encendedor de un golpe."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "refillable lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "Nothing happens."
msgstr "No pasa nada."

#. ~ Description of "refillable lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a lighter featuring a flip top cover and refuelable tank.  It is "
"lit."
msgstr ""
"Es un encendedor con la tapa abatible y el tanque recargable. Está "
"encendido."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "refillable lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "You extinguish the lighter."
msgstr "Apagas el encendedor."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "refillable butane lighter"
msgid_plural "refillable butane lighters"
msgstr[0] "encendedor de butano recargable"
msgstr[1] "encendedores de butano recargables"
msgstr[2] "encendedores de butano recargables"

#. ~ Description of "refillable butane lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a large lighter with a trigger and a safety, reloaded by fitting a "
"can of butane inside the base.  A lighter may be carried to use various "
"drugs, like cigarettes, light explosives like Molotov cocktails, or light "
"nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Un encendedor grande con gatillo y seguro, que se recarga insertando una "
"lata de butano dentro de la base. Puede usarse para consumir diversas drogas"
" como cigarrillos, para encender explosivos como cócteles molotov, o también"
" lo puedes usar para prender fuego a objetos cercanos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "ember carrier"
msgid_plural "ember carriers"
msgstr[0] "braserito"
msgstr[1] "braseritos"
msgstr[2] "braseritos"

#. ~ Description of "ember carrier"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to "
"provide a controlled airflow.  It can nurture a smoldering ember for a long "
"time, to start fires without modern tools."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño recipiente para poner yesca, con agujeros que permiten "
"controlar la entrada de aire. Puede alimentar brasas encendidas por un rato "
"largo, para encender fuegos sin herramientas más modernas."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "ember carrier"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "You light the tinder."
msgstr "Enciendes la yesca."

#. ~ "need_charges_msg" action message of item "ember carrier"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "The ember carrier is out of tinder."
msgstr "El portador de la brasa se ha quedado sin yesca."

#. ~ "need_fire_msg" action message of item "ember carrier"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "You need a lighter or fire to light this."
msgstr "Necesitas un encendedor o fuego para encenderla."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "ember carrier (lit)"
msgid_plural "ember carriers (lit)"
msgstr[0] "braserito (encendido)"
msgstr[1] "braseritos (encendidos)"
msgstr[2] "braseritos (encendidos)"

#. ~ Description of "ember carrier (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is a small container for holding tinder, with holes punched in it to "
"provide a controlled airflow.  An ember is smoldering inside it, and can be "
"used to start a campfire."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño recipiente para poner yesca, con agujeros que permiten "
"controlar la entrada de aire. Adentro tiene una brasa encendida, y puede "
"usarse para encender una fogata."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "ember carrier (lit)"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "The ember is extinguished."
msgstr "Las brasas se extinguieron."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid "mini lighter"
msgid_plural "mini lighters"
msgstr[0] "mini encendedor"
msgstr[1] "mini encendedores"
msgstr[2] "mini encendedores"

#. ~ Description of "mini lighter"
#: data/json/items/tool/fire.json
msgid ""
"This is miniature version of a disposable plastic lighter.  A lighter may be"
" carried to use various drugs, like cigarettes, light explosives like "
"Molotov cocktails, or light nearby items on fire."
msgstr ""
"Es una versión en miniatura del encendedor desechable de plástico.  Puedes "
"llevarlo para usar varias drogas como los cigarrillos, encender explosivos "
"como los cócteles Molotov y también lo puedes usar para prender fuego a "
"objetos cercanos."

#. ~ Same stats as a hatchet (as a tool and weapon), except it has prying
#. instead of hammering.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "crash axe"
msgid_plural "crash axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de accidente"
msgstr[1] "hachas de accidentes"
msgstr[2] "hachas de accidentes"

#. ~ Same stats as a hatchet (as a tool and weapon), except it has prying
#. instead of hammering.
#. ~ Description of "crash axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"A short lightweight emergency tool with a quarter circular blade, a short "
"pick opposite the blade, and an insulated handle.  Used on airplanes to chop"
" down or pry walls, or cabinets to gain access in case of fire."
msgstr ""
"Es una herramienta corta y liviana de emergencia, con una cuchilla circular,"
" un pequeño pico en la parte opuesta a la cuchilla y un mango aislado. Se "
"utiliza en los aviones para romper muros o casilleros para abrirse paso en "
"caso de incendio."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "large fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "large fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintor grande"
msgstr[1] "extintores grandes"
msgstr[2] "extintores grandes"

#. ~ Description of "large fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is an emergency fire extinguisher containing five gallons of fire "
"retardant foam.  It would be useful for putting out adjacent fires."
msgstr ""
"Este es un extintor de emergencia que contiene 18,5 litros de espuma "
"retardante de fuego. Sería útil para apagar incendios adyacentes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "fire axe"
msgid_plural "fire axes"
msgstr[0] "hacha de bombero"
msgstr[1] "hachas de bombero"
msgstr[2] "hachas de bombero"

#. ~ Description of "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a large, two-handed pickhead axe normally used by firefighters.  It "
"makes a powerful melee weapon, but is a bit slow to recover between swings."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una gran hacha de dos manos y con una cara de la cabeza terminada en"
" punta, normalmente utilizada por los bomberos. Es un arma poderosa para el "
"c. a c. pero es un poco lenta entre hachazo y hachazo."

#. ~ Description of a pocket in item "fire axe"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "Marrying strap for a Halligan bar."
msgstr "Correa para una barra Halligan."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "Halligan bar"
msgid_plural "Halligan bars"
msgstr[0] "barra Halligan"
msgstr[1] "barras Halligan"
msgstr[2] "barras Halligan"

#. ~ Description of "Halligan bar"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a heavy multiple-use tool commonly carried by firefighters, law "
"enforcement, and military rescue units.  Use it to open locked doors without"
" destroying them or to lift manhole covers.  You could also wield it to bash"
" some heads in."
msgstr ""
"Esta una herramienta pesada multiusos, comúnmente utilizada por los "
"bomberos, fuerzas de la ley y las unidades militares de rescate. Úsala para "
"abrir puertas cerradas con llave sin destruirlas o para levantar tapas de "
"alcantarillas. También la puedes empuñar para reventar algunas cabezas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "small fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "small fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintor pequeño"
msgstr[1] "extintores pequeños"
msgstr[2] "extintores pequeños"

#. ~ Description of "small fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a hand held fire extinguisher containing a liter of highly "
"compressed CO2 gas.  It would be useful for putting out adjacent fires."
msgstr ""
"Es un extintor portátil que contiene un litro de gas CO2 comprimido. Es útil"
" para apagar fuegos cercanos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "throwable fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintor arrojable"
msgstr[1] "extintores arrojables"
msgstr[2] "extintores arrojables"

#. ~ Description of "throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is a fire extinguisher in grenade form.  While not as effective as a "
"regular fire extinguisher, you can use it from a distance.  It has a plastic"
" plug that can be pulled, but is primarily activated by heat, so just throw "
"it into the flames."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de un extintor en forma de granada. Aunque no es tan eficaz como un"
" extintor normal, se puede utilizar a distancia. Tiene un tapón de plástico "
"del que se puede tirar, pero se activa principalmente con el calor, así que "
"basta con lanzarlo a las llamas."

#. ~ "menu_text" action message of item "throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "Pull plug"
msgstr "Tirar del gancho de seguridad"

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "You pull the plug on the extinguisher grenade."
msgstr "Se tira del pin de la granada extintor."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "active throwable fire extinguisher"
msgid_plural "active throwable fire extinguishers"
msgstr[0] "extintore arrojable activo"
msgstr[1] "extintores arrojables activos"
msgstr[2] "extintores arrojables activos"

#. ~ Description of "active throwable fire extinguisher"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"This is an active extinguisher grenade, likely to burst any second now.  "
"Better throw it!"
msgstr ""
"Esta es una granada de extinción activa, es probable que estalle en "
"cualquier momento. ¡Mejor lánzala!"

#. ~  If the pole itself has a diameter of around 3 cm which is thick, to be
#. frank, then we half it for the radius -> 1,5 cm, square it -> 2,25,
#. mulitplicate with pi -> ~7,07 cm² multiplicate with 160 cm length -> 1130
#. cm³ which is 1,13 liters. We add the hook which is around 100 ml of volume.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "pike pole"
msgid_plural "pike poles"
msgstr[0] "bichero"
msgstr[1] "bicheros"
msgstr[2] "bicheros"

#. ~  If the pole itself has a diameter of around 3 cm which is thick, to be
#. frank, then we half it for the radius -> 1,5 cm, square it -> 2,25,
#. mulitplicate with pi -> ~7,07 cm² multiplicate with 160 cm length -> 1130
#. cm³ which is 1,13 liters. We add the hook which is around 100 ml of volume.
#. ~ Description of "pike pole"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"A durable tool consisting of a sturdy fiberglass shaft tipped with a small "
"steel hook."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta duradera que consiste en un robusto eje de fibra de vidrio "
"con un pequeño gancho de acero en la punta."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid "New York hook"
msgid_plural "New York hooks"
msgstr[0] "New York hook"
msgstr[1] "New York hooks"
msgstr[2] "New York hooks"

#. ~ Description of "New York hook"
#: data/json/items/tool/firefighting.json
msgid ""
"A shaft with a pair of hooks on one end and a pry bar on the other, forged "
"from a single piece of steel."
msgstr ""
"Un mango con un par de ganchos en un extremo y una barra de palanca en el "
"otro, forjado a partir de una sola pieza de acero."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "plastic fish trap"
msgid_plural "plastic fish traps"
msgstr[0] "trampa plástica de peces"
msgstr[1] "trampas plásticas de peces"
msgstr[2] "trampas plásticas de peces"

#. ~ Description of "plastic fish trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"This is a makeshift fish trap made from plastic bottles.  It's simple, even "
"primitive, but easy to use.  The principle of action: the fish swims inside "
"for bait, but can't get out.  Not humane, prohibited by law, but there are "
"no cops left to care."
msgstr ""
"Es una trampa improvisada para peces , hecha con botellas plásticas. Es "
"simple, incluso diríamos primitiva, pero fácil de usar. El principio de "
"acción: el pez se mete buscando la carnada, pero no puede salir. No es muy "
"humano, está prohibido por ley, pero ya no hay policías de los que "
"preocuparse."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "basket fish trap"
msgid_plural "basket fish traps"
msgstr[0] "trampa de cesta para peces"
msgstr[1] "trampas de cesta para peces"
msgstr[2] "trampas de cesta para peces"

#. ~ Description of "basket fish trap"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"This is a long, wicker fish trap made from bark, reeds, cordage or other "
"natural materials.  It's a staple fishing tool in many pre-industrial "
"societies.  The principle of action: the fish swims inside for bait, but "
"can't get out."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de una larga trampa de mimbre para peces fabricada con corteza, "
"cañas, cordaje u otros materiales naturales. Es una herramienta de pesca "
"básica en muchas sociedades preindustriales. El principio de acción: el pez "
"nada en su interior buscando el cebo, pero no puede salir."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "fishing hook"
msgid_plural "fishing hooks"
msgstr[0] "anzuelo"
msgstr[1] "anzuelos"
msgstr[2] "anzuelos"

#. ~ Description of "fishing hook"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "A simple fishing hook."
msgstr "Es un simple anzuelo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "improvised fishing hook"
msgid_plural "improvised fishing hooks"
msgstr[0] "anzuelo improvisado"
msgstr[1] "anzuelos improvisados"
msgstr[2] "anzuelos improvisados"

#. ~ Description of "improvised fishing hook"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "An improvised fishing hook carved from wood or bone."
msgstr "Es una anzuelo tallado de madera o hueso."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "basic fishing rod"
msgid_plural "basic fishing rods"
msgstr[0] "caña básica para pescar"
msgstr[1] "cañas básicas para pescar"
msgstr[2] "cañas básicas para pescar"

#. ~ Description of "basic fishing rod"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"'Fishing rod' might be a bit too charitable of a description.  In truth, "
"this is a stick with a piece of string and a hook."
msgstr ""
"'Caña para pescar' tal vez sea mucho decir esto. La verdad es que es un palo"
" con un pedazo de cuerda y un anzuelo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "pro fishing rod"
msgid_plural "pro fishing rods"
msgstr[0] "caña profesional para pescar"
msgstr[1] "cañas profesionales para pescar"
msgstr[2] "cañas profesionales para pescar"

#. ~ Description of "pro fishing rod"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"A professional fishing rod with a matching set of weights.  With this you "
"should be able to catch 'em all."
msgstr ""
"Es una caña de pescar profesional, con un equipo de plomadas. Con esto "
"deberías ser capaz de pescar de todo."

#. ~ based on the ka-bar kaster
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "plastic hand fishing reel"
msgid_plural "plastic hand fishing reels"
msgstr[0] "carrete de pesca de mano de plástico"
msgstr[1] "carretes de pesca de mano de plástico"
msgstr[2] "carretes de pesca de mano de plástico"

#. ~ based on the ka-bar kaster
#. ~ Description of "plastic hand fishing reel"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"A commercial version of what is often known as a 'hobo fishing reel'.  It is"
" a short rod with a section on one end with fishing line wrapped around it, "
"with a rotating guard around that.  It is not as effective as a normal "
"fishing pole, but is much more compact than them."
msgstr ""
"Una versión comercial de lo que se conoce como \"carrete de pesca para "
"vagabundos\". Es una caña corta con una sección en un extremo con hilo de "
"pescar enrollado, con un protector giratorio alrededor. No es tan eficaz "
"como una caña de pescar normal, pero es mucho más compacta que ellas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid "hobo hand fishing reel"
msgid_plural "hobo hand fishing reels"
msgstr[0] "carrete de pesca manual para vagabundo"
msgstr[1] "carretes de pesca manual para vagabundos"
msgstr[2] "carretes de pesca manual para vagabundos"

#. ~ Description of "hobo hand fishing reel"
#: data/json/items/tool/fishing.json
msgid ""
"What is often known as a 'hobo fishing reel'.  It is a short wooden rod with"
" a section on one end with fishing line wrapped around it, with a notch to "
"put the string to help pull in fish.  It is not as effective as a normal "
"fishing pole, but is much more compact than them."
msgstr ""
"Lo que a menudo se conoce como \"carrete de pesca para vagabundos\". Se "
"trata de una caña de madera corta con una sección en un extremo con hilo de "
"pescar enrollado, con una muesca para poner el hilo que ayuda a tirar de los"
" peces. No es tan eficaz como una caña de pescar normal, pero es mucho más "
"compacta que ellas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "hand press"
msgid_plural "hand presses"
msgstr[0] "prensa manual"
msgstr[1] "prensas manuales"
msgstr[2] "prensas manuales"

#. ~ Description of "hand press"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid ""
"This is a small hand press for hand loading firearm ammunition.  It comes "
"with everything you need to start hand loading your own munitions."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña prensa de mano para cargar munición a mano. Viene con todo lo"
" que se necesita para empezar a cargar a mano tu propia munición."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "makeshift shotshell 'press'"
msgid_plural "makeshift shotshell 'presses'"
msgstr[0] "prensa improvisada para cartucho"
msgstr[1] "prensas improvisadas para cartuchos"
msgstr[2] "prensas improvisadas para cartuchos"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift shotshell 'press'"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid ""
"This is a collection of items improvised for field reloading of shotshells."
"  A plank with a hole cut in the center, a medium-sized nail, and a whittled"
" dowel are used to seat wads, decap primers, and reprime (carefully!) hulls."
"  Powder and shot are measured with a cut down fired shotshell.  The "
"opposite side of the plank has been shaped to allow for roll crimping of the"
" plastic hulls.  There's no provision for resizing, so reloaded hulls will "
"fire best in the firearm they were fired from."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una colección de artículos improvisados para recargar cartuchos. Un "
"tablón con un agujero cortado en el centro, un clavo de tamaño medio y una "
"clavija tallada se utilizan para asentar los fajos, retirar los pistones y "
"recolocar los pistones (¡con cuidado!). La pólvora y el disparo se miden con"
" una cartucho cortado. El lado opuesto del tablón ha sido moldeado para "
"permitir el rizado de los cartuchos de plástico. No se ha previsto cambiar "
"el tamaño, así que los cartuchos recargados dispararán mejor con el arma de "
"fuego con la que fueron previamente disparados."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "kinetic bullet puller"
msgid_plural "kinetic bullet pullers"
msgstr[0] "quitador cinético de balas"
msgstr[1] "quitadores cinético de balas"
msgstr[2] "quitadores cinético de balas"

#. ~ Description of "kinetic bullet puller"
#: data/json/items/tool/handloading.json
msgid "This is a tool used for properly disassembling firearm ammunition."
msgstr ""
"Es una herramienta que se usa para desarmar apropiadamente la munición."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal gasoline tank"
msgid_plural "internal gasoline tanks"
msgstr[0] "tanque interno de gasolina"
msgstr[1] "tanques internos de gasolina"
msgstr[2] "tanques internos de gasolina"

#. ~ Description of "internal gasoline tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "Internal tank for gasoline fuel cell bionic."
msgstr "Tanque interno para la celda de gasolina biónica."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal ethanol tank"
msgid_plural "internal ethanol tanks"
msgstr[0] "tanque interno de etanol"
msgstr[1] "tanques internos de etanol"
msgstr[2] "tanques internos de etanol"

#. ~ Description of "internal ethanol tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "Internal ethanol tank for ethanol burner bionic."
msgstr "Un tanque interno de etanol para el quemador de etanol biónico."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal oil tank"
msgid_plural "internal oil tanks"
msgstr[0] "tanque interno de aceite"
msgstr[1] "tanques internos de aceite"
msgstr[2] "tanques internos de aceite"

#. ~ Description of "internal oil tank"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "Internal oil tank for oil generator bionic."
msgstr "Un tanque interno de aceite para el generador de aceite biónico."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid "internal battery compartment"
msgid_plural "internal battery compartments"
msgstr[0] "compartimento interno para batería"
msgstr[1] "compartimentos internos para batería"
msgstr[2] "compartimentos internos para batería"

#. ~ Description of "internal battery compartment"
#: data/json/items/tool/integrated.json
msgid ""
"Internal compartment for holding medium sized batteries for battery system "
"bionic."
msgstr ""
"Un compartimento interno para contener baterías medianas para el sistema de "
"batería biónica."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "copper knife"
msgid_plural "copper knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de cobre"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de cobre"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de cobre"

#. ~ Description of "copper knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"A knife consisting of crudely-worked copper, and a simple handle.  "
"Primitive, but a step above stone-age."
msgstr ""
"Es un cuchillo que consiste en cobre trabajado toscamente, y un agarre "
"simple. Primitivo, pero un paso más adelante de la edad de piedra."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "bronze knife"
msgid_plural "bronze knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de bronce"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de bronce"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"Cast bronze knife with a full tang, with a handle wrapped in cord and "
"leather, lovingly work-hardened and sharpened to a fine edge."
msgstr ""
"Un cuchillo fundido de bronce con espiga completa y la empuñadura envuelta "
"en cuero y soga, trabajado con cariño y muy afilado."

#. ~ Too small to be effectively used for butchering, still not bad at it due
#. to serrated edge.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "dive knife"
msgid_plural "dive knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de buzo"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de buzo"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de buzo"

#. ~ Too small to be effectively used for butchering, still not bad at it due
#. to serrated edge.
#. ~ Description of "dive knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a short, sturdy knife with a serrated edge for cutting lines and "
"straps, and a blunt tip for prying.  Used primarily by divers, this knife "
"has been fitted with cork to slow its descent if dropped underwater, so it "
"takes up more space than usual."
msgstr ""
"Este es un cuchillo corto y robusto con un filo dentado para cortar cabos y "
"correas, y una punta roma para hacer palanca. Utilizado principalmente por "
"los buceadores, este cuchillo ha sido dotado de corcho para ralentizar su "
"descenso si se deja caer bajo el agua, por lo que ocupa más espacio de lo "
"habitual."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "honey scraper"
msgid_plural "honey scrapers"
msgstr[0] "espátula para miel"
msgstr[1] "espátulas para miel"
msgstr[2] "espátulas para miel"

#. ~ Description of "honey scraper"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"A sharp, knife-like tool used in harvesting honey from beehives.  Makes a "
"passable melee weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta afilada parecida a un cuchillo, que se usa para sacar la "
"miel de las colmenas. También puede servir como arma c. a c."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "pocket knife"
msgid_plural "pocket knives"
msgstr[0] "navaja"
msgstr[1] "navajas"
msgstr[2] "navajas"

#. ~ Description of "pocket knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a small pocket knife.  It isn't great for combat, but it's better "
"than nothing.  It's sharp enough to butcher with."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña navaja. No es muy útil en combate, pero es mejor que nada. Y "
"es bastante afilada como para usarla para descuartizar."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "stone knife"
msgid_plural "stone knives"
msgstr[0] "cuchillo de piedra"
msgstr[1] "cuchillos de piedra"
msgstr[2] "cuchillos de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a sharpened stone set into a hollowed handle.  Not nearly as usable "
"as a proper knife, but it's better than nothing."
msgstr ""
"Es una piedra afilada puesta dentro de un mango ahuecado. No es ni por asomo"
" tan útil como un cuchillo serio, pero es mejor que nada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "boxcutter knife"
msgid_plural "boxcutter knives"
msgstr[0] "cutter"
msgstr[1] "cutters"
msgstr[2] "cutters"

#. ~ Description of "boxcutter knife"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"This is a small knife, designed for opening boxes.  It could cause some "
"damage, but it really should be used against inanimate objects.  It is too "
"small to butcher corpses with."
msgstr ""
"Este es un cuchillo pequeño, diseñado para abrir cajas. Puede causar algo de"
" daño, pero en realidad debe usarse contra objetos inanimados. Es demasiado "
"pequeño para descuartizar cadáveres."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid "stone chopper"
msgid_plural "stone choppers"
msgstr[0] "cortador de piedra"
msgstr[1] "cortadores de piedra"
msgstr[2] "cortadores de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone chopper"
#: data/json/items/tool/knives.json
msgid ""
"A rock with sharpened edges, produced by knapping.  Works as a crude cutting"
" and butchering tool, if nothing else is available."
msgstr ""
"Una roca con bordes afilados, producida por el golpeo. Sirve como "
"herramienta de corte y descuartizado, si no se dispone de otra cosa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "digging stick"
msgid_plural "digging sticks"
msgstr[0] "palo cavador"
msgstr[1] "palos cavadores"
msgstr[2] "palos cavadores"

#. ~ Description of "digging stick"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a large stick, with the end carved into a broad blade for digging.  "
"It could be used to dig shallow pits, but not deep ones."
msgstr ""
"Es un palo largo, con una punta tallada en forma de pala ancha para cavar. "
"Puede ser usada para cavar pozos poco profundos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "trowel"
msgid_plural "trowels"
msgstr[0] "paleta"
msgstr[1] "paletas"
msgstr[2] "paletas"

#. ~ Description of "trowel"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A small, sharp gardening shovel, perfect for digging up grubs and worms."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña pala afilada de jardinería, perfecta para sacar larvas y "
"gusanos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "hoe"
msgid_plural "hoes"
msgstr[0] "azada"
msgstr[1] "azadas"
msgstr[2] "azadas"

#. ~ Description of "hoe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a farming implement.  You can use it to turn tillable land into a "
"slow-to-cross pile of dirt, or dig a shallow pit."
msgstr ""
"Este es un implemento agrícola. Puedes usarlo para convertir la tierra "
"cultivable en una pila de tierra lenta de atravesar, o cavar un hoyo poco "
"profundo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "bronze hoe"
msgid_plural "bronze hoes"
msgstr[0] "azada de bronce"
msgstr[1] "azadas de bronce"
msgstr[2] "azadas de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze hoe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a farming implement made from bronze.  The added heft and durability"
" should let you till soil for farming more easily as well."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta de labranza hecha de bronce.  El peso y la durabilidad que "
"posee debería permitirte labrar la tierra muy fácilmente."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "wooden shovel"
msgid_plural "wooden shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala de madera"
msgstr[1] "palas de madera"
msgstr[2] "palas de madera"

#. ~ Description of "wooden shovel"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a crude shovel with shovelhead made from wood, historically used as "
"an alternative to metal shovels when metal was too expensive.  It works "
"passably well, but really can't compare to a metal shovel."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de una tosca pala con cabeza de pala hecha de madera, utilizada "
"históricamente como alternativa a las palas de metal cuando éstas eran "
"demasiado caras. Funciona pasablemente bien, pero realmente no se puede "
"comparar con una pala de metal."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "metal rake"
msgid_plural "metal rakes"
msgstr[0] "rastrillo de metal"
msgstr[1] "rastrillos de metal"
msgstr[2] "rastrillos de metal"

#. ~ Description of "metal rake"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "A sturdy metal rake, a must-have during autumn."
msgstr "Un robusto rastrillo de metal, un obligatorio en otoño."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "plastic rake"
msgid_plural "plastic rakes"
msgstr[0] "rastrillo de plástico"
msgstr[1] "rastrillos de plástico"
msgstr[2] "rastrillos de plástico"

#. ~ Description of "plastic rake"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A cheap plastic rake.  Will break quite fast if used for anything other than"
" raking leaves."
msgstr ""
"Un rastrillo de plástico barato. Se romperá bastante rápido si se utiliza "
"para otra cosa que no sea rastrillar hojas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "scythe"
msgid_plural "scythes"
msgstr[0] "guadaña"
msgstr[1] "guadañas"
msgstr[2] "guadañas"

#. ~ Description of "scythe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is an old-fashioned farming tool used to cut tall grass.  While it may "
"be a giant blade on the end of a stick, it is incredibly awkward to use for "
"anything but its intended purpose."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta antigua de granja que se usa para cortar la hierba alta. "
"Aunque es una cuchilla gigante en la punta de un palo, es increíblemente "
"incómoda de usar para cualquier cosa que no sea su propósito previsto."

#. ~ Description of "scythe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a dull, cheaply-made replica of an old-fashioned farming tool used "
"to cut tall grass."
msgstr ""
"Una réplica barata sin filo de una guadaña antigua que se utilizaba para "
"cortar el pasto alto."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Pretty similar to the war scythe, but with less weight, more cutting
#. damage and capable of casting a strong offensive spell.
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/enchanted_melee.json
msgid "grim reaper's scythe"
msgid_plural "grim reaper's scythes"
msgstr[0] "guadaña del ángel de la muerte"
msgstr[1] "guadañas del ángel de la muerte"
msgstr[2] "guadañas del ángel de la muerte"

#. ~ Description of "grim reaper's scythe"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a long and crooked tool used to reap souls, with a skull engraved in"
" its blade.  Let the harvest begin."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta larga y curva que se utiliza para cosechar almas, tiene una "
"calavera grabada en su cuchilla. Que comience la cosecha."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "shovel"
msgid_plural "shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala"
msgstr[1] "palas"
msgstr[2] "palas"

#. ~ Description of "shovel"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "This is a digging tool.  Use it to dig pits adjacent to your location."
msgstr ""
"Es una herramienta para cavar. Úsala para cavar pozos en los espacios "
"adyacentes al lugar donde estés parado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "snow shovel"
msgid_plural "snow shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala de nieve"
msgstr[1] "palas de nieve"
msgstr[2] "palas de nieve"

#. ~ Description of "snow shovel"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "This is a sturdy tool used for shoving snow."
msgstr "Esta es una herramienta robusta utilizada para mover la nieve."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "plastic snow shovel"
msgid_plural "plastic snow shovels"
msgstr[0] "pala de nieve de plástico"
msgstr[1] "palas de nieve de plástico"
msgstr[2] "palas de nieve de plástico"

#. ~ Description of "plastic snow shovel"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "A cheap plastic shovel used for shoving snow."
msgstr "Una pala de plástico barata utilizada para mover la nieve."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "stone sickle"
msgid_plural "stone sickles"
msgstr[0] "hoz de piedra"
msgstr[1] "hoces de piedra"
msgstr[2] "hoces de piedra"

#. ~ Description of "stone sickle"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A primitive tool to cut grass with.  The sharp, crescent-shaped stone at the"
" end of the handle is barely good enough for the job."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta primitiva para cortar la hierba. La afilada piedra en forma "
"de media luna en el extremo del mango apenas sirve para el trabajo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json data/mods/MMA/swords_and_blades.json
msgid "sickle"
msgid_plural "sickles"
msgstr[0] "hoz"
msgstr[1] "hoces"
msgstr[2] "hoces"

#. ~ Description of "sickle"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is an old-fashioned farming tool used to cut tall grass.  While it may "
"be a massive curved blade on a handle, it is incredibly awkward to use for "
"anything but its intended purpose."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta antigua de granja que se usa para cortar la hierba alta. "
"Aunque es una enorme cuchilla curva con mango, es increíblemente incómoda de"
" usar para cualquier cosa que no sea su propósito previsto."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "bronze sickle"
msgid_plural "bronze sickles"
msgstr[0] "hoz de bronce"
msgstr[1] "hoces de bronce"
msgstr[2] "hoces de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze sickle"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A hand-held grass-cutting tool with a cast bronze blade, fastened to a wood "
"handle wrapped with leather."
msgstr ""
"Una herramienta de mano con la cuchilla fundida en bronce para cortar el "
"pasto, ajustada a un mango de madera envuelto con cuero."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "bill"
msgid_plural "bills"
msgstr[0] "hocejo"
msgstr[1] "hocejos"
msgstr[2] "hocejos"

#. ~ Description of "bill"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a long, slightly curved and hooked steel blade on the end of a "
"sturdy shaft.  Could be used to thoroughly ruin something's day, or cut "
"branches and small trees."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla larga de acero levemente curvada con forma de gancho, con una "
"empuñadura resistente. Se puede usar para arruinarle el día a alguien o para"
" cortar ramas y arbustos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid "bronze bill"
msgid_plural "bronze bills"
msgstr[0] "corquete de bronce"
msgstr[1] "corquetes de bronce"
msgstr[2] "corquetes de bronce"

#. ~ Description of "bronze bill"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"This is a long, slightly curved and hooked bronze blade on the end of a "
"sturdy shaft.  Could be used to thoroughly ruin something's day, or cut "
"branches and small trees."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla larga de bronce levemente curvada con forma de gancho, con una "
"empuñadura resistente. Se puede usar para arruinarle el día a alguien o para"
" cortar ramas y arbustos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/tools.json
msgid "hedge trimmer (off)"
msgid_plural "hedge trimmers (off)"
msgstr[0] "cortasetos (off)"
msgstr[1] "cortasetos (off)"
msgstr[2] "cortasetos (off)"

#. ~ Description of "hedge trimmer (off)"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A cordless, double-sided, gasoline-powered hedge trimmer.  A long line of "
"sharp-edged teeth extends from the engine; turning the trimmer on will make "
"them rapidly vibrate.  The poor man's chainsaw as far as the zombies are "
"concerned."
msgstr ""
"Un cortasetos a combustible, sin cable y de doble filo. Una larga línea de "
"dientes afilados se extienden desde el motor. Al encender el cortasetos hace"
" que vibren rápidamente. Es la motosierra del pobre, en cuanto a lo que "
"concierne a los zombis."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/items/tools.json
msgid "hedge trimmer (on)"
msgid_plural "hedge trimmers (on)"
msgstr[0] "cortasetos (on)"
msgstr[1] "cortasetos (on)"
msgstr[2] "cortasetos (on)"

#. ~ Description of "hedge trimmer (on)"
#: data/json/items/tool/landscaping.json
msgid ""
"A cordless, double-sided, gasoline-powered hedge trimmer.  It is currently "
"on, ready to do some zombie topiary; use this item to turn it off."
msgstr ""
"Un cortasetos a combustible, sin cable y de doble filo. Está encendido, "
"listo para podar artísticamente algún zombi. Usar para apagar."

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "atomic lamp"
msgid_plural "atomic lamps"
msgstr[0] "lámpara atómica"
msgstr[1] "lámparas atómicas"
msgstr[2] "lámparas atómicas"

#. ~ Description of "atomic lamp"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this very "
"expensive lamp will emit a small amount of light for at least a decade.  "
"Before the Cataclysm, it was mostly an expensive way to show off your "
"preparedness.  Now, it's actually pretty cool.  Use it to close the cover "
"and hide the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la descomposición nuclear y los LEDs de baja "
"energía, esta lámpara muy costosa emitirá una pequeña cantidad de luz "
"durante al menos una década. Antes del cataclismo, era sobre todo una forma "
"cara de mostrar su preparación. Ahora, en realidad es bastante genial. Úsala"
" para cerrar la tapa y esconder la luz."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic lamp"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid "You close the lamp's cover."
msgstr "Cierras la cubierta de la lámpara."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid "atomic lamp (covered)"
msgid_plural "atomic lamps (covered)"
msgstr[0] "lámpara atómica (cubierta)"
msgstr[1] "lámparas atómicas (cubiertas)"
msgstr[2] "lámparas atómicas (cubiertas)"

#. ~ Description of "atomic lamp (covered)"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this very "
"expensive lamp will emit a small amount of light for at least a decade.  "
"Before the Cataclysm, it was mostly an expensive way to show off your "
"preparedness.  Now, it's actually pretty cool.  The cover is closed.  Use it"
" to open the cover and show the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la descomposición nuclear y los LEDs de baja "
"energía, esta lámpara muy costosa emitirá una pequeña cantidad de luz "
"durante al menos una década. Antes del cataclismo, era sobre todo una forma "
"cara de mostrar su preparación. Ahora, en realidad es bastante genial. La "
"tapa está cerrada. Úsala para abrir la tapa y mostrar la luz."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic lamp (covered)"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid "You open the lamp's cover."
msgstr "Abres la cubierta de la lámpara."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid "atomic reading light"
msgid_plural "atomic reading lights"
msgstr[0] "luz atómica de lectura"
msgstr[1] "luces atómicas de lectura"
msgstr[2] "luces atómicas de lectura"

#. ~ Description of "atomic reading light"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this extremely "
"expensive little light will provide just enough light to read by for at "
"least a decade.  It is also available with a cute cartoon bear cover to turn"
" it into a nightlight for a very wealthy child with a fear of the dark.  Use"
" it to close the cover and hide the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la descomposición nuclear y los LEDs de baja "
"energía, esta pequeña luz extremadamente cara proporcionará la luz "
"suficiente para leer durante al menos una década. También está disponible "
"con una linda cubierta de oso de dibujos animados para convertirla en una "
"luz nocturna para un niño muy rico con miedo a la oscuridad. Úsalo para "
"cerrar la cubierta y esconder la luz."

#. ~ "msg" action message of item "atomic reading light"
#. ~ "msg" action message of item "magical reading light"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
msgid "You close the nightlight's cover."
msgstr "Cierras la cubierta del velador."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid "atomic reading light (covered)"
msgid_plural "atomic reading lights (covered)"
msgstr[0] "luz atómica de lectura (cubierta)"
msgstr[1] "luces atómicas de lectura (cubiertas)"
msgstr[2] "luces atómicas de lectura (cubiertas)"

#. ~ Description of "atomic reading light (covered)"
#: data/json/items/tool/lighting.json
msgid ""
"Powered by the magic of nuclear decay and low-energy LEDs, this extremely "
"expensive little light will provide just enough light to read by for at "
"least a decade.  It is also available with a cute cartoon bear cover to turn"
" it into a nightlight for a very wealthy child with a fear of the dark.  The"
" cover is closed.  Use it to open the cover and show the light."
msgstr ""
"Alimentada por la magia de la descomposición nuclear y los LEDs de baja "
"energía, esta pequeña luz extremadamente cara proporcionará la luz "
"suficiente para leer durante al menos una década. También está disponible "
