"A simple wooden acoustic guitar with a strap so you can wear it around, even"
" when not playing."
msgstr ""
"Una simple guitarra acústica de madera con una correa para que la puedas "
"llevar, incluso cuando no la estás tocando."

#. ~ Electric guitar less awesome when there's no electricity.  So I made it
#. much quieter and less fun to play.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "electric guitar"
msgid_plural "electric guitars"
msgstr[0] "guitarra eléctrica"
msgstr[1] "guitarras eléctricas"
msgstr[2] "guitarras eléctricas"

#. ~ Electric guitar less awesome when there's no electricity.  So I made it
#. much quieter and less fun to play.
#. ~ Description of "electric guitar"
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid ""
"A standard factory-made electric guitar.  It's probably better at smashing "
"heads than melting faces, these days.  Has a strap."
msgstr ""
"Una guitarra eléctrica estándar de fábrica. Probablemente es mejor para "
"romper cabezas que para derretir rostros, en estos días. Tiene una correa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "bagpipes"
msgid_plural "bagpipes"
msgstr[0] "gaita"
msgstr[1] "gaitas"
msgstr[2] "gaitas"

#. ~ Description of "bagpipes"
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid ""
"A traditional musical instrument using enclosed reeds fed from a reservoir "
"of air contained within a leather bag.  It has a strap so you can wear it "
"around, even when not playing."
msgstr ""
"Un instrumento musical tradicional que tiene lengüetas incluídas alimentadas"
" por una reserva de aire contenida en una bolsa de cuero. Tiene correas para"
" que te la puedas colgar, incluso cuando no estás tocando."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "tuba"
msgid_plural "tubas"
msgstr[0] "tuba"
msgstr[1] "tubas"
msgstr[2] "tubas"

#. ~ Description of "tuba"
#. ~ ol' is an informal short-form for old, and here is part of big-ol as
#. large-and-cumbersome.
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid ""
"A big ol' tuba.  Much easier to play when wearing.  Thankfully, this one has"
" a harness attached."
msgstr ""
"Una gran tuba. Mucho más fácil de tocar cuando la tienes puesta. Por suerte,"
" esta viene con un arnés."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid "saxophone"
msgid_plural "saxophones"
msgstr[0] "saxofón"
msgstr[1] "saxofones"
msgstr[2] "saxofones"

#. ~ Description of "saxophone"
#: data/json/items/tool/musical_instruments.json
msgid ""
"A brass alto saxophone with a neck strap, so you can wear it while playing."
msgstr ""
"Un saxofón alto de latón con correa para el cuello, para que puedas usarlo "
"mientras tocas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "chicken cage"
msgid_plural "chicken cages"
msgstr[0] "jaula para gallinas"
msgstr[1] "jaulas para gallinas"
msgstr[2] "jaulas para gallinas"

#. ~ Description of "chicken cage"
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"A wire container made for transporting chickens, but you can use it to hold "
"any tiny animal.  Use it on a suitable animal to capture, use it on an empty"
" tile to release."
msgstr ""
"Un contenedor de alambre hecho para el transporte de pollos, pero se puede "
"usar para sostener cualquier animal pequeño. Úselo en un animal adecuado "
"para capturarlo, úselo en una baldosa vacía para liberarlo."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "dog whistle"
msgid_plural "dog whistles"
msgstr[0] "silbato para perros"
msgstr[1] "silbatos para perros"
msgstr[2] "silbatos para perros"

#. ~ Description of "dog whistle"
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"This is a small whistle.  When used, it produces a high tone that causes "
"nearby friendly dogs to either follow you closely and stop attacking, or "
"start attacking enemies if they are currently docile."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño silbato. Cuando es usado, produce un tono alto que causa que "
"todos los perros aliados cercanos te sigan o dejen de atacar, o comiencen a "
"atacar a los enemigos si en ese momento están dóciles."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "shears"
msgid_plural "shears"
msgstr[0] "tijera de esquilar"
msgstr[1] "tijeras de esquilar"
msgstr[2] "tijeras de esquilar"

#. ~ Description of "shears"
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "This is a set of shears designed to obtain wool from sheep."
msgstr "Este es un juego de tijeras diseñado para obtener lana de las ovejas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "forged shears"
msgid_plural "forged shears"
msgstr[0] "tijera forjada para esquilar"
msgstr[1] "tijeras forjadas para esquilar"
msgstr[2] "tijeras forjadas para esquilar"

#. ~ Description of "forged shears"
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"This is a set of heavy-duty shears designed to obtain wool from sheep.  Made"
" of 2 steel blades connected by spring leaf."
msgstr ""
"Un par de tijeras resistentes diseñadas para cortar la lana de las ovejas.  "
"Está hecha con dos cuchillas de acero conectadas por un resorte tipo muelle."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid "bronze shears"
msgid_plural "bronze shears"
msgstr[0] "tijera de bronce para esquilar"
msgstr[1] "tijeras de bronce para esquilar"
msgstr[2] "tijeras de bronce para esquilar"

#. ~ Description of "bronze shears"
#: data/json/items/tool/pets.json
msgid ""
"This is a set of forged single-piece bronze shears for cutting fabrics.  "
"Made of two painstakingly sharpened blades connected by a carefully tempered"
