msgid_plural "German shepherds"
msgstr[0] "pastor alemán"
msgstr[1] "pastores alemanes"
msgstr[2] "pastores alemanes"

#. ~ Description of monster "German shepherd"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The original K-9 breed.  An easily trained and powerful attack dog that will"
" defend its owner to the death, however they don't work well in packs."
msgstr ""
"La raza K-9 original. Un perro de ataque fácil de entrenar y poderoso que "
"defenderá a su dueño hasta la muerte, sin embargo no funcionan bien en "
"manadas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "German shepherd puppy"
msgid_plural "German shepherd puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de pastor alemán"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de pastor alemán"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de pastor alemán"

#. ~ Description of monster "German shepherd puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless German Shepherd puppy.  Much safer to tame than an "
"adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de pastor alemán. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Great Pyrenees"
msgid_plural "Great Pyrenees"
msgstr[0] "Gran Pirineo"
msgstr[1] "Grandes Pirineos"
msgstr[2] "Grandes Pirineos"

#. ~ Description of monster "Great Pyrenees"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A large and powerful breed, the Great Pyrenees has a beautiful, thick white "
"coat.  Originally bred to deter wolves and other predators, now faced with "
"protecting livestock from shambling hordes of undead."
msgstr ""
"Una raza grande y poderosa, el Gran Pirineo tiene un hermoso y grueso pelaje"
" blanco. Originalmente criado para disuadir a los lobos y otros "
"depredadores, ahora se enfrenta a la protección del ganado de las hordas de "
"muertos vivientes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Great Pyrenees puppy"
msgid_plural "Great Pyrenees puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de Gran Pirineo"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de Gran Pirineo"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de Gran Pirineo"

#. ~ Description of monster "Great Pyrenees puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Great Pyrenees puppy.  Much safer to tame than an "
"adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de Gran Pirineo. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "rottweiler"
msgid_plural "rottweilers"
msgstr[0] "rottweiler"
msgstr[1] "rottweilers"
msgstr[2] "rottweilers"

#. ~ Description of monster "rottweiler"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A terrifying breed to face feral, Rottweilers are descended from Roman "
"legion mastiffs.  It's robust, vicious, and quite capable of mauling a human"
" to death."
msgstr ""
"Una raza aterradora para enfrentarse a lo salvaje, los Rottweilers "
"descienden de los mastines de la legión romana. Es robusto, feroz, y "
"bastante capaz de matar a un humano hasta la muerte."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "rottweiler puppy"
msgid_plural "rottweiler puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de rottweiler"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de rottweiler"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de rottweiler"

#. ~ Description of monster "rottweiler puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Rottweiler puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult"
" dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de Rottweiler. Mucho más seguro de "
"domesticar que un perro adulto."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "cattle dog"
msgid_plural "cattle dogs"
msgstr[0] "perro de ganado"
msgstr[1] "perros de ganado"
msgstr[2] "perros de ganado"

#. ~ Description of monster "cattle dog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An agile and sturdy breed that is welcome on any farm, the Australian cattle"
" dog is adept at leaping fences and herding livestock."
msgstr ""
"Es una raza resistente y ágil, bienvenida en cualquier granja. El perro "
"pastor australiano es capaz de saltar sobre cercos y pastorear ganado."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "cattle dog puppy"
msgid_plural "cattle dog puppies"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de perro de ganado"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de perro de ganado"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de perro de ganado"

#. ~ Description of monster "cattle dog puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Australian cattle dog puppy.  Much safer to tame "
"than an adult dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro de perro de ganado australiano. Mucho más "
"seguro de domesticar que un perro adulto."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Samoyed"
msgid_plural "Samoyeds"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "Samoyed"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A large, white, fluffy herding dog from Siberia.  Samoyeds are rarely "
"aggressive: Their smiley face doesn't help either.  They can be agile for "
"their size and can be taught to pull sleds."
msgstr ""
"Un perro de pastoreo grande, blanco y esponjoso de Siberia. Los samoyedos "
"rara vez son agresivos: Su cara sonriente tampoco ayuda. Pueden ser ágiles "
"para su tamaño y se les puede enseñar a tirar de los trineos."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Samoyed puppy"
msgid_plural "Samoyed puppies"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "Samoyed puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless Samoyed puppy.  Much safer to tame than an adult "
"dog."
msgstr ""
"Un adorable e indefenso cachorro samoyedo. Mucho más seguro de domesticar "
"que un perro adulto."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "fox"
msgid_plural "foxes"
msgstr[0] "zorro"
msgstr[1] "zorros"
msgstr[2] "zorros"

#. ~ Description of monster "fox"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small, omnivorous canine with almost cat-like mannerisms.  It is a "
"solitary hunter, and one of the only canids able to climb trees."
msgstr ""
"Un cánido pequeño y omnívoro, con un comportamiento casi felino. Es un "
"cazador solitario y uno de los únicos cánidos capaces de trepar a los "
"árboles."

#. ~ Description of monster "fox"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The red fox, an omnivorous canine and largest of the true foxes, it is a "
"wily hunter with a combative, suspicious temperament."
msgstr ""
"Un zorro rojo, un canino omnívoro y el más grande de los zorros verdaderos. "
"Es un cazador astuto con un temperamento combativo y suspicaz."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "groundhog"
msgid_plural "groundhogs"
msgstr[0] "marmota"
msgstr[1] "marmotas"
msgstr[2] "marmotas"

#. ~ Description of monster "groundhog"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"Also known as the woodchuck, this ground squirrel has no actual talent for "
"chucking wood."
msgstr ""
"La marmota es una ardilla menos ágil, no la vas a ver trepando los árboles."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "jackrabbit"
msgid_plural "jackrabbits"
msgstr[0] "liebre"
msgstr[1] "liebres"
msgstr[2] "liebres"

#. ~ Description of monster "jackrabbit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The snowshoe hare, a small grass-eater with a brown fur coat that changes to"
" white in the wintertime."
msgstr ""
"La liebre americana, un pequeño comedor de hierba con piel marrón que en "
"invierno se pone blanca."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "foal"
msgid_plural "foals"
msgstr[0] "potrillo"
msgstr[1] "potrillos"
msgstr[2] "potrillos"

#. ~ Description of monster "foal"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-"
"looking muscles.  This one is still a juvenile; it'll take a while before it"
" can be ridden."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero de pastoreo herrado con melena, una cola larga y músculos muy "
"potentes. Este todavía es joven, tiene que crecer antes de poder ser "
"montado."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "horse"
msgid_plural "horses"
msgstr[0] "caballo"
msgstr[1] "caballos"
msgstr[2] "caballos"

#. ~ Description of monster "horse"
#. ~ Description of monster "Scott's horse"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#: data/mods/Megafauna/monsters/mf_domestic.json
msgid ""
"A hooved grazing mammal with a mane of hair, a sweeping tail, and powerful-"
"looking muscles.  A stalwart companion to humans for longer than recorded "
"history, with some effort you should be able to get this one to trust you "
"enough to ride it."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero de pastoreo con pezuñas, pelo, cola y músculos poderosos. "
"Compañero incondicional de los humanos desde hace más tiempo que la "
"historia, con un poco de esfuerzo podrás conseguir que confíe en ti lo "
"suficiente como para montarlo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "lemming"
msgid_plural "lemmings"
msgstr[0] "lemming"
msgstr[1] "lemmings"
msgstr[2] "lemmings"

#. ~ Description of monster "lemming"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Northern bog lemming, a small, predominantly vegetarian rodent that "
"spends its life in the murk of swamps and other wetlands.  Contrary to "
"popular belief, these creatures are not particularly hapless or suicidal, "
"but they can eat themselves into scarcity within a few generations."
msgstr ""
"Un lemming de las ciénagas del norte, es un roedor pequeño, "
"predominantemente vegetariano que pasa su vida en la oscuridad de los "
"pantanos y otras zonas húmedas. Al contrario de la creencia popular, estas "
"criaturas no son desgraciadas o suicidas, pero pueden volverse escasas en un"
" par de generaciones."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "mink"
msgid_plural "minks"
msgstr[0] "visón"
msgstr[1] "visones"
msgstr[2] "visones"

#. ~ Description of monster "mink"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The American mink, a partially aquatic weasel, once factory-farmed for its "
"fur.  It is a capable fisher, but the presence of otters in these parts "
"makes it rely more on food from the land."
msgstr ""
"El visón americano, una comadreja parcialmente acuática, una vez cultivada "
"en fábrica por su piel. Es un pescador capaz, pero la presencia de nutrias "
"en estas partes hace que dependa más de la comida de la tierra."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
#: data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "moose"
msgid_plural "moose"
msgstr[0] "alce"
msgstr[1] "alces"
msgstr[2] "alces"

#. ~ Description of monster "moose"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Eastern moose, the largest living species of deer.  While they aren't "
"typically aggressive unless provoked, the autumn mating season can make the "
"bulls quite ill-tempered."
msgstr ""
"El alce oriental, la mayor especie viva de ciervo. Aunque no suelen ser "
"agresivos a menos que se les provoque, la temporada de apareamiento de otoño"
" puede hacer que los machos sean bastante malhumorados."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "moose calf"
msgid_plural "moose calves"
msgstr[0] "cría de alce"
msgstr[1] "crías de alce"
msgstr[2] "crías de alce"

#. ~ Description of monster "moose calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The baby moose is called a calf.  Calves can outrun a human within days of "
"birth and gain weight at an incredible pace."
msgstr ""
"Es la cría de un alce. Unos días después de haber nacido, ya es más rápido "
"que un humano y gana kilos a un ritmo increíble."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "great tusked moose"
msgid_plural "great tusked moose"
msgstr[0] "alce colmilludo grande"
msgstr[1] "alces colmilludos grandes"
msgstr[2] "alces colmilludos grandes"

#. ~ Description of monster "great tusked moose"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The great tusked moose is a mutant variety of megafauna that evolved after "
"the Cataclysm.  Easily recognized by the underslung tusks off the side of "
"each mouth, in addition to an impressive rack of horns.  These moose are "
"more aggressive than their predecessors."
msgstr ""
"El alce de grandes colmillos es una variedad mutante de megafauna que "
"evolucionó después del Cataclismo. Fácil de reconocer por los colmillos "
"sobresaliendo a ambos lados de la boca, además de una impresionante "
"cornamenta. Estos alces son más agresivos que sus predecesores."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "tusked moose calf"
msgid_plural "tusked moose calves"
msgstr[0] "cría de alce colmilludo"
msgstr[1] "crías de alce colmilludo"
msgstr[2] "crías de alce colmilludo"

#. ~ Description of monster "tusked moose calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The baby moose is called a calf so are it's tusked mutant descendants.  "
"Calves can outrun a human within days of birth and gain weight at an "
"incredible pace."
msgstr ""
"La cría de un alce colmilludo mutante. Unos días después de haber nacido, ya"
" es más rápido que un humano y gana kilos a un ritmo increíble."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "muskrat"
msgid_plural "muskrats"
msgstr[0] "rata almizclera"
msgstr[1] "ratas almizcleras"
msgstr[2] "ratas almizcleras"

#. ~ Description of monster "muskrat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A large omnivorous rodent with a thick furry pelt, found in wetlands across "
"the Northern Hemisphere.  It marks its territory with a musky odor for which"
" it is named."
msgstr ""
"Un roedor omnívoro grande con un pelaje peludo y gruesoa, que se encuentra "
"en los humedales del hemisferio norte. Marca su territorio con un olor "
"almizclado por el que recibe su nombre."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
#: data/mods/Dark-Skies-Above/overrides/monsters.json
msgid "gigantic naked mole-rat"
msgid_plural "gigantic naked mole-rats"
msgstr[0] "rata topo desnuda gigante"
msgstr[1] "ratas topo desnudas gigantes"
msgstr[2] "ratas topo desnudas gigantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "gigantic naked mole-rat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A huge, rumbling mutated mass of wrinkly, nearly translucent skin that has "
"been toughened by constant tunneling.  Its hide is riddled with giant scabs,"
" as a pair of incisors the size of an industrial excavator's buckets gnash "
"constantly and several car-length whiskers twitch in the air.  It regularly "
"makes high-pitched chirps as it roams around."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme masa mutada y estruendosa de piel arrugada, casi translúcida, que"
" se ha endurecido por los constantes túneles. Su pellejo está plagado de "
"costras gigantes, como un par de incisivos del tamaño de los cubos de una "
"excavadora industrial que crujen constantemente y varios bigotes de coche se"
" mueven en el aire. Regularmente hace chirridos agudos mientras deambula por"
" ahí."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "opossum"
msgid_plural "opossums"
msgstr[0] "zarigüeya"
msgstr[1] "zarigüeyas"
msgstr[2] "zarigüeyas"

#. ~ Description of monster "opossum"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Virginia opossum, a small omnivorous marsupial native to North America."
"  About the size of a cat, it is hardy and adaptive, and a fairly common "
"sight in urban areas."
msgstr ""
"Es la zarigüeya de Virginia, un pequeño marsupial omnívoro nativo de América"
" del Norte. Más o menos del tamaño de un gato, robusto y de fácil "
"adaptación, es común verlo en las zonas urbanas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "otter"
msgid_plural "otters"
msgstr[0] "nutria"
msgstr[1] "nutrias"
msgstr[2] "nutrias"

#. ~ Description of monster "otter"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The North American river otter, a shy water-dwelling relative of the weasel "
"that lives in large families along the banks of streams.  It is an excellent"
" fisher and a resourceful survivor, using the abandoned dens of beavers and "
"other animals to raise its own young."
msgstr ""
"La nutria de río de Norte América es un tímido pariente de la comadreja que "
"vive en familias grandes a lo largo de las orillas de los arroyos. Es un "
"excelente pescador y un ingenioso superviviente, que utiliza las madrigueras"
" abandonadas de castores y otros animales para criar a sus propias crías."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "piglet"
msgid_plural "piglets"
msgstr[0] "lechón"
msgstr[1] "lechones"
msgstr[2] "lechones"

#. ~ Description of monster "piglet"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and "
"inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral.  Unlike the fully "
"grown version, this juvenile can be tamed."
msgstr ""
"Un omnívoro domesticado descendiente del jabalí, inteligente e inquisitivo. "
"Dejado a su suerte, se ha vuelto salvaje. A diferencia de la versión "
"completamente desarrollada, puede ser domesticado."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "pig"
msgid_plural "pigs"
msgstr[0] "cerdo"
msgstr[1] "cerdos"
msgstr[2] "cerdos"

#. ~ Description of monster "pig"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A domesticated omnivore descended from the wild boar, intelligent and "
"inquisitive.  Left to its own devices, it has gone feral."
msgstr ""
"Un omnívoro domesticado que desciende del jabalí salvaje. Es inteligente y "
"curioso. Dejado a su propio cuidado, se ha vuelto salvaje."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/json/monsters/nether.json
msgid "rabbit"
msgid_plural "rabbits"
msgstr[0] "conejo"
msgstr[1] "conejos"
msgstr[2] "conejos"

#. ~ Description of monster "rabbit"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/json/monsters/nether.json
msgid ""
"A small mammal with a cute wiggling nose, a cotton ball tail, and a body "
"made of delicious flesh."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño mamífero con una simpática nariz que se menea, una cola de bola "
"de algodón y un cuerpo hecho de deliciosa carne."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "raccoon"
msgid_plural "raccoons"
msgstr[0] "mapache"
msgstr[1] "mapaches"
msgstr[2] "mapaches"

#. ~ Description of monster "raccoon"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small mammal native to North America, distinctive for its dexterous paws "
"and facial markings.  It is resourceful and agile enough to open sealed "
"containers in search of food."
msgstr ""
"Pequeño mamífero originario de América del Norte, que se distingue por la "
"destreza de sus patas y sus marcas faciales. Es lo suficientemente ingenioso"
" y ágil como para abrir recipientes cerrados en busca de comida."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "rat king"
msgid_plural "rat kings"
msgstr[0] "rata rey"
msgstr[1] "ratas rey"
msgstr[2] "ratas rey"

#. ~ Description of monster "rat king"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A towering swarm of mutated rats, their tails knotted together in a filthy "
"mass.  A fetid stench flows from its filthy presence."
msgstr ""
"Un enjambre de ratas mutadas formando una torre, sus colas están atadas "
"entre sí formando una desagradable masa. Un hedor fétido fluye de esta "
"desagradable presencia."

#. ~ Death message of monster "rat king"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "Rats suddenly swarm into view."
msgstr "De repente, aparece una manada de ratas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "sewer rat"
msgid_plural "sewer rats"
msgstr[0] "rata de cloaca"
msgstr[1] "ratas de cloaca"
msgstr[2] "ratas de cloaca"

#. ~ Description of monster "sewer rat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A worm-tailed rodent with long whiskers and beady eyes.  The way it squeaks "
"makes it sound… hungry."
msgstr ""
"Un roedor de cola de gusano con largos bigotes y ojos brillantes. La forma "
"en que chirría hace que suene... hambriento."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "lamb"
msgid_plural "lambs"
msgstr[0] "cordero"
msgstr[1] "corderos"
msgstr[2] "corderos"

#. ~ Description of monster "lamb"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever "
"domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool."
msgstr ""
"Es un mamífero de pastoreo herrado tímido, y uno de los primeros animales en"
" haber sido domesticado. Su cuerpo está cubierto de una capa gruesa de lana."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "sheep"
msgid_plural "sheep"
msgstr[0] "oveja"
msgstr[1] "ovejas"
msgstr[2] "ovejas"

#. ~ Description of monster "sheep"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A timid, hooved grazing mammal, and one of the first animals ever "
"domesticated.  Its body is covered in a thick layer of wool, and the males "
"have long, spiraling horns."
msgstr ""
"Un tímido mamífero de pastoreo con pezuñas, y uno de los primeros animales "
"domesticados. Su cuerpo está cubierto de una gruesa capa de lana, y los "
"machos tienen largos cuernos en espiral."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgctxt "goat"
msgid "kid"
msgid_plural "kids"
msgstr[0] "cabrito"
msgstr[1] "cabritos"
msgstr[2] "cabritos"

#. ~ Description of monster "kid"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything."
"  The young are famously cute and cuddly."
msgstr ""
"Es un mamífero folívoro herrado conocido por trepar y comer casi cualquier "
"cosa. Los más jóvenes son lindos y adorables."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "goat"
msgid_plural "goats"
msgstr[0] "cabra"
msgstr[1] "cabras"
msgstr[2] "cabras"

#. ~ Description of monster "goat"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A hooved browsing mammal known for climbing and eating just about anything."
"  Either gender can have horns."
msgstr ""
"Es un mamífero folívoro herrado conocido por trepar y comer casi cualquier "
"cosa. Cualquiera de los dos géneros puede tener cuernos."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "squirrel"
msgid_plural "squirrels"
msgstr[0] "ardilla"
msgstr[1] "ardillas"
msgstr[2] "ardillas"

#. ~ Description of monster "squirrel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small granivorous rodent with a long bushy tail, often seen darting amid "
"the branches of trees.  A skittish varmint with an expression of unwavering "
"austerity, it is the mortal enemy of cat and dog alike."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño roedor granívoro con una cola larga y tupida, a menudo se la ve "
"corriendo a toda velocidad entre las ramas de los árboles. Una alimaña "
"asustadiza con expresión de austeridad inquebrantable. Es el enemigo mortal "
"de los gatos y los perros."

#. ~ Description of monster "squirrel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A tiny opportunistic rodent with a long bushy tail.  The pine squirrel is "
"clever and cute, and hunted by nearly everything in the woods with a taste "
"for meat."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño roedor oportunista con una cola larga y tupida. La ardilla de "
"pino es linda e inteligente, y es cazada por casi todo lo que anda por el "
"bosque que tenga ganas de comer carne."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "weasel"
msgid_plural "weasels"
msgstr[0] "comadreja"
msgstr[1] "comadrejas"
msgstr[2] "comadrejas"

#. ~ Description of monster "weasel"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"The long-tailed weasel, a small but ubiquitous predator whose range extends "
"across the continent.  It forms its den in small burrows, preferring to "
"occupy the nesting holes of its prey."
msgstr ""
"Es una comadreja de cola larga, es un depredador roedor pequeño pero que "
"está por todas partes del continente. Arma su nido en pequeñas madrigueras, "
"y prefiere ocupar las madrigueras de su presa."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "wolf"
msgid_plural "wolves"
msgstr[0] "lobo"
msgstr[1] "lobos"
msgstr[2] "lobos"

#. ~ Description of monster "wolf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A cunning pack predator, once extinct in the New England area, the wolf was "
"successfully reintroduced and their numbers reached record highs in the "
"decade before the Cataclysm.  Lucky you."
msgstr ""
"Un astuto depredador de manada, una vez extinguido en el área de Nueva "
"Inglaterra, el lobo fue reintroducido con éxito y su número alcanzó niveles "
"récord en la década anterior al Cataclismo. Qué suerte."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "wolf puppy"
msgid_plural "wolf puppies"
msgstr[0] "lobezno"
msgstr[1] "lobeznos"
msgstr[2] "lobeznos"

#. ~ Description of monster "wolf puppy"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"An adorable, defenseless wolf pup that will, in time, grow into a not-so-"
"defenseless and debatably-adorable wolf.  Be careful of its parents, who are"
" sure to be around nearby!"
msgstr ""
"Un cachorrito de lobo adorable e indefenso que, con el tiempo, crecerá en un"
" lobo no tan indefenso y debatíblemente adorable. ¡Ten cuidado con los "
"padres que generalmente andan cerca!"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json data/mods/Tamable_Wildlife/mammal.json
msgid "reindeer"
msgid_plural "reindeer"
msgstr[0] "reno"
msgstr[1] "renos"
msgstr[2] "renos"

#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"Also known as the caribou, this deer is native to North America and parts of"
" Eurasia.  Although usually friendly, they can be aggressive during the "
"autumn and winter mating season as well as when hungry."
msgstr ""
"También conocido como caribú, este ciervo es originario de América del Norte"
" y partes de Eurasia. Aunque suele ser amistoso, puede ser agresivo durante "
"la época de apareamiento en otoño e invierno, así como cuando tiene hambre."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "reindeer fawn"
msgid_plural "reindeer fawns"
msgstr[0] "cervatillo de reno"
msgstr[1] "cervatillos de reno"
msgstr[2] "cervatillos de reno"

#. ~ Description of monster "reindeer fawn"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A juvenile caribou, it is smaller than its adult counterparts, as well as "
"having shorter antlers."
msgstr ""
"Un caribú joven, es más pequeño que sus homólogos adultos, además de tener "
"una cornamenta más corta."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "llama calf"
msgid_plural "llama calfs"
msgstr[0] "ternero de llama"
msgstr[1] "terneros de llama"
msgstr[2] "terneros de llama"

#. ~ Description of monster "llama calf"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A baby llama.  Unlike their parents, the calves tend to be more friendly in "
"demeanor."
msgstr ""
"Una cría de llama. A diferencia de sus padres, las crías suelen tener un "
"comportamiento más amistoso."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid "llama"
msgid_plural "llama"
msgstr[0] "llama"
msgstr[1] "llamas"
msgstr[2] "llamas"

#. ~ Description of monster "llama"
#: data/json/monsters/mammal.json
msgid ""
"A big and wooly herbivore domesticated by the Andean cultures of South "
"America.  Llamas and their kin are distant relatives to camels and are "
"adapted to mountain environments."
msgstr ""
"Un herbívoro grande y lanudo domesticado por las culturas andinas de América"
" del Sur. Las llamas son parientes lejanas de los camellos y están adaptadas"
" a las montañas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
msgid "Marloss zealot"
msgid_plural "Marloss zealots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "Marloss zealot"
#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
msgid ""
"Her eyes lie vacant and spittle foams in her mouth, as she recites from the "
"hymns in rapturous ecstasy."
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos están vacíos y escupe espuma en su boca, mientras recita los himnos"
" en un éxtasis extático."

#. ~ Description of monster "Marloss zealot"
#: data/json/monsters/marloss.json
msgid ""
"His eyes lie vacant and spittle foams in his mouth, as he recites from the "
"hymns in rapturous ecstasy."
msgstr ""
"Sus ojos están vacíos y escupe espuma en su boca, mientras recita los himnos"
" en un éxtasis extático."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid "X-03: 'Spectre' Recon Mech"
msgid_plural "X-03: 'Spectre' Recon Mechs"
msgstr[0] "X-03: Meca de Reconocimiento 'Spectre'"
msgstr[1] "X-03: Mecas de Reconocimiento 'Spectre'"
msgstr[2] "X-03: Mecas de Reconocimiento 'Spectre'"

#. ~ Description of monster "X-03: 'Spectre' Recon Mech"
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo RMES (Recon Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be used in a scout-"
"recon-sniper role, due to its mobility, integrated laser sniper rifle, and "
"suite of optics for target designation and battlefield awareness.  It was "
"not deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a few prototypes in"
" the field.  You may be able to hack it to accept you as its pilot.  Like "
"all mech-suits, it can act as a UPS from its large battery."
msgstr ""
"El Boeing-Daewoo EMR (Exoesqueleto Mecánico de Reconocimiento), una "
"adquisición reciente del ejército de los Estados Unidos, fue diseñado para "
"ser utilizado en una función de explorador-reconocimiento-francotirador, "
"debido a su movilidad y a su rifle de francotirador láser integrado y al "
"conjunto de ópticas para la designación de objetivos y el conocimiento del "
"campo de batalla. No se desplegó antes del impacto del Cataclismo, aunque "
"había algunos prototipos en el campo. Es posible que puedas hackearlo para "
"que te acepte como su piloto. Como todos los trajes meca, puede actuar como "
"un UPS por su gran batería."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mech"
msgid_plural "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mechs"
msgstr[0] "X-02: Mecade Combate 'Grunt'"
msgstr[1] "X-02: Mecas de Combate 'Grunt'"
msgstr[2] "X-02: Mecas de Combate 'Grunt'"

#. ~ Description of monster "X-02: 'Grunt' Combat Mech"
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo CMES (Combat Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be used in a fire "
"support role, due to its fearsome integrated gatling laser.  It was not "
"deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a few prototypes in the"
" field.  You may be able to hack it to accept you as its pilot.  Like all "
"mech-suits, it can act as a UPS from its large battery."
msgstr ""
"El Boeing-Daewoo EMC (Exoesqueleto Mecánico de Combate ), una reciente "
"adquisición del ejército de los EE.UU., fue diseñado para ser utilizado en "
"un papel de apoyo de fuego, debido a su temible láser gatling integrado. No "
"se desplegó antes del impacto del Cataclismo, aunque había algunos "
"prototipos en el campo. Puede que seas capaz de hackearlo para que te acepte"
" como su piloto. Como todos los trajes meca, puede actuar como un UPS por su"
" gran batería."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid "X-01: 'Jack' Lifting Mech"
msgid_plural "X-01: 'Jack' Lifting Mechs"
msgstr[0] "X-01: Meca de Elevación 'Jack'."
msgstr[1] "X-01: Mecas de Elevación 'Jack'."
msgstr[2] "X-01: Mecas de Elevación 'Jack'."

#. ~ Description of monster "X-01: 'Jack' Lifting Mech"
#: data/json/monsters/mechsuits.json data/mods/No_Hope/monsters.json
msgid ""
"The Boeing-Daewoo LMES (Lifting Mechanical Exoskeleton Suit), a recent "
"acquisition by the U.S. military, it was designed to be piloted by an "
"operator to load and unload heavy material, and for limited combat support "
"roles.  It was not deployed before the Cataclysm hit, though there were a "
"few prototypes in the field.  You may be able to hack it to accept you as "
"its pilot.  Like all mech-suits, it can act as a UPS from its large battery."
msgstr ""
"El Boeing-Daewoo EME (Exoesqueleto Mecánico de Elevación), una reciente "
"adquisición del ejército de los EE.UU., fue diseñado para ser pilotado por "
"un operador para cargar y descargar material pesado, y para funciones "
"limitadas de apoyo al combate, no fue desplegado antes del impacto del "
"Cataclismo, aunque había unos pocos prototipos en el campo. Es posible que "
"puedas hackearlo para que te acepte como su piloto. Como todos los trajes "
"meca, puede actuar como un UPS por su gran batería."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "mi-go"
msgid_plural "mi-gos"
msgstr[0] "mi-go"
msgstr[1] "mi-gos"
msgstr[2] "mi-gos"

#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid ""
"An alien creature of uncertain origin.  Its shapeless pink body bears "
"numerous sets of paired appendages of unknown function, and a pair of "
"ribbed, membranous wings which seem to be quite useless.  Its odd, vaguely "
"pyramid-shaped head bristles with numerous wavering antennae, and simply "
"gazing upon the unnatural beast fills you with primordial dread."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura alienígena de origen incierto. Su cuerpo rosa sin forma tiene "
"numerosos conjuntos de apéndices de función desconocida, y un par de alas "
"acanaladas y membranosas que parecen ser bastante inútiles. Su cabeza "
"extraña, vagamente en forma de pirámide, se eriza con numerosas antenas "
"vacilantes, y simplemente mirar a la bestia antinatural te llena de temor "
"primordial."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "mi-go slaver"
msgid_plural "mi-go slavers"
msgstr[0] "esclavo mi-go"
msgstr[1] "esclavos mi-go"
msgstr[2] "esclavos mi-go"

#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go slaver"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid ""
"An alien creature of uncertain origin.  Its shapeless pink body bears "
"numerous sets of paired appendages of unknown function, and a pair of "
"ribbed, membranous wings which seem to be quite useless.  Its odd, vaguely "
"pyramid-shaped head bristles with numerous wavering antennae, and simply "
"gazing upon the unnatural beast fills you with primordial dread.  It is "
"carrying an oblong object that hums with an odd keening sound."
msgstr ""
"Esta es una criatura alienígena de origen incierto. Su cuerpo rosa sin forma"
" tiene numerosos conjuntos de apéndices de función desconocida, y un par de "
"alas acanaladas y membranosas que parecen ser bastante inútiles. Su cabeza "
"extraña, vagamente en forma de pirámide, se eriza con numerosas antenas "
"vacilantes, y simplemente mirar a la bestia antinatural te llena de temor "
"primordial. Lleva un objeto oblongo que zumba con un extraño sonido agudo."

#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go slaver"
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go guard"
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "mi-go myrmidon"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "The mi-go's numerous antennae sync their movements for a brief moment."
msgstr ""
"Las numerosas antenas del mi-go sincronizan sus movimientos durante un breve"
" momento."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "mi-go surgeon"
msgid_plural "mi-go surgeons"
msgstr[0] "cirujano mi-go"
msgstr[1] "cirujanos mi-go"
msgstr[2] "cirujanos mi-go"

#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go surgeon"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid ""
"This mi-go has a slender body with snaking carapace along it, and even more "
"paired clawed appendages.  Its claws are smaller and more delicate looking, "
"but that does not make them less unnerving."
msgstr ""
"Este mi-go tiene un cuerpo delgado con un caparazón serpenteante a lo largo "
"de él, e incluso más apéndices con garras emparejadas. Sus garras son más "
"pequeñas y de aspecto más delicado, pero eso no las hace menos inquietantes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "mi-go guard"
msgid_plural "mi-go guards"
msgstr[0] "guardia mi-go"
msgstr[1] "guardias mi-go"
msgstr[2] "guardias mi-go"

#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go guard"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid ""
"A more heavily armored version of the common mi-go.  Its trunk is a "
"shapeless mass of strange flesh encased in an iridescent carapace, from "
"which sprout several appendages terminating in what appear to be devices of "
"some sort.  Its pyramidal head is encrusted in barnacle-like armor, aside "
"from the bristling antennae that serve as its - you assume - sensory devices"
" and mouth."
msgstr ""
"Una versión más blindada del mi-go común. Su tronco es una masa informe de "
"carne extraña envuelta en un caparazón iridiscente, del que brotan varios "
"apéndices que terminan en lo que parecen ser dispositivos de algún tipo. Su "
"cabeza piramidal está incrustada en una armadura parecida a la de los "
"percebes, aparte de las antenas erizadas que le sirven,supones, como "
"dispositivos sensoriales y boca."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "mi-go myrmidon"
msgid_plural "mi-go myrmidons"
msgstr[0] "mirmidón mi-go"
msgstr[1] "mirmidones mi-go"
msgstr[2] "mirmidones mi-go"

#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go myrmidon"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid ""
"This creature resembles the smaller mi-go like a grizzly bear resembles a "
"human.  Its enormous, thick body is covered in an iridescent segmented "
"carapace, like a scarab crossed with an isopod.  It boasts several pairs of "
"deadly looking claws and other appendages, and it moves with a strange, slow"
" grace, like an otherworldly dancer.  It appears to be carrying weaponry."
msgstr ""
"Esta criatura se asemeja al mi-go más pequeño como un oso pardo se asemeja a"
" un humano. Su enorme y grueso cuerpo está cubierto por un caparazón "
"segmentado iridiscente, como un escarabajo cruzado con un isópodo. Presume "
"de tener varios pares de garras de aspecto mortal y otros apéndices, y se "
"mueve con una gracia extraña y lenta, como un bailarín de otro mundo. Parece"
" llevar armas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "partially harvested mi-go"
msgid_plural "partially harvested mi-gos"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "partially harvested mi-go"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid ""
"This creature resembles the smaller mi-go like a grizzly bear resembles a "
"human.  Its enormous, thick body is covered in an iridescent segmented "
"carapace, like a scarab crossed with an isopod.  It has been mostly pulled "
"apart and is stuck to a surgical table that seems to be keeping it alive."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "mi-go scout"
msgid_plural "mi-go scouts"
msgstr[0] "explorador mi-go"
msgstr[1] "exploradores mi-go"
msgstr[2] "exploradores mi-go"

#. ~ Description of monster "mi-go scout"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid ""
"This slender mi-go is a little smaller than most others of its kind.  It has"
" a weird, oblong thing attached to the center of its body with some sort of "
"a diaphragm or a membrane on the end.  The thing seems like an integral part"
" of the mi-go's body, and all its appendages are supporting it to prevent "
"swaying."
msgstr ""
"Este delgado mi-go es un poco más pequeño que la mayoría de los otros de su "
"clase. Tiene una extraña cosa oblonga unida al centro de su cuerpo con una "
"especie de diafragma o membrana en el extremo. La cosa parece ser una parte "
"integral del cuerpo mi-go, y todos sus apéndices lo sostienen para evitar el"
" balanceo."

#. ~ Description of special attack of monster "mi-go scout"
#: data/json/monsters/mi-go.json
msgid "The mi-go scout fires its weapon!"
msgstr "¡El explorador mi-go dispara su arma!"

