"A collection of pipes and frames for supporting a bike or other small "
"vehicle and carrying it on your vehicle.  Move a single tile wide vehicle so"
" that all of that vehicle's tiles are next to bike racks, and then 'e'xamine"
" any bike rack to mount that vehicle onto the bike rack.  'e'xamine the bike"
" rack to unmount the carried vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de tubos y marcos para sostener una bicicleta u otro vehículo "
"pequeño y llevarlo en su vehículo. Mueve un vehículo de un solo azulejo de "
"ancho para que todos los azulejos de ese vehículo estén al lado de los "
"soportes para bicicletas, y luego 'e'xamina cualquier soporte para "
"bicicletas para montar ese vehículo en el soporte para bicicletas. Examina "
"el portabicicletas para desmontar el vehículo transportado."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "mounted spare tire"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/cargo.json
msgid "Spare tire stored on an external carrier rig."
msgstr ""
"La rueda de repuesto está guardada en una plataforma de transporte externa."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid "A combustion engine.  Burns fuel from a tank in the vehicle."
msgstr "Es un motor de combustión. Quema combustible del tanque del vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A combustion engine for use on aircraft.  Burns gasoline or avgas fuel from "
"a tank in the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de combustión para uso en aviones. Quema combustible de gasolina o "
"avgas de un tanque en el vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A combustion engine.  Burns diesel fuel from a tank in the vehicle.  Can "
"also burn biodiesel or kerosene, though somewhat less efficiently."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de combustión. Quema combustible diesel de un tanque en el "
"vehículo. También puede quemar biodiesel o aceite para lámparas, aunque de "
"forma algo menos eficiente."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid "A combustion engine.  Burns gasoline fuel from a tank in the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de combustión. Quema combustible de gasolina de un tanque en el "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"An advanced combustion engine.  Burns gasoline or diesel or aviation fuel "
"from a tank in the vehicle.  Can also burn kerosene, though somewhat less "
"efficiently.  Better power-to-weight ratio than a traditional engine, but "
"consumes more fuel."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de combustión avanzada. Quema gasolina, diésel o combustible de "
"aviación de un depósito del vehículo. También puede quemar aceite para "
"lámparas, aunque con algo menos de eficacia. La relación potencia-peso es "
"mejor que la de un motor tradicional, pero consume más combustible."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "diesel_engine_i6"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"An inline 6-cylinder diesel engine.  Somewhat more powerful but much larger "
"than a V6, you might see an engine like this in a road roller or excavator."
msgstr ""
"Un motor diésel de 6 cilindros en línea. Algo más potente pero mucho mas "
"grande que un V6, podrías encontrar un motor como este en una apisonadora o "
"una excavadora."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "diesel_engine_inline4"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A four-cylinder diesel engine, commonly found in small passenger cars and "
"light trucks."
msgstr ""
"Un motor diésel de cuatro cilindros, que se encuentra habitualmente en "
"pequeños turismos y camiones ligeros."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "diesel_engine_v6"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A powerful 6-cylinder diesel engine, typical of a bus, RV, large van, or "
"armored personnel carrier."
msgstr ""
"Un potente motor diésel de 6 cilindros, típico de un autobús, un vehículo "
"recreativo, una furgoneta grande o un vehículo blindado de transporte de "
"personal."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "diesel_engine_v8"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A large 8-cylinder diesel engine, powerful enough for a semi truck, armored "
"car, or Humvee."
msgstr ""
"Un gran motor diésel de 8 cilindros, suficientemente potente para un "
"semirremolque, un coche blindado o un Humvee."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_1cyl"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A small 1-cylinder gasoline engine delivering around 10 horsepower, enough "
"for a scooter or motorized bicycle."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño motor de gasolina de 1 cilindro que ofrece unos 10 caballos de "
"potencia, suficiente para un scooter o una bicicleta motorizada."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_1cyl_large"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A hefty 1-cylinder gasoline engine of about 55 horsepower, normally found in"
" a motocross or dirt bike."
msgstr ""
"Un potente motor de gasolina de 1 cilindro de unos 55 caballos, que "
"normalmente se encuentra en una moto de cross o de tierra."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_1cyl_small"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A small 1-cylinder gasoline engine with only a few horsepower, suitable for "
"a push lawn mower."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño motor de gasolina de 1 cilindro con pocos caballos de potencia, "
"adecuado para un cortacésped de empuje."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_inline4"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A four-cylinder gasoline engine, commonly found in small passenger cars and "
"light trucks."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de gasolina de cuatro cilindros, que se encuentra habitualmente en "
"pequeños turismos y camiones ligeros."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_v12"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A massive 12-cylinder gasoline engine, with the kind of power you might need"
" in a sports car."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme motor de gasolina de 12 cilindros, con el tipo de potencia que "
"podría necesitar un coche deportivo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "diesel_engine_v12"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid "A massive 12-cylinder diesel engine, typical of a heavy cargo truck."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme motor diesel de 12 cilindros, típico de un camión de carga pesado."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_v6"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A powerful 6-cylinder gasoline engine strong enough for a pickup truck, SUV,"
" or full-size van."
msgstr ""
"Un potente motor de gasolina de 6 cilindros lo suficientemente fuerte para "
"una camioneta, un SUV o una furgoneta de tamaño completo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_v8"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty 8-cylinder gasoline engine, like you might find in a fire "
"truck, ambulance, or tow truck."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de gasolina de 8 cilindros para trabajos pesados, como el que "
"podrías encontrar en un camión de bomberos, una ambulancia o una grúa."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_vtwin"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A 2-cylinder gasoline engine appropriate for a motorcycle or quad bike."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de gasolina de 2 cilindros apropiado para una motocicleta o un "
"quad."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A closed cycle, external combustion steam engine.  Burns coal or charcoal "
"from a bunker in the vehicle to produce steam."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de vapor de combustión externa, con ciclo cerrado. Quema carbón o "
"carbón vegetal de la carbonera del vehículo para producir vapor."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_turbine_small"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A small but powerful gas turbine engine, suitable for powering a small one "
"or two-seat helicopter."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño pero potente motor de turbina de gas, adecuado para propulsar un "
"pequeño helicóptero de una o dos plazas."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_turbine_medium"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty gas turbine engine, like those typically found in a Medevac, "
"Apache, or Blackhawk helicopter."
msgstr ""
"Un motor de turbina de gas de gran potencia, como los que suelen tener los "
"helicópteros Medevac, Apache o Blackhawk."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "engine_turbine_large"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/combustion.json
msgid ""
"A huge gas turbine engine, used to lift large military helicopters such as "
"the V-22 Osprey."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme motor de turbina de gas, utilizado para elevar grandes "
"helicópteros militares como el V-22 Osprey."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "door"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A door.  Has a window so you can see out of it, even when closed."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta. Tiene una ventana para que puedas ver por ella, incluso cuando "
"está cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "cloth flap door"
msgstr "puerta de solapa de tela"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "cloth flap door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid ""
"A cloth sheet that can be fastened into a closed position to act as a door."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de tela que puede fijarse en una posición cerrada para que actúe "
"como puerta."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "cloth curtain door"
msgstr "puerta de cortina de tela"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "cloth curtain door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid ""
"A cloth sheet that can be slid into a closed position to act as a door."
msgstr ""
"Una lámina de tela que puede deslizarse en posición cerrada para actuar como"
" puerta."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "opaque door"
msgstr "puerta opaca"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "opaque door"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "opaque wooden door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al otro lado cuando "
"está cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "heavy-duty door"
msgstr "puerta reforzada"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid ""
"A strong door.  Has a window so you can see out of it, even when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta resistente. Tiene una ventana para poder ver para afuera "
"aunque esté cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "heavy-duty opaque door"
msgstr "puerta opaca reforzada"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty opaque door"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "opaque hatch"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "shutter door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A strong door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when "
"closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta resistente. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al otro "
"lado cuando está cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "internal door"
msgstr "puerta interna"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "internal door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid ""
"An interior door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when "
"closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta interior. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al otro "
"lado cuando está cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "hatch"
msgstr "escotilla"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "hatch"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "A strong door.  A window lets you see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta resistente. Una ventana te permite ver al otro lado cuando "
"está cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "opaque hatch"
msgstr "escotilla opaca"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "heavy-duty hatch"
msgstr "escotilla reforzada"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty hatch"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "A very strong door.  A window lets you see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta muy resistente. Una ventana te permite ver al otro lado cuando"
" está cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid "heavy-duty opaque hatch"
msgstr "puerta opaca reforzada"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty opaque hatch"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/doors.json
msgid ""
"A very strong door.  Solid construction means you can't see through it when "
"closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta muy resistente. Su construcción sólida no te permite ver al "
"otro lado cuando está cerrada."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid "suspending for butchering"
msgid_plural "suspending for butchering"
msgstr[0] "colgar para descuartizar"
msgstr[1] "colgar para descuartizar"
msgstr[2] "colgar para descuartizar"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid "boom crane"
msgstr "brazo de grúa"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "boom crane"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid ""
"A rigid steel boom crane.  If it is in your line of sight and within two "
"tiles of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to "
"jack up the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy "
"component like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must"
" have line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of"
" it."
msgstr ""
"Una grúa rígida de acero. Si está a la vista y a menos de dos espacios de "
"otro vehículo, automáticamente la vas a usar cuando quieras levantar un auto"
" para cambiarle las ruedas. Para usarlo para levantar algún componente "
"pesado como el motor que estás instalando o sacando, la grúa tiene que estar"
" en la línea de visión del lugar a donde va, y dentro de cuatro espacios de "
"distancia."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid "internal boom crane"
msgstr "brazo interno de grúa"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid "telescopic crane"
msgstr "grúa telescópica"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "telescopic crane"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid ""
"An extendable cantilever crane.  If it is in your line of sight and within "
"two tiles of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to"
" jack up the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy "
"component like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must"
" have line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of"
" it."
msgstr ""
"Una grúa en voladizo extensible. Si se encuentra en tu línea de visión y "
"dentro de dos espacios de otro vehículo, la usarás automáticamente cuando "
"quieras levantar el otro vehículo para cambiar sus ruedas. Para usarla para "
"levantar un componente pesado como un motor que está instalando o quitando, "
"la grúa debe tener línea de visión hacia donde va y debe estar dentro de "
"cuatro espacios de ella."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "pallet lifter"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid ""
"A small pallet lifter.  If it is in your line of sight and within two tiles "
"of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to jack up "
"the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy component"
" like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must have "
"line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of it."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño elevador de palets. Si se encuentra en tu línea de visión y "
"dentro de dos espacios de otro vehículo, lo usarás automáticamente cuando "
"quiera levantar el otro vehículo para cambiar sus ruedas. Para usarlo para "
"levantar un componente pesado como un motor que estes instalando o quitando,"
" la grúa debe tener línea de visión hacia donde va y debe estar dentro de "
"cuatro espacios de ella."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid "forklift arm"
msgstr "brazo de montacargas"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "forklift arm"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid ""
"A pair of forklift arms.  If it is in your line of sight and within two "
"tiles of another vehicle, you will automatically use it when you want to "
"jack up the other vehicle to change its wheels.  To use it to lift a heavy "
"component like an engine that you are installing or removing, the crane must"
" have line of sight to where it is going and it must be within four tiles of"
" it."
msgstr ""
"Un par de brazos de montacargas. Si está en su línea de visión y dentro de "
"dos espacios de otro vehículo, lo usará automáticamente cuando quiera "
"levantar el otro vehículo para cambiar sus ruedas. Para usarlo para levantar"
" un componente pesado como un motor que estás instalando o quitando, la grúa"
" debe tener línea de visión hacia donde va y debe estar dentro de cuatro "
"espacios de ella."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "rockwheel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid ""
"A large metal disc, powered by the vehicle's engines.  Use the vehicle "
"controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it will stop the vehicle "
"unless it has a strong engine.  When turned on, it will dig a shallow pit in"
" dirt.  Mount it on the edge of your vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un gran disco de metal, impulsado por los motores del vehículo. Utiliza los "
"controles del vehículo para encenderlo o apagarlo. Cuando se enciende, "
"detendrá el vehículo a menos que tenga un motor fuerte. Cuando se enciende, "
"cavará un hoyo poco profundo en la tierra. Móntelo en el borde del vehículo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid "air jack system"
msgstr "sistema de gato neumático"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "motorcycle kickstand"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/engineering.json
msgid ""
"A kickstand to keep the bike from falling over.  You could use this to lean "
"it forward or backward to change a tire."
msgstr ""
"Un soporte para evitar que la moto se caiga. Puedes usar esto para "
"inclinarla hacia adelante o hacia atrás para cambiar un neumático."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Worn drive belt"
msgstr "Correa de transmisión desgastada"

#. ~ Description of fault "Worn drive belt"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Required for operation of an attached alternator."
msgstr "Se necesita para operar un alternador unido."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Worn drive belt"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Replace worn drive belt"
msgstr "Reemplazar la correa de transmisión desgastada"

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Worn drive belt" to fault "Replace
#. worn drive belt"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You replace the worn drive belt of the %s."
msgstr "Reemplazas la correa de transmisión desgastada de la %s."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Faulty glow plugs"
msgstr "Bujías defectuosas"

#. ~ Description of fault "Faulty glow plugs"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Help when starting an engine in low ambient temperatures."
msgstr "Ayuda a arrancar un motor con bajas temperaturas ambientales."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Faulty glow plugs"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Replace faulty glow plugs"
msgstr "Reemplazar las bujías defectuosas"

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Faulty glow plugs" to fault "Replace
#. faulty glow plugs"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You replace the faulty glow plugs of the %s."
msgstr "Reemplazas las bujías defectuosas del %s."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Active immobiliser"
msgstr "Activar el inmovilizador"

#. ~ Description of fault "Active immobiliser"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Prevents starting of the vehicle without the appropriate key."
msgstr "Evita arrancar un vehículo sin la llave apropiada."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Active immobiliser"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Deactivate immobiliser"
msgstr "Desactivar el inmovilizador"

#. ~ Description of mending method "Active immobiliser" to fault "Deactivate
#. immobiliser"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid ""
"Deactivate the immobiliser that is preventing the vehicle from starting."
msgstr "Desactivar el inmovilizador que impide que el vehículo arranque."

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Active immobiliser" to fault
#. "Deactivate immobiliser"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You successfully deactivate the immobiliser of the %s."
msgstr "Desactivaste con éxito el inmovilizador de la%s."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Faulty diesel pump"
msgstr "Bomba de diesel defectuosa"

#. ~ Description of fault "Faulty diesel pump"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Required to pump and pressurize diesel from a vehicles tank."
msgstr ""
"Se necesita para bombear y presurizar combustible diésel desde el tanque del"
" vehículo."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Faulty diesel pump"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Replace faulty diesel pump"
msgstr "Reemplazar la bomba de diesel defectuosa"

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Faulty diesel pump" to fault "Replace
#. faulty diesel pump"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You replace the faulty diesel pump of the %s."
msgstr "Reemplazas la bomba diesel defectuosa de %s."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Expired air filter"
msgstr "Filtro de aire expirado"

#. ~ Description of fault "Expired air filter"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid ""
"An expired filter reduces fuel efficiency and increases smoke production."
msgstr ""
"Un filtro gastado reduce la eficiencia de combustible y aumenta la "
"generación de humo."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Expired air filter"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Replace expired air filter"
msgstr "Reemplazar el filtro de aire expirado"

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Expired air filter" to fault "Replace
#. expired air filter"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You replace the expired air filter of the %s."
msgstr "Reemplazas el filtro de aire expirado del %s."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Expired fuel filter"
msgstr "Filtro de combustible caducado"

#. ~ Description of fault "Expired fuel filter"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid ""
"An expired filter reduces performance and increases the chance of backfires."
msgstr ""
"Un filtro gastado reduce la performance y aumenta la probabilidad de las "
"detonaciones en el escape."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Expired fuel filter"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Replace expired fuel filter"
msgstr "Reemplazar el filtro de combustible vencido"

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Expired fuel filter" to fault "Replace
#. expired fuel filter"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You replace the expired fuel filter of the %s."
msgstr "Reemplazas el filtro de combustible vencido del %s."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Faulty fuel pump"
msgstr "Bomba de combustible defectuosa"

#. ~ Description of fault "Faulty fuel pump"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Required to pump gasoline from a vehicles tank."
msgstr "Se necesita para bombear gasolina desde el tanque del vehículo."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Faulty fuel pump"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Replace faulty fuel pump"
msgstr "Reemplazar la bomba de combustible defectuosa"

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Faulty fuel pump" to fault "Replace
#. faulty fuel pump"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You replace the faulty fuel pump of the %s."
msgstr "Reemplaza la bomba de combustible defectuosa de la %s."

#. ~ Name of a fault
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Faulty starter motor"
msgstr "Motor de arranque defectuoso"

#. ~ Description of fault "Faulty starter motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Required to initially start the engine."
msgstr "Se necesita para iniciar el motor."

#. ~ Name of mending method to fault "Faulty starter motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
msgid "Replace faulty starter motor"
msgstr "Reemplazar el motor de arranque defectuoso"

#. ~ Success message of mending method "Faulty starter motor" to fault
#. "Replace faulty starter motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/faults.json
#, c-format
msgid "You replace the faulty starter motor of %s."
msgstr "Reemplaza el motor de arranque defectuoso de %s."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "foldable light frame"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "foldable orichalcum frame"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid ""
"A light metal framework, designed to fold.  Other vehicle components can be "
"mounted on it.  If all the frames and components of a vehicle are foldable, "
"the vehicle can be folding into a small package and picked up as a normal "
"item."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis de metal ligero, diseñado para doblarse. Otros componentes del "
"vehículo pueden ser montados en él. Si todos los chasis y componentes de un "
"vehículo son plegables, el vehículo puede ser plegado en un pequeño paquete "
"y recogido como un artículo normal."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "foldable wooden frame"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid ""
"A light wooden framework, designed to fold.  Other vehicle components can be"
" mounted on it.  If all the frames and components of a vehicle are foldable,"
" the vehicle can be folding into a small package and picked up as a normal "
"item."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis de madera ligera, diseñada para doblarse. Otros componentes del "
"vehículo pueden ser montados en él. Si todos los chasis y componentes de un "
"vehículo son plegables, el vehículo puede ser plegado en un pequeño paquete "
"y recogido como un artículo normal."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid "frame"
msgstr "chasis"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "frame"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid ""
"A metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and it "
"can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis de metal. Otros componentes de vehículo pueden ser montado sobre "
"ello, y puede ser unido a otros chasis para incrementar el tamaño de un "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden frame"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid ""
"A wooden framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and it "
"can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  Wood and "
"nail construction means it can be constructed and added to the vehicle "
"without welding tools."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis de madera. Otros componentes de vehículo pueden ser montado sobre "
"ello, y puede ser unido a otros chasis para incrementar el tamaño de un "
"vehículo. La construcción de madera y clavos significa que puede ser "
"construida y añadida al vehículo sin herramientas de soldadura."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "light wooden frame"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid ""
"A light wooden framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, "
"and it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  Wood"
" and rope constructions means it can be constructed and added to the vehicle"
" without welding tools or nails."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis de madera ligera. Otros componentes de vehículo pueden ser montado"
" sobre ello, y puede ser unido a otros chasis para incrementar el tamaño de "
"un vehículo. Las construcciones de madera y soga permiten construirlo y "
"añadirlo a un vehículo sin herramientas de soldadura ni clavos."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty frame"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid ""
"A heavy metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and"
" it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size.  "
"Increased mass makes it more resistant to damage in collisions."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis de metal pesado. Otros componentes de vehículo pueden ser montado "
"sobre ello, y puede ser unido a otros chasis para incrementar el tamaño de "
"un vehículo. Al incrementar la masa se vuelve más resistente al daño durante"
" las colisiones."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid "extra light frame"
msgstr "chasis extra-ligero"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "extra light frame"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "foldable extra light frame"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid ""
"A light metal framework.  Other vehicle components can be mounted on it, and"
" it can be attached to other frames to increase the vehicle's size."
msgstr ""
"Un chasis ligera de metal. Otros componentes de vehículo pueden ser montado "
"sobre ello, y puede ser unido a otros chasis para incrementar el tamaño de "
"un vehículo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/frames.json
msgid "foldable extra light frame"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "aisle lights"
msgstr "luces de espacio lateral"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "atomic lamp"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A bright light, self-powered by an atomic decay reaction that never stops.  "
"When turned on, it illuminates several squares inside the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Es una luz brillante, autoalimentada por una reacción atómica radiactiva que"
" nunca para. Cuando está encendida, ilumina varios espacios adentro del "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "atomic nightlight"
msgstr "luz de noche atómica"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "atomic nightlight"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A very dim light, self-powered by an atomic decay reaction that never stops."
"  When turned on, it illuminates a single square inside the vehicle that "
"isn't suitable for crafting."
msgstr ""
"Una luz muy tenue, autoalimentada por una reacción de descomposición atómica"
" que nunca se detiene. Cuando se enciende, ilumina un solo cuadrado en el "
"interior del vehículo que no es adecuado para la fabricación."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "floodlight"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A very bright, circular light that illuminates the area outside the vehicle "
"when turned on."
msgstr ""
"Una luz circular muy brillante que ilumina el área exterior del vehículo "
"cuando se enciende."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "directed floodlight"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A very bright, directed light that illuminates a half-circular area outside "
"the vehicle when turned on.  During installation, you can choose what "
"direction to point the light."
msgstr ""
"Una luz muy brillante y dirigida que ilumina un área semicircular fuera del "
"vehículo cuando se enciende. Durante la instalación, puedes elegir la "
"dirección en la que apuntar la luz."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "headlight"
msgstr "luz delantera"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "headlight"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A bright light that illuminates a narrow cone outside the vehicle when "
"turned on.  During installation, you can choose what direction to point the "
"light, so multiple headlights can illuminate the sides or rear, as well as "
"the front."
msgstr ""
"Una luz brillante que ilumina un cono estrecho fuera del vehículo cuando se "
"enciende. Durante la instalación, puede elegir la dirección a la que apuntar"
" la luz, de modo que varios faros pueden iluminar los laterales o la parte "
"trasera, así como la parte delantera."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "motorcycle headlight"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A small, lightweight, bright light that illuminates a narrow cone outside "
"the vehicle when turned on.  During installation, you can choose what "
"direction to point the light, so multiple headlights can illuminate the "
"sides or rear, as well as the front."
msgstr ""
"Una luz pequeña, ligera y brillante que ilumina un cono estrecho fuera del "
"vehículo cuando se enciende. Durante la instalación, se puede elegir la "
"dirección hacia la que se dirige la luz, de modo que varios faros pueden "
"iluminar los laterales o la parte trasera, así como la parte delantera."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "wide angle headlight"
msgstr "faro de ángulo ancho"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wide angle headlight"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"A bright light that illuminates a wide cone outside the vehicle when turned "
"on.  During installation, you can choose what direction to point the light, "
"so multiple headlights can illuminate the sides or rear, as well as the "
"front."
msgstr ""
"Una luz brillante que ilumina un amplio cono fuera del vehículo cuando se "
"enciende. Durante la instalación, puede elegir la dirección en la que "
"apuntar la luz, de modo que varios faros pueden iluminar los laterales o la "
"parte trasera, así como la parte delantera."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid ""
"Emergency lights, like a police car's or ambulance's, mounted on the "
"vehicle's roof.  Flashes between red and blue when turned on, attracting "
"attention without illuminating the area."
msgstr ""
"Son luces de emergencia, como las de una patrulla o una ambulancia, puestas "
"en el techo del vehículo. Destellan entre el rojo y el azul cuando están "
"encendidas, atrayendo la atención sin iluminar el área."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "blue light"
msgstr "luz azul"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/lights.json
msgid "red light"
msgstr "luz roja"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid "foot pedals"
msgstr "pedales de pie"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "foot pedals"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid ""
"A set of bicycle style foot pedals.  If mounted on the same tile as seat, "
"they allow you to move the vehicle at the cost of your stamina."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de pedales como los de una bicicleta. Si están puestos en el "
"mismo espacio que un asiento, te permitirán mover el vehículo con tu vigor."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid "hand rims"
msgstr "aros de ruedas"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "hand rims"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/manual.json
msgid ""
"A set of wheelchair style wheels.  If mounted on the same tile as seat, they"
" allow you to move the vehicle at the cost of your stamina."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de ruedas como los de una silla de rueda. Si están puestos en el"
" mismo espacio que un asiento, te permitirán mover el vehículo con tu vigor."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid "wing mirror"
msgstr "espejo lateral"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wing mirror"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid ""
"A small mirror, mounted outside the vehicle.  If you see the mirror, your "
"vision is expanded as though you were standing where the mirror is."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño Un pequeño espejo, montado fuera del vehículo. Si ves el espejo, "
"tu visión se expande como si estuvieras parado donde está el espejo.espejo, "
"montado fuera del vehículo. Si ves el espejo, tu visión se expande como si "
"estuvieras parado donde está el espejo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid "inboard mirror"
msgstr "espejo retrovisor"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "inboard mirror"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/mirrors.json
msgid ""
"A small mirror, mounted inside the vehicle.  If you see the mirror, your "
"vision is expanded as though you were standing where the mirror is."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño espejo, montado dentro del vehículo. Si ves el espejo, tu visión "
"se expande como si estuvieras parado donde está el espejo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "electric motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid "An electric motor."
msgstr "Un motor eléctrico."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "tiny electric motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"An electric motor too small for most vehicles, but just right for powering a"
" bicycle."
msgstr ""
"Un motor eléctrico demasiado pequeño para la mayoría de los vehículos, pero "
"justo para impulsar una bicicleta."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "small electric motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"A light-duty electrical motor, strong enough for an electric bicycle or "
"scooter, but probably not practical for heavier vehicles."
msgstr ""
"Un motor eléctrico ligero, lo suficientemente potente para una bicicleta o "
"un scooter eléctrico, pero probablemente no sea práctico para vehículos más "
"pesados."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "electric motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"A medium-duty electrical motor, suitable for powering ultra-light vehicles, "
"or as part of a hybrid gas-electric drivetrain."
msgstr ""
"Un motor eléctrico de potencia media, adecuado para impulsar vehículos "
"ultraligeros, o como parte de un tren de transmisión híbrido gas-eléctrico."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "large electric motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty electrical motor, capable of propelling a full-size car or SUV "
"through electric power alone, provided you have the battery capacity."
msgstr ""
"Un motor eléctrico de gran potencia, capaz de propulsar un coche o un "
"todoterreno de tamaño normal sólo con energía eléctrica, siempre que se "
"disponga de la capacidad de la batería."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "enhanced electric motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"A powerful high-performance electric motor, as found in those consumer "
"electric sports cars with ridiculous, ludicrous, or similarly hyperbolic "
"acceleration options.  It needs a lot of battery power."
msgstr ""
"Un potente motor eléctrico de alto rendimiento, como el que se encuentra en "
"esos coches deportivos eléctricos de consumo con opciones de aceleración "
"ridículas, lúdicas o igualmente hiperbólicas. Necesita mucha energía de la "
"batería."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "super electric motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"A massive and extremely powerful electric motor, delivering high torque at "
"the cost of significant power drain, this would be well suited to an "
"electric racing car."
msgstr ""
"Un motor eléctrico gigante y extremadamente potente, que ofrece un alto par "
"motor a costa de una importante pérdida de potencia, sería muy adecuado para"
" un coche de carreras eléctrico."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "1,300 HP electric train engine"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/motor.json
msgid ""
"An enormous and heavy electric traction motor, powerful enough to pull a "
"train."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme y pesado motor de tracción eléctrica, lo suficientemente potente "
"como para tirar de un tren."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/obsolete.json
msgid "tracking device"
msgstr "dispositivo de rastreo"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "tracking device"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/obsolete.json
msgid "A small transmitter that lets you locate the vehicle on the map."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño transmisor que te permite localizar vehículos en el mapa."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid ""
"A reinforced ram.  Place at the edge of vehicle to reduce damage taken in "
"collisions, and to increase damaged delivered in collisions, if the ram is "
"the first vehicle part to collide."
msgstr ""
"Un ariete reforzado. Colócalo en el borde del vehículo para reducir el daño "
"recibido durante las colisiones, y para incrementar el daño causado, si es "
"que el ariete es la primera parte del vehículo que choca."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "superalloy ram"
msgstr "ariete de superaleación"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "heavy steel ram"
msgstr "ariete de acero pesado"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "military composite ram"
msgstr "ariete de compuesto militar"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "spiked ram"
msgstr "ariete con púas"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "steel ram"
msgstr "ariete de acero"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "wooden ram"
msgstr "ariete de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "chitin ram"
msgstr "ariete de quitina"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "biosilicified chitin ram"
msgstr "Quitina biosilicificada de carnero"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid "tied mattress"
msgstr "colchón atado"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "tied mattress"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid ""
"A mattress, strapped onto the vehicle.  It could serve to blunt any impact."
msgstr ""
"Un colchón, atado al vehículo. Podría servir para amortiguar cualquier "
"impacto."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "shredder"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rams.json
msgid ""
"A circular blade, powered by the vehicle's engine.  It will dramatically "
"increase the damage the vehicle delivers in collisions.  Mount on the edges "
"of the vehicle, preferably the front."
msgstr ""
"Una cuchilla circular, accionada por el motor del vehículo. Aumentará "
"dramáticamente el daño que el vehículo produce en las colisiones. Se monta "
"en los bordes del vehículo, preferiblemente en la parte delantera."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part ""
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid ""
"A set of aerofoil helicopter rotors, when spun at high speed, they generate "
"thrust via lift."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de rotores de helicóptero aerodinámicos que, al girar a gran "
"velocidad, generan empuje mediante la sustentación."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty military rotors"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "small helicopter rotors"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty military Blackhawk rotors"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid ""
"A set of four military-grade helicopter rotor blades, used to provide lift "
"by rotation."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de cuatro palas de rotor de helicóptero de grado militar, "
"utilizadas para proporcionar elevación por rotación."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "small helicopter rotors"
msgstr "Rotores de helicóptero pequeño"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "heavy-duty military Blackhawk rotors"
msgstr "rotores militares Blackhawk de alta resistencia"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid "heavy-duty military Osprey rotors"
msgstr "rotores Osprey militares de alta resistencia"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty military Osprey rotors"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/rotor.json
msgid ""
"A set of three military-grade helicopter rotor blades, used to provide lift "
"by rotation."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de tres palas de rotor de helicóptero de grado militar, "
"utilizadas para proporcionar elevación por rotación."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "seat"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "A place to sit, or sleep if you're desperate."
msgstr "Un lugar para sentarse, o para dormir si estás desesperado."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "reclining seat"
msgstr "asiento reclinable"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "reclining seat"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid ""
"A place to sit, and the backrest reclines to make it an uncomfortable bed."
msgstr ""
"Un lugar para sentarse, cuyo respaldo se reclina para convertirlo en una "
"cama incómoda."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "reclining leather seat"
msgstr "asiento reclinable de cuero"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "back seat"
msgstr "asiento trasero"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "back seat"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid ""
"A benchlike seat.  Mostly found in the second row, also known as the back or"
" rear seat."
msgstr ""
"Un asiento tipo banco. Se encuentra sobre todo en la segunda fila, también "
"conocido como asiento trasero."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "leather back seat"
msgstr "asiento trasero de cuero"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "saddle"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "A padded wedge that you straddle, like a bicycle or motorcycle."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza acolchada a la que se puede montar, como una bicicleta o una "
"motocicleta."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "foldable seat"
msgstr "asiento plegable"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "foldable seat"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "A crude seat, too uncomfortable to sleep in."
msgstr "Es un asiento simple, demasiado incómodo para dormir encima."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid "steel bench"
msgstr "banco de acero"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "steel bench"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/seats.json
msgid ""
"A steel bench with ankle and wrist restraints built in.  It looks very "
"uncomfortable."
msgstr ""
"Un banco de acero con sujeciones para los tobillos y las muñecas. Parece muy"
" incómodo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "vehicle tank (2L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (2L)"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (2L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (10L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (20L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "vehicle tank (60L)"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids.  If filled with the appropriate fuel "
"for the vehicle's engine, the engine will automatically draw fuel from the "
"tank when the engine is on.  If filled with water, you can access the water "
"from a water faucet, if one is installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a"
" rubber hose to siphon liquids out of a tank."
msgstr ""
"Un espacio de almacenamiento para guardar líquidos. Si se llena con el "
"combustible apropiado para el motor del vehículo, el motor extraerá "
"automáticamente el combustible del depósito cuando el motor esté encendido. "
"Si está lleno de agua, puede acceder al agua desde un grifo, si está "
"instalado en el vehículo. También puedes utilizar una manguera de goma para "
"transvasar líquidos fuera del tanque."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "vehicle tank (10L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (10L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "vehicle tank (20L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (20L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "vehicle tank (60L)"
msgstr "tanque de vehículo (60L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "refrigerated tank (60L)"
msgstr "tanque refrigerado (60L)"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "refrigerated tank (60L)"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid ""
"A 60L refrigerated tank.  When turned on, it will cool the liquid inside, "
"extending the time until the food spoils."
msgstr ""
"Un depósito refrigerado de 60L. Al encenderlo, enfriará el líquido de su "
"interior, alargando el tiempo hasta que los alimentos se estropeen."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "heated tank (60L)"
msgstr "tanque calentador (60L)"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heated tank (60L)"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid ""
"A 60L heated tank.  When turned on, it will prevent the contents from "
"freezing."
msgstr ""
"Un tanque calentador de 60L.  Cuando se enciende previene que el contenido "
"se congele."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "external tank (100L)"
msgstr "tanque externo (100L)"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "external tank (100L)"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids, mounted outside the vehicle's walls and"
" armor.  If filled with the appropriate fuel for the vehicle's engine, the "
"engine will automatically draw fuel from the tank when the engine is on.  If"
" filled with water, you can access the water from a water faucet, if one is "
"installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a rubber hose to siphon liquids "
"out of a tank."
msgstr ""
"Un espacio de almacenamiento para guardar líquidos, montado fuera de las "
"muros y el blindaje del vehículo. Si se llena con el combustible apropiado "
"para el motor del vehículo, el motor extraerá automáticamente el combustible"
" del depósito cuando el motor esté encendido. Si está lleno de agua, puede "
"acceder al agua desde un grifo, si está instalado en el vehículo. También "
"puedes utilizar una manguera de goma para transvasar líquidos fuera del "
"tanque"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "roof-mounted external tank (100L)"
msgstr "tanque externo montado en techo (100L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "external tank (200L)"
msgstr "tanque externo (200L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "roof-mounted external tank (200L)"
msgstr "tanque externo de techo (200L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "wooden barrel (100L)"
msgstr "barril de madera (100L)"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden barrel (100L)"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "steel drum (100L)"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid ""
"A storage space for holding liquids, mounted inside the cargo or passenger "
"space.  If filled with the appropriate fuel for the vehicle's engine, the "
"engine will automatically draw fuel from the tank when the engine is on.  If"
" filled with water, you can access the water from a water faucet, if one is "
"installed in the vehicle.  You can also use a rubber hose to siphon liquids "
"out of a tank."
msgstr ""
"Un espacio de almacenamiento para guardar líquidos, montado dentro del "
"espacio de carga o de pasajeros. Si se llena con el combustible apropiado "
"para el motor del vehículo, el motor extraerá automáticamente el combustible"
" del depósito cuando el motor esté encendido. Si está lleno de agua, puede "
"acceder al agua desde un grifo de agua, si hay uno instalado en el vehículo."
" También puede utilizar una manguera de goma para transvasar líquidos fuera "
"del tanque."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "fuel bunker"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "A small tank for pressurized gasses."
msgstr "Un pequeño tanque para gases presurizados."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "small pressurized tank"
msgstr "tanque pequeño presurizado"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "small pressurized tank"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "A tank for pressurized gasses."
msgstr "Un tanque para gases presurizados."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "large pressurized tank"
msgstr "gran tanque presurizado"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "large pressurized tank"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "XL pressurized tank"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "A large tank for pressurized gasses."
msgstr "Un gran tanque para gases presurizados."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "XL pressurized tank"
msgstr "Tanque presurizado XL"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "external aluminum tank (100L)"
msgstr "tanque de aluminio externo (100L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "roof-mounted external aluminum tank (100L)"
msgstr "tanque externo montado en techo (100L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "external aluminum tank (200L)"
msgstr "tanque de aluminio externo (200L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/tanks.json
msgid "roof-mounted external aluminum tank (200L)"
msgstr "tanque externo montado en techo (200L)"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid "kitchen unit"
msgstr "cocina"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "kitchen unit"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid ""
"A small but complete kitchen unit, powered from the vehicle's batteries."
msgstr ""
"Es una unidad de cocina pequeña pero completa, alimentada por las baterías "
"del vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "FOODCO kitchen buddy"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid ""
"A multi-function crafting station, with a water purifier, food dehydrator, "
"vacuum sealer, and hand press for making ammo.  Draws power from the "
"vehicle's batteries.  'e'xamine the tile with the kitchen buddy to access "
"the water faucet or to purify water in a vehicle tank or in a container in "
"your inventory.  If you attempt to craft an item that needs one of the "
"kitchen buddy's functions, it will automatically be selected as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Una estación de fabricación multifuncional, con un purificador de agua, un "
"deshidratador de alimentos, un sellador de vacío y una prensa manual para "
"hacer municiones. 'e'xaminar el espacio con el compañero de cocina para "
"acceder al grifo de agua o para purificar el agua en el tanque de un "
"vehículo o en un contenedor de tu inventario. Si intentas fabricar un objeto"
" que necesite una de las funciones del compañero de cocina, será "
"automáticamente seleccionado como herramienta."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "onboard chemistry lab"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid ""
"A small chemistry station, including a hotplate and electrolysis setup "
"powered by the vehicle's batteries.  'e'xamine the tile with the chemistry "
"lab to access the water faucet or to heat up food with the hotplate.  If you"
" attempt to craft an item that needs one of the chemistry lab's functions, "
"it will automatically be selected as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña estación de química, incluyendo una placa de cocción y un equipo"
" de electrólisis alimentado por las baterías del vehículo. 'e'xaminar el "
"espacio con el laboratorio químico para acceder al grifo del agua o para "
"calentar comida con la placa de cocción. Si intentas fabricar un artículo "
"que necesita una de las funciones del laboratorio de química, será "
"automáticamente seleccionado como una herramienta."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "mounted electric forge"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid ""
"A electric forge for metalworking, powered by the vehicle's batteries.  With"
" a hammer and other tools, you could use this for metalworking.  If you "
"attempt to craft an item that needs a forge, you will be given the option of"
" selecting it as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Una forja eléctrica para trabajar el metal, alimentada por las baterías del "
"vehículo. Con un martillo y otras herramientas, podrías usar esto para "
"trabajar el metal. Si intentas fabricar un artículo que necesite una forja, "
"se te dará la opción de seleccionarlo como herramienta."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "mounted electric kiln"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid ""
"A electric kiln for baking brick or clay, powered by the vehicle's "
"batteries.  You could use this to harden bricks or clay.  If you attempt to "
"craft an item that needs a kiln, you will be given the option of selecting "
"it as a tool."
msgstr ""
"Un horno eléctrico para cocer ladrillos o arcilla, alimentado por las "
"baterías del vehículo. Se puede usar para endurecer ladrillos o arcilla. Si "
"intentas fabricar un artículo que necesite un horno, se te dará la opción de"
" seleccionarlo como herramienta."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "mounted electric oil press"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid "A heavy-duty press used to create vegetable oil from nuts or seeds."
msgstr ""
"Una prensa reforzada utilizada para crear aceite vegetal a partir de frutos "
"secos o semillas."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid "binoculars"
msgstr "binoculares"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "binoculars"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/utilities.json
msgid "Binoculars secured near the seat."
msgstr "Binoculares asegurados cerca del asiento."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "null part"
msgstr "parte no válida"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "yoke and harness"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"Attach this part to a beast of burden to allow it to pull your vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Ata esta parte a una bestia de carga para permitirle tirar de tu vehículo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "cart handle"
msgstr "mango del carro"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "cart handle"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A metal handle, a creature with hands could use it to push a vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un mango de metal, una criatura con manos podría usarlo para empujar un "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "bed"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A small but comfortable bed."
msgstr "Una cama pequeña pero cómoda"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "handle"
msgstr "manivela"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "handle"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden handle"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "light wooden handle"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A pair of handles.  You can mount other items on top of it."
msgstr "Un par de asas. Puedes montar otros objetos encima."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden handle"
msgstr "manivela de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "light wooden handle"
msgstr "manivela ligera de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "aisle"
msgstr "espacio lateral"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "aisle"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden aisle"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "An aisle."
msgstr "Un espacio latera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden aisle"
msgstr "espacio lateral de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "collapsible wooden aisle"
msgstr "pasillo de madera plegable"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "collapsible wooden aisle"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A collapsible aisle."
msgstr "Un pasillo plegable."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "floor trunk"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "An aisle.  A hatch lets you access a cargo space beneath it."
msgstr ""
"Un espacio lateral. Una escotilla te permite acceder a un espacio de carga "
"debajo de ella."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "cloth roof"
msgstr "techo de tela"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "cloth roof"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A cloth roof."
msgstr "Un techo de tela."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "roof"
msgstr "techo"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "roof"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A metal roof."
msgstr "Un techo de metal."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "heavy-duty roof"
msgstr "techo reforzado"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty roof"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A thick metal roof."
msgstr "Es un techo de metal grueso."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "blade"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A blade, welded to the vehicle, for cutting up zombies."
msgstr "Es una cuchilla soldada al vehículo... para cortar zombis."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "spike"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A metal spike, welded to the vehicle, to increase injury when crashing into "
"things."
msgstr ""
"Es una púa de metal soldada al vehículo, para incrementar el daño causado "
"cuando choca contra algo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "programmable autopilot"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A computer system hooked up to the steering and engine of the vehicle to "
"allow it to follow simple paths."
msgstr ""
"Un sistema informático conectado a la dirección y al motor del vehículo para"
" permitirle seguir caminos sencillos."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "swappable storage battery case"
msgstr "caja para batería de alm. cambiable"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "swappable storage battery case"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A battery case for storage batteries.  Allows quick removal or addition of a"
" storage battery, if you can lift the battery."
msgstr ""
"Es una caja para baterías de almacenamiento. Permite sacar o poner "
"rápidamente una batería, si puedes levantar la batería..."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "tool battery mount"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A mount for batteries usually used in handheld tools.  Allows quick removal "
"or addition of such batteries into vehicular power grid."
msgstr ""
"Un soporte para las baterías que suelen utilizarse en las herramientas "
"manuales. Permite retirar o añadir rápidamente dichas baterías a la red "
"eléctrica del vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "military black box"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An armored black box, a device meant to record and preserve data of a "
"military vehicle in the field in case it gets destroyed."
msgstr ""
"Una caja negra blindada, un dispositivo destinado a registrar y preservar "
"los datos de un vehículo militar en el campo en caso de que sea destruido."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "minireactor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small nuclear reactor.  When loaded with plutonium cells and turned on, "
"will generate a lot of electrical power."
msgstr ""
"Es un pequeño reactor nuclear. Cuando está cargado con celdas de plutonio y "
"es encendido, generará mucha energía eléctrica."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "minifridge"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small fridge.  When turned on, it will cool the food inside, extending the"
" time until the food spoils."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña nevera. Cuando está encendida enfriará la comida que contenga, "
"extendiendo el tiempo de duración de los alimentos."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "washing machine"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small washing machine.  With detergent, water, and some electrical power, "
"you could clean a lot of clothes.  'e'xamine the tile with the washing "
"machine to use it."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña lavadora. Con detergente, agua y algo de energía eléctrica, "
"podrías limpiar mucha ropa. e'xamine el azulejo con la lavadora para usarlo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "portable dishwasher"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small dishwasher.  With detergent, water, and some electrical power, you "
"could clean your dishes… or something more useful like a CBM dripping with "
"zombie gore.  'e'xamine the tile with the dishwasher to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño lavavajillas. Con detergente, agua y algo de energía eléctrica, "
"podrías limpiar los platos... ...o algo más útil como un MBC goteando con "
"sangre de zombi. ...e'xamina la posición del lavavajillas para usarlo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "autoclave"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"This is an autoclave.  It's useful for sterilizing things like CBMs.  "
"'e'xamine the tile with the autoclave to use it."
msgstr ""
"Esto es un autoclave. Es útil para esterilizar cosas como los MBC. 'e'xamina"
" el azulejo con el autoclave para usarlo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "trunk"
msgstr "maletero"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "travois"
msgstr "travois"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wood box"
msgstr "caja de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "folding wood box"
msgstr "caja plegable de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wood table"
msgstr "mesa de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "flat-packable table"
msgstr "mesa plana para empaquetable"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden boat hull"
msgstr "casco de madera de bote"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden boat hull"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A wooden board that keeps the water out of your boat."
msgstr "Una tabla de madera que mantiene el agua fuera de tu barco."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "raft boat hull"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "Logs tied together that will keep your boat out of the water."
msgstr "Leños atados que mantendrán tu barco fuera del agua."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "plastic boat hull"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A rigid plastic sheet that keeps water out of your boat."
msgstr "Una lámina de plástico rígido que mantiene el agua fuera del barco."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "metal boat hull"
msgstr "casco de barco de metal"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "metal boat hull"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A metal sheet that keeps the water out of your boat."
msgstr "Una lámina de metal que mantiene el agua fuera de tu barco."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "carbon fiber boat hull"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A light weight, advanced carbon fiber rigid sheet that keeps the water out "
"of your boat."
msgstr ""
"Es una lámina rígida y liviana de fibra de carbono que mantiene el agua "
"fuera de tu bote."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "hand paddles"
msgstr "palas manuales"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "reins and tackle"
msgstr "riendas y aparejos"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "reins and tackle"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A set of leather bindings to control a creature pulling a vehicle, such as a"
" cart."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de ataduras de cuero para controlar a una criatura que tira de "
"un vehículo, como un carro."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "controls"
msgstr "controles"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "controls"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A steering wheel and accelerator and brake pedals."
msgstr "Es un volante y pedales para acelerar y frenar."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "dashboard"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A frame containing some lights and controls."
msgstr "Un chasis que contiene controles y luces."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "vehicle-mounted heater"
msgstr "calentador montado en un vehículo"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "small vehicle-mounted heater"
msgstr "calentador montado en un vehículo pequeño"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "vehicle-mounted cooler"
msgstr "refrigerador montado en un vehículo"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "electronics control unit"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "Some switches and knobs to control the vehicle's electrical systems."
msgstr ""
"Algunos interruptores y botones para controlar los sistemas eléctricos del "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "muffler"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A metal pipe that somewhat reduces engine noise.  Also vents heat from an "
"installed vehicle cooler."
msgstr ""
"Un tubo metálico que reduce en cierta medida el ruido del motor. También "
"ventila el calor de un refrigerador instalado en el vehículo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "seatbelt"
msgstr "cinturón de seguridad"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "seatbelt"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A belt, attached to a seat."
msgstr "Un cinturón, enganchado a un asiento."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "security system"
msgstr "sistema de seguridad"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "security system"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A bunch of electronics that make it difficult to start the vehicle without "
"the proper key, and that will sound an alarm if you try.  The alarm can be "
"disabled."
msgstr ""
"Un montón de electrónica que dificulta el arranque del vehículo sin la llave"
" adecuada, y que hará sonar una alarma si lo intentas. La alarma puede ser "
"desactivada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "smart engine controller"
msgstr "smart engine controller"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "smart engine controller"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
#, c-format
msgid ""
"Electronic module that automatically switches combustion and electric "
"engines on and off minimizing fuel consumption and optimizing power output "
"and battery charge rate.  Must be turned on to work.  Simplified ruleset: 1."
" When throttling, maximize acceleration.  2. Keep battery at 90%.  3. "
"Minimize fuel consumption."
msgstr ""
"Módulo electrónico que enciende y apaga automáticamente los motores de "
"combustión y eléctricos, minimizando el consumo de combustible y optimizando"
" la potencia y la tasa de carga de la batería. Debe estar encendido para "
"funcionar. Conjunto de reglas simplificadas: 1. Cuando se acelera, se "
"maximiza la aceleración. 2. Mantener la batería al 90%. 3. Minimizar el "
"consumo de combustible."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "5-point harness"
msgstr "arnés de 5 puntos"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "5-point harness"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A series of straps attached to the seat, intended to fasten together after "
"going over your shoulders and hips and between your legs."
msgstr ""
"Una serie de correas fijadas al asiento, destinadas a unirse después de "
"pasar por encima de los hombros y las caderas y entre las piernas."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "curtain"
msgstr "cortina"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "curtain"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A sheet over a window."
msgstr "Es una cortina sobre una ventana."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "aisle curtain"
msgstr "cortina de espacio lateral"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "aisle curtain"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A sheet across an aisle."
msgstr "Una sábana al otro lado del compartimento."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "water wheel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A water wheel."
msgstr "Un molino de agua."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "large water wheel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A large water wheel with wooden supports."
msgstr ""
"Una gran rueda hidráulica con soportes de madera.Una gran rueda hidráulica "
"con soportes de madera."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "solar panel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A solar panel."
msgstr "Un panel solar."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wind turbine"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A small wind turbine."
msgstr "Una pequeña turbina eólica."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "large wind turbine"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A large wind turbine with stabilizing legs.  Will cause extra drag on the "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un gran aerogenerador con soportes estabilizadores. Causará un arrastre "
"extra en el vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "collapsible solar array"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small array of solar panels designed to be able to fold into one another."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña matriz de paneles solares diseñados para poder plegarse unos a "
"otros."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "advanced collapsible solar array"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small array of high-performance solar panels designed to be able to fold "
"into one another."
msgstr ""
"Pequeño conjunto de paneles solares de alta eficiencia diseñados para poder "
"plegarse sobre si mismos."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "reinforced solar panel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A solar panel.  Reinforced with armored glass to make it more resistant to "
"damage."
msgstr ""
"Un panel solar. Reforzado con cristal blindado para hacerlo más resistente a"
" los daños."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "advanced solar panel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A high-performance solar panel."
msgstr "Un panel solar de alta eficiencia."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "advanced reinforced solar panel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A high-performance solar panel.  Reinforced with armored glass to make it "
"more resistant to damage."
msgstr ""
"Un panel solar de alta eficiencia. Reforzado con cristal blindado para "
"hacerlo mas resistente al daño."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "water faucet"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A water faucet."
msgstr "Un grifo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden armor"
msgstr "blindaje de madera"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "spiked plating"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A spiked plate that will increase the damage delivered to someone else in "
"collisions."
msgstr ""
"Una placa de púas que aumentará el daño causado a otro ser en las "
"colisiones."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "military composite armor plating"
msgstr "chapas blindadas de compuesto militar"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "bicycle horn"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small horn.  Use the vehicle controls and select the honk option to make "
"noise."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño claxon. Utilice los controles del vehículo y seleccione la opción"
" de bocina para hacer ruido."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "car horn"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A horn.  Use the vehicle controls and select the honk option to make noise."
msgstr ""
"Un claxon. Utilice los controles del vehículo y seleccione la opción de "
"bocina para hacer ruido."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "truck horn"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A powerful truck horn.  Use the vehicle controls and select the honk option "
"to make noise."
msgstr ""
"Es una potente bocina de camión. Usa los controles del vehículo para "
"seleccionar la bocina y hacerla sonar."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "back-up beeper"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An electronic noise maker.  It will automatically make noise when you drive "
"in reverse, alerting things behind you to move out of the way."
msgstr ""
"Es un generador de ruido electrónico. Automáticamente, hará sonar un pitido "
"cuando conduces marcha atrás, alertando a las cosas detrás tuyo para que se "
"corran."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "trunk door"
msgstr "puerta de maletero"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "trunk door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A short door.  You can always see over it, open or closed."
msgstr "Una puerta corta. Siempre puedes ver sobre ella, abierta o cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "heavy-duty trunk door"
msgstr "puerta del maletero reforzada"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty trunk door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A strong, short door.  You can always see over it, open or closed."
msgstr ""
"Una puerta fuerte y corta. Siempre puedes ver sobre ella, abierta o cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "shutter door"
msgstr "puerta de persiana"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "sliding door"
msgstr "puerta corrediza"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "sliding door"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A door.  A window lets you see through it when closed."
msgstr ""
"Es una puerta. Una ventana te permite ver al otro lado cuando está cerrada."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "cargo space"
msgstr "espacio de carga"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "livestock stall"
msgstr "puesto de ganado"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "livestock stall"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A cargo space for carrying livestock.  'e'xamine it to capture an animal "
"next to you, or to release the animal currently contained.  When selecting "
"an animal to capture, choose its tile relative to you, not the part."
msgstr ""
"Un espacio de carga para el transporte de ganado. Lo 'e'xaminar para "
"capturar un animal que esté a tu lado, o para liberar el animal que "
"actualmente está encerrado. Al seleccionar un animal para capturar, elige su"
" cuadrado relativo a ti, no la parte."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "animal compartment"
msgstr "compartimento de animales"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "animal compartment"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A large locker for transporting smaller animals.  'e'xamine it to capture an"
" animal next to you, or to release the animal currently contained.  When "
"selecting an animal to capture, choose its tile relative to you, not the "
"part."
msgstr ""
"Un gran armario para transportar animales más pequeños. 'e'xaminar para "
"capturar un animal a su lado, o para liberar el animal que actualmente este "
"encerrado. Al seleccionar un animal para capturar, elige su cuadrado "
"relativo a ti, no al armario."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "recharging station"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A device for recharging batteries.  When turned on, it charges any "
"rechargeable batteries (battery cells, lead-acid batteries, etc) placed "
"directly in the attached storage space, drawing power from the vehicle's "
"batteries."
msgstr ""
"Un dispositivo para recargar baterías. Cuando está encendido, carga "
"cualquier batería recargable (de celdas, de plomo y ácido, etc.) que esté "
"puesta directamente en el espacio de almacenamiento drenando energía de las "
"baterías del vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "battery charger"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small, low-power consumer device for recharging batteries.  It slowly "
"charges any rechargeable batteries (battery cells, lead-acid batteries, etc)"
" placed directly in the attached storage space, drawing power from the "
"vehicle's batteries."
msgstr ""
"Es un dispositivo pequeño de bajo consumo para recargar baterías. Carga "
"lentamente cualquier batería recargable (de celdas, de plomo y ácido, etc.) "
"que estén puestas directamente en el espacio de almacenamiento usando la "
"energía de las baterías del vehículo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "chimes"
msgstr "campanas"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "chimes"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A collection of electronic bells.  Use the vehicle's controls to turn it on "
"or off.  When turned on, it makes noise, attracting neighborhood children."
msgstr ""
"Una colección de campanas electrónicas. Utiliza los controles del vehículo "
"para encenderlo o apagarlo. Cuando se enciende, hace ruido, atrayendo a los "
"niños del vecindario."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "jumper cable"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"Thick copper cable with leads on either end.  Attach one end to one vehicle "
"and the other to another, and you can transfer electrical power between the "
"two."
msgstr ""
"Cable de cobre grueso con cables en cada extremo. Conecta un extremo a un "
"vehículo y el otro a otro, y puedes transferir energía eléctrica entre los "
"dos."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "extension cord"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A long orange extension cord for connecting appliances.  Currently plugged "
"in."
msgstr ""
"Un cable largo naranja para conectar aparatos. Actualmente está enchufado."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "outdoor extension cord"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An extra long 30m orange extension cord for connecting outdoor appliances.  "
"Currently plugged in."
msgstr ""
"Un cable extensor naranja extra largo de 30m para conectar aparatos de "
"exterior. Actualmente está enchufado."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty cable"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"Very thick copper cable with leads on either end.  Attach one end to one "
"vehicle and the other to another, and you can transfer electrical power "
"between the two."
msgstr ""
"Un cable de cobre muy grueso con cables en cada extremo. Conecta un extremo "
"a un vehículo y el otro a otro, y puedes transferir energía eléctrica entre "
"los dos."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "heavy-duty tow cable"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A heavy-duty tow cable, if the other end was attached to another vehicle, it"
" could pull it."
msgstr ""
"Un cable reforzado para remolcar.  Si la otra punta está enganchada a otro "
"vehículo podría remolcarlo."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "flimsy wooden seat"
msgstr "asiento endeble de madera"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "flimsy wooden seat"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden seat"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A place to sit."
msgstr "Un lugar para sentarse."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden seat"
msgstr "asiento de madera"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden bench"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A benchlike place to sit."
msgstr "Un lugar parecido a un banco para sentarse."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden spike"
msgstr "púa de madera"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden spike"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A wooden spike, attached to the vehicle, to increase injury when crashing "
"into things."
msgstr ""
"Un pincho de madera, fijado al vehículo, para aumentar las lesiones "
"producidas al chocar contra las cosas."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "wooden door"
msgstr "puerta de madera"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "opaque wooden door"
msgstr "puerta opaca de madera"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "wooden roof"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A wooden roof."
msgstr "Un techo de madera."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "chitin plating"
msgstr "placas de quitina"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "biosilicified chitin plating"
msgstr "Revestimiento de quitina biosilicificada"

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "door motor"
msgstr "puerta de motor"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "door motor"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small electric motor.  Installed on the same frame as a door or curtain, "
"it will allow you to remotely open the door or curtain from the vehicle "
"controls."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño motor eléctrico. Instalado en el mismo marco que una puerta o "
"cortina, te permite controlar su apertura de manera remota desde los "
"controles del vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "drive by wire controls"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A sophisticated set of electronic controls that allow you to control the "
"vehicle from a vehicle remote while you are not in it.  You can 'e'xamine "
"the tile to access the controls, or use the vehicle control key (default "
"'^')."
msgstr ""
"Un sofisticado conjunto de controles electrónicos que permiten controlar el "
"vehículo desde un mando a distancia mientras no se está en él. Puedes "
"'e'xaminar el cuadrado para acceder a los controles, o usar la llave de "
"control del vehículo (por defecto '^')."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "camera control system"
msgstr "sistema de cámara de control"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "camera control system"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An LCD attached to one or more cameras.  When turned on, it lets you see "
"from the cameras, but drains power from the vehicle's batteries.  You can "
"'e'xamine the tile to access the controls, or use the vehicle control key "
"(default '^')."
msgstr ""
"Una pantalla LCD conectada a una o más cámaras. Cuando se enciende, permite "
"ver desde las cámaras, pero consume la energía de las baterías del vehículo."
" Puedes 'e'xaminar el espacio para acceder a los controles, o usar la llave "
"de control del vehículo (por defecto '^')."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "security camera"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A small camera.  Will relay what it can see to a camera control station."
msgstr ""
"Es una pequeña cámara. Transmite lo que ve a la estación de control de "
"cámaras."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "robot controls"
msgstr "controles de robot"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "robot controls"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A set of controls to allow a vehicle to drive itself, or you to drive it "
"remotely using a controller."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de controles para permitir que un vehículo se conduzca por sí "
"mismo, o que tú lo conduzcas a distancia usando un controlador."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "clock"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A clock, so you know what time it is."
msgstr "Es un reloj, así puedes saber la hora."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "leather funnel"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "birchbark funnel"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "makeshift funnel"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "funnel"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "metal funnel"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "A funnel that will collect rainwater into the tank beneath it."
msgstr "Un embudo que recogerá el agua de lluvia en el tanque debajo de él."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "scoop"
msgstr "pala mecánica"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "scoop"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A scoop.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it"
" will scoop up loose items that it travels over until it's full."
msgstr ""
"Una pala. Utiliza los controles del vehículo para encenderlo o apagarlo. "
"Cuando se enciende, recogerá los objetos sueltos sobre los que se desplace "
"hasta que esté lleno."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "water purifier"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A water purifier, powered by the vehicle's batteries.  You can use it to "
"purify water in a container or in the vehicle's tanks.  'e'xamine the tile "
"with the purifier to use it."
msgstr ""
"Un purificador de agua, alimentado por las baterías del vehículo. Puedes "
"usarlo para purificar el agua en un contenedor o en los tanques del "
"vehículo. e'xamine el cuadrado con el purificador para usarlo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "plow"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A plow.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When turned on, it "
"will create a furrow in any dirt it travels over, making it suitable for "
"planting seeds.  It should be placed in front of any seed drills on the "
"vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Un arado. Use los controles del vehículo para encenderlo o apagarlo. Cuando "
"se enciende, creará un surco en la suciedad que atraviesa, haciéndolo "
"adecuado para plantar semillas. Debe colocarse delante de cualquier "
"sembradora en un vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "seed drill"
#. ~ Description of vehicle part "advanced seed drill"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A seed drill.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  You can load "
"it with seeds by examining it.  When turned on, it will drop seeds as the "
"vehicle moves, or plant them in furrowed dirt.  It should be placed behind "
"any plows on the vehicle, and any wheels should be placed so they won't run "
"over the plants."
msgstr ""
"Una sembradora. Utiliza los controles del vehículo para activarla o "
"desactivarla. Puedes examinarla para cargarla con semillas. Cuando está "
"activa, dejará caer las semillas a medida que el vehículo avanza, o las "
"plantará en tierra arada. Debería estar ubicado atrás del arado, y las "
"ruedas deben estar puestas de manera que no pasen por encima de las plantas."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "reaper"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An automatic reaper.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When "
"on, it will cut down plants that it travels over.  It should be placed in "
"front of any plows in the vehicle for efficient operation.  It does not "
"include cargo space of its own so you need install a cargo space of some "
"kind elsewhere in the vehicle."
msgstr ""
"Una cosechadora automática. Usa los controles del vehículo para encenderlo o"
" apagarlo. Cuando esté encendido, cortará las plantas por las que viaja. "
"Debe ser colocado delante de cualquier arado en el vehículo para un "
"funcionamiento eficiente. No incluye espacio de carga propio, por lo que "
"debe instalarse un espacio de carga de algún tipo en otra parte del "
"vehículo."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "advanced reaper"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"An automatic reaper.  Use the vehicle controls to turn it on or off.  When "
"on, it will cut down plants and store them in the vehicle's cargo.  It "
"should be placed in front of any plows in the vehicle for efficient "
"operation.  It has internal cargo space for collecting the harvest."
msgstr ""
"Una segadora automática. Utiliza los controles del vehículo para encenderla "
"o apagarla. Cuando esté encendida, cortará las plantas y las almacenará en "
"la carga del vehículo. Debe colocarse delante de cualquier arado del "
"vehículo para que funcione con eficacia. Dispone de un espacio de carga "
"interno para recoger la cosecha."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "cargo lock"
msgstr "Cerradura de carga"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "cargo lock"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A set of locks.  Attached to a suitable cargo space, it will prevent other "
"people from accessing the cargo and taking your stuff."
msgstr ""
"Un juego de cerraduras. Fijadas a un espacio de carga adecuado, impedirá que"
" otras personas accedan a la carga y se lleven tus cosas."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "turret mount"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A rotating, universal mount for a weapon.  If your hands are empty, you can "
"stand on the same tile as a turret mount and 'f'ire the weapon."
msgstr ""
"Una montura giratoria y universal para un arma. Si tus manos están vacías, "
"puedes pararte en el mismo azulejo que la montura de una torreta y disparar "
"pulsando 'f' el arma."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "turret control unit"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"A set of motor, camera, and an AI unit which allows for tracking targets, "
"friend-or-foe identification, and firing the connected turret in full "
"automatic mode.  When installed over the turret, it will enable auto "
"targeting mode for said turret."
msgstr ""
"Un conjunto de motor, cámara y una unidad de IA que permite el seguimiento "
"de los objetivos, la identificación de amigos o enemigos y el disparo de la "
"torreta conectada en modo totalmente automático. Cuando se instala sobre la "
"torreta, habilitará el modo de disparo automático para dicha torreta."

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "aluminum boat hull"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "An aluminum hull that keeps the water out of your boat."
msgstr "Una lámina de aluminio que mantiene el agua fuera de tu barco."

#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "plugged 3-inch ordnance rifle"
msgstr "Fusil de artillería de 3 pulgadas taponado"

#. ~ Description of vehicle part "plugged 3-inch ordnance rifle"
#: data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, some responsible killjoy poured concrete in the barrel of "
"this historic cannon to make it safe for display."
msgstr ""
"Desgraciadamente, algún aguafiestas responsable vertió hormigón en el cañón "
"de este histórico cañón para hacerlo seguro para su exhibición."

