msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor_helmets.json
msgid "carbide raider's helmet"
msgid_plural "carbide raider's helmets"
msgstr[0] "casco de carburo de saqueador"
msgstr[1] "cascos de carburo de saqueador"
msgstr[2] "cascos de carburo de saqueador"

#. ~ Description of "carbide raider's helmet"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor_helmets.json
msgid ""
"This helmet is designed for the individual that is worried about catching "
"heavy weapons fire to the face.  It is unwieldy and heavy, and lacks basic "
"environmental protection features, but it just might stop even the largest "
"of ballistic rounds."
msgstr ""
"Este casco está diseñado para el individuo que está preocupado por recibir "
"disparos de armas pesadas en la cara. Es poco manejable y pesado, y carece "
"de las características básicas de protección ambiental, pero puede detener "
"incluso las balas más grandes."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor_helmets.json
msgid "UICAS Tip of the Spear helmet"
msgid_plural "UICAS Tip of the Spear helmets"
msgstr[0] "Casco Punta de Lanza UICA"
msgstr[1] "Cascos Punta de Lanza UICA"
msgstr[2] "Cascos Punta de Lanza UICA"

#. ~ Description of "UICAS Tip of the Spear helmet"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor_helmets.json
msgid ""
"An all-environment combat helmet issued to UICA espatiers.  Commonly known "
"as 'the jar' due to its unusual clear polymer canopy that leaves its "
"wearer's face visible."
msgstr ""
"Un casco de combate para todos los entornos, usado por los espatiers de "
"UICA. Comúnmente conocido como 'el tarro' debido a su inusual polímero "
"transparente que deja visible la cara del usuario."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor_helmets.json
msgid "UICAS Point of Impact helmet"
msgid_plural "UICAS Point of Impact helmets"
msgstr[0] "casco Punto de Impacto UICAS"
msgstr[1] "cascos Punto de Impacto UICAS"
msgstr[2] "cascos Punto de Impacto UICAS"

#. ~ Description of "UICAS Point of Impact helmet"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/armor_helmets.json
msgid ""
"A lightweight black helmet that provides excellent protection from all sorts"
" of damage, unless it's airborne.  UICAS makes the point of designing all "
"headgear whenever possible with clear faceplates, in order to provide a "
"human touch to all interactions."
msgstr ""
"Un casco negro y ligero que proporciona una excelente protección contra todo"
" tipo de daños. UICAS se esfuerzan por diseñar todos los cascos, siempre que"
" sea posible, con placas faciales transparentes, para dar un toque humano a "
"todas las interacciones."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid "living brain in a jar"
msgid_plural "jars full of living brains"
msgstr[0] "tarro lleno de cerebros vivos"
msgstr[1] "tarros llenos de cerebros vivos"
msgstr[2] "tarros llenos de cerebros vivos"

#. ~ Description of "living brain in a jar"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid ""
"This jar contains a human brain kept alive by mi-go technology.  It has "
"metal veined tendrils that appear to allow it to connect to various devices."
msgstr ""
"Este tarro contiene un cerebro humano que se mantiene vivo gracias a la "
"tecnología mi-go. Tiene zarcillos con venas metálicas que parecen permitirle"
" conectarse a varios dispositivos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid "humming heart"
msgid_plural "humming hearts"
msgstr[0] "corazón palpitante"
msgstr[1] "corazones palpitantes"
msgstr[2] "corazones palpitantes"

#. ~ Description of "humming heart"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid ""
"This heartlike organ has multiple valves and upon its proper removal from "
"the bioweapons corpse each valve sealed itself.  It hums gently in your "
"hands, as if waiting for an appropriate receptacle."
msgstr ""
"Este órgano similar al corazón tiene múltiples válvulas y al ser retirado "
"del cadáver del bioarma cada válvula se sella por sí misma. Tararea "
"suavemente en las manos, como si esperara un receptáculo apropiado."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid "sensory cluster"
msgid_plural "sensory clusters"
msgstr[0] "grupo sensorial"
msgstr[1] "grupos sensoriales"
msgstr[2] "grupos sensoriales"

#. ~ Description of "sensory cluster"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid ""
"This lump of flesh has various lobes protruding from it that at intervals "
"will emit toned sounds.  Perhaps it works via echolocation.  Like all mi-go "
"bioparts the openings on this piece closed up after it was cut free and it "
"seems to have gone into a form of hibernation with the pulses occurring "
"slower and slower as it conserves energy."
msgstr ""
"Este trozo de carne tiene varios lóbulos que sobresalen de él y que a "
"intervalos emitirán sonidos tonificados. Tal vez funciona a través de la "
"ecolocalización. Como todas las biopartes mi-go, las aberturas de esta pieza"
" se cerraron después de ser cortada y parece haber entrado en una forma de "
"hibernación, con los pulsos ocurriendo más y más lentamente a medida que "
"conserva energía."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid "bioweapon chassis"
msgid_plural "bioweapon chassis"
msgstr[0] "chasis de bioarma"
msgstr[1] "chasis de bioarmas"
msgstr[2] "chasis de bioarmas"

#. ~ Description of "bioweapon chassis"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid ""
"This cross between a sea anemone and what you imagine a dragon's mouth would"
" look like is the core body of the bioweapon.  You cannot imagine what you "
"could make out of this but maybe someone somewhere does."
msgstr ""
"Esta mezcla entre una anémona marina y lo que te parece la boca de un dragón"
" pareciera ser la parte central de un bioarma. No te puedes imaginar qué "
"podrías hacer con esto pero tal vez alguien lo sepa."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid "broken mi-go turret"
msgid_plural "broken mi-go turrets"
msgstr[0] "torreta mi-go rota"
msgstr[1] "torretas mi-go rotas"
msgstr[2] "torretas mi-go rotas"

#. ~ Description of "broken mi-go turret"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid ""
"A broken mi-go turret.  It's leaking fluids and smells you can't identify.  "
"Could be butchered for parts."
msgstr ""
"Una torreta mi-go rota. Está perdiendo fluidos y olores que no puedes "
"identificar. Podría ser masacrado por partes."

#. ~ Name of a gun
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid "vibrating bioblaster"
msgid_plural "vibrating bioblasters"
msgstr[0] "bioblaster vibratorio"
msgstr[1] "bioblasters vibratorios"
msgstr[2] "bioblasters vibratorios"

#. ~ Description of gun "vibrating bioblaster"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/bioparts.json
msgid ""
"You ripped this from a mi-go abomination.  You think you should wear gloves "
"to reload it."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid "original copy of Housefly"
msgid_plural "original copies of Housefly"
msgstr[0] "copia original de Mosca Doméstica"
msgstr[1] "copias originales de Mosca doméstica"
msgstr[2] "copias originales de Mosca doméstica"

#. ~ Description of "original copy of Housefly"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid ""
"The only copy of Housefly in existence - a long book about three individuals"
" drawn together by fate in the early 1800s to save their English town of "
"Victoria from a mysterious threat.  You never got to publish it, but reading"
" it lets you forget the horrors of the Cataclysm, if only for a moment."
msgstr ""
"La única copia de Mosca Doméstica que existe: un largo libro acerca de tres "
"individuos unidos por el destino a principios del siglo XIX para salvar "
"Victoria, su pueblo inglés, de una amenaza misteriosa. Nunca llegaste a "
"publicarlo, pero leerlo te hace olvidar los horrores del Cataclismo, aunque "
"sea solo por un momento."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 1"
msgid_plural "copies of Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 1"
msgstr[0] "Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 1"
msgstr[1] "copias de Historia no Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 1"
msgstr[2] "copias de Historia no Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 1"

#. ~ Description of "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 1"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid ""
"Welcome to Frozen Hell, an unofficial history of Salus IV by Bette Lapin.  "
"Salus IV was founded in the early days of the Hyperspace Era as a joint "
"venture between Mercurial Genomics and a Soviet Design Bureau.  At its "
"height several hundred years ago Salus IV had just over 110 million citizens"
" (including both uplifts and humans). However, that population had begun to "
"decline even before the Discontinuity as people migrated to planets that, "
"while more hostile to life during the earliest colonization phases than "
"Salus IV, were much simpler to terraform into a place more enjoyable by "
"human and uplift citizens."
msgstr ""
"Bienvenidos al Infierno Congelado, una historia no oficial de Salus IV por "
"Bette Lapin. Salus IV fue fundado en los primeros días de la Era "
"Hiperespacial como una aventura comercial entre Mercurial Genomics y el "
"Departamento de Diseño Soviético. En su apogeo, hace varios cientos de años,"
" Salus IV contaba con algo más de 110 millones de ciudadanos (incluyendo "
"tanto a los ascendidos como a los humanos). Sin embargo, esa población "
"empezó a declinar incluso antes de la Discontinuidad, ya que la gente emigró"
" a planetas que, aunque eran más hostiles a la vida durante sus fases "
"iniciales de colonización que Salus IV, eran mucho más sencillos de "
"terraformar para convertirlos en un lugar más agradable para los ciudadanos "
"humanos y ascendidos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 2"
msgid_plural "copies of Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 2"
msgstr[0] "Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 2"
msgstr[1] "copias de Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 2"
msgstr[2] "copias de Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 2"

#. ~ Description of "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 2"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid ""
"Even during the Discontinuity Salus IV's population continued to drop as "
"there were easier places to live even in the Salus system - from honeycombed"
" asteroid habitats to domed cities with gorgeous views.  Mercurial Genomics "
"was an early member of the nascent post-Discontinuity government efforts.  "
"As a result of this membership, they have successfully reclaimed Salus IV in"
" the court system set up by ESCA.  The Whately family, which runs Mercurial "
"Genomics, began leasing development and exploitation permits and allows the "
"establishment of minor UICA outposts within Salus IV.  There is an official "
"citizen count of less than twenty thousand sentient beings, albeit mostly in"
" orbit.  It is believed, however, that there are at least that many non-"
"citizen sentients spread amongst squatter, smuggler, pirate, and feral "
"uplift communities."
msgstr ""
"Incluso durante la Discontinuidad, la población de Salus IV siguió cayendo, "
"ya que había lugares más cómodos para vivir incluso en el sistema Salus, "
"desde hábitats de asteroides en forma de panal hasta ciudades abovedadas con"
" preciosas vistas. Mercurial Genomics fue creada como uno de los primeros "
"miembros como parte de los esfuerzos gubernamentales posteriores a la "
"Discontinuidad. Como resultado de esta afiliación, han reclamado con éxito "
"Salus IV en el sistema judicial establecido por la ESCA. La familia Whately,"
" que dirige Mercurial Genomics, comenzó a arrendar permisos de desarrollo y "
"explotación para permitir el establecimiento de pequeños puestos de avanzada"
" de la UICA en Salus IV. Hay un recuento oficial de ciudadanos de menos de "
"veinte mil seres conscientes, aunque la mayoría en órbita. Sin embargo, se "
"cree que hay al menos ese mismo número de seres conscientes no ciudadanos "
"repartidos entre comunidades de ocupantes ilegales, contrabandistas, piratas"
" y ascendidos."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 3"
msgid_plural "copies of Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 3"
msgstr[0] "Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 3"
msgstr[1] "copias de Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 3"
msgstr[2] "copias de Historia No Autorizada de Salus IV Vol. 3"

#. ~ Description of "Unofficial History of Salus IV Vol. 3"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid ""
"The Salus system is what is called a hinge system for the new FTL travels.  "
"This system contains a number of easy exit points to star systems that have "
"no other easy way to travel to each other than through a series of systems "
"with low to zero civilization in them.  Salus has several interstellar "
"refueling points.  These stations are often blind to each other as the "
"planets and other objects rotate around the sun.  Mercurial seems to have no"
" interest in managing or protecting the traffic that flows through the Salus"
" system or in neighboring systems beyond the bare minimum effort required by"
" UICA.  As a result of this neglect; victims of pirate attacks, engine "
"failure and other critical issues regularly limp to whatever safety they can"
" find in the Salus system.  Unfortunately for many of them they will crash "
"land on Salus IV where there are few regular shuttles between its scattered "
"ports and the outside universe.  As the locals are fond of saying 'Getting "
"to Salus IV is hard, getting off may be impossible'."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid "Nuclear Physics Made Easy"
msgid_plural "copies of Nuclear Physics Made Easy"
msgstr[0] "Física Nuclear Hecha Fácil"
msgstr[1] "copias de Física Nuclear Hecha Fácil"
msgstr[2] "copias de Física Nuclear Hecha Fácil"

#. ~ Description of "Nuclear Physics Made Easy"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid ""
"A book detailing the workings of state of the art atomic technology, and the"
" physics behind it."
msgstr ""
"Un libro que detalla el funcionamiento de la tecnología atómica puntera, y "
"la física detrás de ella."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid "mealworm farm logbook"
msgid_plural "mealworm farm logbooks"
msgstr[0] "registro de la Ggranja de gusanos de la harina"
msgstr[1] " registros de granja de gusanos de la harina"
msgstr[2] " registros de granja de gusanos de la harina"

#. ~ Description of "mealworm farm logbook"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json
msgid ""
"A binder containing detailed production logs from an industrial mealworm "
"farm.  You could use its recordings to start your own farming operations."
msgstr ""
"Un archivador que contiene registros detallados de la producción de una "
"granja industrial de gusanos de harina. Podrías usar sus grabaciones para "
"iniciar tus propias operaciones agrícolas."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json data/mods/No_Hope/items.json
msgid "chicken walker schematics"
msgid_plural "chicken walker schematics"
msgstr[0] "esquema de gallina caminante"
msgstr[1] "esquemas de gallina caminante"
msgstr[2] "esquemas de gallina caminante"

#. ~ Description of "chicken walker schematics"
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/books.json data/mods/No_Hope/items.json
msgid ""
"Bearing the logo of Northrop, those are assembly plans, design specs, and "
"technical drawings for the chicken walker.  Most of this is useless to you, "
"but you could use the assembly plans to re-assemble the robot from salvaged "
"parts."
msgstr ""
"Con el logo de Northrop, son planos de montaje, especificaciones de diseño y"
" dibujos técnicos para la gallina caminante. La mayoría de esto es inútil "
"para ti, pero podrías usar los planos de ensamblaje para reensamblar el "
"robot a partir de piezas recuperadas."

