#. ~ In terms of alchemy the gastrolith could serve to combie different
#. effects, such as safely mixing together potions, or it could be used as an
#. element of change, such as for shapechanging potions.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
msgid "owlbear gastrolith"
msgid_plural "owlbear gastroliths"
msgstr[0] "gastrolitos de buhoso"
msgstr[1] "gastrolitos de buhoso"
msgstr[2] "gastrolitos de buhoso"

#. ~ In terms of alchemy the gastrolith could serve to combie different
#. effects, such as safely mixing together potions, or it could be used as an
#. element of change, such as for shapechanging potions.
#. ~ Description of "owlbear gastrolith"
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
msgid ""
"This strangely shaped rock was once a part of an owlbear's complex digestive"
" system, creating a link between owl throat and bear stomach.  It is "
"possible that it could serve a similar purpose in alchemy, helping to bind "
"together two disparate halves."
msgstr ""
"Esta roca de forma extraña fue una vez parte del complejo sistema digestivo "
"de un búho, creando un vínculo entre la garganta del búho y el estómago del "
"oso. Es posible que pudiera servir un propósito similar en la alquimia, "
"ayudando a unir dos mitades dispares."

#. ~ Potion recipes that require a full owlbear egg could also instead require
#. larger amounts of stone shell.  Since 1 egg gives 3 shells, you could
#. perhaps have 1 egg be equivalent to 5 or more shells when making potions.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/mods/Magiclysm/items/alchemy_items.json
msgid "stone shell"
msgid_plural "stone shells"
msgstr[0] "cascara de piedra"
msgstr[1] "cascaras de piedra"
msgstr[2] "cascaras de piedra"

#. ~ Potion recipes that require a full owlbear egg could also instead require
