#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "rhea"
msgid_plural "rheas"
msgstr[0] "ñandú"
msgstr[1] "ñandús"
msgstr[2] "ñandús"

#. ~ Description of monster "rhea"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A distant relative of the Ostrich and the Emu.  Found only on the grasslands"
" and other dry places of South America."
msgstr ""
"Pariente lejano del avestruz y del emú. Sólo se encuentra en las praderas y "
"otros lugares secos de Sudamérica."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "guinea fowl"
msgid_plural "guinea fowls"
msgstr[0] "gallina de guinea"
msgstr[1] "gallinas de guinea"
msgstr[2] "gallinas de guinea"

#. ~ Description of monster "guinea fowl"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A domestic bird that originated from Africa.  Easily recognizable for the "
"strange helmet on its head and its white-gray plumage."
msgstr ""
"Ave doméstica originaria de África. Fácilmente reconocible por el extraño "
"casco que lleva en la cabeza y su plumaje blanco-grisáceo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "quail"
msgid_plural "quails"
msgstr[0] "codorniz"
msgstr[1] "codornices"
msgstr[2] "codornices"

#. ~ Description of monster "quail"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"The common quail is one of the smallest domestic birds used for meat and "
"eggs.  It originated in Eurasia but can be found worldwide and is raised "
"sometimes for hunting or as an ornamental bird."
msgstr ""
"La codorniz común es una de las aves domésticas más pequeñas que se utilizan"
" para obtener carne y huevos. Es originaria de Eurasia, pero se encuentra en"
" todo el mundo y se cría a veces para la caza o como ave ornamental."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "toucan"
msgid_plural "toucans"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "toucan"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A small bird with dark plumage and a bright colored face and beak.  These "
"tropical birds can be found all around the Americas feeding on fruits and "
"seeds."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "parrot"
msgid_plural "parrots"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "parrot"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A small to medium bird with bright colored plumage and a short hooked beak."
"  These birds are considered to be quite intelligent and have been "
"domesticated heavily as pets."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "cockatoo"
msgid_plural "cockatoos"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "cockatoo"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A small to medium bird with bright colored plumage and a short hooked beak."
"  These relatives of parrots originate from Indonesia and Oceania, and are "
"well known for their antics and head plumage."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "budgerigar"
msgid_plural "budgerigars"
msgstr[0] "periquito"
msgstr[1] "periquitos"
msgstr[2] "periquitos"

#. ~ Description of monster "budgerigar"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A small bird with with bright colored plumage and a short hooked beak.  "
"These small relatives of the parrot come from Australia but were "
"domesticated worldwide as pets."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño pájaro con un plumaje de colores vivos y un pico corto y "
"ganchudo. Estos pequeños parientes del loro proceden de Australia, pero "
"fueron domesticados en todo el mundo como mascotas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "macaw"
msgid_plural "macaws"
msgstr[0] "guacamayo"
msgstr[1] "guacamayos"
msgstr[2] "guacamayos"

#. ~ Description of monster "macaw"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A medium to large bird with bright colored plumage and a short hooked beak."
"  These are the largest flying parrots in the world, living usually in the "
"thickest rainforests."
msgstr ""
"Un ave de tamaño mediano a grande con un plumaje de colores brillantes y un "
"pico corto y ganchudo. Son los loros voladores más grandes del mundo, que "
"viven normalmente en las selvas tropicales más espesas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "tinamou"
msgid_plural "tinamous"
msgstr[0] "tintorero"
msgstr[1] "tintoreros"
msgstr[2] "tintoreros"

#. ~ Description of monster "tinamou"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"One of several species of the Tinamidae family.  These birds converged into "
"shapes similar to fowl but are actually more closely related to the extinct "
"moas."
msgstr ""
"Una de las varias especies de la familia Tinamidae. Estas aves convergen en "
"formas similares a las aves de corral, pero en realidad están más "
"relacionadas con las extintas moas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "seriema"
msgid_plural "seriemas"
msgstr[0] "seriema"
msgstr[1] "seriemas"
msgstr[2] "seriemas"

#. ~ Description of monster "seriema"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A medium sized bird with long legs and a small crest.  It lives on the "
"grasslands of South America and is considered the only living relative of "
"the extinct terror birds."
msgstr ""
"Es un ave de tamaño medio con patas largas y una pequeña cresta. Vive en las"
" praderas de Sudamérica y se considera el único pariente vivo de las "
"extintas aves del terror."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "chachalaca"
msgid_plural "chachalacas"
msgstr[0] "chachalaca"
msgstr[1] "chachalacas"
msgstr[2] "chachalacas"

#. ~ Description of monster "chachalaca"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A bird belonging to the Cracidae family.  They resemble turkeys to a degree "
"and live on scrubby habitats."
msgstr ""
"Ave perteneciente a la familia de los cracidos. Se parecen un poco a los "
"pavos y viven en hábitats de matorrales."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "guan"
msgid_plural "guans"
msgstr[0] "guano"
msgstr[1] "guanos"
msgstr[2] "guanos"

#. ~ Description of monster "guan"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A bird belonging to the Cracidae family.  They resemble turkeys to a degree "
"and live on forested areas."
msgstr ""
"Ave perteneciente a la familia de los cracidos. Se parecen un poco a los "
"pavos y viven en zonas boscosas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "curassow"
msgid_plural "curassows"
msgstr[0] "curassow"
msgstr[1] "curassows"
msgstr[2] "curassows"

#. ~ Description of monster "curassow"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A bird belonging to the Cracidae family.  They resemble turkeys to a degree "
"and live on forested areas, easily distinguished by their crested heads."
msgstr ""
"Ave perteneciente a la familia de los cracidos. Se parecen un poco a los "
"pavos y viven en zonas boscosas; se distinguen fácilmente por su cabeza "
"crestada."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "flamingo"
msgid_plural "flamingos"
msgstr[0] "flamenco"
msgstr[1] "flamencos"
msgstr[2] "flamencos"

#. ~ Description of monster "flamingo"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A medium to large bird with white and pink plumage.  They can be found on "
"both hemispheres living around shallow waters rich on plankton and small "
"crustaceans."
msgstr ""
"Un ave de tamaño medio a grande con plumaje blanco y rosa. Se encuentran en "
"ambos hemisferios y viven en aguas poco profundas, ricas en plancton y "
"pequeños crustáceos."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid "flamingo chick"
msgid_plural "flamingo chicks"
msgstr[0] "polluelo de flamenco"
msgstr[1] "polluelos de flamenco"
msgstr[2] "polluelos de flamenco"

#. ~ Description of monster "flamingo chick"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_bird.json
msgid ""
"A baby flamingo covered in fuzzy plumage.  Unlike their parents they are "
"born gray or white and obtain their pink color as they grow feeding on "
"crustaceans."
msgstr ""
"Una cría de flamenco cubierta de plumaje velloso. A diferencia de sus "
"padres, nacen grises o blancos y obtienen su color rosado a medida que "
"crecen alimentándose de crustáceos."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "crab"
msgid_plural "crabs"
msgstr[0] "cangrejo"
msgstr[1] "cangrejos"
msgstr[2] "cangrejos"

#. ~ Description of monster "crab"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A crustacean belonging to either Trichodactylidae or Pseudothelphusidae.  "
"Freshwater crabs are widely spread around Central and South America, some "
"even found in mountain streams."
msgstr ""
"Crustáceo perteneciente a los Trichodactylidae o Pseudothelphusidae. Los "
"cangrejos de agua dulce están muy extendidos por América Central y del Sur, "
"y algunos se encuentran incluso en arroyos de montaña."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "baby crab"
msgid_plural "baby crabs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "baby crab"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A crab in its larval stage, incredibly fragile and tiny but produced by a "
"truckload of eggs that have been carried by their mother."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "pancora crab"
msgid_plural "pancora crabs"
msgstr[0] "cangrejo pancora"
msgstr[1] "cangrejos pancora"
msgstr[2] "cangrejos pancora"

#. ~ Description of monster "pancora crab"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A crustacean belonging to the Aeglidae family.  They are among the only "
"living freshwater anomurans, being restricted solely to South America."
msgstr ""
"Crustáceo de la familia Aeglidae. Es uno de los únicos anomuros de agua "
"dulce vivos, ya que se limita a Sudamérica."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "baby pancora crab"
msgid_plural "baby pancora crabs"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "baby pancora crab"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A pancora crab in its larval stage, incredibly fragile and tiny but produced"
" by a truckload of eggs that have been carried by their mother."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "bull shark"
msgid_plural "bull sharks"
msgstr[0] "tiburón toro"
msgstr[1] "tiburones toro"
msgstr[2] "tiburones toro"

#. ~ Description of monster "bull shark"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"The bull shark is one of the few known species of shark capable of living in"
" both fresh and salty waters.  With the advent of the Cataclysm many of them"
" have migrated up river to exploit the new food sources in the waters."
msgstr ""
"El tiburón toro es una de las pocas especies conocidas de tiburones capaces "
"de vivir tanto en aguas dulces como saladas. Con la llegada del Cataclismo, "
"muchos de ellos han emigrado río arriba para explotar las nuevas fuentes de "
"alimento de las aguas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "bull shark pup"
msgid_plural "bull shark pups"
msgstr[0] "cría de tiburón toro"
msgstr[1] "crías de tiburón toro"
msgstr[2] "crías de tiburón toro"

#. ~ Description of monster "bull shark pup"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"Unlike other fish bull sharks are viviparous and their pups are as well "
"equipped as their parents."
msgstr ""
"A diferencia de otros peces, los tiburones toro son vivíparos y sus crías "
"están tan bien equipadas como sus padres."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "lungfish"
msgid_plural "lungfish"
msgstr[0] "pez pulmón"
msgstr[1] "peces pulmón"
msgstr[2] "peces pulmón"

#. ~ Description of monster "lungfish"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A lungfish.  This strange fish has relatives in both Africa and Australia, "
"all of them can breathe air and some consider them living fossils."
msgstr ""
"Un pez pulmonado. Este extraño pez tiene parientes tanto en África como en "
"Australia, todos ellos pueden respirar aire y algunos los consideran fósiles"
" vivientes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "electric eel"
msgid_plural "electric eels"
msgstr[0] "anguila eléctrica"
msgstr[1] "anguilas eléctricas"
msgstr[2] "anguilas eléctricas"

#. ~ Description of monster "electric eel"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"An electric eel.  A strange elongated fish known for its hability to use "
"electricity to hunt prey, despite their name they are not actually eels."
msgstr ""
"Una anguila eléctrica. Un extraño pez alargado conocido por su capacidad de "
"utilizar la electricidad para cazar presas, a pesar de su nombre no son "
"realmente anguilas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "pacu"
msgid_plural "pacus"
msgstr[0] "pacu"
msgstr[1] "pacus"
msgstr[2] "pacus"

#. ~ Description of monster "pacu"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A pacu.  There are several species of these piranha relatives in the rivers "
"of South America, they are usually small to medium size."
msgstr ""
"Un pacú. Hay varias especies de estos parientes de las pirañas en los ríos "
"de Sudamérica, suelen ser de tamaño pequeño a mediano."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "tambaqui"
msgid_plural "tambaquis"
msgstr[0] "tambaqui"
msgstr[1] "tambaquis"
msgstr[2] "tambaquis"

#. ~ Description of monster "tambaqui"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"Also known as black or giant pacu.  This is the largest member of the family"
" and the most known worldwide."
msgstr ""
"También se le conoce como pacú negro o gigante. Es el miembro más grande de "
"la familia y el más conocido a nivel mundial."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "piranha"
msgid_plural "piranhas"
msgstr[0] "piraña"
msgstr[1] "pirañas"
msgstr[2] "pirañas"

#. ~ Description of monster "piranha"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A small to medium fish with a wide diet.  Contrary to popular belief these "
"fish are not vicious predators and instead react to the availability of food"
" in their environment."
msgstr ""
"Es un pez de tamaño pequeño a mediano con una dieta amplia. Contrariamente a"
" la creencia popular, estos peces no son depredadores feroces, sino que "
"reaccionan a la disponibilidad de alimentos en su entorno."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "arowana"
msgid_plural "arowanas"
msgstr[0] "arowana"
msgstr[1] "arowanas"
msgstr[2] "arowanas"

#. ~ Description of monster "arowana"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A member of the Osteoglossidade family.  These fishes can be found on South "
"America, Asia and Australia."
msgstr ""
"Pertenece a la familia de los Osteoglossidade. Estos peces se encuentran en "
"Sudamérica, Asia y Australia."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "arapaima"
msgid_plural "arapaimas"
msgstr[0] "arapaima"
msgstr[1] "arapaimas"
msgstr[2] "arapaimas"

#. ~ Description of monster "arapaima"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A member of the Arapaimidae family.  These fishes can be found on South "
"America and Africa, some species can grow to truly huge sizes."
msgstr ""
"Pertenece a la familia Arapaimidae. Estos peces se encuentran en Sudamérica "
"y África, y algunas especies pueden alcanzar tamaños realmente enormes."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "piraiba"
msgid_plural "piraibas"
msgstr[0] "piraiba"
msgstr[1] "piraibas"
msgstr[2] "piraibas"

#. ~ Description of monster "piraiba"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A huge species of South American catfish native to the Amazon and Orinoco "
"rivers, they can reach almost 3 meters in length."
msgstr ""
"Se trata de una enorme especie de pez gato sudamericano originario de los "
"ríos Amazonas y Orinoco, que puede alcanzar casi 3 metros de longitud."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "pleco"
msgid_plural "plecos"
msgstr[0] "pleco"
msgstr[1] "plecos"
msgstr[2] "plecos"

#. ~ Description of monster "pleco"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A catfish species native to South America, Panama and even Costa Rica.  They"
" are distinguished by their bony spines and suction adapted mouths."
msgstr ""
"Especie de pez gato originaria de Sudamérica, Panamá e incluso Costa Rica. "
"Se distinguen por sus espinas óseas y su boca adaptada a la succión."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "river stingray"
msgid_plural "river stingray"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "river stingray"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A fish of the Potamotrygonidae family.  These freshwater stingrays are found"
" mostly in South America with a few bred in other parts of the world."
msgstr ""
"Un pez de la familia Potamotrygonidae. Estas rayas de agua dulce se "
"encuentran sobre todo en América del Sur, con algunas criadas en otras "
"partes del mundo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "stingray fry"
msgid_plural "stingray fries"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "stingray fry"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A baby stingray.  Like many other cartilaginous fishes, river stingrays are "
"ovoviviparous and carry the eggs until the fries are ready to get out in to "
"the world."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "gar"
msgid_plural "gars"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""
msgstr[2] ""

#. ~ Description of monster "gar"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A fish belonging to the Lepisosteidae family.  These enormous fishes can be "
"found from North America to the Caribbean and are well known for their "
"prehistoric appearance."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "tucunaré"
msgid_plural "tucunarés"
msgstr[0] "tucunaré"
msgstr[1] "tucunarés"
msgstr[2] "tucunarés"

#. ~ Description of monster "tucunaré"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A vicious predatory cichlid found along the northern tributaries of South "
"America from Panama to the Amazon.  Very sought among sport fishing "
"enthusiasts."
msgstr ""
"Un voraz cíclido depredador que se encuentra a lo largo de los afluentes del"
" norte de Sudamérica, desde Panamá hasta el Amazonas. Muy buscado entre los "
"aficionados a la pesca deportiva."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "discus"
msgid_plural "discuses"
msgstr[0] "discuse"
msgstr[1] "discuses"
msgstr[2] "discuses"

#. ~ Description of monster "discus"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A round and colorful genus of fish native to the Amazon river basin.  Very "
"popular in aquariums but expensive to maintain in captivity."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "angelfish"
msgid_plural "angelfish"
msgstr[0] "pez ángel"
msgstr[1] "peces ángel"
msgstr[2] "peces ángel"

#. ~ Description of monster "angelfish"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A genus of freshwater fish with a triangular shape native to South America."
"  Unrelated to the marine angel fishes and known to be semi-aggressive in "
"captivity."
msgstr ""
"Género de peces de agua dulce con forma triangular originarios de "
"Sudamérica. No está relacionado con los peces ángeles marinos y se sabe que "
"es semiagresivo en cautividad."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "goldfish"
msgid_plural "goldfish"
msgstr[0] "pez dorado"
msgstr[1] "peces de dorados"
msgstr[2] "peces de dorados"

#. ~ Description of monster "goldfish"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A tiny domestic fish related to the carp.  This one must be part of a feral "
"population but still keeps the golden hue of its domestic counterpart."
msgstr ""
"Un pequeño pez doméstico emparentado con la carpa. Este debe formar parte de"
" una población asilvestrada, pero sigue manteniendo el tono dorado de su "
"homólogo doméstico."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "koi"
msgid_plural "kois"
msgstr[0] "koi"
msgstr[1] "kois"
msgstr[2] "kois"

#. ~ Description of monster "koi"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A domestic variant of the Amur carp originally bred in Japan for its color "
"variations.  These fishes are known to devolve quickly to feral status if "
"left to escape."
msgstr ""
"Una variante doméstica de la carpa Amur criada originalmente en Japón por "
"sus variaciones de color. Se sabe que estos peces evolucionan rápidamente "
"hasta convertirse en asilvestrados si se les deja escapar."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "tilapia"
msgid_plural "tilapias"
msgstr[0] "tilapia"
msgstr[1] "tilapias"
msgstr[2] "tilapias"

#. ~ Description of monster "tilapia"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A genus of cichlids native to Africa but bred worldwide for food.  They are "
"adaptable herbivorous fishes that can survive well even in salt water."
msgstr ""
"Género de cíclidos originario de África pero criado en todo el mundo para su"
" alimentación. Son peces herbívoros adaptables que pueden sobrevivir bien "
"incluso en agua salada."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "sabalo"
msgid_plural "sabalos"
msgstr[0] "sabalo"
msgstr[1] "sabalos"
msgstr[2] "sabalos"

#. ~ Description of monster "sabalo"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A fish belonging to the Prochilodontidae family.  They are native to South "
"America and most species can be found feeding on detritus."
msgstr ""
"Pez de la familia Prochilodontidae. Son nativos de Sudamérica y la mayoría "
"de las especies se alimentan de detritus."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "oscar"
msgid_plural "oscars"
msgstr[0] "oscare"
msgstr[1] "oscares"
msgstr[2] "oscares"

#. ~ Description of monster "oscar"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A species of omnivorous cichlid native to South America.  Quite popular in "
"aquariums with several different colored breeds."
msgstr ""
"Especie de cíclido omnívoro originario de Sudamérica. Bastante popular en "
"los acuarios con varias razas de diferentes colores."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "guapote"
msgid_plural "guapotes"
msgstr[0] "guapote"
msgstr[1] "guapotes"
msgstr[2] "guapotes"

#. ~ Description of monster "guapote"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A genus of cichlids found in Central America.  All of the species are "
"predatory with different coloration and sizes."
msgstr ""
"Género de cíclidos de América Central. Todas las especies son depredadoras "
"con diferentes coloraciones y tamaños."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid "mayaheros"
msgid_plural "mayaheri"
msgstr[0] "mayaheri"
msgstr[1] "mayaheri"
msgstr[2] "mayaheri"

#. ~ Description of monster "mayaheros"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fish.json
msgid ""
"A genus of adaptable cichlids native to Central America.  They can survive "
"in marine environments with some populations even reaching Florida."
msgstr ""
"Género de cíclidos adaptables originarios de América Central. Pueden "
"sobrevivir en ambientes marinos y algunas poblaciones llegan hasta Florida."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_monsters.json
msgid "fungal elephant"
msgid_plural "fungal elephants"
msgstr[0] "elefante fúngico"
msgstr[1] "elefantes fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "elefantes fúngicos"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal elephant"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_monsters.json
msgid ""
"A horrifying image with tendrils seeping out of many oozing wounds, this "
"elephant's form appears more eldritch than animal."
msgstr ""
"Una imagen horripilante con zarcillos que se filtran de muchas heridas "
"supurantes, la forma de este elefante parece más sobrenatural que animal."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal termite"
msgid_plural "fungal termites"
msgstr[0] "termita fúngica"
msgstr[1] "termitas fúngicas"
msgstr[2] "termitas fúngicas"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal termite"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A sickly looking termite riddled with fungal spores.  Traces of a gray "
"substance dribble from its mandibles."
msgstr ""
"Una termita de aspecto enfermizo plagada de esporas de hongos. Restos de una"
" sustancia gris gotean de sus mandíbulas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal scorpion"
msgid_plural "fungal scorpions"
msgstr[0] "escorpión fúngico"
msgstr[1] "escorpiones fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "escorpiones fúngicos"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal scorpion"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A huge scorpion infected with fungus.  The stinger on its tail gushes with "
"an ominous gray liquid."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme escorpión infectado por un hongo. El aguijón de su cola mana un "
"siniestro líquido gris."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal cultivator"
msgid_plural "fungal cultivators"
msgstr[0] "cultivador fúngico"
msgstr[1] "cultivadores fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "cultivadores fúngicos"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal cultivator"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A massive mycoid that shambles around the spore infested environment.  "
"Clusters of small fungal pods seem to grow and from its body."
msgstr ""
"Un micoide gigantesco que se desplaza por el entorno infestado de esporas. "
"Racimos de pequeñas vainas de hongos parecen crecer y de su cuerpo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal ganglion"
msgid_plural "fungal ganglions"
msgstr[0] "ganglio fúngico"
msgstr[1] "ganglios fúngicos"
msgstr[2] "ganglios fúngicos"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal ganglion"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"An enormous fungus rooted to the ground that seems to be the nexus for all "
"the fungus in the area.  It periodically gives birth to new saprolings."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme hongo arraigado al suelo que parece ser el nexo de unión de todos "
"los hongos de la zona. Periódicamente da a luz a nuevos saprolings."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "saproling"
msgid_plural "saprolings"
msgstr[0] "saproling"
msgstr[1] "saprolings"
msgstr[2] "saprolings"

#. ~ Description of monster "saproling"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A very small mycoid born out of a fungal pod.  Very vulnerable but overtime "
"it will become a proper fungaloid."
msgstr ""
"Un micoide muy pequeño nacido de una vaina fúngica. Muy vulnerable, pero con"
" el tiempo se convertirá en un verdadero fungaloide."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal caretaker"
msgid_plural "fungal caretakers"
msgstr[0] "hongo cuidador"
msgstr[1] "hongos cuidadores"
msgstr[2] "hongos cuidadores"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal caretaker"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A young mycoid that has grown some time on the spore growth.  It is still a "
"juvenile but it can already fend for itself to a degree."
msgstr ""
"Un joven micoide que ha crecido algún tiempo en el crecimiento de las "
"esporas. Todavía es un juvenil pero ya puede valerse por sí mismo hasta "
"cierto punto."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal perforator"
msgid_plural "fungal perforators"
msgstr[0] "hongo perforador"
msgstr[1] "hongos perforadorer"
msgstr[2] "hongos perforadorer"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal perforator"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A skittering fungal creature with a sharp needle-like appendage.  Its sting "
"probably contains spores."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura fúngica escurridiza con un apéndice afilado en forma de aguja. "
"Su aguijón contiene probablemente esporas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal quillbag"
msgid_plural "fungal quillbags"
msgstr[0] "saco de hongos"
msgstr[1] "sacos de hongos"
msgstr[2] "sacos de hongos"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal quillbag"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A strange fungal creature with a thorny covering.  The barbs on its body may"
" contain spores."
msgstr ""
"Una extraña criatura fúngica con una cubierta de espinas. Las púas de su "
"cuerpo pueden contener esporas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal moldspring"
msgid_plural "fungal moldsprings"
msgstr[0] "hongo mohoso"
msgstr[1] "hongos mohosos"
msgstr[2] "hongos mohosos"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal moldspring"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A large and amorphous fungal creature.  It slithers around the ground "
"leaving a trail of spores in its wake."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura fúngica grande y amorfa. Se desliza por el suelo dejando un "
"rastro de esporas a su paso."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid "fungal dispersor"
msgid_plural "fungal dispersors"
msgstr[0] "hongo dispersor"
msgstr[1] "hongos dispersores"
msgstr[2] "hongos dispersores"

#. ~ Description of monster "fungal dispersor"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_fungus.json
msgid ""
"A strange fungal creature similar to a moving balloon.  It releases a cloud "
"of spores in all directions."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "large scorpion"
msgid_plural "large scorpions"
msgstr[0] "escorpión grande"
msgstr[1] "escorpiones grandes"
msgstr[2] "escorpiones grandes"

#. ~ Description of monster "large scorpion"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "A mutated scorpion the size of a dog."
msgstr "Un escorpión mutado del tamaño de un perro."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_insect_spider.json
msgid "giant scorpion"
msgid_plural "giant scorpions"
msgstr[0] "escorpión gigante"
msgstr[1] "escorpiones gigantes"
msgstr[2] "escorpiones gigantes"

#. ~ Description of monster "giant scorpion"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A menacing arachnid with a second set of pedipalps, clacking rabidly as an "
"engorged stinger looms over its body."
msgstr ""
"Un arácnido amenazante con un segundo juego de pedipalpos, chasqueando "
"rabiosamente mientras un aguijón hinchado se cierne sobre su cuerpo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "termite nymph"
msgid_plural "termite nymphs"
msgstr[0] "ninfa de termita"
msgstr[1] "ninfas de termita"
msgstr[2] "ninfas de termita"

#. ~ Description of monster "termite nymph"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"Unlike ants, Termites produce nymphs instead of larvae.  Their nymphs grow "
"first into workers before diverging into the higher castes."
msgstr ""
"A diferencia de las hormigas, las termitas producen ninfas en lugar de "
"larvas. Sus ninfas crecen primero hasta convertirse en obreras antes de "
"divergir en castas superiores."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "termite worker"
msgid_plural "termite workers"
msgstr[0] "trabajador termita"
msgstr[1] "trabajadores termita"
msgstr[2] "trabajadores termita"

#. ~ Description of monster "termite worker"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"An adult termite dedicated to tending the colony.  Termite workers while "
"developed are still capable of growing into soldiers or alates given the "
"time."
msgstr ""
"Una termita adulta dedicada a cuidar la colonia. Las termitas obreras, "
"aunque desarrolladas, son capaces de convertirse en soldados o alados si se "
"les da tiempo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "termite soldier"
msgid_plural "termite soldiers"
msgstr[0] "soldado termita"
msgstr[1] "soldados termita"
msgstr[2] "soldados termita"

#. ~ Description of monster "termite soldier"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"An enormous termite dedicated to the defense of the colony.  It has a pair "
"of enormous mandibles capable of cutting bone and chitin."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme termita dedicada a la defensa de la colonia. Tiene un par de "
"enormes mandíbulas capaces de cortar hueso y quitina."

#. ~ Description of monster "termite soldier"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"An enormous termite dedicated to the defense of the colony.  It has a "
"strange horn-like projection on its head."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme termita dedicada a la defensa de la colonia. Tiene un extraño "
"saliente en forma de cuerno en la cabeza."

#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "termite soldier"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "The termite sprays a sticky chemical out of its head!"
msgstr "¡La termita rocía un producto químico pegajoso de su cabeza!"

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "termite alate"
msgid_plural "termite alates"
msgstr[0] "alado termita"
msgstr[1] "alados termita"
msgstr[2] "alados termita"

#. ~ Description of monster "termite alate"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"An enormous winged termite dedicated to spreading new colonies.  They are "
"not violent but will respond to aggression if molested."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme termita alada que se dedica a extender nuevas colonias. No son "
"violentas, pero responden con agresividad si son molestadas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "termite king"
msgid_plural "termite kings"
msgstr[0] "rey termita"
msgstr[1] "reyes termita"
msgstr[2] "reyes termita"

#. ~ Description of monster "termite king"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A gigantic termite dedicated to protecting the queen and their offspring.  "
"While its main role is breeding the king is certainly well armed."
msgstr ""
"Una gigantesca termita dedicada a proteger a la reina y a sus crías. Aunque "
"su función principal es la cría el rey está ciertamente bien armado."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "termite queen"
msgid_plural "termite queens"
msgstr[0] "reina termita"
msgstr[1] "reinas termitas "
msgstr[2] "reinas termitas "

#. ~ Description of monster "termite queen"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A colossal termite which is the basis of the colony along with her king.  "
"Its enlarged abdomen limits her movements but she barely needs to do so."
msgstr ""
"Una termita colosal que es la base de la colonia junto con su rey. Su "
"abdomen agrandado limita sus movimientos, pero apenas necesita hacerlo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "velvet worm"
msgid_plural "velvet worms"
msgstr[0] "gusano terciopelo"
msgstr[1] "gusanos terciopelo"
msgstr[2] "gusanos terciopelo"

#. ~ Description of monster "velvet worm"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"A mutated velvet worm several times its normal size.  These peculiar "
"creatures hunt at night using silent feet and sticky attacks."
msgstr ""
"Un gusano terciopelo mutado en varias veces su tamaño normal. Estas "
"peculiares criaturas cazan de noche utilizando el sigilo y ataques "
"pegajosos."

#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "velvet worm"
#. ~ Monster message of special attack of monster "velvet wyrm"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"The velvet worm shoots sticky strings of goo from two appendages in its "
"head!"
msgstr ""
"El gusano terciopelo dispara hilos pegajosos de pegamento desde dos "
"apéndices en su cabeza."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid "velvet wyrm"
msgid_plural "velvet wyrms"
msgstr[0] "wyrm terciopelo"
msgstr[1] "wyrms terciopelo"
msgstr[2] "wyrms terciopelo"

#. ~ Description of monster "velvet wyrm"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_insect_spider.json
msgid ""
"An enormous velvet worm the length of several humans.  Its mouthparts and "
"skin have reinforced to hunt down and defend against the new fauna of the "
"Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"Un enorme gusano terciopelo de la longitud de varios humanos. Sus piezas "
"bucales y su piel se han reforzado para cazar y defenderse de la nueva fauna"
" del Cataclismo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_mammal.json
msgid "bush elephant"
msgid_plural "bush elephants"
msgstr[0] "elefante arbusto"
msgstr[1] "elefantes de arbusto"
msgstr[2] "elefantes de arbusto"

#. ~ Description of monster "bush elephant"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
#: data/mods/desert_region/desert_mammal.json
msgid ""
"The African Bush Elephant is a massive terrestrial animal with two long "
"tusks protruding from its mouth.  Elephantry is on the rise since the "
"Cataclysm."
msgstr ""
"El elefante africano de arbusto es un animal terrestre gigante con dos "
"largos colmillos que sobresalen de su boca. La elefantería está en aumento "
"desde el Cataclismo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "jaguar"
msgid_plural "jaguars"
msgstr[0] "jaguar"
msgstr[1] "jaguares"
msgstr[2] "jaguares"

#. ~ Description of monster "jaguar"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"The largest native feline in the Americas.  With the advent of the Cataclysm"
" these spotted felines have recovered some territory."
msgstr ""
"El mayor felino nativo de América. Con la llegada del Cataclismo estos "
"felinos moteados han recuperado parte del territorio."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "spectacled bear"
msgid_plural "spectacled bears"
msgstr[0] "oso de anteojos"
msgstr[1] "osos de anteojos"
msgstr[2] "osos de anteojos"

#. ~ Description of monster "spectacled bear"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"The Andean bear, sometimes called spectacled bear is the only bear species "
"native to South America.  It lives in a very diverse array of ecosystems on "
"low to high altitudes."
msgstr ""
"El oso andino, a veces llamado oso de anteojos, es la única especie de oso "
"autóctona de Sudamérica. Vive en una gama muy diversa de ecosistemas en "
"altitudes bajas y altas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "spectacled bear cub"
msgid_plural "spectacled bear cubs"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de oso de anteojos"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de oso de anteojos"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de oso de anteojos"

#. ~ Description of monster "spectacled bear cub"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A juvenile spectacled bear.  Its mother could be nearby, better not to mess "
"around it."
msgstr ""
"Un oso de anteojos joven. Su madre podría estar cerca, mejor no meterse con "
"ella."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "ocelot"
msgid_plural "ocelots"
msgstr[0] "ocelote"
msgstr[1] "ocelotes"
msgstr[2] "ocelotes"

#. ~ Description of monster "ocelot"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A widespread medium sized feline known for its spotted and streaked fur.  It"
" can be found as north as the southern US and even the Caribbean."
msgstr ""
"Un felino de tamaño medio muy extendido, conocido por su pelaje manchado y "
"rayado. Se puede encontrar en el norte de Estados Unidos e incluso en el "
"Caribe."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "tapir calf"
msgid_plural "tapir calfs"
msgstr[0] "ternero de tapir"
msgstr[1] "terneros de tapir"
msgstr[2] "terneros de tapir"

#. ~ Description of monster "tapir calf"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A baby tapir.  Unlike the adults, tapir calves are born with spots and "
"streaks on their fur for camouflage."
msgstr ""
"Una cría de tapir. A diferencia de los adultos, las crías de tapir nacen con"
" manchas y vetas en su pelaje para camuflarse."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "tapir"
msgid_plural "tapirs"
msgstr[0] "tapir"
msgstr[1] "tapires"
msgstr[2] "tapires"

#. ~ Description of monster "tapir"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A medium to large herbivore distantly related to the Rhinoceros.  It is both"
" a capable runner and swimmer in order to evade predators."
msgstr ""
"Herbívoro de tamaño medio a grande, emparentado con el rinoceronte. Es capaz"
" de correr y nadar para evitar a los depredadores."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "camel"
msgid_plural "camels"
msgstr[0] "camello"
msgstr[1] "camellos"
msgstr[2] "camellos"

#. ~ Description of monster "camel"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A large herbivore introduced from the old world via zoos and private owners."
"  Ironically, camels were once native to North America in distant times."
msgstr ""
"Un gran herbívoro introducido desde el viejo mundo a través de zoológicos y "
"propietarios privados. Irónicamente, los camellos fueron nativos de América "
"del Norte en tiempos lejanos."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "coati"
msgid_plural "coatis"
msgstr[0] "coati"
msgstr[1] "coatis"
msgstr[2] "coatis"

#. ~ Description of monster "coati"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A relative of the raccoon, coatis can be easily distinguished by their long "
"noses and sometimes ringed tails.  They live as north as Arizona, and form "
"large family groups."
msgstr ""
"Pariente del mapache, los coatíes se distinguen fácilmente por su larga "
"nariz y su cola a veces anillada. Viven hasta el norte de Arizona y forman "
"grandes grupos familiares."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "bush dog"
msgid_plural "bush dogs"
msgstr[0] "perro de caza"
msgstr[1] "perros de caza"
msgstr[2] "perros de caza"

#. ~ Description of monster "bush dog"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small and elusive canid native to South and Central America.  It is "
"harmless to humans but their packs can take on prey several times their "
"size."
msgstr ""
"Un cánido pequeño y escurridizo originario de América del Sur y Central. Es "
"inofensivo para el ser humano, pero sus manadas pueden enfrentarse a presas "
"de varias veces su tamaño."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "coipo"
msgid_plural "coipos"
msgstr[0] "coipos"
msgstr[1] "coipos"
msgstr[2] "coipos"

#. ~ Description of monster "coipo"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A big rodent similar in shape to a beaver.  In the past it was hunted and "
"raised for its fur."
msgstr ""
"Es un roedor de gran tamaño, similar a un castor. En el pasado se cazaba y "
"criaba por su piel."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "baby capybara"
msgid_plural "baby capybaras"
msgstr[0] "cria capibara"
msgstr[1] "crias capibaras"
msgstr[2] "crias capibaras"

#. ~ Description of monster "baby capybara"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A baby capybara.  Like most rodents they are born by the numbers as they "
"usually get eaten early in their lives by many predators."
msgstr ""
"Una cría de capibara. Como la mayoría de los roedores, nacen en masa, ya que"
" suelen ser devorados al principio de su vida por muchos depredadores."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "capybara"
msgid_plural "capybaras"
msgstr[0] "capibara"
msgstr[1] "capibaras"
msgstr[2] "capibaras"

#. ~ Description of monster "capybara"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"The largest rodent in the world.  Capybaras are pretty chill aquatic "
"herbivores that roam around wetlands and rivers in South America."
msgstr ""
"El mas grande roedor del mundo. Los capibaras son herbívoros acuáticos "
"bastante fríos que vagan por los humedales y ríos de Sudamérica."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "hippopotamus"
msgid_plural "hippopotamus"
msgstr[0] "hipopótamo"
msgstr[1] "hipopótamos"
msgstr[2] "hipopótamos"

#. ~ Description of monster "hippopotamus"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A massive and aggressive aquatic mammal.  Hippos originate from Africa but "
"were brought to the Americas by zoos and particularly eccentric criminals."
msgstr ""
"Un mamífero acuático grande y agresivo. Los hipopótamos son originarios de "
"África, pero fueron traídos a América por zoológicos y delincuentes "
"especialmente excéntricos."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "peccari piglet"
msgid_plural "peccari piglets"
msgstr[0] "lechón de pecarí"
msgstr[1] "lechones de pecarí"
msgstr[2] "lechones de pecarí"

#. ~ Description of monster "peccari piglet"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"The small offspring of a peccari.  Much like true boar piglets, this one has"
" a mottled fur as camouflage."
msgstr ""
"La pequeña cría de un pecarí. Al igual que los verdaderos lechones de "
"jabalí, éste tiene un pelaje moteado como camuflaje."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "peccari"
msgid_plural "peccaris"
msgstr[0] "pecarí"
msgstr[1] "pecarís"
msgstr[2] "pecarís"

#. ~ Description of monster "peccari"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small furred omnivore native to the American continent.  Despite looking "
"like a boar it is not directly related to them or their domestic brethren."
msgstr ""
"Pequeño omnívoro de pelaje natural del continente americano. A pesar de su "
"aspecto de jabalí, no está directamente relacionado con ellos ni con sus "
"hermanos domésticos."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "guinea pig"
msgid_plural "guinea pigs"
msgstr[0] "cobaya"
msgstr[1] "cobayas"
msgstr[2] "cobayas"

#. ~ Description of monster "guinea pig"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"Also called cuy by the people of the Andes.  This small rodent was bred "
"originally for food but it has gained the hearts of many as a pet."
msgstr ""
"También llamado cuy por la gente de los Andes. Este pequeño roedor se criaba"
" originalmente para alimentarse, pero se ha ganado el corazón de muchos como"
" mascota."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "wallaby joey"
msgid_plural "wallaby joeys"
msgstr[0] "cachorro de wallaby"
msgstr[1] "cachorros de wallaby"
msgstr[2] "cachorros de wallaby"

#. ~ Description of monster "wallaby joey"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A baby wallaby.  Most of the time they hide inside their mother's pouch but "
"eventually grow too big."
msgstr ""
"Una cría de ualabí. La mayor parte del tiempo se esconden dentro de la bolsa"
" de su madre, pero con el tiempo crecen demasiado."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid "wallaby"
msgid_plural "wallabies"
msgstr[0] "Ualabí"
msgstr[1] "Ualabies"
msgstr[2] "Ualabies"

#. ~ Description of monster "wallaby"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_mammal.json
msgid ""
"A small to large hopping marsupial from Australia and New Guinea.  Even "
"before the Cataclysm there were many feral populations of them around the "
"world."
msgstr ""
"Un marsupial saltarín de pequeño a gran tamaño de Australia y Nueva Guinea. "
"Incluso antes del cataclismo había muchas poblaciones asilvestradas de ellos"
" en todo el mundo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "aether krill"
msgid_plural "aether krills"
msgstr[0] "krill éter"
msgstr[1] "krills éter"
msgstr[2] "krills éter"

#. ~ Description of monster "aether krill"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A tiny flying alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely "
"resembles a marine crustacean like shrimp."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña criatura alienígena voladora traída por las tormentas del "
"portal. Se parece vagamente a un crustáceo marino como el camarón."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "paddle crab"
msgid_plural "paddle crabs"
msgstr[0] "cangrejo pala"
msgstr[1] "cangrejos pala"
msgstr[2] "cangrejos pala"

#. ~ Description of monster "paddle crab"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"An alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a crab"
" or lobster with paddles instead of legs."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se parece "
"vagamente a un cangrejo o langosta con palas en lugar de patas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "emperor prawn"
msgid_plural "emperor prawns"
msgstr[0] "langosta emperador"
msgstr[1] "langostas emperador"
msgstr[2] "langostas emperador"

#. ~ Description of monster "emperor prawn"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A large alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a"
" prehistoric crustacean with flippers and a set of pincers."
msgstr ""
"Una gran criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se parece "
"vagamente a un crustáceo prehistórico con aletas y pinzas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "triglav star"
msgid_plural "triglav stars"
msgstr[0] "estrella triglav"
msgstr[1] "estrellas triglav"
msgstr[2] "estrellas triglav"

#. ~ Description of monster "triglav star"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A tiny alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a "
"sea star crawling on three spindly legs."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se "
"parece vagamente a una estrella de mar que se arrastra sobre tres patas "
"delgadas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "scale urchin"
msgid_plural "scale urchins"
msgstr[0] "erizo de escama"
msgstr[1] "erizos de escama"
msgstr[2] "erizos de escama"

#. ~ Description of monster "scale urchin"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A tiny alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a "
"sea urchin with scales instead of spines."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se "
"parece vagamente a un erizo de mar con escamas en lugar de espinas."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "thornothurian"
msgid_plural "thornothurians"
msgstr[0] "espinófilo"
msgstr[1] "espinófilos"
msgstr[2] "espinófilos"

#. ~ Description of monster "thornothurian"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"An alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a sea "
"cucumber with a set of thorns running on its body."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se parece "
"vagamente a un pepino de mar con un conjunto de espinas que recorren su "
"cuerpo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "aer jelly"
msgid_plural "aer jellies"
msgstr[0] "medusa volador"
msgstr[1] "medusas voladoras"
msgstr[2] "medusas voladoras"

#. ~ Description of monster "aer jelly"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A tiny flying alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely "
"resembles a jellyfish with balloon-like body."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña criatura alienígena voladora traída por las tormentas del "
"portal. Se parece vagamente a una medusa con cuerpo de globo."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "sea papalotl"
msgid_plural "sea papalomeh"
msgstr[0] "papalote marina"
msgstr[1] "papalotes marinas"
msgstr[2] "papalotes marinas"

#. ~ Description of monster "sea papalotl"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"An alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a "
"floating box jellyfish with a translucent body."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se asemeja "
"vagamente a una medusa caja flotante con un cuerpo translúcido."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "sky phantom"
msgid_plural "sky phantoms"
msgstr[0] "fantasma celestial"
msgstr[1] "fantasmas celestiales"
msgstr[2] "fantasmas celestiales"

#. ~ Description of monster "sky phantom"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A huge alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It resembles a "
"portuguese man'o'war fused to a zeppelin."
msgstr ""
"Una enorme criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se "
"parece a un man'o'war portugués fusionado con un zepelín."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "wizard snail"
msgid_plural "wizard snails"
msgstr[0] "caracol mago"
msgstr[1] "caracoles mago"
msgstr[2] "caracoles mago"

#. ~ Description of monster "wizard snail"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A tiny alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a "
"gastropod with a hat-like shell."
msgstr ""
"Una pequeña criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se "
"parece vagamente a un gasterópodo con un caparazón en forma de sombrero."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "hyolith conch"
msgid_plural "hyolith conchs"
msgstr[0] "concha de hollín"
msgstr[1] "conchas de hollín"
msgstr[2] "conchas de hollín"

#. ~ Description of monster "hyolith conch"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"An alien creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles a "
"large conch snail with a straight shell."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura alienígena traída por las tormentas del portal. Se asemeja "
"vagamente a un gran caracol de concha recta."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "nimbelemnite"
msgid_plural "nimbelemnites"
msgstr[0] "belemnite"
msgstr[1] "belemnites"
msgstr[2] "belemnites"

#. ~ Description of monster "nimbelemnite"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"An alien flying creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles"
" an ancient cephalopod and moves quite fast."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura voladora alienígena traída por las tormentas de portal. Se "
"parece vagamente a un cefalópodo antiguo y se mueve bastante rápido."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "atmmonoid"
msgid_plural "atmmonoids"
msgstr[0] "ammonoidea"
msgstr[1] "ammonoideas"
msgstr[2] "ammonoideas"

#. ~ Description of monster "atmmonoid"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"An alien flying creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely resembles"
" a prehistoric cephalopod with a helix shell."
msgstr ""
"Una criatura voladora alienígena traída por las tormentas de portal. Se "
"parece vagamente a un cefalópodo prehistórico con caparazón en forma de "
"hélice."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid "ballistoceras"
msgid_plural "ballistocerae"
msgstr[0] "ballistocerae"
msgstr[1] "ballistocerae"
msgstr[2] "ballistocerae"

#. ~ Description of monster "ballistoceras"
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
msgid ""
"A large alien flying creature brought by the portal storms.  It vaguely "
"resembles a prehistoric cephalopod with a long straight shell."
msgstr ""
"Una gran criatura voladora alienígena traída por las tormentas de portal. Se"
" parece vagamente a un cefalópodo prehistórico con un caparazón largo y "
"recto."

#. ~ Monster name
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/monsters/tropical_nether.json
